chel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3082473d-d19d-52f2-a312-28b2ed4a792d', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3082473d-d19d-52f2-a312-28b2ed4a792d'}, {'abstract': 'America has always been a beacon for those unable to live a life of liberty, and the gay marriage ruling sends a strong signal to other countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/opinion/the-courts-global-message-on-doma.html', 'snippet': 'America has always been a beacon for those unable to live a life of liberty, and the gay marriage ruling sends a strong signal to other countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — LAST week’s Supreme Court decision to strike down the core provisions of the Defense of Marriage Act is a stride toward greater equality in the United States. But it is also a shift that will reverberate far beyond our shores. America has always been a beacon for those unable to live a life of liberty in their homelands, and the ruling sends a strong signal of encouragement to such individuals, and to their governments, about what we consider fair and morally acceptable. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/13/opinion/Suri-Manil-circular/Suri-Manil-circular-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Court’s Global Message on DOMA', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Court’s Global Message on DOMA', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suri, Manil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T01:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manil Suri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/53cd3ab2-8ae8-5845-9cc8-77ab589c96f8', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53cd3ab2-8ae8-5845-9cc8-77ab589c96f8'}, {'abstract': 'Combine ill-thought-out government incentives with a misguided corporate tax system and what do you get? A blockbuster drug.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/06/30/the-orphan-jackpot/', 'snippet': 'Combine ill-thought-out government incentives with a misguided corporate tax system and what do you get? A blockbuster drug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE sure sign that federal regulations and policies are out of whack is when companies start making a business model out of gaming them. That’s particularly true in two areas of government rule making — drug regulation and corporate taxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Orphan Jackpot', 'kicker': 'Steven Rattner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Orphan Jackpot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz Pharmaceuticals Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T01:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1471f518-1cc6-5532-8606-a4aa27af5e4c', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1471f518-1cc6-5532-8606-a4aa27af5e4c'}, {'abstract': 'Norman Siegel, who led the New York Civil Liberties Union from 1985 to 2000, remains a defender of free speech, no matter how unpopular a group and its opinions may be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/nyregion/a-mellower-mr-negative-but-still-passionate-about-free-expression.html', 'snippet': 'Norman Siegel, who led the New York Civil Liberties Union from 1985 to 2000, remains a defender of free speech, no matter how unpopular a group and its opinions may be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a July 2 about 10 years ago, Norman Siegel had a constitutional crisis all his own. In Barcelona on vacation, he realized that he had left his copy of the United States Constitution back home in New York. This was terrible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/01/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/01/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-t