words': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MEDICAL ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T04:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57138bc9-7674-5b5e-b7c1-ff616e2839d0', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57138bc9-7674-5b5e-b7c1-ff616e2839d0'}, {'abstract': 'The Devils took Anthony Brodeur, an 18-year-old goalie, with the 208th pick of the 211-pick draft, sending their seventh-round pick in 2015 to the Kings in exchange for the chance to pick Brodeur.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/devils-work-a-trade-so-they-can-select-brodeurs-son/', 'snippet': 'The Devils took Anthony Brodeur, an 18-year-old goalie, with the 208th pick of the 211-pick draft, sending their seventh-round pick in 2015 to the Kings in exchange for the chance to pick Brodeur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Martin Brodeur added another accomplishment to his distinguished Devils career Sunday: stepping to the podium at the Prudential Center and announcing the selection of his son Anthony at the N.H.L. draft. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Devils Work a Trade So They Can Select Brodeur’s Son', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brodeur, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T04:16:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/891a5c21-bcd0-5125-a67d-66aa5474d8db', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891a5c21-bcd0-5125-a67d-66aa5474d8db'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:50 A.M. (STARZ) A DANGEROUS METHOD (2011) A disturbed young Russian, Sabina Spielrein (Keira Knightley), is brought to a clinic in Zurich in the early 20th century, and a doctor named Carl Jung (Michael Fassbender, above with Ms. Knightley) performs a new treatment called psychoanalysis to help her. Soon she becomes his lover and finally a colleague. But as emotionally connected as Sabina is to Jung, it is with his mentor, Sigmund Freud (Viggo Mortensen), that she finds a more cerebral affinity. Writing in The New York Times, A. O. Scott called this film from David Cronenberg, based on a play by its screenwriter, Christopher Hampton, and drawn from a book by John Kerr, a “subtle and intellectually thrilling true story.” The movie “is full of ideas about sexuality — some quite provocative, even a century after their first articulation — but it also recognizes and communicates the erotic power of ideas,” he said. “There are scenes of kinky activity between Sabina and Jung that will no doubt enjoy long life in specialized corners of the Internet, but the most unsettling aspect of ‘A Dangerous Method’ may be the links it suggests between sex and thinking. The mind is both slave and master of the body’s appetites, and the absurd and terrifying task of stabilizing that dynamic, in theory and in practice, is embraced equally by the film and the fragile, serious historical figures who inhabit it.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T04:19:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf3b218-c5dd-52a6-a2b1-99ca2ebc2ddc', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf3b218-c5dd-52a6-a2b1-99ca2ebc2ddc'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 1, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/pageoneplus/corrections-july-1-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 1, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 1, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T04:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64c510c3-5120-53eb-8f71-10