cessed foods – like pizzas. So I made some pizza dough and marinara sauce, picked up some vegetables, fired up my Weber, and spent a delightful late afternoon making pizzas on it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1323, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forget Tofu Hot Dogs: Pizza on the Grill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pizza', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T06:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf870ba0-fd11-57b1-8a30-c97d8bc60658', 'word_count': 1665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf870ba0-fd11-57b1-8a30-c97d8bc60658'}, {'abstract': 'Prakash Bhatt, 36, was among the many volunteers who risked their own lives to save pilgrims and locals stranded in Uttarakhand during the flash floods.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/in-uttarakhand-everest-climbers-became-rescue-men/', 'snippet': 'Prakash Bhatt, 36, was among the many volunteers who risked their own lives to save pilgrims and locals stranded in Uttarakhand during the flash floods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI— On the morning of June 17, Prakash Bhatt, a 36-year-old soldier in the Indian Army and an instructor at the government-run Nehru Institute of Mountaineering in Uttarkashi in the northern Indian state of Uttarakhand, was teaching a class. Mr. Bhatt is one of the 10 soldiers on a three-year assignment to the mountaineering institute, which trains mountaineering enthusiasts and provides lessons in search and rescue operations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/27/world/asia/27-army-rescue-IndiaInk/27-army-rescue-IndiaInk-articleL