 start a loan brokerage, I guess it’s pretty clear what that makes me — along with thousands of other small-business owners and entrepreneurs I have met over the years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Cuban Thinks I’m a Moron', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clinton Global Initiative', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T15:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/711e5c21-0a36-5000-8462-b9bce0d47db0', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/711e5c21-0a36-5000-8462-b9bce0d47db0'}, {'abstract': 'In another sign of the strong Broadway season for plays, Christopher Durang’s comedy “Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike” has recouped its $2.75 million capitalization and will have the rest of the summer to earn profits.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/broadways-vanya-and-sonia-recoups-investment/', 'snippet': 'In another sign of the strong Broadway season for plays, Christopher Durang’s comedy “Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike” has recouped its $2.75 million capitalization and will have the rest of the summer to earn profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another sign that Broadway’s 2012-13 season was strong overall for plays at the box office, Christopher Durang’s comedy “Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike” has recouped its $2.75 million capitalization and will have the rest of the summer to earn profits for its investors, the producers announced on Monday. “Vanya and Sonia,” starring David Hyde Pierce and Sigourney Weaver, is the fifth play from the season to recoup, joining “Glengarry Glen Ross” (which starred Al Pacino), “The Heiress” (Jessica Chastain), “Lucky Guy” (Tom Hanks) and “I’ll Eat You Last” (Bette Midler). Another play, “Grace,” narrowly missed recouping, in part due to the fall-out of Hurricane Sandy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-vanya/01artsbeat-vanya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-vanya/01artsbeat-vanya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-vanya/01artsbeat-vanya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-vanya/01artsbeat-vanya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-vanya/01artsbeat-vanya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-vanya/01artsbeat-vanya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLa