': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7070e80b-36cd-5303-83f6-5adf0e1d87b7', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7070e80b-36cd-5303-83f6-5adf0e1d87b7'}, {'abstract': 'Justices Ruth Bader Ginsburg, Sonia Sotomayor and Elena Kagan often came down on the same side in the past term, but look to ideology, not biology, for an explanation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/us/bound-together-on-the-court-but-by-beliefs-not-gender.html', 'snippet': 'Justices Ruth Bader Ginsburg, Sonia Sotomayor and Elena Kagan often came down on the same side in the past term, but look to ideology, not biology, for an explanation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — You can tell a lot about the Supreme Court by looking at who voted with whom. There are 36 possible pairs of justices, and in the term just concluded something interesting happened.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/us/02BAR/02BAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/us/02BAR/02BAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/us/02BAR/02BAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/us/02BAR/02BAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/us/02BAR/02BAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legac