-5acc-90e9-8f39a70619e5'}, {'abstract': 'As the state legislature meets in the wake of a dramatic Democratic filibuster over an abortion bill, Gov. Rick Perry is likely to regain the upper hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/us/texas-democrats-try-to-keep-their-momentum-going.html', 'snippet': 'As the state legislature meets in the wake of a dramatic Democratic filibuster over an abortion bill, Gov. Rick Perry is likely to regain the upper hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — All eyes are on Texas today, but the drama at the end of the first special session of the 83rd state legislature is not likely to repeat itself — at least not yet. While Gov. Rick Perry has brought back the 150 members of the House and the 31 members of the Senate to deal with unfinished business on abortion, transportation and criminal justice, they’ll almost surely gavel in, refer bills to committee and gavel out. Except for a few serial grandstanders, most lawmakers won’t be heard from in any meaningful way inside the Capitol.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Democrats Try to Keep Their Momentum Going', 'kicker': 'Statehouse Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Wendy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T18:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evan Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evan', 'mi