raph': 'Alison Lundergan Grimes, the Kentucky secretary of state and a Democrat, announced on Monday that she will challenge Senator Mitch McConnell, a Republican, in 2014.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Re-Election Is Likely for McConnell, but Not Guaranteed', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimes, Alison Lundergan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T21:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/217d6314-b8d9-5054-b1c8-726e17909617', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/217d6314-b8d9-5054-b1c8-726e17909617'}, {'abstract': 'Park Avenue Summer (today’s name) will hopefully open in a new location.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/seasonal-park-avenue-restaurant-to-close/', 'snippet': 'Park Avenue Summer (today’s name) will hopefully open in a new location.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Park Avenue Summer (and Autumn, Winter and Spring; the restaurant changes its name and look each season) will close at the end of the year. Michael Stillman, a partner in Fourth Wall Restaurants, the owner, said the lease was up after 21 years and an agreement could not be reached with the co-op board, which runs the building. He said they hoped to relocate. “We definitely want to continue with this concept,” Mr. Stillman said. “It’s been doing very well, and everyone seems to like the seasonal changes.” He also said they would close the Post House, in the Lowell Hotel, in August because the restaurant and the hotel lobby are being renovated, a job expected to take about six months. “That one is a question mark,” he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seasonal Park Avenue Restaurant to Close', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lowell Hotel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T21:13:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cfa6e98-0d52-5ea7-a29a-e495ca328543', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cfa6e98-0d52-5ea7-a29a-e495ca328543'}, {'abstract': 'Ghaya Oliveira has been promoted to executive pastry chef at Daniel.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/chefs-on-the-move-2/', 'snippet': 'Ghaya Oliveira has been promoted to executive pastry chef at Daniel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ghaya Oliveira, the pastry chef at Boulud Sud and Bar Boulud, has been promoted to executive pastry chef at Daniel Boulud’s flagship, Daniel. A native of Tunisia who worked in finance, she switched careers after emigrating to America. At Boulud Sud she added several Middle Eastern dishes to the dessert menu, including grapefruit givré with sesame halva and rose loukoum; pistachio kataifi, and rose-marzipan gelato. She replaces Sandro Micheli, who has been the executive pastry chef for nearly two years and who plans to return to France. Tyler Atwell, who was at the Mandarin Oriental in New York, will succeed her at Boulud Sud and Bar Boulud.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chefs on the Move', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boulud, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliveira, Ghaya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daniel (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T21:17:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d3efe8-4091-5f47-9753-cf67c95d5ed0', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d3efe8-4091-5f47-9753-cf67c95d5ed0'}, {'abstract': 'Elise Doganieri is a creator of “The Amazing Race,” and her travel, like the show, has an edge of the extreme.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/business/the-drama-of-travel-made-into-television.html', 'snippet': 'Elise Doganieri is a creator of “The Amazing Race,” and her travel, like the show, has an edge of the extreme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY very first international trip was on TWA back in 1990. I went to Madrid and went backpacking with my college roommate for about five weeks. I went with $1,000, and we lived on wine, cheese, bread and chocolate. That trip changed my life.', 'print_sectio