eb, is about to close its URL forever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an alternate universe where someone would ask you a question you don’t know the answer to and you would respond, “I don’t know, why don’t you AltaVista it?” Instead, in the real world, you reply, “Why don’t you Google it?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/technology/bits-alta/bits-alta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 206, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/technology/bits-alta/bits-alta-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 206, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/technology/bits-alta/bits-alta-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/01/technology/bits-alta/bits-alta-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'AltaVista. What’s That?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AltaVista', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digital Equipment Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T21:35:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dacc51f-d7b8-5b12-8c57-96f73d7e48b1', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dacc51f-d7b8-5b12-8c57-96f73d7e48b1'}, {'abstract': 'When a museum faces a demand that it give up an item, it must consider its public relations needs, the donor of the disputed item and even the country that is asking for its return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/arts/design/museums-property-claims-are-not-simply-about-evidence.html', 'snippet': 'When a museum faces a demand that it give up an item, it must consider its public relations needs, the donor of the disputed item and even the country that is asking for its return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The decision by the Metropolitan Museum of Art to return two ancient Khmer statues to Cambodia last month, less than a year after their ownership was challenged, shows how quickly museums can act on cultural property claims in an era when source countries are far more demanding. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/returns/returns-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 876, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/returns/returns-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 876}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/returns/returns-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/returns/returns-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1538, 'width': 1054, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJum