s “Sylvia” at the Metropolitan Opera House, with American, Argentine, Brazilian, Cuban, Italian and Russian dancers in the lead roles; I love both the work’s music and its choreography. But on Saturday night, as I watched three types of classical Indian dance at the Kumble Theater in Brooklyn, I wanted to bring all those thousands of Lincoln Center balletomanes with me to see how this was just as marvelous — sometimes even more so.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 982, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN/02MOHAPATRA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/arts/dance/02MOHAPATRA_SP