 asylum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/world/europe/snowden-speaks-out-in-moscow-for-first-time.html', 'snippet': 'The former security contractor denounced President Obama, accusing him of blocking his efforts to seek asylum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edward J. Snowden, the fugitive former American security contractor, appeared to break his silence on Monday for the first time since he flew to Moscow eight days earlier. WikiLeaks, the anti-secrecy group, issued a statement attributed to him that denounced President Obama for revoking his passport, opposing his asylum requests and leaving him a “stateless person.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snowden Is Said to Claim U.S. Is Blocking Asylum Bids', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaker Is Said To Claim U.S. Is Blocking Asylum Bids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Rafael', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-01T23:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline