meron and Tyler Winklevoss to create an exchange-traded fund dealing in bitcoins could make the digital currency more accessible to ordinary investors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/first-name-in-the-first-fund-for-bitcoins-winklevoss/', 'snippet': 'A proposal by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss to create an exchange-traded fund dealing in bitcoins could make the digital currency more accessible to ordinary investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bitcoin has been promoted as an alternative crypto-currency that exists outside the realms of governments and central banks. Now, two backers of the digital money are seeking to bring bitcoin into the investing mainstream — if they win the approval of the United States government.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winklevoss Twins Plan First Fund for Bitcoins', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winklevoss Twins Plan First Fund For Bitcoins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exchange Traded Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winklevoss, Cameron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winklevoss, Tyler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bitcoin Project', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winklevoss Bitcoin Trust', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T00:53:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72cda7d3-4f15-5c02-9108-3373626c8d69', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72cda7d3-4f15-5c02-9108-3373626c8d69'}, {'abstract': 'What is a bitcoin? As a virtual currency, it is hardly an easy or intuitive concept. In plainer terms, a bitcoin is digital money that can be bought and sold online in exchange for traditional currencies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/for-starters-its-not-a-coin/', 'snippet': 'What is a bitcoin? As a virtual currency, it is hardly an easy or intuitive concept. In plainer terms, a bitcoin is digital money that can be bought and sold online in exchange for traditional currencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is a bitcoin?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Starters, It’s Not a Coin', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Starters, It’s Not a Coin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T00:55:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3191a47b-47d1-5653-b7a1-46887d3d11bf', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3191a47b-47d1-5653-b7a1-46887d3d11bf'}, {'abstract': 'The vote approved procedures under which the United States Railroad Retirement Board will cut off the benefits, which, officials said, are costing the agency $2 million a month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/nyregion/600-long-island-rail-road-retirees-lose-disability-pay-in-us-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The vote approved procedures under which the United States Railroad Retirement Board will cut off the benefits, which, officials said, are costing the agency $2 million a month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 600 Long Island Rail Road retirees will lose their disability benefits after a federal agency voted last week to halt the payments, amid a sweeping investigation into what prosecutors have called a major disability fraud scheme, according to agency documents and officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '600 Long Island Rail Road Retirees to Lose Disability Pay in U.S. Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '600 Long Island Rail Road Retirees Lose Disability Pay in U.S. Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Island Rail Road Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Railroad Retirement Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disability Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T00:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f3ee58a-2299-5b57-a203-3f3d84a4562d', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f3ee58a-2299-5b57-a203-3f3d84a4562d'}, {'abstract': 'The writer of narrative is often seeking the unknown — the story behind the facts.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/01/how-to-listen/', 'snippet': 'The writer of narrative is often seeking the unknown — the story behind the facts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, I met once a week, 9 a.m. sharp, with a therapist whom I will call Dr. Mason. We would settle in well-worn chairs, Dr. Mason, a slender, balding middle-ager in blazer and striped tie, and me, an anxious academic in Levi’s and tweeds. Sometimes I’d plunge into whatever was on my mind, but other times we would sit and look at each other in silence as I struggled for words. But Dr. Mason had a simple method of getting me to begin. He would lean slightly forward, all the while maintaining eye contact and then when he got my attention, he would nod. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Listen', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T01:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lee Gutkind', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutkind', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea0cb1d3-48fe-5c99-a48b-ce948e48b0ce', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea0cb1d3-48fe-5c99-a48b-ce948e48b0ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court has further limited the ability to sue corporations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/opinion/justice-for-big-business.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court has further limited the ability to sue corporations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IRVINE, Calif. — THE Supreme Court’s momentous decisions last week on affirmative action, voting rights and same-sex marriage overshadowed a disturbing trend: in the final two weeks of its term, the court ruled in favor of big business and closed the courthouse doors to employees, consumers and small businesses seeking remedy for serious injuries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice for Big Business', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice for Big Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chemerinsky, Erwin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liability for Products', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T01:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erwin Chemerinsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erwin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chemerinsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd32b45b-86ce-5d25-8e3a-5407f6b83a4e', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd32b45b-86ce-5d25-8e3a-5407f6b83a4e'}, {'abstract': 'It may be a disaster zone, but it’s our disaster zone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/opinion/living-with-fire.html', 'snippet': 'It may be a disaster zone, but it’s our disaster zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESCOTT, Ariz. — WHEN you build a fire in a fireplace, you start with paper, add kindling, and finally arrange the larger logs on to