ion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Kevin Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/ebf3368d-9b32-5f6c-88da-b08a184781d3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ebf3368d-9b32-5f6c-88da-b08a184781d3'}, {'abstract': 'On the 150th anniversary of the Battle of Gettysburg, letters written by soldiers recall the profundities of loyalty and sacrifice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/opinion/brooks-why-they-fought.html', 'snippet': 'On the 150th anniversary of the Battle of Gettysburg, letters written by soldiers recall the profundities of loyalty and sacrifice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday is the 150th anniversary of the second day of the Battle of Gettysburg. In his eloquent new account, “Gettysburg: the Last Invasion,” the historian Allen Guelzo describes the psychology of the fighters on that day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why They Fought', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why They Fought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T01:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/32056b60-c3cd-51d5-a16f-d6f35e4f2841', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32056b60-c3cd-51d5-a16f-d6f35e4f2841'}, {'abstract': 'In a California lucha libre-style wrestling match, Blue Demon Jr., a self-proclaimed defender of Mexican immigrants, does battle against wrestlers who portray United States border patrol agents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/opinion/border-patrol-body-slam.html', 'snippet': 'In a California lucha libre-style wrestling match, Blue Demon Jr., a self-proclaimed defender of Mexican immigrants, does battle against wrestlers who portray United States border patrol agents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, I stumbled across a Pro Wrestling Revolution show in the Mission District of San Francisco and soon found myself standing up and screaming, “Mexico, Mexico!” along with an almost entirely Latino crowd. The promoter Gabriel Ramirez wanted to bring lucha libre, traditional Mexican-style professional wrestling, to the United States. When he dressed American professional wrestlers as Border Patrol agents to play the main villains, he knew he had a lucrative idea that would appeal to Latino audiences. More than entertainment, however, what he built is a type of Theater of the Oppressed, where social hierarchies are turned upside down and where, unlike in some media coverage, the Mexicans are the heroes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/opinion/video-opdoc-mxwrestling/video-opdoc-mxwrestling-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Border Patrol Body Slam’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Border Patrol Body Slam’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wrestling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Border Patrol (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T01:07:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fea2ace5-f5be-5dd7-addb-cb01e7690bf9', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fea2ace5-f5be-5dd7-addb-cb01e7690bf9'}, {'abstract': 'A movement in Egypt illustrates the greatest strengths and the most glaring weaknesses of the youth groups that have driven many of Egypt’s most fundamental political transformations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/world/middleeast/egypts-young-activists-rouse-protests-but-leave-next-steps-in-hands-of-public.html', 'snippet': 'A movement in Egypt illustrates the greatest strengths and the most glaring weaknesses of the youth groups that have driven many of Egypt’s most fundamental political transformations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Two months ago, five young activists at a Cairo coffee shop hatched a simple plot to capture the growing public frustration with the direction of their country: collect signatures calling for the ouster of President Mohamed Morsi and organize a protest at the presidential palace on June 30, the anniversary of his inauguration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Activists Rouse Egypt Protests but Leave Next Steps to Public', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Young Activists Rouse Protests, but Leave Next Steps in Hands of Public', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Badr, Mahmoud', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdel-Aziz, Mohammed', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shahin, Hassan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heikal, Mohammed', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahba, Mai', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T01:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac2a9ee-4429-54a3-8260-896b184cb6fb', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac2a9ee-4429-54a3-8260-896b184cb6fb'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg argued that critics of his stop-and-frisk policy needed to brush up on math and logic. The same could be said of His Honor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/opinion/mr-bloombergs-logic.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg argued that critics of his stop-and-frisk policy needed to brush up on math and logic. The same could be said of His Honor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Mayor Michael Bloomberg was trying to stem the criticism of his constitutionally suspect stop-and-frisk policy over the weekend, he took a rather strange approach with his loopy logic and discredited arguments. Speaking on his weekly radio program, Mr. Bloomberg dismissed the idea that the policy, under which hundreds of thousands of mainly minority citizens are stopped on the streets every year, is racially imbalanced because it singles out people based on race.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Bloomberg’s Logic', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Bloomberg’s Logic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T01:13:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/acfe380e-cf85-5d3b-b75f-0ffe33696da9', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acfe380e-cf85-5d3b-b75f-0ffe33696da9'}, {'abstract': 'The country is facing a dangerous moment with no guarantee that another transition will be any more successful than the last.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/opinion/military-ultimatum-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The country is facing a dangerous moment with no guarantee that another transition will be any more successful than the last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than two years after Egyptians overthrew an authoritarian, military-backed leader and later installed their first democratically elected president, Mohamed Morsi, the country is facing the possibility of more forcible change — from the military. It is a dangerous moment with no guarantee that another transition will be any more successful than the last.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Military Ultimatum in Egypt', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Military Ultimatum in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-