oposals for eliminating tax deductions, Senate leaders are posturing and wasting everyone’s time with their talk of tax reform, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/zero-based-tax-reform/', 'snippet': 'If they don’t make specific proposals for eliminating tax deductions, Senate leaders are posturing and wasting everyone’s time with their talk of tax reform, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zero-Based Tax Reform', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tax Policy Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T04:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0285eb1f-cce9-5fd9-ba46-b4671fbf60f9', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0285eb1f-cce9-5fd9-ba46-b4671fbf60f9'}, {'abstract': 'Concern over the number of available units shrinking to a near record low was allayed by a robust level of transactions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/nyregion/manhattan-apartment-sales-increase-despite-reduced-inventory.html', 'snippet': 'Concern over the number of available units shrinking to a near record low was allayed by a robust level of transactions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite a continuing depletion of inventory in Manhattan apartment listings this spring that left house hunters with the fewest available second-quarter listings in 13 years, the marketplace was the opposite of stagnant. Not only were there modest upticks in median and average sales prices but, according to a report by the Douglas Elliman brokerage firm that will be released on Tuesday, the market experienced its most vibrant springtime burst of activity since 2007. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manhattan Apartment Sales Increase Despite Reduced Inventory', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apartment Sales Increase Despite Reduced Inventory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T04:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7c1ac41-ed72-5227-b1f0-fa4baf75372d', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7c1ac41-ed72-5227-b1f0-fa4baf75372d'}, {'abstract': 'Robinson Cano hit two homers, and the Yankees scored 10 runs, their highest total since May 10, to help Andy Pettitte remain unbeaten in his last 13 starts against the Twins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/cano-homers-twice-as-yankees-offense-rescues-an-uneven-pettitte.html', 'snippet': 'Robinson Cano hit two homers, and the Yankees scored 10 runs, their highest total since May 10, to help Andy Pettitte remain unbeaten in his last 13 starts against the Twins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — As poorly as the Yankees have played recently, and as miserable as their offense has been, there is nothing so bad that it cannot be fixed by a visit to Minnesota and a date with the Twins.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/02yankeesgame1-img/02yankeesgame1-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cano Homers Twice as Yankees’ Offense Rescues an Uneven Pettitte', 'kicker': 'Yankees 10, Twins 4', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cano Homers Twice as Yankees’ Offense Rescues an Uneven Pettitte', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T04:23:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f17e43ee-a294-5673-b7ab-d10f1981e619', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f17e43ee-a294-5673-b7ab-d10f1981e619'}, {'abstract': 'Another quality start by Shaun Marcum and a two-out, two-run single by Andrew Brown in the 13th inning lifted the Mets over the Diamondbacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/sports/baseball/decent-start-for-marcum-great-finish-for-the-mets.html', 'snippet': 'Another quality start by Shaun Marcum and a two-out, two-run single by Andrew Brown in the 13th inning lifted the Mets over the Diamondbacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In previous seasons the Mets have had attractive trade chips heading toward the July 31 deadline. But after having gutted the team of most of its high priced players, the Mets will have little to offer this summer. If, as expected, they refuse to offer closer Bobby Parnell in a trade, the most likely player to be dealt could be the starter Shaun Marcum. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1469, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/sports/METS/METS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Decent Start for Marcum; Great Finish for the Mets', 'kicker': 'Mets 5, Diamondbacks 4 (13 innings)', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Decent Start for Marcum; Great Finish for the Mets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arangure, Jorge Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcum, Shaun', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T04:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arangure', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf89d47e-f222-5d94-b08b-96d2b14652e7', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf89d47e-f222-5d94-b08b-96d2b14652e7'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11 A.M. (Sundance) RAN (1985) In his masterwork inspired by Shakespeare’s “King Lear,” the Japanese director Akira Kurosawa tells the story of Hidetora Ichimonji (Tatsuya Nakadai), an exhausted 70-year-old warlord who wants to turn the vast dominion acquired through 50 years of bloodshed over to his three sons, on whose kindness he will then depend. The two older sons agree to their father’s terms and swear loyalty to him and to each other. But when the youngest argues that by dividing the lands, Hidetora is creating conditions that will lead to disaster, his father sends him into exile. At the same time, the wife (Mieko Harada, above) of his oldest son — the daughter of a lord conquered by Hidetora — encourages her husband to humiliate his father so he can assume control of the family in his own name. “Though big in physical scope and of a beauty that suggests a kind of drunken, barbaric lyricism, ‘Ran’ has the terrible logic and clarity of a morality tale seen in tight close-up, of a myth that, while being utterly specific and particular in its time and place, remains ageless, infinitely adaptable,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T05:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6acb981d-ae8f-5f25-aa16-4c761d3048bb', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6acb981d-ae8f-5f25-aa16-4c761d3048bb'}, {'abstract': 'With his political isolation deepening, President Mohamed Morsi of Egypt demanded late Tuesday that the military rescind its ultimatum against him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/world/middleeast/egypt-protests.html', 'snippet': 'With his political isolation deepening, President Mohamed Morsi of Egypt demanded late Tuesday that the military rescind its ultimatum against him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — President Mohamed Morsi rejected an ultimatum in an angry speech Tuesday night as Egypt edged closer to a return to military rule.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morsi Defies\r\nEgypt Army’s\r\nUltimatum to\r\nBend to Protest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egyptian President Defies Military Ultimatum to Step Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ElBaradei, Mohamed', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T07:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick and Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47cfad29-1afc-5d66-aa18-ff03b1280503', 'word_count': 1197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47cfad29-1afc-5d66-aa18-ff03b1280503'}, {'abstract': 'Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh, the mothership of India’s Hindu right, loses its ideological battle against Cricket.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/why-does-the-rashtriya-swayemsewak-sangh-resent-cricket/', 'snippet': 'Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh, the mothership of India’s Hindu right, loses its ideological battle against Cricket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nagpur, a city of nearly 2.5 million in central Indian state of Maharashtra, has the slow rhythms of a small town. The noise and edginess of the new Indian metropolis, the gargantuan \xa0\xa0shopping malls and luxury automobiles, have yet to overwhelm it. Nagpur seeks half-hearted recognition as India’s Orange City, for being a major trade center for oranges cultivated in the region. Nagpur makes an appearance on the national stage when the right-wing guardians of the Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS), pronounce their views on Indian politics or society from their headquarters in the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/world/asia/01-RSS-IndiaInk/01-RSS-IndiaInk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/01/world/asia/01-RSS-IndiaInk/01-RSS-IndiaInk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 589}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/world/asia/01-RSS-IndiaInk/01-RSS-IndiaInk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1005, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/world/asia/01-RSS-IndiaInk/01-RSS-IndiaInk-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1340, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/world/asia/01-RSS-IndiaInk/01-RSS-IndiaInk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/01/world/asia/01-RSS-IndiaInk/01-RSS-IndiaInk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thu