istration has gone to some lengths to reassure Americans that “metadata” is definitely not “content,” which unlike your “metadata” presumably enjoys Fourth Amendment protections. But Glenn Greenwald, among others, has said that’s a distinction without a difference: “In reality, it is hard to distinguish email metadata from email content.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the N.S.A. Knows About You', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MIT Media Lab', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T13:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bf75d69-d198-5683-aaf4-247b0ec68406', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bf75d69-d198-5683-aaf4-247b0ec68406'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of a small Ohio town fight back against speed cameras, and the fake Ferrari from “Ferris Bueller” heads to the auction block.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/wheelies-the-big-brother-is-watching-you-edition/', 'snippet': 'Residents of a small Ohio town fight back against speed cameras, and the fake Ferrari from “Ferris Bueller” heads to the auction block.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/automobiles/wheels/ohio-speed-cameras/ohio-speed-cameras-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 