 up in Myanmar last year has continued unabated despite the government’s pledges to enforce the rule of law. On Sunday night in the town of Thandwe, in the western state of Rakhine, two Muslim houses were reportedly burned down by a Buddhist mob in retaliation for the alleged rape of a Buddhist girl by a Muslim man. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Order of the Heedless', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National League for Democracy (Myanmar)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time (Magazine)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meiktila (Myanmar)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yangon (Myanmar)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T14:36:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Swe Win', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Swe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Win', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f07cb01-b798-572c-9b43-375bcc