acio.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/the-scene-paris-couture-fashion-week-iris-van-herpen/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the couture fashion week photo diary of Barbara Anastacio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the couture fashion week photo diary of Barbara Anastacio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Couture Fashion Week: Iris van Herpen Fall 2013', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Anastacio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anastacio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d95a368-45ea-53b2-8c55-2c430090c2f0', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d95a368-45ea-53b2-8c55-2c430090c2f0'}, {'abstract': 'Was Confederate Gen. Richard S. Ewell responsible for losing Gettysburg?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/general-ewells-dilemma/', 'snippet': 'Was Confederate Gen. Richard S. Ewell responsible for losing Gettysburg?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gen. Richard S. Ewell of the Confederate Army was frustrated and angry on the afternoon of July 1, 1863, the first day of the Battle of Gettysburg. The cause of his grief was Robert E. Lee, who had just issued a confusing order that forced Ewell to reconsider whether he should carry out an important attack. What he did next may have arguably decided the battle, and certainly became one of the most controversial series of events of the entire war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General Ewell’s Dilemma', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Robert E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of the Potomac', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:39:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry L. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c74d4088-9bc3-53af-9760-d4ab1f3c3608', 'word_count': 2607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c74d4088-9bc3-53af-9760-d4ab1f3c3608'}, {'abstract': 'In the wake of the hoopla over the proposed Winklevoss exchange traded fund in bitcoins, the author offers a modest proposal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/an-e-t-f-too-far/', 'snippet': 'In the wake of the hoopla over the proposed Winklevoss exchange traded fund in bitcoins, the author offers a modest proposal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exchange-traded funds are taking over the financial world. At last official count, there were nearly 1,200 of them at the end of 2012, compared with about 100 a decade ago, according to the Investment Company Institute trade group. With a new issue now linking to the virtual currency Bitcoin, the $1.3 trillion index tracker industry seems to cover nearly everything. And yet the most important asset class of all has been ignored. Breakingviews stands ready to remedy the situation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An E.T.F. Too Far', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exchange Traded Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winklevoss, Cameron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winklevoss, Tyler', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:48:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Thal Larsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'Thal', 'lastname': 'Larsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32b86430-5a7f-5c27-88c3-0c1ba0c1df8c', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32b86430-5a7f-5c27-88c3-0c1ba0c1df8c'}, {'abstract': 'AirAsia, a Malaysian low-cost airline, will launch its operations in India later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/image-of-the-day-july-2/', 'snippet': 'AirAsia, a Malaysian low-cost airline, will launch its operations in India later this year.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1466, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk/02-POD-AirAsia-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: July 2', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIRASIA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tata Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:52:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c899c4-243b-5fa1-82bc-ac7b67484f9f', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75c899c4-243b-5fa1-82bc-ac7b67484f9f'}, {'abstract': 'With its frantic, Looney Tunes-style madness, “Despicable Me 2” is consistently diverting and so cute you’ll want to pet it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/movies/despicable-me-2-stars-steve-carell-and-kristen-wiig.html', 'snippet': 'With its frantic, Looney Tunes-style madness, “Despicable Me 2” is consistently diverting and so cute you’ll want to pet it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its frantic, Looney Tunes-style madness, “Despicable Me 2” brings to mind a cautionary children’s story about an aspiring baker who learns the hard way that doubling the recipe for bread doesn’t mean doubling the baking time. It tries so hard to double your pleasure that it emerges from the test kitchen slightly burned. Like the jams and jellies that its reformed main character, Gru, makes in his new line of work, the film combines too many flavors, along with extra sugar. Once again, the lesson that more is not necessarily better, something rarely learned by blockbuster sequels, is forgotten. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ex-Villain Returns as Mr. Sweets', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Ex-Villain Returns as Mr. Sweets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carell, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coffin, Pierre', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renaud, Chris', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:52:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/53179f6d-feea-575e-b39b-b717adeabba5', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53179f6d-feea-575e-b39b-b717adeabba5'}, {'abstract': 'For the third time this year, N.H.T.S.A. has challenged a G.M. recall, calling for expansion after receiving more complaints about a brake light problem.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/n-h-t-s-a-again-challenges-adequacy-of-g-m-recall/', 'snippet': 'For the third time this year, N.H.T.S.A. has challenged a G.M. recall, calling for expansion after receiving more complaints about a brake light problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is intensifying its investigation into whether General Motors should have recalled about 551,000 vehicles instead of 8,000 for a brake light problem, according to a report posted on the agency’s Web site. It is the third time this year N.H.T.S.A. has challenged the adequacy of G.M. recalls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.T.S.A. Again Challenges Adequacy of G.M. Recall', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buick Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pontiac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saab Automobile AB', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fda1b75-a30c-59c5-ae59-946a47383fd8', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fda1b75-a30c-59c5-ae59-946a47383fd8'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s decision striking down the federal Defense of Marriage Act offers hope to people who are stuck in marriages they cannot dissolve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/us/ruling-might-also-ease-the-way-for-same-sex-divorces.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s decision striking down the federal Defense of Marriage Act offers hope to people who are stuck in marriages they cannot dissolve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Cardinal’s wedded life began happily in New Hampshire, where same-sex marriages are legal. It went sour three years later in Florida, where they are not.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03divorce/03divorce-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruling on Same-Sex Marriage May Help Resolve Status of Divorce ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruling on Same-Sex Marriage May Help Resolve Status of Divorce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T15:57:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d93898fa-7668-5d2b-ad25-05a3d8e62cc4', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d93898fa-7668-5d2b-ad25-05a3d8e62cc4'}, {'abstract': 'Prescription painkiller addiction, long seen as mainly a man’s problem, is rising at a far faster rate among women, a federal analysis of data found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/health/rate-of-painkiller-overdose-deaths-rises-among-women.html', 'snippet': 'Prescription painkiller addiction, long seen as mainly a man’s problem, is rising at a far faster rate among women, a federal analysis of data found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTSMOUTH, Ohio — Prescription pain pill addiction was originally seen as a man’s problem, a national epidemic that began among workers doing backbreaking labor in the coal mines and factories of Appalachia. But a new analysis of federal data has found that deaths in recent years have been rising far faster among women, quintupling since 1999.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/us/03overdose/03overdose-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharp Rise in Women’s Deaths From Overdose of Painkillers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharp Rise in Women’s Deaths From Overdose of Painkillers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'OxyContin (Drug)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T16:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9fe547-51d6-5998-af77-e637ad13bb66', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9fe547-51d6-5998-af77-e637ad13bb66'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of men in the 134th New York Infantry died so that forces under Gen. Carl Schurz could live.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/a-regiment-is-sacrificed-at-gettysburg/', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of men in the 134th New York Infantry died so that forces under Gen. Carl Schurz could live.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Union forces along the northern edge of Gettysburg, Pa., occupied a precarious position on July 1, 1863. Advancing Confederates poured deadly volleys into the rapidly thinning blue ranks as a steady stream of wounded trickled into the normally peaceful Pennsylvania town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Regiment is Sacrificed at Gettysburg', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schurz, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T16:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c8bc919-9fa8-5892-bc9c-98dd64d8139d', 'word_count': 1815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c8bc919-9fa8-5892-bc9c-98dd64d8139d'}, {'abstract': 'President Hamid Karzai’s appointment of five new human rights commissioners has drawn criticism from inside and outside the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/world/asia/afghan-donors-want-human-rights-panel-reconsidered.html', 'snippet': 'President Hamid Karzai’s appointment of five new human rights commissioners has drawn criticism from inside and outside the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — President Hamid Karzai’s widely criticized appointment of five new human rights commissioners has become a sore point with the countries that support Afghanistan financially. Major donor nations and the United Nations will call on Wednesday for Mr. Karzai to reconsider the appointments, according to two Western diplomats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donors Are Likely to Ask Karzai to Rethink Rights Panel Choices', 'kicke