private to $19 a share from an earlier bid of $18.20.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/founding-family-raises-bid-for-american-greetings/', 'snippet': 'The founding family of American Greetings has raised its offer to take the company private to $19 a share from an earlier bid of $18.20.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The founding family of American Greetings has raised its offer to take the company private after shares rose above the previous bid and a special committee set up to evaluate the transaction asked the family to reconsider the price.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Founding Family Raises Bid for American Greetings', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiss, Morry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T17:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/360041f6-b51a-5a9d-81d6-7957c131e076', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/360041f6-b51a-5a9d-81d6-7957c131e076'}, {'abstract': 'Agents from the federal Department of Agriculture captured geese at the Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge and the surrounding area on Tuesday in the name of human air safety.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/annual-goose-roundup-under-way-in-jamaica-bay/', 'snippet': 'Agents from the federal Department of Agriculture captured geese at the Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge and the surrounding area on Tuesday in the name of human air safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual roundup and slaughter of the region’s Canada geese in the name of human air safety is under way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Annual Goose Roundup Under Way in Jamaica Bay', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Friends of Animals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T17:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c542a4ad-493b-5607-9bde-b7d31497e55b', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c542a4ad-493b-5607-9bde-b7d31497e55b'}, {'abstract': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission’s new policy on requiring some defendants to admit misconduct when settling cases will make will make pursuing the big fish draining for the agency, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/requiring-defendants-to-admit-guilt-will-be-costly-for-s-e-c/', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission’s new policy on requiring some defendants to admit misconduct when settling cases will make will make pursuing the big fish draining for the agency, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Zaring is assistant professor of legal studies at the Wharton School of Business at the University of Pennsylvania.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Requiring Defendants to Admit Guilt Will Be Costly for S.E.C.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T17:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Zaring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e68eee-579f-5aa4-be61-8110023a95fe', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e68eee-579f-5aa4-be61-8110023a95fe'}, {'abstract': 'Gore Verbinski’s reimagining of “The Lone Ranger” tries to give today’s kids their own version of the white-hat western hero with his laconic Indian sidekick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/movies/in-the-lone-ranger-tonto-takes-center-stage.html', 'snippet': 'Gore Verbinski’s reimagining of “The Lone Ranger” tries to give today’s kids their own version of the white-hat western hero with his laconic Indian sidekick.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Who was that masked man?” That is not a question likely to resonate much with young people today, unless they are asking it in earnest puzzlement. By young, I mean under 70. The Lone Ranger belongs to the ancient pop culture of the Great Depression and the early baby boom. His adventures were heard on radio, starting in the 1930s, and seen on television from 1949 to 1957, but unlike some of his cape-wearing peers, he has mostly stayed in the past, an object of fuzzy nostalgia and mocking incredulity, a symbol of simple pleasures and retrograde attitudes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hero Rides Again, With Big Boots to Fill', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hero Rides Again, With Big Boots to Fill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Lone Ranger (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verbinski, Gore', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Depp, Johnny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruckheimer, Jerry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, Armie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T17:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0545fea7-415e-5c6d-8304-daa06e8033d2', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0545fea7-415e-5c6d-8304-daa06e8033d2'}, {'abstract': 'The A.C.L.U. wants more information on the legal opinions supporting the N.S.A. surveillance program.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/how-can-we-debate-secret-law/', 'snippet': 'The A.C.L.U. wants more information on the legal opinions supporting the N.S.A. surveillance program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the problems with the debate over the necessity and legality of the National Security Agency’s data-mining program is that we’re having it in the dark. The surveillance programs are based on legal arguments delivered in secret by government lawyers to a court that operates out of public view and issues opinions that are classified as too secret for mere mortals to read.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Can We Debate Secret Law?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapper, James R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T17:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7f42e6e-f9d6-5385-8b7f-2d7e3bf6de77', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7f42e6e-f9d6-5385-8b7f-2d7e3bf6de77'}, {'abstract': 'Both companies have working fuel cell-powered models, but want to pool their resources to reach the next step in development.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/g-m-and-honda-to-collaborate-on-fuel-cell-development/', 'snippet': 'Both companies have working fuel cell-powered models, but want to pool their resources to reach the next step in development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Motors and Honda on Tuesday announced an agreement to jointly develop a hydrogen fuel cell to be shared by both automakers for vehicles they would produce around the end of the decade.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi