'}, {'abstract': 'If any quality defines Novak Djokovic, the world No. 1 in tennis, it is his flexibility, some of it natural and some of it a result of his commitment to stretching.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/sports/tennis/djokovic-bends-and-twists-but-doesnt-break.html', 'snippet': 'If any quality defines Novak Djokovic, the world No. 1 in tennis, it is his flexibility, some of it natural and some of it a result of his commitment to stretching.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The subject of the interview at Wimbledon was flexibility, and Novak Djokovic was asked if he knew about Gumby.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Djokovic Bends and Twists, but Doesn’t Break', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘He is like Gumby.’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarey, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Bobby', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gencic, Jelena', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sampras, Pete', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Courier, Jim', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-02T20:57:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e456de7e-4dda-57fe-a199-0fc4542dd37d', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e456de7e-4dda-57fe-a199-0fc4542dd37d'}, {'abstract': 'Uncle Boons in NoLIta turns out fresh and dynamic Thai flavors hot enough to make you wish you had a handkerchief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/dining/reviews/restaurant-review-uncle-boons-in-nolita.html', 'snippet': 'Uncle Boons in NoLIta turns out fresh and dynamic Thai flavors hot enough to make you wish you had a handkerchief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The smallest blackout I’ve ever lived through was limited to the interior of a Thai restaurant on Spring Street, just off the Bowery, named Uncle Boons, where early one night the electricity kept cutting out, then flicking back on a few minutes later. Almost every foot of wall space is covered with pictures that might have been picked up at a Bangkok flea market: portraits of Thailand’s kings, thrift-store paintings, prints of jungle beasts, a monster-movie poster in Thai and semi-English (“Once again dinosaur shake the erath!”). But staging a Southeast Asian power failure seemed to be taking the conceit a bit far. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/dining/03REST_SPAN/03REST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/03/dining/03REST_SPAN/03REST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/dining/03REST_SPAN/03REST_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/dining/03REST_SPAN/03REST_SPA