a common design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Motors and Honda will develop and share a hydrogen fuel cell for vehicles they would produce around the end of the decade, the automakers announced on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/03/business/FUELCELL/FUELCELL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For G.M. and Honda, a Fuel-Cell Partnership', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For G.M. And Honda, A Fuel-Cell Partnership', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydrogen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T01:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Brooke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c45b9cb-8a0b-5ac0-aec0-facca8f98799', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c45b9cb-8a0b-5ac0-aec0-facca8f98799'}, {'abstract': 'The anger being vented by governments in Europe over spying by the United States may be feigned, but the concerns about privacy are real.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/opinion/listening-in-on-europe.html', 'snippet': 'The anger being vented by governments in Europe over spying by the United States may be feigned, but the concerns about privacy are real.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There seems a touch of playacting in the outrage that France, Germany and other European governments have been venting since the online edition of Der Spiegel, the German newsmagazine, reported last weekend that the National Security Agency had bugged diplomatic offices and monitored their internal computer systems. Spying on allies looks bad and is rarely discussed in public except when, as now, spy agency documents are leaked to the press. But governments on both sides of the Atlantic (and almost everywhere else) have spied on allies and enemies alike for a long time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listening In on Europe', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Listening In on Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T01:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/14de76ae-7ea9-5939-8c5a-9bba7d8bd496', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14de76ae-7ea9-5939-8c5a-9bba7d8bd496'}, {'abstract': 'Those who are allowed to work should be able to get driver’s licenses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/opinion/more-unfairness-toward-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'Those who are allowed to work should be able to get driver’s licenses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One year ago, the Obama administration declared that it was halting the deportations of some unauthorized immigrants who were brought to the United States as children and would allow them to seek work-authorization papers and Social Security numbers. This raised a question for the states: Would these young people, known as “Dreamers,” also be allowed to drive? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Unfairness Toward Immigrants', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Unfairness Toward Immigrants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drivers Licenses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T01:25:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/25540767-1d06-59a2-9d33-de8e171b5e87', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25540767-1d06-59a2-9d33-de8e171b5e87'}, {'abstract': 'When word got out that the Obama administration planned to approach the major sports leagues to promote reform, Republican leaders decided to commit interference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/opinion/a-chance-for-pro-sports-to-help-on-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'When word got out that the Obama administration planned to approach the major sports leagues to promote reform, Republican leaders decided to commit interference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration thought it had a smart way to publicize the benefits of health care reform: get some professional athletes to help spread the word.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance for Pro Sports to Help on Health Care', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chance for Pro Sports to Help on Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornyn, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T01:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/36ba9c12-3a39-5cdd-8463-25cfd46b49e2', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36ba9c12-3a39-5cdd-8463-25cfd46b49e2'}, {'abstract': 'The founding documents of our democracy were products of debate, revision and compromise, which could have turned out differently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/opinion/when-the-bill-of-rights-had-12-amendments.html', 'snippet': 'The founding documents of our democracy were products of debate, revision and compromise, which could have turned out differently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We treat the Declaration of Independence and the Bill of Rights almost like sacred texts, inevitable and immutable. But if you’re in Manhattan on Wednesday, you can see drafts of the Declaration of Independence and the Bill of Rights when they were still works in progress. To celebrate the Fourth of July, the New York Public Library is displaying these documents side by side for the first time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Bill of Rights Had 12 Amendments', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Bill of Rights Had 12 Amendments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jefferson, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Declaration of Independence (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bill of Rights (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T01:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9432250-dd26-57f7-80cf-9456716749bb', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9432250-dd26-57f7-80cf-9456716749bb'}, {'abstract': 'As the deadline nears, the plan to regulate trading by American banks in London and beyond has set off a rare breakdown of decorum at an agency long known for its cordial style and unanimous votes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/02/deadline-splits-an-agency-on-trading-rules-abroad/', 'snippet': 'As the deadline nears, the plan to regulate trading by American banks in London and beyond has set off a rare breakdown of decorum at an agency long known for its cordial style and unanimous votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street lobbyists, seeking to delay a July 12 deadline for rules that would rein in lucrative trading by banks overseas, pressed their case before a top Washington re