'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Sneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d93255fc-7bbb-5650-a41b-61a0a915c89c', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d93255fc-7bbb-5650-a41b-61a0a915c89c'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a recent thaw in relations, the United States placed a senior Burmese general on its sanctions list on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/world/asia/myanmar-general-lands-on-american-sanctions-list.html', 'snippet': 'Despite a recent thaw in relations, the United States placed a senior Burmese general on its sanctions list on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Despite a recent thaw in relations, the United States placed a senior Burmese general on its sanctions list on Tuesday, accusing him of buying military equipment from North Korea in defiance of international sanctions. A Treasury Department statement emphasized that the penalties, including an asset freeze, affect only Lt. Gen. Thein Htay, the head of Myanmar’s Directorate of Defense Industries, and not government figures. The list did not detail what equipment he had bought. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar: General Lands on American Sanctions List', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar: General Lands On American Sanctions List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Htay', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T03:46:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d289bc0-6a83-5385-87c0-846efc51af0c', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d289bc0-6a83-5385-87c0-846efc51af0c'}, {'abstract': 'Moving to enforce cabinet discipline, President François Hollande on Tuesday fired Delphine Batho, the environment minister.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/world/europe/france-political-guillotine-flashes-and-party-discipline-is-served.html', 'snippet': 'Moving to enforce cabinet discipline, President François Hollande on Tuesday fired Delphine Batho, the environment minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moving to enforce cabinet discipline, President François Hollande on Tuesday fired Delphine Batho, the environment minister, who had said earlier on Tuesday that the proposed 2014 budget was “bad.” Ms. Batho, 40, had expressed her unhappiness with the 7 percent cut projected for her ministry. She also said, “There’s a disappointment with regard to the government, there’s a doubt about our will for change.” Prime Minister Jean-Marc Ayrault summoned her for a meeting after her comments, on RTL Radio. She will be replaced by Philippe Martin, 59. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Political Guillotine Flashes, and Party Discipline Is Served', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Political Guillotine Flashes, And Party Discipline Is Served', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major':