9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verdasco, Fernando', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T03:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db7664ce-06aa-5381-a77f-239b97473482', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db7664ce-06aa-5381-a77f-239b97473482'}, {'abstract': "A festival and exhibition in the city of Hyères showcases Europe's up-and-coming designers, alongside one established star.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/t-magazine/by-design-emerging-talent-on-display-in-the-south-of-france.html', 'snippet': "A festival and exhibition in the city of Hyères showcases Europe's up-and-coming designers, alongside one established star.", 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cote d’Azur has inspired generations of artists and designers, so it’s no surprise that it is emerging as a locus for the international design scene. The eighth annualDesign Parade, a three-day festival and competition at the Villa Noailles, the iconic Modernist house overlooking the French city of Hyères, opens to the public on Friday. It features the work of 10 young designers from Austria, Switzerland, Belgium, France and Italy, who will exhibit their work to an international jury, with one taking home the Grand Prix. (This year’s festival also includes, among others, exhibitions devoted to the work of the architect and furniture designer Marcel Breuer, and a collaboration between the Dutch designer Aldo Bakker and the French porcelain manufacturer Sèvres.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emerging Talent on Display in the South of France', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker