rticle', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de06b4a8-8f1a-55c5-b057-929226e882e3', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de06b4a8-8f1a-55c5-b057-929226e882e3'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (BBC America) MASTER AND COMMANDER: THE FAR SIDE OF THE WORLD (2003) In Peter Weir’s adaptation of two novels by Patrick O’Brian, Russell Crowe, above, stars as Capt. Jack Aubrey, the commander of a British frigate whose crew must battle a faster, larger French vessel off the coast of South America during the Napoleonic wars. Paul Bettany is Stephen Maturin, the ship’s surgeon — so deft he even operates on his own abdomen — and the sensitive foil to his friend Aubrey’s fierceness. Writing in The New York Times, A. O. Scott said that the film, which won Oscars for best cinematography and sound editing, and whose land-based scenes were filmed on the Galápagos Islands, “hums with humor, passion and life.” He added, “It makes you wish Napoleon were still around, so we — that is, I mean, the British Empire — could beat him all over again.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8013a01-b444-5a76-98e6-8b5acd14f064', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8013a01-b444-5a76-98e6-8b5acd14f064'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors in the death penalty phase of the trial of Ronell Wilson showed jurors a video in which he was forcibly subdued after refusing to leave a recreation area at the Metropolitan Detention Center in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/video-detectives-killer-is-presented-as-a-threat-in-jail/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors in the death penalty phase of the trial of Ronell Wilson showed jurors a video in which he was forcibly subdued after refusing to leave a recreation area at the Metropolitan Detention Center in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jurors in the federal death penalty part of the trial of Ronell Wilson, a Staten Island man who was convicted of murdering two undercover police detectives, watched a dramatic video on Monday that was made inside a federal jail, showing several correction officers storming a confined recreation area to subdue Mr. Wilson, who had refused to comply with demands to leave the area. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Detectives’ Killer Is Presented as a Threat in Jail', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Ronell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T06:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfbf7d42-8036-5af4-8991-3d840c2740be', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfbf7d42-8036-5af4-8991-3d840c2740be'}, {'abstract': 'Pat Cash points out potential trouble spots for Novak Djokovic and Andy Murray.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/former-champion-sees-a-tough-road-for-well-everyone/', 'snippet': 'Pat Cash points out potential trouble spots for Novak Djokovic and Andy Murray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The only certainty about Wimbledon 2013 is that the tournament is sure to continue staunchly avoiding predictability. Whenever you suspect that the cast-iron favorites are finally emerging through the carnage, the next day’s play upends all expectations. One might as well spin the roulette wheel when it comes to picking the eventual champions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Champion Sees Tough Road for, Well, Everyone', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, Pat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'del Potro, Juan Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T07:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/345a97d1-dc9b-5443-b021-fbf120cfd203', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/345a97d1-dc9b-5443-b021-fbf120cfd203'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s former chairman and two other former executives were convicted of hiding billions of dollars in losses dating to the 1990s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/business/global/suspended-sentences-in-olympus-accounting-fraud-case.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s former chairman and two other former executives were convicted of hiding billions of dollars in losses dating to the 1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The former chairman of Olympus, the camera maker that has been embroiled in one of Japan’s biggest accounting frauds, was found guilty of abetting a $1.7 billion cover-up by a Tokyo court on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/olympus-web/olympus-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/business/olympus-web/olympus-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 824}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/olympus-web/olympus-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/olympus-web/olympus-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1492, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'c