www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/world/asia/drone-attack-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'The attack, which targeted a compound housing people suspected of being militants, came a month after Pakistan’s new prime minister called for an end to American drone strikes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — At least 16 people were killed and five others wounded when an American drone strike hit a suspected Haqqani militant compound in a remote tribal region of northwestern Pakistan late Tuesday, according to Pakistani government and intelligence officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Drone Strike in Pakistan Kills at Least 16', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Drone Strike Kills at Least 16', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haqqani Network', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T07:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood and Ihsanullah Tipu Mehsud', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ihsanullah', 'middlename': 'Tipu', 'lastname': 'Mehsud', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb7fa0f3-c3b0-59b7-b9c6-2241e7351332', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb7fa0f3-c3b0-59b7-b9c6-2241e7351332'}, {'abstract': 'Latin American leaders condemned the refusal to let Bolivia’s president fly over European nations over what Bolivian officials said were suspicions that Edward J. Snowden was on board.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/world/snowden.html', 'snippet': 'Latin American leaders condemned the refusal to let Bolivia’s president fly over European nations over what Bolivian officials said were suspicions that Edward J. Snowden was on board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — The geopolitical storm churned up by Edward J. Snowden, the fugitive American intelligence contractor, continued to spread on Wednesday as Latin American leaders roundly condemned the refusal to let Bolivia’s president fly over several European nations, rallying to his side after Bolivian officials said the president’s plane had been thwarted because of suspicions that Mr. Snowden was on board.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1510, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/snowden/snowden-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barring of Bolivian Plane Infuriates Latin America as Snowden Case Widens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barring of Bolivian Plane Infuriates Latin America as Snowden Case Widens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bolivia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morales, Evo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vienna (Austria)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T08:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman and Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0e01fac-1009-5914-b82e-9bb12a30b6fa', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0e01fac-1009-5914-b82e-9bb12a30b6fa'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Modi was quick to arrive in Uttarakhand to yet again show leadership, courage and administrative acumen while Mr. Gandhi showed up only days later.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/indian-politicians-scramble-for-electoral-benefits-from-flood-relief-work-in-uttarakhand/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Modi was quick to arrive in Uttarakhand to yet again show leadership, courage and administrative acumen while Mr. Gandhi showed up only days later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — A week after floods began to ravage the Himalayan state of Uttarakhand on June 16, Narendra Modi, the chief minister of the western Indian state of Gujarat, an ambitious and controversial politician seeking to topple the Congress Party-led United Progressive Alliance coalition in New Delhi, visited the disaster-struck state with a team of bureaucrats experienced in disaster management to help evacuate stranded pilgrims. A newspaper reported that he helped rescue 15,000 Gujarati pilgrims. A friend quipped, “How could he get so many on a single plane?” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-rahul-gandhi-IndiaInk/02-rahul-gandhi-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-rahul-gandhi-IndiaInk/02-rahul-gandhi-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/02/world/asia/02-rahul-gandhi-IndiaInk/02-rahul-gandhi-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'c