itial public offering, citing adverse market conditions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/deutsche-annington-shelves-i-p-o-plans/', 'snippet': 'Deutsche Annington Immobilien, the real estate company owned by Terra Firma, which is run by the British financier Guy Hands, has shelved a planned initial public offering, citing adverse market conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – A German real estate company owned by Terra Firma, the private equity firm run by the British financier Guy Hands, has shelved a planned initial public offering, citing adverse market conditions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Annington Shelves I.P.O. Plan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hands, Guy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Annington', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Terra Firma Capital Partners Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T11:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea07bc8-1963-5df0-8abb-586eec3bf219', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea07bc8-1963-5df0-8abb-586eec3bf219'}, {'abstract': 'A Dell special committee has encouraged Michael S. Dell to raise his offer. | The Commodity Futures Trading Commission is divided over a plan to rein in lucrative trading by banks overseas. | The Fed approved rules intended to make banks more resilient to losses. | The Koch brothers want to be seen as major players in deals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/pressure-to-raise-offer-for-dell/', 'snippet': 'A Dell special committee has encouraged Michael S. Dell to raise his offer. | The Commodity Futures Trading Commission is divided over a plan to rein in lucrative trading by banks overseas. | The Fed approved rules intended to make banks more resi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael S. Dell may have to raise his $24.4 billion bid for the computer company he founded, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced reports. A special committee of Dell’s directors encouraged Mr. Dell over the weekend to raise the offer price of $13.65 a share, a person briefed on the matter said on Tuesday. But Mr. Dell has not committed to a course of action and has not discussed raising the current price with his private equity partner, Silver Lake, Mr. de la Merced reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressure to Raise Offer for Dell', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T11:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d2f4b75-7401-59f2-aeec-058693ebaff0', 'word_count': 1746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d2f4b75-7401-59f2-aeec-058693ebaff0'}, {'abstract': 'The actor Michael Cera, currently in “Crystal Fairy” and “This Is the End,” has been directing short films and writing new episodes of “Arrested Development.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/movies/the-actor-michael-cera-is-now-writing-and-directing-too.html', 'snippet': 'The actor Michael Cera, currently in “Crystal Fairy” and “This Is the End,” has been directing short films and writing new episodes of “Arrested Development.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early on in “This Is the End,” a fame-inflected look at the end of days, Michael Cera, played by Michael Cera, is impaled and hoisted high above Los Angeles, wriggling, covered in blood and patting his pockets for his lost cellphone. He finds the phone, but the rest of it doesn’t go so well.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07CERA_SPAN/07CERA_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unarrested Development', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unarrested Development', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cera, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silva, Sebastian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'This Is the END (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ARRESTED DEVELOPMENT (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Crystal Fairy (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T12:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3a819cc-1012-5577-83fb-2aef2e130ebc', 'word_count': 2207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3a819cc-1012-5577-83fb-2aef2e130ebc'}, {'abstract': 'Diarrheal disease kills more than a million young children each year. Can Coca-Cola’s huge distribution network be leveraged to deliver the remedy?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/making-medicine-as-easy-to-get-as-a-can-of-coke/', 'snippet': 'Diarrheal disease kills more than a million young children each year. Can Coca-Cola’s huge distribution network be leveraged to deliver the remedy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diarrheal disease, which kills a million children younger than 5 each year, has an image problem. It doesn’t raise much alarm in industrialized countries, where it is merely a nuisance that can be treated with inexpensive, readily accessible remedies. In poorer countries, though, where a large majority of these children are dying, those remedies often cannot be found. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making a Medicine as Easy to Find as a Can of Coke', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diarrhea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T12:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarika Bansal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bansal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98e6fe20-b66c-56e3-9197-177f23084ba3', 'word_count': 1760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98e6fe20-b66c-56e3-9197-177f23084ba3'}, {'abstract': 'NoChains helps users search for the best dishes in town. When the app reaches 300 to 400 downloads a day, the owner said, “we’ll essentially be a food search engine.”', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/heres-an-app-to-help-you-find-a-local-find/', 'snippet': 'NoChains helps users search for the best dishes in town. When the app reaches 300 to 400 downloads a day, the owner said, “we’ll essentially be a food search engine.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010 Rich Winley was running a marketing company in Greenville, S.C., when he decided to participate in a seven-week business exchange program to Australia through his local Rotary Club. The group traveled from the small town of Darwin in the north down to Sydney, visiting a different city every two or three days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Here’s an App to Help You Find a Local ‘Find’', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenville (SC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T12:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cae57150-c2ab-5b3c-a8e5-5177d50b248b', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cae57150-c2ab-5b3c-a8e5-5177d50b248b'}, {'abstract': 'The actress plays up the masculine tailoring of a Chanel jacket at the brand’s couture show in Paris, France.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/the-look-kristen-stewart-shakes-up-the-chanel-suit/', 'snippet': 'The actress plays up the masculine tailoring of a Chanel jacket at the brand’s couture show in Paris, France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Girl: With slicked-back hair and a masculine tailored jacket, the actress brings an androgynous look to the classic Chanel suit at the brand’s couture show in Paris. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kristen Stewart Shakes Up the Chanel Suit', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', '