cern-than-pain.html', 'snippet': 'In cities that have required employers to provide paid sick leave, some small-business owners say they overestimated the law’s added expense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2007, as a new paid sick leave law — the first in the nation — was about to take effect in San Francisco, Bill Stone was worried. Mr. Stone owns the Atlas Cafe in the city’s Mission District, and the new law directed him to provide his 21 employees with one hour of paid time off for every 30 hours worked, up to nine days a year. “Basically, it’s just going to make it more expensive to operate your business,” Mr. Stone told NPR at the time. “Small business is going to have to pass that cost onto their customers.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/04sbiz/04sbiz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paid Sick Leave Laws Generate Concern, but Not Much Pain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paid Sick Leave Laws Generate Concern, but Not Much Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Benefits', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T15:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4868159a-4b74-54f9-af1f-0a480d3e7a2d', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4868159a-4b74-54f9-af1f-0a480d3e7a2d'}, {'abstract': 'A report by a research group affiliated with The Economist looks at the reasons Asian technology companies have been held back from cross-border growth. Among the reasons cited in the report is the lack of trusted online payment systems.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/why-asian-internet-companies-struggle-to-become-global/', 'snippet': 'A report by a research group affiliated with The Economist looks at the reasons Asian technology companies have been held back from cross-border growth. Among the reasons cited in the report is the lack of trusted online payment systems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asia is home to nearly half of the 2 billion Internet users in the world. It makes most of the hardware — laptops, smartphones, tablets and other gadgets — that is used to gain access to the Internet. In countries like South Korea and Japan, it has some of the fastest wired and wireless networks for carrying Internet traffic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1245, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/03bits-tencent/03bits-tencent-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Asian Internet Companies Struggle to Become Global', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T15:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/194390db-1a45-5116-a232-f07a91f3a46c', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/194390db-1a45-5116-a232-f07a91f3a46c'}, {'abstract': 'What do you think? Are the business owners protesting paid sick leave laws overreacting?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/is-paid-sick-leave-as-damaging-as-some-businesses-fear/', 'snippet': 'What do you think? Are the business owners protesting paid sick leave laws overreacting?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever lawmakers debate new regulations for businesses, it is easy to find business owners who fear the worst. Six years ago, the nation’s first paid sick leave law was set to take effect in San Francisco, and Bill Stone wasn’t happy. Mr. Stone owns Atlas Cafe, in the city’s Mission District. “Basically, it’s just going to make it more expensive to operate your business,” Mr. Stone told NPR at the time. “Small business is going to have to pass that cost onto their customers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Paid Sick Leave as Damaging as Some Businesses Fear?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Benefits', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name