d shoulder was the result of a malignant sarcoma. David was an extraordinary essayist — the book won the Thurber Prize for American Humor, and, like his two previous collections, was a best seller — so it came as some surprise when he called his editor at Doubleday to say that he wanted his next book to be a novel written in rhyme.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/arts/07SUBRAKOFF_SPAN/07SUBRAKOFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love’s Labors, Published', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love’s Labors, Published', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovell, Joel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T16:16:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a95ef85-f98e-5545-a6a8-ee371ccb4aed', 'word_count': 1943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a95ef85-f98e-5545-a6a8-ee371ccb4aed'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas M. Joyce has unexpectedly resigned from Knight Capital a few days after it was formally taken over by the high-speed trading firm Getco.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/knight-capital-chief-quits/', 'snippet': 'Thomas M. Joyce has unexpectedly resigned from Knight Capital a few days after it was formally taken over by the high-speed trading firm Getco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The popular leader of the trading firm Knight Capital, Thomas M. Joyce, unexpectedly resigned from the company a few days after it was formally taken over by the high-speed trading firm Getco.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knight Capital Chief Quits', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {