ational Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56265165-bbf9-5231-9855-8109924dfde7', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56265165-bbf9-5231-9855-8109924dfde7'}, {'abstract': 'Maxiskirts work especially well for summer because of their versatility.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/the-long-and-the-long-of-maxiskirts/', 'snippet': 'Maxiskirts work especially well for summer because of their versatility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Floor-sweeping and lean, with a romantic floaty movement, maxiskirts work especially well for summer because of how easily they dress up and down. During the day, pair with a silk tank, worn loose, and flat sandals or wedges, then pop on a blazer for a meeting. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long and the Long of Maxiskirts', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Long And the Long of It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:24:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd0dddf4-e539-584b-8ab6-8b2cc4742216', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd0dddf4-e539-584b-8ab6-8b2cc4742216'}, {'abstract': 'AB A Brand Apart makes handbags with modern world travelers in mind.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/a-clean-cut-bag-that-respects-its-owners-style/', 'snippet': 'AB A Brand Apart makes handbags with modern world travelers in mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The woman who is drawn to the cosmopolitan natural leather bags from the young Italian label AB A Brand Apart is likely to have innate style but may not necessarily be able to identify the “bag of the season.” Designed by Andrea Brà, AB (for his initials) A Brand Apart is, as the designer puts it, “kind of an outsider in the fashion system.” Made with modern world travelers in mind, the collection includes this shoulder bag, clean and classic with a metallic silver closure (also in black with a green closure), $650; minimalist totes with the Latin phrase “Omnia mea mecum porto” (“All that’s mine I carry with me”) inscribed on an interior pouch, $450; and a metallic envelope clutch, $226, that’s chic and easy to toss into a suitcase.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Clean-Cut Bag That Respects Its Owner’s Style', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Clean-Cut Bag That Respects Its Owner’s Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:28:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfc4c2d6-54de-523d-8e2e-518c08d127fb', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfc4c2d6-54de-523d-8e2e-518c08d127fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Weinstein Company plans further action after losing arbitration over the right to use the title “The Butler,” the name of a 1916 Warner Brothers short.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/its-weinstein-vs-warner-brothers-over-use-of-the-title-the-butler/', 'snippet': 'The Weinstein Company plans further action after losing arbitration over the right to use the title “The Butler,” the name of a 1916 Warner Brothers short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES —Never ones to avoid controversy, especially when it comes to selling a movie, Harvey Weinstein and the Weinstein Company now have an attention-getting fight over Lee Daniels’s coming film “The Butler” on their hands. Warner Brothers had objected to the title, citing rights to a similarly titled short from 1916, and won in industry arbitration this week. Now Weinstein— according to a flurry of press reports, including those on the Deadline.com site — has asked its lawyer David Boies to appeal or take further legal action.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Weinstein vs. Warner Brothers Over Use of the Title ‘The Butler’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weinstein Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a79a907b-bd90-54a5-97c4-79abcabfca6c', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a79a907b-bd90-54a5-97c4-79abcabfca6c'}, {'abstract': 'Jamaica will enact a nationwide ban on smoking in public places on July 15.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/jamaica-to-prohibit-smoking-in-public-places/', 'snippet': 'Jamaica will enact a nationwide ban on smoking in public places on July 15.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jamaica will soon join the ranks of countries that prohibit smoking in public places. The nationwide ban will take effect July 15. People will no longer “have to involuntarily inhale tobacco smoke, with its over 40 carcinogens,” Fenton Ferguson, the minister of heath, said in a statement when the new regulations were announced in late June.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jamaica to Prohibit Smoking in Public Places', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica (West Indies)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77ba462c-389b-523f-8fce-78ff07388fc8', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77ba462c-389b-523f-8fce-78ff07388fc8'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Lo’s glittered T-shirts depict watermelons and tiger lilies.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/glittery-tees-for-after-the-fireworks/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Lo’s glittered T-shirts depict watermelons and tiger lilies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Lo, an emerging designer in London, is not afraid of girly-ness: he uses loads of pink and glitter, and cites pop cultural references like “Ally McBeal” and the Bonnie Tyler song “Total Eclipse of the Heart.” His collection for summer, inspired in part by the artist Yayoi Kusama and Studio 54, includes T-shirts with glittered fruit and flowers — watermelon, tiger lily, dragon fruit, a kiwi patch. “I just wanted something fresh and sweetly erotic for the summertime,” Mr. Lo said. “The tees kind of remind me of the famous Japanese candy Hi-Chew.” Yum.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glittery Tees for After the Fireworks', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sparklers For After The Fireworks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76e57441-74e3-5369-82e6-0599211329a3', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76e57441-74e3-5369-82e6-0599211329a3'}, {'abstract': 'Shabd Simon-Alexander has written a book about tie-dyeing.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/a-guide-to-tie-dye/', 'snippet': 'Shabd Simon-Alexander has written a book about tie-dyeing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an artist living in New York, Shabd Simon-Alexander discovered the perfect medium for her work when, by chance, she attended a garden party where there was a table set up for tie-dyeing. Hooked from that moment, and with experience in fashion design, she spent a year developing tie-dye techniques (and enjoying nonstop compliments for the pieces she wore) before introducing her namesake label. This summer she spreads the love, with “Tie-Dye: Dye It, Wear It, Share It,” which includes history and color theory, along with detailed how-to projects. “People have a very narrowly defined idea of what tie-dye is,” she said, “but there’s a 2,000-year history.” Happily timed for a season of elevated tie-dye on the runway (Miu Miu, Band of Outsiders) and from popular designers like Raquel Allegra, the book is a nice summer BBQ gift. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to Tie-Dye', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharing The Fabric Of Her Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dyes and Dyestuffs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon-Alexander, Shabd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Band of Outsiders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miu Miu', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:40:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bea5e521-b409-5941-8c04-50fe83f4c69b', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bea5e521-b409-5941-8c04-50fe83f4c69b'}, {'abstract': 'A lack of clarity may be at fault in the misunderstanding between a writer for the You’re the Boss blog and a publicist.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/no-quid-pro-quo-by-youre-the-boss-writer-but-intrigue-anyway/', 'snippet': 'A lack of clarity may be at fault in the misunderstanding between a writer for the You’re the Boss blog and a publicist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Zitron may not be the savviest public relations person around. When he e-mailed a New York Times business editor, he asked for the strictest anonymity about his complaint: that a writer for the You’re the Boss small-business blog was demanding money as a trade for mentioning his clients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Quid Pro Quo by You’re the Boss Writer, but Intrigue, Anyway', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T18:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/787cf41c-69aa-5010-a7ca-cb41f11809d3', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/787cf41c-69aa-5010-a7ca-cb41f11809d3'}, {'abstract': 'The plan is intended to open the way for hundreds of Swiss banks to end the threat of criminal prosecution by the United States Justice Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/business/global/swiss-proposal-aims-to-defuse-tax-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'The plan is intended to open the way for hundreds of Swiss banks to end the threat of criminal prosecution by the United States Justice Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The Swiss government said on Wednesday that it had found a way to allow the country’s banks to turn over data to the United States in spite of strict banking secrecy laws, potentially opening the way for hundreds of lenders to end the threat of criminal prosecution by the Justice Department.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/business/Swisstax/Swisstax-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Swiss Offer Plan to Solve Dispute Over Data on U.S. Tax Evaders', 'kicker': None, 'conte