d_paragraph': 'I grew up in a small town (Deshler, Ohio, population 1,799) and that small town is stockpiled with great nicknames. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Didn’t Name Him Wowee', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T19:23:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Wensink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wensink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78328ae3-5bfa-5928-b2de-af314b13ec96', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78328ae3-5bfa-5928-b2de-af314b13ec96'}, {'abstract': 'A new analysis finds that CT angiography, a powerful tool in detecting pulmonary embolisms, is overused in diagnosing such blockages, leading to overtreatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/health/ct-scan-may-be-too-good-at-finding-lung-problems-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'A new analysis finds that CT angiography, a powerful tool in detecting pulmonary embolisms, is overused in diagnosing such blockages, leading to overtreatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CT imaging is a very good way to find pulmonary embolisms — sudden blockages of an artery in the lung, which can be fatal if not treated quickly. But a new analysis finds that the procedure might be too good, revealing tiny embolisms that are harmless and leading to treatments that are unnecessary, expensive and potentially dangerous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlar