e until 2015 before they will have to provide insurance or face penalties. The administration’s explanation is that it is listening to businesses’ concerns about getting their coverage ready in time, and trying to be flexible. But what people are really concerned about is whether this will make a difference in health care coverage and the progress of reform.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Insurance Delay Won’t Affect Many', 'kicker': 'Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T20:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezekiel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Emanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62122f10-ffaf-5764-829f-b60b3ebe37cb', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62122f10-ffaf-5764-829f-b60b3ebe37cb'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Robert Kolker talks about “Lost Girls: An Unsolved American Mystery”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Chuck Klosterman discusses “I Wear the Black Hat”; Meghan O’Rourke on her essay about authors “recording their own deaths as they happen”; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/07/07/books/review/07books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Robert Kolker talks about “Lost Girls: An Unsolved American Mystery”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Chuck Klosterman discusses “I Wear the Black Hat”; Meghan O’Rourke on her essay about authors “recording their own deaths as th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Robert Kolker talks about “Lost Girls: An Unsolved American Mystery”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Chuck Klosterman discusses “I Wear the Black Hat”; Meghan O’Rourke on her essay about authors “recording their own deaths as they happen”; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The New York Times Book Review: Robert Kolker’s ‘Lost Girls’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T20:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/e9a665d6-a859-52d1-9461-b22516c4a6be', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/e9a665d6-a859-52d1-9461-b22516c4a6be'}, {'abstract': 'Yoga aficionados gain followers on Instagram.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/fashion/yoga-practitioners-gaze-at-their-inner-selfies.html', 'snippet': 'Yoga aficionados gain followers on Instagram.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many yoga aficionados, Laura Kasperzak, 36, practices early in the morning when she can get some time by herself. “No one’s up at 5:30 with me,” she said, referring to her husband and two young children. But unlike most other Zen seekers, before she does her first downward dog, she sets the timer on her Nikon camera to photograph herself every two seconds. After all, about 245,000 people who follow her on Instagram are waiting to see the results.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':