nning and development from Penn State University in 1992.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/26/booming/26expertquery-booming-illness/26expertquery-booming-illness-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 227, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/26/booming/26expertquery-booming-illness/26expertquery-booming-illness-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 227, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/26/booming/26expertquery-booming-illness/26expertquery-booming-illness-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/26/booming/26expertquery-booming-illness/26expertquery-booming-illness-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/26/booming/26expertquery-booming-illness/26expertquery-booming-illness-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advice for Caregivers of Relatives With Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospice Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T21:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffd3b22a-963e-5413-9246-ee4bd6e7fcc9', 'word_count': 4453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffd3b22a-963e-5413-9246-ee4bd6e7fcc9'}, {'abstract': 'The price of a Tony Award rises to $2,500 for producers (and that’s not counting a producer’s original investment).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/theater/theaterspecial/broadway-success-has-a-price-2500.html', 'snippet': 'The price of a Tony Award rises to $2,500 for producers (and that’s not counting a producer’s original investment).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Reinis didn’t make any producing decisions on the Broadway musical “Pippin,” but he put $125,000 into the $8.5 million show, enough to receive a prominent producer’s credit. Yet after “Pippin” won the Tony Award for best musical revival last month, Mr. Reinis was invited to pay more — $2,500 in return for his very own Tony. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/arts/04TONYjp/04TONYjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/arts/04TONYjp/04TONYjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 865}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/arts/04TONYjp/04TONYjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 711, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't