morialize-the-fallen/', 'snippet': 'Logan Stark, who served in Afghanistan, discusses the making of a short film about his friend and fellow Marine, Kevin, who was shot in the head in the Sangin district in Helmand Province.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The year was 2010. Like so many Marines before me, I faced a nagging question: How would I react in combat? I wanted to know, and there was only one way to find out: I joined a unit heading to Afghanistan, the Third Battalion, Fifth Marine Regiment, the “Darkhorse” battalion, as a scout sniper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making of a Film to Memorialize the Fallen', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T21:13:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Logan Stark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Logan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24bd17a8-fb25-546e-9de5-752ee6b083c2', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24bd17a8-fb25-546e-9de5-752ee6b083c2'}, {'abstract': 'Negotiations between the railroad and two unions failed to produce a new contract, leaving no chance of restarting service by July Fourth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/us/talks-end-without-agreement-pushing-bay-area-transit-strike-into-third-day.html', 'snippet': 'Negotiations between the railroad and two unions failed to produce a new contract, leaving no chance of restarting service by July Fourth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Negotiations over a new contract between the San Francisco Bay Area’s main commuter railroad and striking workers ended without an agreement early Wednesday morning as train service remained stalled for a third day.', 'print_section':