on': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04DEALS/04DEALS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04DEALS/04DEALS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04DEALS/04DEALS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04DEALS/04DEALS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales at Vermont Woods Studio, Nancy Koltes and Others', 'kicker': 'Currents | Deals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Furniture, Bedding And Pillows for Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beds and Bedding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T22:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41e63afa-d600-5011-aaea-7f0f5d9ab86b', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41e63afa-d600-5011-aaea-7f0f5d9ab86b'}, {'abstract': 'The classic chair is reintroduced in sustainable fiberglass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/garden/an-eames-chair-returns-to-its-roots.html', 'snippet': 'The classic chair is reintroduced in sustainable fiberglass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The classic molded plastic chair designed in 1949 by Charles and Ray Eames was originally made of fiberglass. It was manufactured by Herman Miller for 40 years, until growing awareness of the material’s health hazards led the company to halt production. A safer polypropylene version was released in 2000, but it lacked the threaded, almost wood-like, appearance that appealed to the original buyers. Last month, at the NeoCon furniture fair in Chicago, the chair was reintroduced in fiberglass, but now the material emits no harmful gases or particles and is fully recyclable, representatives of Herman Miller said. The new version is offered in its nine original colors, in armchair and side chair versions, with a variety of bases. It will be available in September and will cost from $399 to $628. Information: hermanmiller.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 804, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 804}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1529, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04FURNITURE/04CURR5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eames Chair Returns to Its Roots', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Classic Chair Returns to Its Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eames, Ray', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herman Miller Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T22:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Feldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40bed2b6-2c48-58d2-bd30-1daba8238760', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40bed2b6-2c48-58d2-bd30-1daba8238760'}, {'abstract': 'Elephant, a new crib, takes 10 minutes to assemble and requires just a screwdriver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/garden/a-crib-to-remember.html', 'snippet': 'Elephant, a new crib, takes 10 minutes to assemble and requires just a screwdriver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Sophie Demenge and Michael Ryan, furniture designers, found out that they were about to be parents, they began searching for a crib but were disappointed with what was available. “There was nothing modern or simple, and most had awful drop-side rails, which Michael rightly refused to buy,” Ms. Demenge said. So they designed their own. Oeuf, the couple’s furniture company for children, is now 10 years old and has just introduced Elephant, a crib created with Carlos Tíscar, a Spanish designer. Elephant takes 10 minutes to assemble and requires only a screwdriver. Like all Oeuf cribs, it can be transformed into a toddler bed (a conversion kit, sold separately, will be available in a few months). The material is medium-density fiberboard with a water-based nontoxic finish. Available in white or gray, it measures 57 by 33.75 by 34.75 inches and costs $675. Information: (718) 965-1216 or oeufnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04KIDS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04KIDS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04KIDS2_SPAN/04KIDS2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Crib to Remember', 'kicker': 'Currents | Kids', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Crib To Remember', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Arlene', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cribs (Baby Beds)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T22:16:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19fc69c4-b8fe-56d2-a1bf-d13b9c1aaa8b', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19fc69c4-b8fe-56d2-a1bf-d13b9c1aaa8b'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of one-of-a-kind light fixtures produced by a ceramic artist (she provides the base) and a product designer (he does the shades).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/garden/ceramic-table-lamps-and-pendants-designed-from-the-bottom-up.html', 'snippet': 'A collection of one-of-a-kind light fixtures produced by a ceramic artist (she provides the base) and a product designer (he does the shades).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friends for more than a decade, Frances Palmer, a ceramic artist, and Chad Jacobs, a lighting designer, never thought to collaborate until one of Ms. Palmer’s clients asked her to design a lamp. She asked Mr. Jacobs, whose company is called Bone Simple Design, for help with the shade and wiring. Three years later, the pair has developed a collection of 16 table lamps and 10 pendants, all one of a kind. Ms. Palmer made the bases, some inspired by Korean ceramics, others by Alberto Giacometti’s lamps for Jean-Michel Frank, and Mr. Jacobs decided on appropriate shades. He explored different materials, including elastic banding and rope, and even hand-painted stylized dahlias on one, inspired by Ms. Palmer’s garden. “He gave me free rein, and I did the same,” Ms. Palmer said. Pendant lamps start at $1,200; table lamps range from $1,800 to $3,800. Information: (212) 627-0876.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LIGHTING/04CURR3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ceramic Table Lamps and Pendants Designed From the Bottom Up', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Designing From the Bottom Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lamps and Lampshades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Chad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Frances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T22:18:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7110f061-e11a-5f61-a8cf-5e7c26220d51', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7110f061-e11a-5f61-a8cf-5e7c26220d51'}, {'abstract': 'A new store offers everything needed to dress a bed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/garden/sleep-studio-opens-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'A new store offers everything needed to dress a bed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sleep Studio, an emporium for slumber, opens in SoHo on Monday. The 3,700-square-foot store offers apothecary items, teas, loungewear and everything needed to dress a bed. But the star is a proprietary sleep system, developed with the German manufacturer Froli, that can be added to your existing bed or custom-ordered with one of the beds the shop sells. The system features plastic springs that look like pods, which can be adjusted to provide different degrees of resistance. “The pods move laterally as well as up and down, so we can customize the support level for different zones of your body, and on each side of the bed,” said Michael Rothbard, Sleep Studio’s president. The Froli system starts at $2,000; other items range from an $18 essential oil blend by the Aromatherapy Company to a $33,000 walnut dresser by Chi Wing Lo for Giorgetti; 73 Wooster Street (Spring Street), (212) 756-1280, sleepstudio.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1469, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04OPEN_SPAN/04CURR4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleep Studio Opens in SoHo', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Everything You Need To Get, Except Tired', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beds and Bedding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sleep Studio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T22:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de3e22a2-3f79-5c2f-8ac0-19c4f6be3b3c', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de3e22a2-3f79-5c2f-8ac0-19c4f6be3b3c'}, {'abstract': 'Especially in the business world.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/nobody-pays-any-attention-to-what-i-say/', 'snippet': 'Especially in the business world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Or that’s what people keep telling me. Actually, one of the odd but revealing things about modern conservatives is the way they alternate between paranoia about the vast left-wing conspiracy and insistence that people who disagree with them are part of a tiny fringe with no real following. Joe Scarborough thinks (or thought — has he updated?) that I was all alone in questioning deficit panic; the fairly large anti-me industry has been insisting for around a decade that I’ve lost all credibility except among credulous New York liberals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nobody Pays Any Attention To What I Say', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-03T22:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b06b89b5-16e4-53ca-9afc-a17f378e94dc', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b06b89b5-16e4-53ca-9afc-a17f378e94dc'}, {'abstract': 'A quirky 1929 home left clues as to its designer, a master of detail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/07/04/greathomesanddestinations/20130704-LOCATION.html', 'snippet': 'A quirky 1929 home left clues as to its designer, a master of detail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A quirky 1929 home left clues as to its designer, a master of detail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/greathomesanddestinations/20130704-LOCATION-slide-NIUA/20130704-LOCATION-slide-NIUA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/greathomesanddestinations/20130704-LOCATION-slide-NIUA/20130704-LOCATION-slide-NIUA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/greathomesanddestinations/20130704-L