-urges-citizens-to-leave-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The United States raised its travel warning because of the political upheavals in Egypt and the possibility of lethal violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Increasingly alarmed about the violent Egyptian political upheaval, the United States sharply raised the threat level in its travel advisory to Egypt on Wednesday, warning citizens to defer visits and advising American residents there to leave.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Department Urges U.S. Citizens to Leave Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Department Urges U.S. Citizens to Leave Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T00:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cf0d86d-730e-52a9-ac55-c4d9c8200ba4', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cf0d86d-730e-52a9-ac55-c4d9c8200ba4'}, {'abstract': 'Michael R. Bloomberg hasn’t always seemed thrilled with the lighter, grin-and-bear-it ceremonies that come with being mayor. But there have been some high points.', 'web_url': 'https://