let of stories on the “decline of the humanities.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Humanities in Crisis? Not at Most Schools', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Humanities in Crisis? Not at Most Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T01:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Saul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdd36d13-b39e-5b53-9af0-516aea530595', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdd36d13-b39e-5b53-9af0-516aea530595'}, {'abstract': 'It would be tragic if Egyptians allowed the 2011 revolution to end with this rejection of democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/opinion/crisis-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'It would be tragic if Egyptians allowed the 2011 revolution to end with this rejection of democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite his failings, and there were plenty, President Mohamed Morsi was Egypt’s first democratically elected leader, and his overthrow by the military on Wednesday was unquestionably a coup. It would be tragic if Egyptians allowed the 2011 revolution that overthrew the dictator Hosni Mubarak to end with this rejection of democracy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crisis in Egypt', 'kicker':