: 'nyt://article/344b61f6-cec5-5af4-bbe2-69267669e79d', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/344b61f6-cec5-5af4-bbe2-69267669e79d'}, {'abstract': 'Giving employers another year before they will be required to offer health insurance is a sensible decision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/opinion/letting-employers-off-the-hook-for-now.html', 'snippet': 'Giving employers another year before they will be required to offer health insurance is a sensible decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration made a reasonable decision this week to give employers another year before they will be required to make available affordable insurance to their workers or pay a fine. Republicans are portraying the decision as evidence that the whole health care reform is headed for a train wreck, but it actually affects only a narrow slice of companies and workers. It should have no bearing on whether the core provisions of the Affordable Care Act — notably the opening of health care exchanges and subsidized coverage for people on modest incomes — take effect on Jan. 1, 2014, as scheduled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letting Employers Off the Hook, for Now', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letting Employers Off the Hook, for Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T01:11:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad8b65fe-45db-5a9b-ab94-0e7d3b8b642d', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad8b65fe-45db-5a9b-ab94-0e7d3b8b642d'}, {'abstract': 'The Fourth of July and its significance retains a simplicity that resembles no other major holiday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/opinion/every-ordinary-fourth.html', 'snippet': 'The Fourth of July and its significance retains a simplicity that resembles no other major holiday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here we are in the high seas of summer, rounding the corner called the Fourth of July. Most years, it seems, we barely get a glimpse of it before changing tack and sailing on toward all those months that end in “ber.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Every Ordinary Fourth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Every Ordinary Fourth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T01:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf06844a-5c42-5e2e-bce5-97c9133e46ff', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf06844a-5c42-5e2e-bce5-97c9133e46ff'}, {'abstract': 'Newly released court documents make it shockingly clear that Cardinal Timothy Dolan shielded millions of dollars from victims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/opinion/cardinal-dolan-and-the-sex-abuse-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Newly released court documents make it shockingly clear that Cardinal Timothy Dolan shielded millions of dollars from victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tragic as the sexual abuse scandal in the Roman Catholic Church has been, it is shocking to discover that Cardinal Timothy Dolan, while archbishop of Milwaukee, moved $57 million off the archdiocesan books into a cemetery trust fund six years ago in order to protect the money from damage suits by victims of abuse by priests. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cardinal Dolan and the Sexual Abuse Scandal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cardinal Dolan and the Sexual Abuse Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Timothy M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T01:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd627169-4416-580e-9a23-bef29872f102', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd627169-4416-580e-9a23-bef29872f102'}, {'abstract': 'The legislative marathons of State Senator Wendy Davis last week and Bill Meier in 1977 were the rarest of human endeavors — hours of wasted time that actually made a difference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/us/politics/you-call-that-a-filibuster-texas-still-claims-record.html', 'snippet': 'The legislative marathons of State Senator Wendy Davis last week and Bill Meier in 1977 were the rarest of human endeavors — hours of wasted time that actually made a difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT WORTH, Tex. — State Senator Wendy Davis’s exhausting filibuster of at least 11 hours at the Texas Capitol last week turned her into a national political star. Bill Meier’s filibuster in the same building — on the same floor, at the same desk — 36 years earlier left him with a stiff back, rubbery legs, a ragged voice and a footnote-size place in history, though few people outside Texas remember.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/us/04filibuster1/04filibuster1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/us/04filibuster1/04filibuster1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/us/04filibuster1/04filibuster1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/us/04filibuster1/04filibuster1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1331, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/us/04filibuster1/04filibuster1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/us/04filibuster1/04filibuster1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 