exploded in euphoria, parts of the city fell silent where President Mohamed Morsi’s loyalists protested to stave off what they saw as a threat to democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Over speakers, the news came Wednesday and some people fainted. An hour later it had settled in, and President Mohamed Morsi’s supporters sat dazed on sidewalks or walked home, glassy-eyed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/world/street1/street1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Egypt’s Islamists, Confusion and Fear Amid Celebration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Egypt’s Islamists, Confusion and Fear Amid Celebration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T01:40:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc73cbd8-97f5-569a-9ad9-2640c9c5e27f', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc73cbd8-97f5-569a-9ad9-2640c9c5e27f'}, {'abstract': 'Tomas Berdych had seized the momentum from Novak Djokovic in a quarterfinal at Wimbledon on Wednesday, then promptly gave it back.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/03/berdych-djokovic-analysis-its-all-about-momentum/', 'snippet': 'Tomas Berdych had seized the momentum from Novak Djokovic in a quarterfinal at Wimbledon on Wednesday, then promptly gave it back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomas Berdych regrouped after losing the first set to Novak Djokovic in a tiebreaker. Sensing a slight lull in his opponent, Berdych broke serve to open the second set then held to go up two love. In the third game, Berdych fought off two game points, and his powerful ground game began to push Djokovic farther behind the baseline. When he ripped a forehand winner to secure his second service break, Berdych changed ends with energy in his step and a 3-love lead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berdych-Djokovic Analysis: It’s All About Momentum', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdych, Tomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T01:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f021a2f6-2e95-5d58-9f7b-61f5ae0edf3c', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f021a2f6-2e95-5d58-9f7b-61f5ae0edf3c'}, {'abstract': 'Fire officials said they hoped to begin allowing hundreds of residents evacuated from the towns of Yarnell and Peeples Valley to begin returning as soon as Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/us/officials-say-they-see-signs-of-a-slowdown-in-deadly-arizona-wildfire.html', 'snippet': 'Fire officials said they hoped to begin allowing hundreds of residents evacuated from the towns of Yarnell and Peeples Valley to begin returning as soon as Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PEEPLES VALLEY, Ariz. — A wildfire that killed 19 firefighters and destroyed dozens of homes nestled in the mountains here showed signs of slowing Wednesday as hundreds of firefighters on the ground tried to shore up the perimeters of the blaze. It has consumed