at Pyro Spectaculars by Souza to create some of the designs formed by the 40,000 shells — about 1,500 a minute — that explode from six barges on the Hudson River; one design is a beating heart. Nick Cannon M.C.’s the fireworks display, the largest in the nation. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T05:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b7dab5b-4424-5164-b4d2-c3afe38d2820', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b7dab5b-4424-5164-b4d2-c3afe38d2820'}, {'abstract': 'The papers of George Washington, John Adams, Thomas Jefferson, James Madison, Alexander Hamilton and Benjamin Franklin are now online in easily searchable digitized form.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/founding-fathers-go-electric/', 'snippet': 'The papers of George Washington, John Adams, Thomas Jefferson, James Madison, Alexander Hamilton and Benjamin Franklin are now online in easily searchable digitized form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fireworks-phobic Americans have a new excuse for celebrating the Fourth of July indoors this year, thanks to a landmark project aimed at launching the words of the Founders into the digital ether, from sea to shining sea.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Founding Fathers Go Electric', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he