doch criticizing the police investigation of Britain’s phone hacking scandal as “totally incompetent.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Embroiled in inquiries into the behavior of journalists and executives working for his newspapers here, the media tycoon Rupert Murdoch faced new questions on Thursday after a television broadcast of what appeared to be a clandestine recording of him criticizing the police investigation of Britain’s phone hacking scandal as “totally incompetent.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Tape, Murdoch Criticizes Hacking Inquiry, Broadcaster Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Tape, Murdoch Criticizes Hacking Inquiry, Broadcaster Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T08:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/760b225e-40c7-5d3c-8329-a218a0b8fa4c', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/760b225e-40c7-5d3c-8329-a218a0b8fa4c'}, {'abstract': 'The executive order establishes a legal right to food and will create what may be the world’s 