 from your computer to your phone can be a big hassle, especially when they don’t use the same operating system. With so many Android phones out there, it’s an annoyance a lot of people face.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Leef for Sharing Files to Your Phone', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T14:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd7c965e-5035-578a-a34e-d8369e15c91c', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd7c965e-5035-578a-a34e-d8369e15c91c'}, {'abstract': 'Beware of bookish buyouts.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/a-textbook-case-of-excessive-leverage/', 'snippet': 'Beware of bookish buyouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Worth Publishers alerted us to this story, partly to reassure us that Krugman/Wells royalties will continue on schedule. And I have absolutely no comment to make:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Textbook Case of Excessive Leverage', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T14:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f702542-04d4-58c6-861c-d584bcce1a3e', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f702542-04d4-58c6-861c-d584bcce1a3e'}, {'abstract': 'Marion Bartoli of France, the No. 15 seed, and Sabine Lisicki of Germany, the No. 23 seed, will face each other on Saturday, and one will win their first Grand Slam title.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/sports/tennis/bartoli-advances-to-wimbledon-finals.html', 'snippet': 'Marion Bartoli of France, the No. 15 seed, and Sabine Lisicki of Germany, the No. 23 seed, will face each other on Saturday, and one will win their first Grand Slam title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Marion Bartoli of France and Sabine Lisicki of Germany have played the best tennis of their careers at the All England Club, and on Saturday, Bartoli and Lisicki will meet in the Wimbledon final, each trying to win her first Grand Slam title. It will be first time since 1998 that the Wimbledon women’s final will feature two players bidding for their first major championship.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/sports/tennis/05wimbledon_337/05wimbledon_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 197, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/sports/tennis/05wimbledon_337/05wimbledon_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 197}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/sports/tennis/05wimbledon_337/05wimbledon_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/sports/tennis/05wimbledon_337/05wimbledon_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJu