er known as Angola, is joining the collection of the National Museum of African American History and Culture in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As donations go, it’s a fairly unusual one. A\xa020-foot-tall prison guard tower from the Louisiana State Penitentiary, better known as Angola, is joining the collection of the new National Museum of African American History and Culture in Washington.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prison Tower to Join New Museum’s Collection', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Institutional Change For Angola Guard Tower', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State Penitentiary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of African American History and Culture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T14:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9925cbde-f915-5767-885e-1fbc92733fd6', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9925cbde-f915-5767-885e-1fbc92733fd6'}, {'abstract': 'A 16th-century painting by Jan Mostaert depicting Spanish invaders aiming guns at a naked indigenous population was acquired by the Rijksmuseum.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/an-early-vision-of-america-sold-to-amsterdams-rijksmuseum/', 'snippet': 'A 16th-century painting by Jan Mostaert depicting Span