The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/travel/05newmex/05newmex-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Mexico Rides with ‘The Lone Ranger’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Depp, Johnny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T16:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d99d8e-bd12-5078-b53a-070db3489cff', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d99d8e-bd12-5078-b53a-070db3489cff'}, {'abstract': 'Whoever rules Egypt next will be aware of the fate of rulers who lose the faith of the Egyptians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/opinion/a-coup-in-egypt-but-backed-by-the-people.html', 'snippet': 'Whoever rules Egypt next will be aware of the fate of rulers who lose the faith of the Egyptians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — I took part in the June 30 protests, marched on the presidential palace and chanted that Mohamed Morsi must step down as president and that the Muslim Brotherhood’s yearlong rule of Egypt must come to an end. And on Wednesday I got what I wanted. But I cannot fully celebrate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Coup, but Backed by the People', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T16:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Khorshid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khorshid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/75bb91ed-9be2-5bf5-86cc-a39e5ed77464', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75bb91ed-9be2-5bf5-86cc-a39e5ed77464'}, {'abstract': 'The Fourth of July brought out the first visitors to the Statue of Liberty since Hurricane Sandy shut down the most famous monument in New York Harbor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/nyregion/crowds-line-up-to-see-storm-survivor-statue-of-liberty.html', 'snippet': 'The Fourth of July brought out the first visitors to the Statue of Liberty since Hurricane Sandy shut down the most famous monument in New York Harbor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ninety-nine Boy Scouts and their troop leaders set sail on Thursday morning, rubbing sleep from their eyes. The Statue of Liberty stood out on the horizon, a destination for the tired, huddled and intrepid for more than 125 years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/liberty1/liberty1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After 8 Months Away, Crowds Swarm to See a Storm Survivor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 8 Months Away, Crowds Swarm to See a Storm Survivor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statue of Liberty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberty Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T16:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de9c2bcd-9992-560d-8b00-e2dd478647ce', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de9c2bcd-9992-560d-8b00-e2dd478647ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Syrian president, Bashar al-Assad, saw the ouster of the Egyptian president, Mohamed Morsi, as a vindication of his government’s fight against the two-year Syrian uprising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/world/middleeast/morsis-fall-in-egypt-lauded-by-syrias-assad.html', 'snippet': 'The Syrian president, Bashar al-Assad, saw the ouster of the Egyptian president, Mohamed Morsi, as a vindication of his government’s fight against the two-year Syrian uprising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The jubilation among opponents of Egypt’s deposed Muslim Brotherhood president in Cairo was matched Thursday in the halls of power in Syria’s capital, Damascus, where President Bashar al-Assad declared that the Egyptian events signified the fall of “political Islam” and a vindication of his government’s fight against the two-year Syrian uprising.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Leader Is Jubilant at Morsi’s Fall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian Leader Is Jubilant At Morsi’s Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T16:22:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27545c51-6c87-577d-ab9b-84baff2cae46', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27545c51-6c87-577d-ab9b-84baff2cae46'}, {'abstract': 'Nat Faxon and Jim Rash, the co-writers and co-directors of “The Way, Way Back,” narrate a scene from their film.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/anatomy-of-a-scene-video-the-way-way-back/', 'snippet': 'Nat Faxon and Jim Rash, the co-writers and co-directors of “The Way, Way Back,” narrate a scene from their film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writers Nat Faxon and Jim Rash, who won an Academy Award for their work on the screenplay for “The Descendants,” have made their feature directorial debut with a coming-of-age comedy “The Way, Way Back.” In this video, they discuss elements of a scene that introduces some of the film’s large ensemble cast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene Video: ‘The Way, Way Back’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Faxon, Nat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rash, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T16:32:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/681048de-755d-51ec-ac9e-45df3e7e8581', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/681048de-755d-51ec-ac9e-45df3e7e8581'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks have retained J.R. Smith, who won the sixth man of the year award, and Pablo Prigioni, a backup point guard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/sports/basketball/smith-agrees-to-4-year-deal-with-the-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks have retained J.R. Smith, who won the sixth man of the year award, and Pablo Prigioni, a backup point guard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. R. Smith has agreed to a four-year, $24.5 million deal with the Knicks, ensuring four more years of thrills, cr