l", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'River to River Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bard Music Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T18:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd0687f-e965-518d-878f-7cdf2ebf0724', 'word_count': 1694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd0687f-e965-518d-878f-7cdf2ebf0724'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to walks, talks, exhibitions, readings, celebrations and other events in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/arts/spare-times-for-july-5-11.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to walks, talks, exhibitions, readings, celebrations and other events in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swimming in the City (daily through Labor Day) If you start now, you will have just enough time before Labor Day — with a little to spare — to dip a toe each day into one of the city’s 55 free outdoor public pools. Among them is the Olympic-size pool in McCarren Park, in Greenpoint-Williamsburg, Brooklyn, above, reachable from Lorimer Street. Normal operating hours for pools run by the Department of Parks and Recreation are daily, 11 a.m. to 7 p.m. — with an hour break for cleaning from 3 to 4 p.m. Some pools open earlier for lap swimming or for swimming lessons for children, and at night some offer swimming lessons and water aerobics sessions for those 18 and older; for more information, nyc.gov/parks/pools. In Brooklyn Bridge Park a pop-up pool operated by the Brooklyn Bridge Park Conservancy is in its second season. The 3 ½-foot-deep pool, reachable from Old Fulton and Furman Streets, Dumbo, was closed earlier this week for repairs, but it is now open for free swimming; brooklynbridgepark.org/pool. And the outdoor pool at Riverbank State Park, 679 Riverside Drive, near 145th Street in Hamilton Heights, is open daily for recreational swimming, beginning at 9 a.m., for a modest fee ($2; $1 for those 5 to 15; free for those 4 and younger); nysparks.com/parks/93. Grab the sunscreen and start treading water. (Anne Mancuso)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for July 5-11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T18:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2203fc65-1091-58fe-96e9-0ed6957bc217', 'word_count': 2812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2203fc65-1091-58fe-96e9-0ed6957bc217'}, {'abstract': 'The Arab-American and North African Cultural Street Festival will be on the Great Jones Street block in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/arts/music/an-arab-cultural-turn-for-a-block-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'The Arab-American and North African Cultural Street Festival will be on the Great Jones Street block in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great Jones Street is a blip on