ract': 'The New York Public Library’s plan to renovate its main building on Fifth Avenue in Manhattan is being challenged in a lawsuit.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/opponents-sue-to-block-new-york-public-library-renovation-plan/', 'snippet': 'The New York Public Library’s plan to renovate its main building on Fifth Avenue in Manhattan is being challenged in a lawsuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some opponents of the New York Public Library’s plan to renovate its Fifth Avenue headquarters, which will involve removing its research stacks, filed a lawsuit on Wednesday in New York State Supreme Court to stop the project.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opponents Sue to Block New York Public Library Renovation Plan', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Public Library Is Sued Over Renovation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T19:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/678f7c93-25c8-5ebc-b3a2-36d8e81426ac', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/678f7c93-25c8-5ebc-b3a2-36d8e81426ac'}, {'abstract': 'A selected, critical guide to shows playing in New York, with attention to productions in previews and near opening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/theater/theater-listings-for-july-5-11.html', 'snippet': 'A selected, critical guide to shows playing in New York, with attention to productions in previews and near opening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theater', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Listings for July 5-11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T19:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/010992e0-cb73-558a-a4b0-9883ecdf86df', 'word_count': 5233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/010992e0-cb73-558a-a4b0-9883ecdf86df'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (TCM) FRIDAY NIGHT SPOTLIGHT: THE FILMS OF FRANÇOIS TRUFFAUT A monthlong tribute to this film critic turned director, and mainstay of the French New Wave, kicks off with four films starring Jean-Pierre Léaud, Truffaut’s on-screen alter ego. This first installment begins with “The 400 Blows” (1959), above, Truffaut’s feature film debut, in which he drew inspiration from his childhood for a story about Antoine Doinel, a 12-year-old who escapes his dysfunctional family by turning to crime. “Words cannot state simply how fine is Jean-Pierre Léaud in the role of the boy,” Bosley Crowther wrote in The New York Times. “Out of this brand-new youngster, M. Truffaut has elicited a performance that will live as a delightful, provoking and heartbreaking monument to a boy.” The homage continues at 9:45 with “Antoine and Colette,” Truffaut’s episode from “Love at Twenty” (1962) — an omnibus project featuring five segments directed by five filmmakers from five countries — and a short sequel to “The 400 Blows,” set three years later, in which Antoine has his first sentimental adventure. In “Stolen Kisses” (1968), at 10:30, Antoine, fresh out of the army, looks for work and ponders an affair with an older woman. In “Bed and Board” (1970), at 12:15 a.m., Antoine faces up to the responsibilities of adulthood. And in “Love on the Run” (1979), at 2, Antoine, now divorced, continues his search for romantic fulfillment. The night ends at 4 with “The Green Room” (1978), based in part on “The Altar of the Dead” and two other stories by Henry James, in which Truffaut stars as a writer and World War I veteran who spends his life grieving the loss of his young wife.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T19:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/015b9f7c-4823-5a1a-a1b5-3b3bc92747c2', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/015b9f7c-4823-5a1a-a1b5-3b3bc92747c2'}, {'abstract': 'Muscat wines from Alsace can be dry, slightly sweet or hauntingly nectar-like. Always, though, they are fragrant with a beguiling perfume.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/dining/on-the-scent-of-summer.html', 'snippet': 'Muscat wines from Alsace can be dry, slightly sweet or hauntingly nectar-like. Always, though, they are fragrant with a beguiling perfume.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few romantics operate on the assumption that the glandular secretions of the male musk deer are essential for setting the mood. Yet the musk deer supplies the crucial ingredients for some of the world’s most cherished perfumes, and it is precisely this association between musk and perfume that gave name to the muscat grape, source of one of the world’s most distinctively aromatic wines.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/dining/10POUR1_SPAN/10POUR1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Scent of Summer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Scent of Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T19:12:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3011674-dda1-5e1b-9a2b-1a413733f8f3', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3011674-dda1-5e1b-9a2b-1a413733f8f3'}, {'abstract': 'André Greipel beat Peter Sagan and Mark Cavendish to the finish for his first victory in this year’s Tour de France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/sports/cycling/german-sprints-to-victory-in-stage-6.html', 'snippet': 'André Greipel beat Peter Sagan and Mark Cavendish to the finish for his first victory in this year’s Tour de France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTPELLIER, France — The Tour de France’s team time trial may have taken place earlier this week, but members of Team Lotto-Belisol rode as if it had not ended during the final half-mile of Stage 6 on Thursday. Speeding toward the finish in Montpellier at the front of the peloton, they peeled off one by one, until only their star sprinter, André Greipel, remained. From there, Greipel, a German, needed no more help. He outsprinted Peter Sagan and Mark Cavendish for his first victory of this year’s Tour.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/sports/05tour/05tour-articleLarge.jpg',