ount': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e1a8c75-050b-52a3-bbf0-837072a364eb'}, {'abstract': 'A musical look at the storied past and uncertain future of the last resting place of fallen American heroes.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/a-song-for-the-fallen-on-independence-day/', 'snippet': 'A musical look at the storied past and uncertain future of the last resting place of fallen American heroes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you missed earlier iterations of this song (about half of Dot Earth readers on any particular day are new to the blog), here’s my Independence Day ode to the last resting place of many who sacrificed their lives for our freedom — Arlington National Cemetery. The chorus asks this simple question: Where will they go when there’s no more room in Arlington? (I’m in the final stages of recording my first album, and this ballad will be on it.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Song for the Fallen on Independence Day', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cemeteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Robert E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arlington National Cemetery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T20:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt