eople have many different reasons to be armed.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s hard, it’s hot, it shoots things out,” says one excited interviewee in “A Girl and a Gun,” Cathryne Czubek’s cross-country survey of American women and their firearms. “It’s my first boyfriend,” coos another, tenderly stroking the barrel of her sleek companion, while the blogger Violet Blue just loves her Lady Smith revolver. “It’s owning my womanhood,” says Ms. Blue, who purchased her first weapon after receiving death threats while writing for The San Francisco Chronicle.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN/05RDP_GIRLANDAGUN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN/05RDP_GIRLANDAGUN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 210}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN/05RDP_GIRLANDAGUN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN/05RDP_GIRLANDAGUN_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN/05RDP_GIRLGUN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0,