in New York City mayoral races, but the Metropolitan Transportation Authority has a few rules, like pick up your fliers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stay away from the MetroCard machine. Do not block the staircase. And please: pick up your pamphlets before they flutter onto the track and cause a fire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/nyregion/trailside/trailside-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Platform That Attracts Many Mayoral Candidates: The Subway Stop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Popular Platform For Many Candidates: The Subway Stop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T22:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1852bae3-8ed2-580c-af65-de5ed23ea4ad', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1852bae3-8ed2-580c-af65-de5ed23ea4ad'}, {'abstract': 'The South Street Seaport is still closed because of the damage wrought by Hurricane Sandy in October, but the TKTS discount booth will reopen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/theater/tkts-booth-to-reopen-at-south-street-seaport.html', 'snippet': 'The South Street Seaport is still closed because of the damage wrought by Hurricane Sandy in October, but the TKTS discount booth will reopen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The South Street Seaport is still mainly closed because of the damage wrought by Hurricane Sandy in October, but there is one bright spot: The TKTS discount booth, where people can buy half-price tickets to Broadway and Off Broadway shows, is scheduled to reopen at 11 a.m. on Friday in a temporary location at the corner of Fulton and South Streets. “We felt that we owed it to the community to be back for them this summer,” said Michael Naumann, the managing director of the Theater Development Fund, the nonprofit group that runs the booths downtown, in Times Square and in Brooklyn at 1 MetroTech Center. TKTS offers same-day tickets for evening performances and next-day tickets for matinees.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TKTS Booth to Reopen at South Street Seaport', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TKTS Booth to Reopen At South Street Seaport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TKTS Booth (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T22:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/717e65e1-78c3-51d5-9397-ed5b8da4ea67', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/717e65e1-78c3-51d5-9397-ed5b8da4ea67'}, {'abstract': 'Surveillance rears its head in the spam traps of Jay-Z’s new release, “Magna Carta ... Holy Grail.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/arts/music/jay-z-is-watching-and-he-knows-your-friends.html', 'snippet': 'Surveillance rears its head in the spam traps of Jay-Z’s new release, “Magna Carta ... Holy Grail.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Jay’s Back ASAP,” a song on a 2010 mixtape called “Creative Control,” Jay-Z was indignant about phone surveillance and bribing witnesses: “They tap, them feds don’t play fair/They pay rats to say that they’re part of your operation,” he rapped. But to market his new album, “Magna Carta ... Holy Grail,” he didn’t exactly stand on principle. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05B-JAYZ/B-JayZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 598, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05B-JAYZ/B-JayZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 598, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05B-JAYZ/B-JayZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05B-JAYZ/B-JayZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05B-JAYZ/B-JayZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jay-Z Is Watching, and He Knows Your Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jay-Z Is Watching, and He Knows Your Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T22:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization