for a Brand New Beat,” a new book by Mark Kurlansky, tells the story behind the 1964 song “Dancing in the Street.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Ready for a Brand New Beat” Mark Kurlansky explains why a hit record needs a great hook, the kind that rivets attention in 20 seconds. Books need those hooks too, especially when their authors specialize in eccentric micro-nonfiction, as Mr. Kurlansky does. He has already written books about salt, cod, sports, Clarence Birdseye, nonviolence, the year 1968, Basque history and oysters. In terms of titles with hooks, his personal best: “What? Are These the 20 Most Important Questions in Human History — Or Is This a Game of 20 Questions?” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05BOOKKURLANSKY2/JPBOOKKURLANSKY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05BOOKKURLANSKY2/JPBOOKKURLANSKY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 709}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05BOOKKURLANSKY2/JPBOOKKURLANSKY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 867, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05BOOKKURLANSKY2/JPBOOKKURLANSKY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1734, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05BOOKKURLANSKY2/JPBOOKKURLANSKY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05BOOKKURLANSKY2/JPBOOKKURL