': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/design/20130705-TRAYLOR-slide-7080/20130705-TRAYLOR-slide-7080-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/design/20130705-TRAYLOR-slide-7080/20130705-TRAYLOR-slide-7080-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/design/20130705-TRAYLOR-slide-7080/20130705-TRAYLOR-slide-7080-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storytelling Figures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Traylor, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FOLK ART MUSEUM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T23:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/50185a8f-846e-58f7-ba8f-cecf045da33a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/50185a8f-846e-58f7-ba8f-cecf045da33a'}, {'abstract': 'From his home in the Virgin Islands, Mr. Mosler is waging a well-financed academic battle against economists who want to cut government spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/business/economy/warren-mosler-a-deficit-lover-with-a-following.html', 'snippet': 'From his home in the Virgin Islands, Mr. Mosler is waging a well-financed academic battle against economists who want to cut government spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHRISTIANSTED, V.I. — Warren Mosler is a card-carrying member of the 1 percent. A deeply tanned, tennis-lean hedge fund executive, Mr. Mosler lives on this run-down but jewel-toned Caribbean island for tax reasons. Transitioning into an active retirement, he recently designed and had built an $850,000 catamaran called Knot My Problem. He whizzes around St. Croix in a white, low-slung sports car he created himself, too.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1202, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/business/MOSLER/MOSLER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Warren Mosler, a Deficit Lover With a Following', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Deficit Lover With a Following', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mosler, Warren', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T23:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e725dcd0-e68a-5d1f-85bb-03f43ffe35d8', 'word_count': 1411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e725dcd0-e68a-5d1f-85bb-03f43ffe35d8'}, {'abstract': 'Further reading on Warren Mosler, a leading proponent of modern monetary theory, which holds that governments need not worry about balancing budgets.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/04/warren-mosler-a-reading-list/', 'snippet': 'Further reading on Warren Mosler, a leading proponent of modern monetary theory, which holds that governments need not worry about balancing budgets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Business Day on Friday, I profile Warren Mosler, a charismatic gearhead and hedge fund executive who is among the best-known proponents of modern monetary theory. It is an unusual understanding of how money and economies work, and one of its main ideas is that governments never need to balance their budgets, ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warren Mosler: A Reading List', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mosler, Warren', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-04T23:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49f9e6d7-0538-5380-b67d-fddee042b258', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49f9e6d7-0538-5380-b67d-fddee042b258'}, {'abstract': 'Two exhibitions at the American Folk Art Museum give the marvelous self-taught artist Bill Traylor his due.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/arts/design/bill-traylor-finally-gets-a-spotlight-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Two exhibitions at the American Folk Art Museum give the marvelous self-taught artist Bill Traylor his due.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Traylor’s talent surfaced suddenly in 1939 when he was 85 and had 10 years to live. By then he had left the plantation in southern Alabama where he had been born a slave in 1854, and, after Emancipation, scratched out a living as a sharecropper. He moved to Montgomery, the state capital, where he slept on a pallet in the back room of a funeral parlor and spent his days sitting on a wood box watching the world go by on Monroe Street, the center of the city’s lively black district.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/05TRAYLOR_SPAN/JPTRAYLOR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'c