b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/opinion/0705LETTERSsub/0705LETTERSsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/opinion/0705LETTERSsub/0705LETTERSsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/opinion/0705LETTERSsub/0705LETTERSsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lure of the Fast-Food Menu', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lure of the Fast-Food Menu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T02:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/67f15b82-af51-5c3b-94f9-137193ddd0c1', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67f15b82-af51-5c3b-94f9-137193ddd0c1'}, {'abstract': 'A Greek parliamentary committee on Thursday recommended that former Finance Minister George Papaconstantinou be indicted on criminal charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/world/europe/greece-parliamentary-group-advises-criminal-charges-for-ex-finance-chief.html', 'snippet': 'A Greek parliamentary committee on Thursday recommended that former Finance Minister George Papaconstantinou be indicted on criminal charges.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Greek parliamentary committee on Thursday recommended that former Finance Minister George Papaconstantinou be indicted on criminal charges over his handling of a list of more than 2,000 wealthy Greeks with Swiss bank accounts — a potential source of tax revenue that was never used by the authorities, fueling public anger in the debt-racked nation. Mr. Papaconstantinou, above, has denied accusations that he removed the names of four of his relatives from the list, known as the Lagarde list after Christine Lagarde, currently the managing director of the International Monetary Fund, who gave him a computer disk bearing the names in 2010 when she was France’s finance minister in a bid to aid Greece’s efforts to fight tax evasion. But last month, Greece’s financial crimes squad said it had traced more than $7.8 million in undeclared assets in the bank accounts of the four relatives. Mr. Papaconstantinou faces charges of tampering with a document, breach of faith and violation of duty after 7 of the 13 lawmakers on a cross-party panel formed in January proposed that Greece’s Parliament should vote on whether to indict him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/world/briefs-papaconstantinou/briefs-papaconstantinou-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/world/briefs-papaconstantinou/briefs-papaconstantinou-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/world/briefs-papaco