aned in apparent pain, had violent reactions to the drugs, or waited hours as executioners failed to find a vein. It is the most common way to administer capital punishment in the United States, China and, eventually, Vietnam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fatal Jabs', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T10:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lien Hoang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cf7a16e-69a5-54b4-b6f7-87e0278ecd5f', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cf7a16e-69a5-54b4-b6f7-87e0278ecd5f'}, {'abstract': 'For the fourth week of our contest, judges from Vocabulary.com will choose winners. They will be announced on July 22.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/summer-reading-contest-what-interested-you-most-in-the-times-this-week-3/', 'snippet': 'For the fourth week of our contest, judges from Vocabulary.com will choose winners. They will be announced on July 22.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The Times this week: The Dining section’s special “pie issue,” with recipes, graphics, articles and how-to‘s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/dining/piegrid-LN/piegrid-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'