d on Friday, announcing that a second miracle had been attributed to John Paul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — Pope Francis sped two of his predecessors toward sainthood on Friday: John Paul II, who guided the Roman Catholic Church during the end of the cold war, and John XXIII, who assembled the liberalizing Second Vatican Council in the 1960s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Former Popes to Be Made Saints', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Former Popes Are Accepted for Sainthood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beatifications and Canonizations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John Paul II', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T12:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec5a5277-b8b4-5f48-9618-5f1cd1db2512', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec5a5277-b8b4-5f48-9618-5f1cd1db2512'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Francis approved sainthood for two predecessors and also issued his first encyclical, co-written with Benedict XVI.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/world/europe/papal-encyclical-gets-2-authors-for-first-time.html', 'snippet': 'Pope Francis approved sainthood for two predecessors and also issued his first encyclical, co-written with Benedict XVI.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — Showing more of his sprightly personality and his priorities, Pope Francis sped two of his pre