le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b0acd7b-06be-5216-bb11-f3a7554ffaae', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b0acd7b-06be-5216-bb11-f3a7554ffaae'}, {'abstract': 'Objectionable cartographers; free-range moviegoers; Trojan Camels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/magazine/map-or-menace.html', 'snippet': 'Objectionable cartographers; free-range moviegoers; Trojan Camels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the basement of my German grandmother’s farmhouse, I found a large, framed map of her homeland. It is beautifully illustrated, with drawings of churches, castles and factories, coats of arms from various cities and a quotation from Goethe. It is, however, from 1937, a date that is prominently displayed. Although the map has no Third Reich iconography, Germany’s borders greatly exceed its current ones. Is it ethical to hang it in my living room? ALEX HOYT, NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Map or Menace?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Map or Menace?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klosterman, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T13:25:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dc1624d-a59d-544f-ada8-10b625a5e4f5', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dc1624d-a59d-544f-ada8-10b625a5e4f5'}, {'abstract': 'The television actress on why TV treats women better than film does.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/magazine/what-marcia-gay-harden-knows-about-trophy-wives.html', 'snippet': 'The television actress on why TV treats women better than film does.', 'lead_paragraph': ' You’re joining Aaron Sorkin’s “Newsroom” this season. Because Sorkin is famous for writing long speeches, I wonder if it’s a mixed blessing for an actor: meaty parts, but so much dialogue to learn.  When I first got the role, Jeff Daniels said: “I’ll give you a little Aaron Sorkin tip: Come to set with your lines down for the rehearsal.” I said, “What?” Usually the actor learns them during the day. But as an actress, I have never had a sigh of consternation when I get something complicated. You know how it is when you feel used in a good way. It’s like that old song, “keep on using me, ’til you use me up.” I just feel grateful.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07talk/mag-07Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07talk/mag-07Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07talk/mag-07Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 396, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07talk/mag-07Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07talk/mag-07Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07