': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T13:25:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7a114313-b22a-5807-a81e-bf1a7d09931f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7a114313-b22a-5807-a81e-bf1a7d09931f'}, {'abstract': 'In the shadow of Disney World, an endangered species is practicing the secrets of the deep.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/magazine/the-last-mermaid-show.html', 'snippet': 'In the shadow of Disney World, an endangered species is practicing the secrets of the deep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only a two-hour drive across Central Florida from Disney World to Weeki Wachee Springs, but the distance traveled was much further, from sleek theme parks, hotels with room service and package vacation deals to a rundown motel with broken Wi-Fi situated across the highway from a thrift store and a Hooters. To get there, I took State Road 50 through mile after mile of swamp and farmland, which was dotted with pawn shops looking to buy guns and gold, and billboards with photographs of babies and reminders that “my heart beat 18 days from conception.” Strip malls were broken up by new town-home complexes, old trailer parks and churches.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07mermaid_ss-slide-3UO1/07mermaid_ss-slide-3UO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/magazine/07mermaid_ss-slide-3UO1/07mermaid_ss-slide-3UO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 45