song “Karma” with a shout to the audience of “Ma koreh, Tel Aviv?” (Hebrew for “What’s happening, Tel Aviv?”), Alicia Keys opened her July 4 concert at the Nokia Arena there, The Jerusalem Post reported. The show had drawn protests while in its planning stages but went ahead without incident — other than a cameo appearance from Ms. Keys’s 2-year-old son, Egypt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/keys/keys-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/keys/keys-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/keys/keys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/arts/keys/keys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tel Aviv, Alicia Keys Performs Concert That Had Drawn Protests', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raichel, Idan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T14:28:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/245bd8c6-c221-5a28-ad5d-eee9c66c0367', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/245bd8c6-c221-5a28-ad5d-eee9c66c0367'}, {'abstract': 'The June jobs report saw a surge in part-time workers, and the health care law that starts coming into full effect next year might be in part responsible.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/a-surge-in-part-time-workers/', 'snippet': 'The June jobs report saw a surge in part-time workers, and the health care law that starts coming into full effect next year might be in part responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The June jobs report saw a surge in part-time workers, and the health care law that starts coming into full effect next year might be in part responsible. The number of part-time workers for economic reasons climbed to 8.2 million in June from 7.6 million in March.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Surge in Part-Time Workers', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surge in Part-Time Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T14:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13d7c300-63e2-5978-ad3a-c74758542bc6', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13d7c300-63e2-5978-ad3a-c74758542bc6'}, {'abstract': 'Answers about charging renters for carbon monoxide detectors; a neighbor’s encroaching tree roots; and work done in a condo apartment without a permit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/realestate/real-estate-q-a.html', 'snippet': 'Answers about charging renters for carbon monoxide detectors; a neighbor’s encroaching tree roots; and work done in a condo apartment without a permit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Replacing Detectors Comes at a Price', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Estate Q & A', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q & A', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T14:35:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Romano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0581383-8855-55c8-bd5e-2c82b212887d', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0581383-8855-55c8-bd5e-2c82b212887d'}, {'abstract': 'A novel of love, narcissism and ailing cattle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/books/review/idiopathy-by-sam-byers.html', 'snippet': 'A novel of love, narcissism and ailing cattle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A donkey is tethered between two identical pails, each filled with the same amount and type of oats. If free will exists, the donkey will eat from one before the other. But if free will doesn’t exist, the donkey — lacking any justification for its preference — will just sag in place until it starves to death. “Buridan’s Ass” became an Enlightenment joke at the expense of medieval determinism, specifically that of the French cleric Jean Buridan, whose critics reduced his philosophy to a caricature: between equivalent options, there can be no choice.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/books/review/0707-bks-COHEN/0707-bks-COHEN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], '