e the anger of some users about Photoshop’s plans to convert to a monthly or yearly subscription program.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/photoshops-new-rental-program-and-the-outrage-factor/', 'snippet': 'Readers points out alternatives to Photoshop and note the anger of some users about Photoshop’s plans to convert to a monthly or yearly subscription program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My review of Photoshop CC on Thursday — especially its availability only as a rental, with a monthly or yearly subscription fee — generated a lot of reader feedback. Some of it was astonishing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photoshop’s New Rental Program, and the Outrage Factor', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADOBE SYSTEMS INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Change.org', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:41:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01f49e2b-c070-5a44-8578-4bb1bc7d8b86', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01f49e2b-c070-5a44-8578-4bb1bc7d8b86'}, {'abstract': 'Fans of Krysta Rodriguez can see her on Broadway again in “First Date,” a musical comedy that begins previews this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/theater/insecurities-loud-and-clear.html', 'snippet': 'Fans of Krysta Rodriguez can see her on Broadway again in “First Date,” a musical comedy that begins previews this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katharine McPhee’s character on the ill-fated TV series “Smash” may not have been happy when Ana Vargas, played by Krysta Rodriguez, started to edge into the spotlight. But for some of us it was a pleasure to watch Ms. Rodriguez in some of the stronger numbers. Fans of Ms. Rodriguez, who originated the role of Wednesday Addams in the 2010 Broadway production of “The Addams Family,” can see her on Broadway again in “First Date,” a musical comedy that begins previews this week. She stars with Zachary Levi, new to Broadway but known on TV as a charming nerd in “Chuck.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insecurities Loud and Clear', 'kicker': 'Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Insecurities Loud and Clear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04b0de37-08f0-5688-b57b-fe0d53220788', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b0de37-08f0-5688-b57b-fe0d53220788'}, {'abstract': 'Shooting erupted outside the barracks where the ousted president Mohamed Morsi is believed to be held.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/videos-show-shooting-of-protester-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'Shooting erupted outside the barracks where the ousted president Mohamed Morsi is believed to be held.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Ben Hubbard, David Kirkpatrick and Mayy El-Sheikh report from Cairo, large protests in support of the ousted president Mohamed Morsi were marred by violence on Friday, when witnesses said that at least five demonstrators were killed by security forces outside the Republican Guards barracks where it is believed Mr. Morsi is being held.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows Shooting of Protester in Egypt', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7268c2e1-e589-5924-9451-d85a4b6c0499', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7268c2e1-e589-5924-9451-d85a4b6c0499'}, {'abstract': 'The annual Latin Alternative Music Conference returns this week, eclectic as ever and stretching to the Bronx, where it starts on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/music/latin-excitement-in-three-boroughs.html', 'snippet': 'The annual Latin Alternative Music Conference returns this week, eclectic as ever and stretching to the Bronx, where it starts on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Music isn’t waiting for immigration reform; ideas cross borders. The annual Latin Alternative Music Conference returns this week, eclectic as ever and stretching to the Bronx, where it starts on Tuesday with a free show at 7 p.m. at Crotona Park (Claremont Parkway and Crotona Avenue) by the Brooklyn rapper Joell Ortiz and two Chilean disc jockeys, DJ Raff and Latin Bitman. Free concerts at Central Park SummerStage, midpark at 70th Street, include the rappers Fat Joe (from the Bronx), Cuarto Poder (from Venezuela) and Los Rakas (from Panama via Oakland, Calif.) on Wednesday at 6 p.m.; the Mexican trad-rocker Lila Downs on Thursday at 6 p.m.; and the Mexican pop-folk songwriters Julieta Venegas and Carla Morrison on Saturday at 3 p.m. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latin Excitement in Three Boroughs', 'kicker': 'Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latin Excitement In Three Boroughs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Latin Alternative Music Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e52954c-e7c1-5569-b429-e0ce2966eec2', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e52954c-e7c1-5569-b429-e0ce2966eec2'}, {'abstract': 'A new incarnation of Batman will arrive when the Cartoon Network introduces “Beware the Batman” as part of its DC Nation, a group of shows based on DC Comics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/television/batman-is-back-and-he-bruises.html', 'snippet': 'A new incarnation of Batman will arrive when the Cartoon Network introduces “Beware the Batman” as part of its DC Nation, a group of shows based on DC Comics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every generation is apparently destined to have its own Batman. Octogenarians no doubt think of the original comic book character, who first appeared in 1939. For people in their 50s, perhaps the 1966 television series starring Adam West comes to mind. Younger fans primarily know the various movies.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Batman Is Back, and He Bruises', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Batman Is Back, And He Bruises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:47:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cfb78c2-a348-5467-abf7-d2f5f1394eb5', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cfb78c2-a348-5467-abf7-d2f5f1394eb5'}, {'abstract': 'Latinbeat, the annual survey of Latin American cinema, begins with “La Paz,” the newest movie by the Argentine director and playwright Santiago Loza.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/movies/the-view-from-argentina.html', 'snippet': 'Latinbeat, the annual survey of Latin American cinema, begins with “La Paz,” the newest movie by the Argentine director and playwright Santiago Loza.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Latinbeat, the Film Society of Lincoln Center’s annual survey of Latin American cinema, Friday through July 21, begins with “La Paz,” the newest movie by the Argentine director and playwright Santiago Loza, whose work is remarkable for its empathy and its attention to atmosphere. “La Paz” follows the gradual progress of Liso (Lisandro Rodríguez), a young upper-middle-class man, struggling to reconnect with those around him after being discharged from a mental hospital. The only people he can relate to are his family’s Bolivian maid and his grandmother.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The View From Argentina', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The View From Argentina', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:48:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a93f098-8cb4-5108-bee2-20f87b14a1c1', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a93f098-8cb4-5108-bee2-20f87b14a1c1'}, {'abstract': 'The Original Music Workshop in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, is presenting concerts in its unfinished space and elsewhere in town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/music/where-the-sounds-are-site-specific.html', 'snippet': 'The Original Music Workshop in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, is presenting concerts in its unfinished space and elsewhere in town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Original Music Workshop, a multidisciplinary arts organization that is building a modern performance and rehearsal facility in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, is presenting concerts in its unfinished space and elsewhere in town. This week, the workshop is collaborating with the River to River Festival to produce Ex-Situ, a series of three site-specific events. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Sounds Are Site Specific', 'kicker': 'Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Sounds Are Site Specific', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edee669b-16a0-50a8-8e33-4406c9231020', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edee669b-16a0-50a8-8e33-4406c9231020'}, {'abstract': 'Paul McCarthy’s “Life Cast” is a neat and quiet exhibition of the artist at the uptown Hauser & Wirth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/design/casting-himself-in-different-modes.html', 'snippet': 'Paul McCarthy’s “Life Cast” is a neat and quiet exhibition of the artist at the uptown Hauser & Wirth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Paul McCarthy’s raucous, messy, emotionally wrenching recasting of the Snow White myth taking up lots of space at the Park Avenue Armory and his revisiting of the film “Rebel Without a Cause” doing the same at Hauser & Wirth in Chelsea, it is easy to forget “Life Cast,” his neater and quieter exhibition at the uptown Hauser & Wirth. It emphasizes a different side of his sensibility, something relatively classical against the Expressionism of the other shows.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting Himself in Different Modes', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting Himself In Different Modes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Paul (1945- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83dce809-fde4-5e01-8bfe-f84255b0df8d', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83dce809-fde4-5e01-8bfe-f84255b0df8d'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet comes to the Saratoga Performing Arts Center, its lush summer home of almost five decades, for just one week this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/dance/city-ballet-al-fresco.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet comes to the Saratoga Performing Arts Center, its lush summer home of almost five decades, for just one week this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City Ballet comes to the Saratoga Performing Arts Center, its lush summer home of almost five decades, for just one week this season, down from two weeks each year since 2009 and, before that, a luxurious three. Let’s hope the pattern doesn’t continue; the combination of these dancers, a clear night and seating on the lawn is one of the great pleasures of summer dance.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Ballet Al Fresco', 'kicker': 'Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Ballet Al Fresco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f33a78a6-78a9-5042-9a20-2a6f80b490e5', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f33a78a6-78a9-5042-9a20-2a6f80b490e5'}, {'abstract': 'Nate Chinen and Ben Ratliff assess the decline and nautical re-emergence of smooth jazz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/07/05/arts/music/05popcast_pod.html', 'snippet': 'Nate Chinen and Ben Ratliff assess the decline and nautical re-emergence of smooth jazz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nate Chinen and Ben Ratliff assess the decline and nautical re-emergence of smooth jazz.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sail Away, Mellow Cruisers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T16:57:38+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/251e3af0-eed8-5377-9d23-d8f8f56039ff', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/251e3af0-eed8-5377-9d23-d8f8f56039ff'}, {'abstract': 'New pop releases include those by Pretty Lights, India Arie, Thriftstore Masterpiece, Daughn Gibson and Cheyenne Mize.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/music/new-albums-by-pretty-lights-india-arie-thriftstore-masterpiece-daughn-gibson-and-cheyenne-mize.html', 'snippet': 'New pop releases include those by Pretty Lights, India Arie, Thriftstore Masterpiece, Daughn Gibson and Cheyenne Mize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pretty Lights', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'sour