aragraph': 'While “Game of Thrones” is filmed in places like Morocco, Iceland and Croatia, home base is Northern Ireland. Here’s a fan’s guide to some publicly accessible locations north and south of Belfast, culled from details provided by the Northern Ireland Tourist Board and Northern Ireland Screen. [Related Article]', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-articleLarge.png', 'height': 531, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 531}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-jumbo.png', 'height': 796, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-superJumbo.png', 'height': 796, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07-game-map/07-game-map-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mapping ‘Game of Thrones’ Sites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Game of Thrones (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T17:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44b47e0d-d7bb-5b75-8646-d304bb9b710a', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44b47e0d-d7bb-5b75-8646-d304bb9b710a'}, {'abstract': 'The HBO fantasy series is drawing fans to Northern Ireland, but there is far more to tourism here than the hit show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/travel/following-game-of-thrones-to-belfast-and-beyond.html', 'snippet': 'The HBO fantasy series is drawing fans to Northern Ireland, but there is far more to tourism here than the hit show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dark Hedges are not easy to find. You must follow a serpentine road along a bucolic stretch of Northern Ireland, past sheep, and glens and yellow fields of rapeseed until somewhere between the sleepy towns of Ballycastle and Ballymoney — if you keep your eyes peeled and your foot off the gas pedal — you spot a shadowy lane flanked by centuries-old beech trees. These are the Dark Hedges. Their sinewy branches twist toward the sky like the many arms of the Indian goddess Durga. The highest boughs stretch across the lane to the trees on the opposite side, their leaves overlapping, eclipsing the sun. Locals say this place is haunted by a solitary ghost known as the Grey Lady.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 560}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1867, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/travel/07GAMES_SPAN/07GAMES_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following ‘Game of Thrones’ to Belfast and Beyond', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ireland, North by North-Westeros', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenbloom, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Game of Thrones (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belfast (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Titanic (Ship)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Titanic Belfast', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T17:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83e4f6a7-d605-5d98-8e9b-585f3662829e', 'word_count': 2924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83e4f6a7-d605-5d98-8e9b-585f3662829e'}, {'abstract': 'While Michael S. Dell and Silver Lake strongly believe that their bid for the company is fair, they also appear to be daring the proxy advisory firm to recommend that shareholders vote against the deal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/a-game-of-chicken-at-dell-as-a-proxy-advisers-report-looms/', 'snippet': 'While Michael S. Dell and Silver Lake strongly believe that their bid for the company is fair, they also appear to be daring the proxy advisory firm to recommend that shareholders vote against the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a shareholder vote on the proposed buyout of Dell Inc. approaches, its founder, Michael S. Dell, and the investment firm Silver Lake are standing firm, not raising their $24.4 billion offer.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Game of Chicken at Dell as a Proxy Adviser’s Report Looms', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Founder and Silver Lake Decline to Raise Their $24 Billion Offer for Dell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Shareholder Services Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Asset Management', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T17:36:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f0ed85-b69d-5155-9fdd-a54c60b2cfa2', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f0ed85-b69d-5155-9fdd-a54c60b2cfa2'}, {'abstract': 'A blast from the past.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/crib-sheet-how-i-work-self-indulgent/', 'snippet': 'A blast from the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlie Stross — who is, sad to say, my favorite living science-fiction author now that Iain Banks has died — has been writing a series of “crib sheets” on his blog: explanations of how his various novels came to be written. (Have I mentioned that Neptune’s Brood — which is, among other things, about interstellar monetary economics — is one of his best yet?) I, at least, find this kind of thing fascinating. And then I read Felix Salmon on the growing plague of link rot, and realized that the closest thing I’ve ever done to one of Stross’s crib sheets, a piece I wrote 20 years ago about my work in trade theory and posted to my long-moribund MIT web page, could all too easily vanish from human ken.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crib Sheet: How I Work (Self-indulgent)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T17:38:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c094c3c-6173-533d-a516-4ec6361d18fd', 'word_count': 4760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c094c3c-6173-533d-a516-4ec6361d18fd'}, {'abstract': 'George Zimmerman, on trial in the death of Trayvon Martin, has claimed that the teen attacked him, but a medical examiner said that Mr. Martin’s hands bore only a few scrapes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/us/martins-hands-were-almost-free-of-wounds-medical-examiner-says.html', 'snippet': 'George Zimmerman, on trial in the death of Trayvon Martin, has claimed that the teen attacked him, but a medical examiner said that Mr. Martin’s hands bore only a few scrapes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANFORD, Fla. — George Zimmerman’s mother testified on Friday that it was her son who was overheard crying for help in a 911 call made the night he fatally shot Trayvon Martin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/us/ZIMMERMAN-1/ZIMMERMAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/06/us/ZIMMERMAN-1/ZIMMERMAN-1-a