y a garment is constructed, the reason it’s done by hand, and how that literally gives shape to fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I LOVE THE DEBATE here on the blog about the Dior show and whether Raf Simons’s haute couture collection broke contemporary ground. The comments range from “bo-ring” and “failed experiment” to accolades from longtime blog regulars Marko, E. Frantz and Augustuzs Neto, who said of Mr. Simons’s efforts: “This is the apex of fashion designing, true designing. The man should get a statue on the Ave. Montaigne in recognition for such extraordinary and massive achievements.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Paris Couture Fashion Week, the Shape in Things to Come', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Paris, the Shape in Things to Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viktor & Rolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T18:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0ef3765-1d56-5cde-967e-0ff94a6eccda', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0ef3765-1d56-5cde-967e-0ff94a6eccda'}, {'abstract': 'For years, photographers have been bracing for the moment when video technology will eclipse photography. But as the short clips shared on social me