ional stability for decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Sees a Chance for More Reliable Ties With Egypt and a Weakening of Hamas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Sees a Chance for More Reliable Ties With Egypt and a Weakening of Hamas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdul-Fattah el-', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T20:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b9f4cb-ab86-5cc2-8487-1b5fba442cec', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b9f4cb-ab86-5cc2-8487-1b5fba442cec'}, {'abstract': 'Though Peter Sagan won Stage 7, Juan José Oroz and his Euskaltel-Euskadi team would not be too disappointed: the 100th Tour heads into their home turf, the Pyrenees, this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/sports/cycling/pyrenees-bring-in-some-of-tours-most-passionate-fans.html', 'snippet': 'Though Peter Sagan won Stage 7, Juan José Oroz and his Euskaltel-Euskadi team would not be too disappointed: the 100th Tour heads into their home turf, the Pyrenees, this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBI, France — Juan José Oroz worked furiously in the breakaway on Friday, the ikurriña, the red-green-and-white Basque flag, on the backside of his jersey shining brightly in the sun. Though he was eventually collected by the peloton in the final two miles of Stage 7, won in a sprint finish by Peter Sagan, the flag was a reminder that Oroz and his Euskaltel-Euskadi team would not be too disappointed: the 100th Tour heads into their home turf, the Pyrenees, this weekend.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/06tour1/06tour1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/06tour1/06tour1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/06tour1/06tour1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/06tour1/06tour1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/06tour1/06tour1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/06tour1/06tour1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im