er&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T21:02:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6fb7ef0-80c7-59cf-8b11-f074fbbcf2f7', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6fb7ef0-80c7-59cf-8b11-f074fbbcf2f7'}, {'abstract': 'The longtime director of the State Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts is stepping down, weeks after trying to involve President Vladimir V. Putin in a dispute with the Hermitage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/arts/design/a-russian-museum-feud-with-putin-in-the-middle.html', 'snippet': 'The longtime director of the State Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts is stepping down, weeks after trying to involve President Vladimir V. Putin in a dispute with the Hermitage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Russia — The resignation this week of Irina Antonova as director of the State Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts in Moscow would seem to be connected to her age. After all, Ms. Antonova, the Pushkin’s director since 1961 and the grande dame of the Russian museum world, is 91.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Russian Museum Feud With Putin in the Middle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Russian Museum Feud With Putin in the Middle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kishkovsky, Sophia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T21:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3be22291-0be3-572a-9abf-6f7e4ba18789', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3be22291-0be3-572a-9abf-6f7e4ba18789'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Communications Commission on Friday cleared the way for the $21.6 billion purchase of Sprint by SoftBank of Japan, as well as Sprint’s offer to buy the broadband network Clearwire.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/f-c-c-clears-sprint-deals-with-softbank-and-clearwire/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Communications Commission on Friday cleared the way for the $21.6 billion purchase of Sprint by SoftBank of Japan, as well as Sprint’s offer to buy the broadband network Clearwire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Communications Commission on Friday cleared the way for the $21.6 billion purchase of Sprint by SoftBank of Japan. The approval ends months of posturing and uncertainty about the deal, as a rival, Dish Corp., had challenged the deal on national security grounds and tried to mount a rival takeover bid.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Clears Sprint Deals With SoftBank and Clearwire', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.C.C. Approves Softbank’s Deal To Buy Sprint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T21:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstnam