n State respond to a Sunday Review news analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Value of Menu Labeling', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Value of Menu Labeling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calories', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T23:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/514d9fd9-832a-58ab-a35a-fcf661899525', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/514d9fd9-832a-58ab-a35a-fcf661899525'}, {'abstract': 'As a group, the 2010 merlot wines released by the members of Merliance are showing great quality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/nyregion/a-great-vintage-for-merlot-grapes.html', 'snippet': 'As a group, the 2010 merlot wines released by the members of Merliance are showing great quality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long Island’s terrific 2010 vintage helps make the argument that merlot, in single-variety wines or dominant in red blends, should be accepted as the region’s signature red grape. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Great Vintage for Merlot Grapes', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Great Vintage For Merlot Grapes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Merlot (Wine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merliance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T23:16:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09ff91d5-5f56-5693-80b4-70fcb3d3175b', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09ff91d5-5f56-5693-80b4-70fcb3d3175b'}, {'abstract': 'Following are translated closing remarks by Aleksei A. Navalny, the opposition leader, at his trial in the Russian city of Kirov on July 5, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/world/europe/text-of-navalnys-closing-remarks-in-russian-court.html', 'snippet': 'Following are translated closing remarks by Aleksei A. Navalny, the opposition leader, at his trial in the Russian city of Kirov on July 5, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Aleksei A. Navalny, Russia’s most prominent political opposition leader, delivered an emotional speech on Friday in response to a prosecutor’s closing arguments demanding that Mr. Navalny be convicted on embezzlement charges and sentenced to six years in prison. A co-defendant, Pyotr Ofitserov, faced a five-year sentence. With the court proceedings in Kirov, a regional capital, streamed live on the Internet, Mr. Navalny delivered a rhetorical broadside against the Kremlin, in which he said his opposition work would not stop, and sought to rally public support. “I cannot run away from myself,” he said. “I have nothing else but this.” The judge said a verdict would be issued on July 18. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 741}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1659, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/world/europe/06russia-text/06russia-text-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Text of Navalny’s Closing Remarks in Russian Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T23:18:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/451b4ea4-1755-5284-ab88-f7b361437205', 'word_count': 1365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451b4ea4-1755-5284-ab88-f7b361437205'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to news articles and an editorial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/opinion/watching-a-drama-play-out-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to news articles and an editorial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching a Drama Play Out in Egypt', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watching a Drama Play Out in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-05T23:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1099ac1-e96a-5e45-baf2-e1be516979f3', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1099ac1-e96a-5e45-baf2-e1be516979f3'}, {'abstract': 'Madison and Main is the latest offering from Michael Gluckman, who has operated a number of East Hampton restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/nyregion/a-review-of-madison-and-main-restaurant-in-sag-harbor.html', 'snippet': 'Madison and Main is the latest offering from Michael Gluckman, who has operated a number of East Hampton restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a lot of experience behind Madison and Main, which opened in Sag Harbor in April. Michael Gluckman, an owner, has opened and later sold a number of East Hampton restaurants: Bamboo, the Lodge and the Boathouse (all since closed). His partner, Eric Miller, who is also the executive chef, has an impressive résumé that includes City Cafe in Manhattan and Cavo in Queens. Helping out in the kitchen this season is Keith Rennie, who once cooked at Pisces and at Mad Fish, also in Manhattan. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07DINELI3/07DINELI3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07DINELI3/07DINELI3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07DINELI3/07DINELI3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 981, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07DINELI3/07DINELI3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1786, 'width': 1711, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07DINELI3/07DINELI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop