labor force status of individuals from one month to the next. Here’s a chart showing the flows for unemployed workers — that is, if a worker was unemployed last month, what is his or her labor status this month?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How One Month’s Jobless Fare a Month Later', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T00:09:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a96c97-12ca-52f4-a5ab-73b06f122d70', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a96c97-12ca-52f4-a5ab-73b06f122d70'}, {'abstract': 'Some mayoral candidates are cramming to learn Spanish in hopes of winning over a rapidly growing population of Latino voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/nyregion/learning-what-to-say-in-a-second-language.html', 'snippet': 'Some mayoral candidates are cramming to learn Spanish in hopes of winning over a rapidly growing population of Latino voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some dread having to produce an authentic-sounding “buenas noches” before crowds in East Harlem. Others take pride in belting out flawless renditions of “La Borinqueña,” Puerto Rico’s official anthem, at parades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/nyregion/trailside/trailside