of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a5eefe9-3e4a-5eda-af27-76cbd155e765', 'word_count': 1260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a5eefe9-3e4a-5eda-af27-76cbd155e765'}, {'abstract': 'What should retiring baby boomers do with the companies they have built up? Sell to their employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/opinion/the-legacy-of-the-boomer-boss.html', 'snippet': 'What should retiring baby boomers do with the companies they have built up? Sell to their employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLLEGE PARK, Md. — OVER the next decade millions of business owners born during the baby boom will retire. Many, with no obvious succession strategy, will simply sell their companies, the backbone of Main Street economies across the country, to large corporations. All too often the result will be consolidations, plant closures and lost jobs for the people who helped build and sustain their companies for decades. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/opinion/0706OPEDstolle/0706OPEDstolle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/06/opinion/0706OPEDstolle/0706OPEDstolle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/opinion/0706OPEDstolle/0706OPEDstolle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/opinion/0706OPEDstolle/0706OPEDstolle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1105, 'width': 1820, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '