in Port St. Lucie, Fla., the same year, the person he took along to verify the result and share in the fun was Dickey.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/06/sports/Y-BATS-1/Y-BATS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Mets Pitchers Facing Off in Toronto', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Mets Pitchers Facing Off in Toronto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelfrey, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T02:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67d7075d-526f-5866-91af-8d691e6b2e85', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67d7075d-526f-5866-91af-8d691e6b2e85'}, {'abstract': 'At 1-4 of the third set against Jerzy Janowicz, Andy Murray played a nearly flawless service game, giving him an extra kick at a critical point in the match.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/in-one-quick-game-murray-changes-pace-of-a-match/', 'snippet': 'At 1-4 of the third set against Jerzy Janowicz, Andy Murray played a nearly flawless service game, giving him an extra kick at a critical point in the match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jerzy Janowicz was feeling it. After breaking Andy Murray early in the third set of their Wimbledon semifinal Friday, he held serve with authority, thumping an ace to go up, 4-1. With the light beginning to dwindle, he was two games from taking a two-sets-to-one lead, and he knew the roof over Centre Court would have to be closed for the match to continue. To that point, Janowicz was weaving a potent spell of powerful serving, aggressive baseline play and deft drop shots to keep Murray from finding a rhythm. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In One Quick Game, Murray Changes Pace of a Match', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Janowicz, Jerzy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T02:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97b91487-35c4-5774-a85e-061ba03a404d', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97b91487-35c4-5774-a85e-061ba03a404d'}, {'abstract': 'Detroit has sued a bond insurer, Syncora Guarantee Inc., blaming it for the withholding as much as $11 million a month in casino revenue, the city’s emergency manager said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/us/michigan-detroit-sues-syncora-guarantee-inc-over-casino-money.html', 'snippet': 'Detroit has sued a bond insurer, Syncora Guarantee Inc., blaming it for the withholding as much as $11 million a month in casino revenue, the city’s emergency manager said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Detroit has sued a bond insurer, Syncora Guarantee Inc., blaming it for the withholding as much as $11 million a month in casino revenue, Kevyn Orr, the city’s emergency manager, said Friday. Mr. Orr was appointed in March to lead the city out of a fiscal crisis that has put it on the brink of bankruptcy. Detroit seeks a court order barring Syncora and other defendants from limiting its access to money from its three casinos. Syncora insures some of the $1.4 billion in “certificates of participation” issued by the city to shore up two public employee pension funds as well as swap agreements through which the city hedges interest rates payable on some of the certificates. Casino-derived revenues were pledged to secure the swaps, Mr. Orr said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Detroit Sues Insurer Over Casino Money', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Detroit Sues Insurer Over Casino Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syncora Guarantee Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orr, Kevyn D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T02:34:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9919d336-eeb7-5f29-ae46-43cf36e1c5ee', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9919d336-eeb7-5f29-ae46-43cf36e1c5ee'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Breslin scours the city to identify alleyways and vistas that directors would find ideal.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/05/finding-the-perfect-spot-to-shoot/', 'snippet': 'Kevin Breslin scours the city to identify alleyways and vistas that directors would find ideal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A member of the Teamsters union and the Directors Guild of America, Kevin Breslin is a filmmaker and a location scout for commercials. Over 20 years, he has maneuvered crews through the city and arranged thousands of shoots, including the New York Lottery’s “If I Had a Million Dollars” and Verizon’s “Can You Hear Me Now?” spots. Mr. Breslin, 56, lives in Belle Harbor, Queens, with his wife and youngest son.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1656, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1656}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 372, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07QA/07QA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding the Perfect Spot to Shoot', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Directors Guild of America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T02:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/434541ee-8c36-575a-8099-122572745bca', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434541ee-8c36-575a-8099-122572745bca'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrating a signed contract on an apartment with a dinner of barbecue in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/nyregion/good-friends-big-helpings.html', 'snippet': 'Celebrating a signed contract on an apartment with a dinner of barbecue in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alchemy, Texas, a barbecue joint that opened in the back of a sports bar in Jackson Heights, Queens, on April 1, has a solid pedigree — it’s a spinoff of the highly rated John Brown Smokehouse in Long Island City — and enviable early love from the foodie nation, including the Village Voice, which called the prime rib “nothing short of spectacular.” And yet it still hasn’t quite caught on with the city’s barbecue-obsessed. “It’s weird out there,” said Josh Bowen, the chef and one of the owners, adding that the restaurant was not permanently committed to the site. “One night we’ll sell out, and the next there’ll be no one there.” On a rainy night last week (was there any other kind?), three of the six tables were empty, in contrast to the robust trade at the Legends sports bar in the front. Meats were served by the pound, on paper plates, and plastic checked tablecloths and paper towels caught the overflow of good stuff, which Mr. Bowen said combined Texas tradition with the neighborhood’s South Asian spices, plus touches that belonged to neither school. The next night, Mr. Bowen said, he would feature frog legs on the chalkboard menu. “This is a place to experiment,” he said. Hence the name.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1901, 'width': 1901, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07TABLE_SPAN/07TABLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Friends, Big Helpings', 'kicker': 'At the Table | Alchemy, Texas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Friends, Big Helpings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alchemy, Texas (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Heights (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T02:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9dfcbd5-c1bd-54e0-856a-24d3c7c7fc74', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9dfcbd5-c1bd-54e0-856a-24d3c7c7fc74'}, {'abstract': 'A new app introduced by the borough’s Chamber of Commerce serves as an all-purpose tour guide, but it isn’t comprehensive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/nyregion/looking-for-fun-in-all-the-queens-places.html', 'snippet': 'A new app introduced by the borough’s Chamber of Commerce serves as an all-purpose tour guide, but it isn’t comprehensive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are almost too many events to keep track of in Queens this summer. The usual draws, including the MoMA PS1  Warm Up  dance parties and the U.S. Open tennis tournament, remain as enticing as ever. And then there’s the Major League Baseball All-Star Game, which takes place at Citi Field on July 16. Add in the  Thunderbird Intertribal Powwow  and the annual Hot Jazz/Cool Garden concert series, and it seems as if a trip to the city’s largest, most diverse borough is inevitable.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07SUBAPP-CITY/07SUBAPP-CITY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 600, 'subType'