le in Flushing, Queens, the day begins quite early.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/nyregion/before-the-songs-a-precisely-made-chai.html', 'snippet': 'For Chandrika Krishnamurthy Tandon, the Grammy nominee who leads a choir at a Hindu temple in Flushing, Queens, the day begins quite early.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chandrika Krishnamurthy Tandon, a financial adviser and a New York University trustee, is also a Grammy-nominated musician who released her third album, “Soul March,” in April. Her albums are produced under a nonprofit label that donates the proceeds to various causes. Ms. Tandon, 58, who was born in Madras, India, and came to New York in 1979, lives on the Upper East Side with her husband, Ranjan, 62, a hedge fund manager. They have a daughter who lives in Washington, D.C., and visits often on weekends. On Sundays, Ms. Tandon leads a choir at the Ganesh Hindu Temple in Flushing, Queens.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1603, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/nyreg