tysburg.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/an-orange-blossom-in-the-devils-den/', 'snippet': 'A New York company gets trapped in the most horrific fighting at Gettysburg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy and George Hoover looked on as rebels traipsed through the couple’s modest Pennsylvania farm during the days immediately following the Battle of Gettysburg. The disappointed, yet still defiant, Confederates camped in the fields around the Hoover homestead near Waynesboro, about 20 miles west of the battlefield.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Orange Blossom in the Devil’s Den', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T15:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fdb40cd-9d30-54ef-82da-8b039e6eec40', 'word_count': 2337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fdb40cd-9d30-54ef-82da-8b039e6eec40'}, {'abstract': 'Brendan Emmett Quigley has us going in circles.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/variety-marching-bands-2/', 'snippet': 'Brendan Emmett Quigley has us going in circles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — You don’t need me for this. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Marching Bands', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword P