ry — and concluded that the case for euro membership was not good.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rationality and the Euro', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T17:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5abb45d-1037-551e-a269-7b031275529f', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5abb45d-1037-551e-a269-7b031275529f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers sound off on the latest sports headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/sports/letters-to-the-sports-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers sound off on the latest sports headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Ballpark, a Hefty Price Tag', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Sports Editor', 'kicker': 'In-Box', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T17:18:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac4e1736-fc53-5e0a-9897-5d01134c48bd', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac4e1736-fc53-5e0a-9897-5d01134c48bd'}, {'abstract': 'Many mutual funds slumped near the end of the second quarter amid signs that the Federal Reserve might pull back on its bond-buying. For investors, the future now looks harder to read.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/business/mutfund/from-the-fed-mixed-signals-for-main-street.html', 'snippet': 'Many mutual funds slumped near the end of the second quarter amid signs that the Federal Reserve might pull back on its bond-buying. For investors, the future now looks harder to read.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRICES of stocks, bonds and other investments sank toward the end of the second quarter as the Federal Reserve signaled that it might begin what Wall Street has called “the taper” — the reduction and then the possible reversal of bond purchases that the Fed has used for years to support the economy and markets. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-LEDE/07-LEDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-LEDE/07-LEDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 498}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-LEDE/07-LEDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-LEDE/07-LEDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1699, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-LEDE/07-LEDE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-LEDE/07-LEDE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred