uri': 'nyt://article/916dec61-2e35-53a2-8b25-94a557c653d1'}, {'abstract': 'The Sino-Soviet split is ancient history. Russia and China are closer than ever, and that’s bad news for the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/opinion/sunday/a-new-anti-american-axis.html', 'snippet': 'The Sino-Soviet split is ancient history. Russia and China are closer than ever, and that’s bad news for the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE flight of the leaker Edward J. Snowden from Hong Kong to Moscow last month would not have been possible without the cooperation of Russia and China. The two countries’ behavior in the Snowden affair demonstrates their growing assertiveness and their willingness to take action at America’s expense. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1439, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Anti-American Axis?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Anti-American Axis?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T18:25:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie H. Gelb and Dimitri K. Simes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Gelb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dimitri', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Simes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a88b2c4b-d071-534d-9ed5-7bc60bcfe9ba', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a88b2c4b-d071-534d-9ed5-7bc60bcfe9ba'}, {'abstract': 'Your reward for an 11th drink: we will refrain from hatefully scowling at you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/opinion/sunday/java-jive-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Your reward for an 11th drink: we will refrain from hatefully scowling at you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The coffee you are about to enjoy was brewed the old-fashioned way, in a slow-drip machine powered by a mustachioed man pedaling a penny-farthing bicycle. Stop for a moment to admire the sumptuous curvature of our coffee maker’s gold-hued cylinders, crafted by Japanese artisans who reside, for reasons unknown, within the central vent of an active volcano. Have you witnessed such glory outside the walls of a major city’s museum? ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Java Jive, 2013', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Java Jive, 2013', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruttenberg, Jay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffeehouses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Ruttenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruttenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/468f4ec1-616d-50c5-b399-58eeba7f19ca', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/468f4ec1-616d-50c5-b399-58eeba7f19ca'}, {'abstract': 'Firefighters are taught to be self-reliant, but it is dangerous to emphasize individual behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/opinion/sunday/fighting-wildfires-processing-death.html', 'snippet': 'Firefighters are taught to be self-reliant, but it is dangerous to emphasize individual behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHY young men from the country become firefighters is hard to explain to people who are not from the country. For most of us, it’s not about the rush, which fades with time, or the paycheck. We could earn more working for the railroad or a car dealership. I figure it’s about the land. It’s what we know best — these woods, dirt roads, small towns — and if given the chance to make a living outside with our backs, under a blue, hot sky, then by God yes we’re going to take it. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sunday-review/07FIRE/07FIRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Wildfires, Processing Death', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting Wildfires, Processing 