re health to the Continent’s depressed economy.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Delayed Banking Union', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe’s Delayed Banking Union', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/caacbfda-f5a8-5bf3-aa23-422b9f79bc49', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caacbfda-f5a8-5bf3-aa23-422b9f79bc49'}, {'abstract': 'At his trial, James (Whitey) Bulger seems stung by the witnesses who say he was an F.B.I. informer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/opinion/sunday/from-gypo-to-whitey.html', 'snippet': 'At his trial, James (Whitey) Bulger seems stung by the witnesses who say he was an F.B.I. informer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there such a thing as Irish omertà? The insistence that there is a code of honor for an Irish-American hoodlum that would stop him from ever becoming an F.B.I. informer is the most intriguing part of the criminal defense being offered by James (Whitey) Bulger in his trial in Boston. Mr. Bulger stands accused of a raft of violent crimes from his years as an underworld boss, including involvement in 19 murders. Yet it is the prosecution’s spelling out his role as an alleged informer who turned on his own kind in South Boston that seems most stinging for him — to the point of his snarling expletives at people who say so on the witness stand.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Gypo to Whitey', 'kicker': 'Editiorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Gypo to Whitey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Informers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/17a0bcf4-8aff-54e6-9a63-96bf0d1ac773', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17a0bcf4-8aff-54e6-9a63-96bf0d1ac773'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of past bills and invoices means all of my mistakes are on record.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/opinion/sunday/the-farm-drawer.html', 'snippet': 'A collection of past bills and invoices means all of my mistakes are on record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day, a question arose: How deep is my well? That’s the kind of number I should know by heart, if only because it’s so interesting to talk about wells with other well owners — a conversation that barely gets off the ground if you don’t know how deep your well is. I remember having work done on my well ages ago when a check valve failed. Surely on the bill someone had written the depth in feet. All I had to do was find the bill.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Farm Drawer', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Farm Drawer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinkenborg, Verlyn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wells', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8699f941-81cb-5544-b53f-065c6f62791e', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8699f941-81cb-5544-b53f-065c6f62791e'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes it’s hard to avoid sports terms in the workplace, as the manager of a hotel restaurant (and former soccer player) can attest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/jobs/going-the-distance-with-sports-analogies.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes it’s hard to avoid sports terms in the workplace, as the manager of a hotel restaurant (and former soccer player) can attest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY boss, Edward Mady, general manager of the Beverly Hills Hotel, can’t get enough of sports. His office walls are lined with souvenir baseballs and photographs of him posing with famous athletes. His corporate lingo is laced with sports metaphors and analogies. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1184, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-PRE/07-PRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going the Distance, With Sports Analogies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Know Your Terms, And Go The Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pepe De Anda', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pepe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Anda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a96654af-a41d-52b3-a741-0d9416c398e0', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a96654af-a41d-52b3-a741-0d9416c398e0'}, {'abstract': 'I’m, at very best, 77 percent focused on entertaining my kids.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/a-writers-mommy-guilt/', 'snippet': 'I’m, at very best, 77 percent focused on entertaining my kids.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’m reading your book, and now I’m worried about you,” an acquaintance told me about my (fictional) novel, which concerns the (fictional) misadventures of a (fictional) depressed mother. My whole head flushed. My immediate response was anger, then denial, then guilt. I was practically going through stages of mourning, and maybe I was in mourning, mourning for the simpler vision of myself I was able to project on Facebook, or you know, in person or whatever.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Writer’s Mommy Guilt', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Writer’s Mommy Guilt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Shearn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shearn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/717d4e4f-e647-52f6-80bb-4d116439792d', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/717d4e4f-e647-52f6-80bb-4d116439792d'}, {'abstract': 'The Shareholder Rights Project has had  remarkable early success in persuading companies to put directors up for re-election every year, instead of in staggered terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/business/new-momentum-for-change-in-corporate-board-elections.html', 'snippet': 'The Shareholder Rights Project has had  remarkable early success in persuading companies to put directors up for re-election every year, instead of in staggered terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHAREHOLDER efforts that actually succeed in changing dubious corporate governance policies are so rare that when they happen, it makes you sit up and take notice. So it’s worth examining the results achieved so far this year by the Shareholder Rights Project, a program operating at the Harvard Law School. And with any luck, its success might shame do-nothing investment managers, like those running many mutual funds, into action.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Momentum for Change in Corporate Board Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '35 Big Steps To Accountability', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenson, Gretchen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:11:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9af3b751-a4bf-5a94-8b18-02b9a8721f36', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9af3b751-a4bf-5a94-8b18-02b9a8721f36'}, {'abstract': 'Fear about government debt has put the brakes on much American infrastructure investment, even when the future benefits far outweigh the repayment costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/business/austerity-wont-work-if-the-roof-is-leaking.html', 'snippet': 'Fear about government debt has put the brakes on much American infrastructure investment, even when the future benefits far outweigh the repayment costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I RECENTLY spent a week in Berlin, where the entire city seemed under construction. In every direction, cranes and other heavy equipment dominated the landscape. Although many projects are in the private sector, innumerable others — including bridge and highway repairs, new subway stations and other infrastructure work — are financed by taxpayers.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Austerity Won’t Work if the Roof Is Leaking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Austerity Won’t Work If the Roof Is Leaking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Robert H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert H. Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/665f2ae5-1a48-5e68-b4ea-1cd749d958dd', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/665f2ae5-1a48-5e68-b4ea-1cd749d958dd'}, {'abstract': 'To better understand the work of  the sales force, a top GlaxoSmithKline executive sometimes accompanies reps on their visits to clients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/jobs/a-glaxo-executive-seeing-through-a-sales-reps-eyes.html', 'snippet': 'To better understand the work of  the sales force, a top GlaxoSmithKline executive sometimes accompanies reps on their visits to clients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS born and raised in San Juan, one of nine children of an Irish-American father and a Puerto Rican mother. They met at the chapel of Bellevue Hospital in New York when they were taking care of relatives who were patients there.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 777}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 913, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/business/07-BOSS/07-BOSS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Glaxo Executive, Seeing Through a Sales Rep’s Eyes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Through a Sales Rep’s Eyes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:28:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deirdre P. Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deirdre', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27edec9f-49c2-5309-870d-ace9753db1a1', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27edec9f-49c2-5309-870d-ace9753db1a1'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Pettitte persevered through early trouble to pitch six and two-thirds innings, and Eduardo Nunez drove in the winning run against the Orioles after coming off the disabled list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/sports/baseball/yankees-rescue-an-uneven-pettitte-for-sixth-straight-victory.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Pettitte persevered through early trouble to pitch six and two-thirds innings, and Eduardo Nunez drove in the winning run against the Orioles after coming off the disabled list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a tumultuous 2013 season, Andy Pettitte has spent time on the disabled list, won his 250th game and set a Yankees strikeout mark, but over all, it has been a subpar year by his standard. At times, he has struggled to find his command and has even acknowledged losing the feel for his signature cutter. Worse, he has struggled to find answers. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 466, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 466}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1589, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/sports/07YANKEES/07YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Rescue Uneven Pettitte for 6th Straight Win', 'kicker': 'Yankees 5, Orioles 4', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pettitte Is Uneven Against Orioles, but Yanks Win Their Sixth Straight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arangure, Jorge Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nunez, Eduardo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:52:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arangure', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff594557-ea86-5f57-aa33-8637716dfebd', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff594557-ea86-5f57-aa33-8637716dfebd'}, {'abstract': 'What’s happening above the clouds mirrors what’s happening on the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/class-struggle-in-the-sky/', 'snippet': 'What’s happening above the clouds mirrors what’s happening on the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choice of “snacks” on some recent flights I’ve taken include blue potato chips, a cranberry-almond bar, a packet of trail mix and — a selection I haven’t been offered before — popcorn. But it makes sense: the cabin already feels like a movie theater at the end of a showing, even though we still have an hour to go. The floor is strewn with candy-bar wrappers and broken headsets, crumpled napkins and cracked plastic glasses. There’s so little legroom that I have to push my knees against the seat in front of me as if I’m doing crunches. Welcome to economy.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Class Struggle in the Sky', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Class Struggle In the Sky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T20:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Atlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Atlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a738e72-7dee-5e0e-98c0-203e4d4e56d5', 'word_count': 1647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a738e72-7dee-5e0e-98c0-203e4d4e56d5'}, {'abstract': 'His grandfather was a mighty Hollywood force, but Casey Wasserman has chosen the sports world for making his mark, with a rapidly growing management and marketing firm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/business/a-sports-agent-with-hollywood-in-his-blood.html', 'snippet': 'His grandfather was a mighty Hollywood force, but Casey Wasserman has chosen the sports world for making his mark, with a rapidly growing management and marketing firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRETTY much forever, one question has hovered over Casey Wasserman: 