6db9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8edfeeb2-3e32-53ce-b4d5-614fb8bf6db9'}, {'abstract': 'A small freight company in Portland, Ore., makes its deliveries not with semitrailers but with electric-assisted trikes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/business/in-cargo-delivery-the-three-wheelers-that-could.html', 'snippet': 'A small freight company in Portland, Ore., makes its deliveries not with semitrailers but with electric-assisted trikes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S well-known that Portland really likes its bicycles. But its embrace of bike culture goes beyond its catering to commuters, leisure riders and athletes. So bike-centric is Portland that its residents can have any of the following delivered to their doorsteps by cycle: a pizza, a keg of pilsner, plumbing services or a hot tub. And the list grows from there. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Cargo Delivery, the Three-Wheelers That Could', 'kicker': 'Prototype', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Three-Wheelers\r\nThat Could', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delivery Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Claire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Pedal Power LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'B-Line Sustainable Urban Delivery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freight (Cargo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T21:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fe98108-4c58-50e3-bf2c-f60c08cc681b', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fe98108-4c58-50e3-bf2c-f60c08cc681b'}, {'abstract': 'Varieties of wrongness.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/regions-of-derpistan/', 'snippet': 'Varieties of wrongness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Barro has made a very useful contribution to policy discussion by adapting the term “derp” for a certain kind of all-too-prevalent stance in economic debate, which Noah Smith somewhat euphemistically describes as “the constant, repetitive reiteration of strong priors”. In other words, people who take a position and refuse to alter that position no matter how strongly the evidence refutes it, who continue to insist that they have The Truth despite being wrong again and again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regions of Derpistan', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T21:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0eb7dc0-5b4d-56de-a323-6b0aa8e127e0', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0eb7dc0-5b4d-56de-a323-6b0aa8e127e0'}, {'abstract': 'Turmoil in Egypt and the uncertain fate of immigration reform share the spotlight on the Sunday shows this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/06/sunday-breakfast-menu-july-7/', 'snippet': 'Turmoil in Egypt and the uncertain fate of immigration reform share the spotlight on the Sunday shows this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With tensions mounting in Egypt after the removal of President Mohamed Morsi,\xa0the news broke Saturday that Mohamed ElBaradei, a Nobel Prize-winning diplomat who is an opponent of Mr. Morsi, would be named the country’s interim prime minister. NBC’s “Meet the Press” will have an interview with Mr. ElBaradei about the transition to a new government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, July 7', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ElBaradei, Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menendez, Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MEDICAL ASSN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T21:36:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2e9bcc0-2e3a-503f-b338-5c242eab0e1e', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2e9bcc0-2e3a-503f-b338-5c242eab0e1e'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to “Politics Aside, a Common Bond” (Economic View, June 30).', 'web_url