ne, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lahore (Pakistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-06T23:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Waqar Gillani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Waqar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e24c13f7-72a8-50e2-9ca3-5e92ca627bf8', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e24c13f7-72a8-50e2-9ca3-5e92ca627bf8'}, {'abstract': 'With the secret FISA court’s approval, the National Security Agency is collecting data not only on terrorism cases but also other foreign intelligence issues like nuclear proliferation and cyberattacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/us/in-secret-court-vastly-broadens-powers-of-nsa.html', 'snippet': 'With the secret FISA court’s approval, the National Security Agency is collecting data not only on terrorism cases but also other foreign intelligence issues like nuclear proliferation and cyberattacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In more than a dozen classified rulings, the nation’s surveillance court has created a secret body of law giving the National Security Agency the power to amass vast collections of data on Americans while pursuing not only terrorism suspects, but also people possibly involved in nuclear proliferation, espionage and cyberattacks, officials say.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Secret, Court Vastly Broadens Powers of N.S.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':