ing in print on July 7, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 7, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T04:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4550bfe-864a-555b-b602-34fc0c6ae292', 'word_count': 1316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4550bfe-864a-555b-b602-34fc0c6ae292'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/arts/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13, 49) ENDEAVOUR, SERIES 1: GIRL In this new “Masterpiece Mystery!” series, created as a prequel to “Inspector Morse,” Shaun Evans plays the young Detective Constable Endeavour Morse, a rookie police officer on the Oxford force in the 1960s who immediately makes enemies when the inspector Fred Thursday (Roger Allam, above right, with Mr. Evans, center) chooses him for a position that should have gone to a sergeant. In this first of four episodes, Morse and Thursday investigate burgled gas meters, a dead secretarial student, a string of post office robberies and a love child. “The lead actors do good work, even though their job, to some extent, is to make themselves part of the period décor,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. “In the course of Sunday’s episode Morse develops one of his patented hopeless crushes on a suspect, and it gets him busted down from bagman to general duty. You’re a good detective but a poor policeman, Thursday tells him, and something similar could be said of ‘Endeavour’: it’s a poor mystery, but it’s not a bad meal.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T06:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9b08202-4065-5b0e-9d55-e71061447eaf', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9b08202-4065-5b0e-9d55-e71061447eaf'}, {'abstract': 'The pilot at the controls on Asiana Flight 214 was said to have had only 43 hours of experience flying a Boeing 777, and an airline spokeswoman said that it was his first time piloting a 777 into San Francisco.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/us/san-francisco-plane-crash.html', 'snippet': 'The pilot at the controls on Asiana Flight 214 was said to have had only 43 hours of experience flying a Boeing 777, and an airline spokeswoman said that it was his first time piloting a 777 into San Francisco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — The nearly 11-hour trip across the Pacific had gone smoothly as Asiana Flight 214 approached San Francisco International Airport — an uneventful flight for the 291 passengers, including dozens of Chinese teenagers who were arriving for a summer camp to study English and tour colleges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/07/world/07plane_7/07plane_7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/07/world/07plane_7/07plane_7-articleLarge.jpg', 'x