', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/705cafac-4751-5c3b-8bd9-f7bedded0654', 'word_count': 2901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/705cafac-4751-5c3b-8bd9-f7bedded0654'}, {'abstract': 'Two Buddhist monks were injured after a series of low intensity blasts went off at the Mahabodhi Temple complex in Bodh Gaya on Sunday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/bomb-blasts-at-indias-buddhist-mecca-in-bihar/', 'snippet': 'Two Buddhist monks were injured after a series of low intensity blasts went off at the Mahabodhi Temple complex in Bodh Gaya on Sunday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nine low intensity bombs went off within fifteen minutes early Sunday morning inside the Mahabodhi temple complex, a Unesco World Heritage site, and one of the holiest sites associated with the life of Buddha in Bodh Gaya in the northern Indian state of Bihar. India’s Home Secretary, Anil Goswami told reporters that four explosions occurred inside the temple complex, three others shook a nearby monastery and an eighth exploded near a statue of Buddha. Two other bombs were defused, Mr. Goswami added.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Blasts at India’s Buddhist Mecca in Bihar', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bihar (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'val