rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/bedcf40f-78bd-521c-b53c-a4a02b81b8c5', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bedcf40f-78bd-521c-b53c-a4a02b81b8c5'}, {'abstract': 'American Advertising Federation, Washington, elected its board for 2013-14.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-ad-industry.html', 'snippet': 'American Advertising Federation, Washington, elected its board for 2013-14.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Advertising Federation, Washington, elected its board for 2013-14. Wendy Clark, senior vice president of the Global Sparkling Brand Center at the Coca-Cola Company, becomes the new chairwoman, succeeding the immediate past chairman, John Osborn, president and chief executive at BBDO New York. Rich Stoddart, president for North America at Leo Burnett, becomes the new vice chairman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T20:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f7e006f-bd25-58a5-9433-9ce75e102177', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f7e006f-bd25-58a5-9433-9ce75e102177'}, {'abstract': 'Hannah Arendt’s dispatches from Adolf Eichmann’s trial did not portray him as a robotic bureaucrat, but as a fanatical ‘joiner’ convinced he was serving a higher good.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/misreading-hannah-arendts-eichmann-in-jerusalem/', 'snippet': 'Hannah Arendt’s dispatches from Adolf Eichmann’s trial did not portray him as a robotic bureaucrat, but as a fanatical ‘joiner’ convinced he was serving a higher good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The movie “Hannah Arendt,” which opened in New York in May, has unleashed emotional commentary that mirrors the fierce debate Arendt herself ignited over half a century ago, when she covered the trial of the notorious war criminal Adolf Eichmann. One of the pre-eminent political thinkers of the 20th century, Arendt, who died in 1975 at the age of 69, was a Jew arrested by the German police in 1933, forced into exile and later imprisoned in an internment camp. She escaped and fled to the United States in 1941, where she wrote the seminal books “The Origins of Totalitarianism” and “The Human Condition.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misreading ‘Eichmann in Jerusalem’', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARENDT, HANNAH', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eichmann, Adolf', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T21:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Berkowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55a87366-d7bc-5cb7-b696-db1c2cff742d', 'word_count': 2115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55a87366-d7bc-5cb7-b696-db1c2cff742d'}, {'abstract': 'With some standout moments, American Ballet Theater concluded its New York season with seven performances of “Sleeping Beauty.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/arts/dance/american-ballet-theater-presents-sleeping-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'With some standout moments, American Ballet Theater concluded its New York season with seven performances of “Sleeping Beauty.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because American Ballet Theater’s annual eight-week New York spring season occurs at the huge Metropolitan Opera House and presents an impressive selection of stars, this block of performances has a prestigious spot on the international dance calendar. It’s not unusual, however, for the company to squander large parts of the season on works that degrade ballet itself; and so again it proved this year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 891}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 690, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1379, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/ABT/ABT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Castle Denizens Spring to Life (Some More So)', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Castle Denizens Spring to Life (Some More So)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Sleeping Beauty (Ballet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T21:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99ee0f88-1964-5e5b-8054-286210a976a3', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99ee0f88-1964-5e5b-8054-286210a976a3'}, {'abstract': '“Drenched,” choreographed by Luke Murphy, addresses love’s many facets with movement and snippets from film and television history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/arts/dance/luke-murphy-performs-his-drenched-at-la-mama.html', 'snippet': '“Drenched,” choreographed by Luke Murphy, addresses love’s many facets with movement and snippets from film and television history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The La MaMa Moves! festival concluded over the weekend with an attempt at romance, which afforded little in the way of surprises. A man and a woman? References to romantic films? They’re both prominent parts of “Drenched,” a work choreographed by Luke Murphy that included snippets from “Gone With the Wind” and “The Bachelor.” Instead of a rose ceremony, this dance incorporated petals — red ones, of course — which fell from the ceiling like rain. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/arts/DRENCHED/DRENCHED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love Hurts, and I’ve Got the Moves and Movie Scenes to Prove It', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love Hurts, and I’ve Got the Moves and Movie Scenes to Prove It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Luke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T21:19:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfea2d9b-9c3d-5fe9-ab98-ba3fd2ca20be', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfea2d9b-9c3d-5fe9-ab98-ba3fd2ca20be'}, {'abstract': 'The Tokyo String Quartet, which is disbanding, said farewell to its longtime association with the Norfolk Chamber Music Festival with a program of Haydn, Debussy and Bartok.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/arts/music/the-tokyo-string-quartet-says-farewell-at-norfolk-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Tokyo String Quartet, which is disbanding, said farewell to its longtime association with the Norfolk Chamber Music Festival with a program of Haydn, Debussy and Bartok.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORFOLK, Conn. — Many string quartets start out as a family and then over time morph into an institution. As long-serving members retire, new players join in, subtly altering the sound and style until only the name remains unchanged. The\xa0Tokyo String Quartet\xa0decided to retire as a family rather than continue with further changes in its lineup. On Saturday\xa0evening, the quartet, which was founded in 1969, gave a passionate and emotionally charged performance here at the Norfolk Chamber Music Festival\xa0that the ensemble says will be its last.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chamber Ensemble’s Passionate Swan Song', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chamber Ensemble’s Passionate Swan Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo String Quartet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-07T21:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c2cf0b2-f8e4-5d35-9622-08c95ba6cd79', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c2cf0b2-f8e4-5d35-9622-08c95ba6cd79'}, {'abstract': 'The English composer Gustav Holst’s orchestral suite “The Planets” was wedded with imagery of the solar system at a Summertime Classics concert by the New York Philharmonic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/arts/music/new-york-philharmonics-the-planets-builds-on-holsts-work.html', 'snippet': 'The English composer Gustav Holst’s orchestral suite “The Planets” was wedded with imagery of the solar system at a Summertime Classics concert by the New York Philharmonic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outside 