1db55-1100-5ead-a07e-5938376da824'}, {'abstract': 'Yielding to pressure from New York’s attorney general, Thomson Reuters is expected to suspend the early release of a closely watched consumer confidence index, which it has delivered two seconds in advance to clients willing to pay extra.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/thomson-reuters-to-suspend-early-peeks-at-key-index/', 'snippet': 'Yielding to pressure from New York’s attorney general, Thomson Reuters is expected to suspend the early release of a closely watched consumer confidence index, which it has delivered two seconds in advance to clients willing to pay extra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last several years, an exclusive group of investors has paid a steep premium to receive the results of a closely watched economic survey a full two seconds before its broader release. Those two seconds can mean millions of dollars in profits for the investors, who practice a computer-driven strategy called high-frequency trading.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomson Reuters to Suspend Early Peeks at Key Index', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reuters To Suspend Early Peeks At Key Index', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thomson Reuters Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T01:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6507dfe-66fd-53dc-bcd7-a0f47d7abb77', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6507dfe-66fd-53dc-bcd7-a0f47d7abb77'}, {'abstract': 'Having once suppressed the idea of devotion to elderly parents, the Communist Party now orders it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/opinion/yu-when-filial-piety-is-the-law.html', 'snippet': 'Having once suppressed the idea of devotion to elderly parents, the Communist Party now orders it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s revised law on the Protection of the Rights and Interests of Elderly People took effect last Monday. A clause now stipulates: “Family members living apart from the elderly should frequently visit or send greetings to the elderly persons.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/Yu-contributor/contributors-images-slide-XXIY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/Yu-contributor/contributors-images-slide-XXIY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/Yu-contributor/contributors-images-slide-XXIY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/Yu-contributor/contributors-images-slide-XXIY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'c