riginal': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9e4a139-500a-5b46-9838-0633249c367c', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9e4a139-500a-5b46-9838-0633249c367c'}, {'abstract': 'A new study suggests that biologists don’t really know enough about the grizzly population to take the animals off the endangered list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/opinion/counting-bears.html', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that biologists don’t really know enough about the grizzly population to take the animals off the endangered list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is nothing simple about counting grizzly bears. But counting them accurately will help determine whether they remain on the endangered species list or are delisted. The Interior Department’s Fish and Wildlife Service says there are about 700 grizzlies in the greater Yellowstone ecosystem, more than the 500 it deems essential for a healthy population. But a new study in the journal Conservation Letters calls those numbers into question. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Counting Bears', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Counting Bears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T01:11:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/28a9b95b-2bc5-5983-9a8e-6b1475ddbe59', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a9b95b-2bc5-5983-9a8e-6b1475ddbe59'}, {'abstract': 'A startling jump in the number of deaths means doctors need to prescribe more cautiously and do more to educate patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/opinion/painkiller-overdoses-in-women.html', 'snippet': 'A startling jump in the number of deaths means doctors need to prescribe more cautiously and do more to educate patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every month the federal Centers for Disease Control and Prevention turns its spotlight on a public health problem that merits attention. This month the C.D.C. has focused on a problem that is rapidly getting worse: the rise of prescription painkiller overdoses, especially among women. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Painkiller Overdoses in Women', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Painkiller Overdoses in Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T01:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b900cd-4d75-5705-b828-f46c5890c499', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b900cd-4d75-5705-b828-f46c5890c499'}, {'abstract': 'A doctor who earned a Bronze Star in Afghanistan got a special exception to wear a beard and turban, and he is working to make it easier for other Sikhs to enlist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/us/taking-on-rules-so-other-sikhs-join-the-army.html', 'snippet': 'A doctor who earned a Bronze Star in Afghanistan got a special exception to wear a beard and turban, and he is working to make it easier for other Sikhs to enlist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Sikhs of northwestern India have for centuries cherished their rich military history. Wearing long beards and turbans into combat, they have battled Mughals in Punjab, Afghans near the Khyber Pass and Germans in the bloody trenches of the Somme.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/us/SIKH/SIKH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking On Rules to Ease Sikhs’ Path to the Army', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking On Rules So Other Sikhs Join the Army', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dao, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turbans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beards and Mustaches', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T01:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf3a9686-f8f6-5578-80d7-1c91c4c64ee7', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf3a9686-f8f6-5578-80d7-1c91c4c64ee7'}, {'abstract': 'Some diagnostic tests have escaped regulation to ensure that they are safe and effective.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/opinion/the-gap-in-medical-testing.html', 'snippet': 'Some diagnostic tests have escaped regulation to ensure that they are safe and effective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An alarming number of diagnostic medical tests have never been tested for safety and accuracy. That’s because the federal government has a two-tier system for regulating such tests. If a diagnostic test is made by a traditional device manufacturer, the Food and Drug Administration reviews its safety and effectiveness before approving it for marketing. However, if a test is developed by a clinical laboratory for use at its own facilities, it can be sold without a premarket review.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gap in Medical Testing', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Gap in Medical Testing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T01:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf8af8cc-ce4c-5075-b33c-687dc25dc67d', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf8af8cc-ce4c-5075-b33c-687dc25dc67d'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans hold the future of a country, and their party, in their hands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/opinion/immigration-in-the-house.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans hold the future of a country, and their party, in their hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican caucus of the United States House of Representatives is holding a private meeting on Wednesday. The subject will be immigration. Perhaps it will be a showdown or a summit that will reset the party’s direction on this issue. Maybe party leaders and moderates will push back against Tea Party no-dealers and hard-core members, like Steve King of Iowa, who want to kill any bill that allows undocumented immigrants to become Americans. Maybe Republicans will decide to accept bipartisan immigration reform as a step toward becoming a party with something to offer Latino and Asian voters besides hostility and fear. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigration in the House', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Immigration in the House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T01:13:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0a4e050-b93e-5f96-a979-d332f94cc402', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0a4e050-b93e-5f96-a979-d332f94cc402'}, {'abstract': 'Footage, shot by an amateur cameraman, corroborates eyewitness accounts of the plane’s descent and crash.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/video-of-san-francisco-air-crash-emerges/', 'snippet': 'Footage, shot by an amateur cameraman, corroborates eyewitness accounts of the plane’s descent and crash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Video broadcast Sunday showed the crash of an Asiana Airlines Boeing 777, with 307 passengers aboard, at San Francisco International