8280b2198'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (NBC) GET OUT ALIVE WITH BEAR GRYLLS In his broadcast network debut, Mr. Grylls, left, the survivalist star of Discovery’s “Man vs. Wild,” tests 10 teams of two contestants in challenges of increasing difficulty amid the dense forests, rocky summits and glacier crevasses of New Zealand’s South Island. Their mission: to withstand the wilderness, travel as a group and avoid elimination while each team is assigned a task — including taking charge of food, fire, shelter or obstacles — throughout the various legs of the journey. One team will be sent home each week. The team that Mr. Grylls says has shown the most survival spirit, resourceful skill and determination in its quest to “get out alive” will win $500,000.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/62110d7c-b783-50ee-81f2-3816298fb50d', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62110d7c-b783-50ee-81f2-3816298fb50d'}, {'abstract': 'As an antiques dealer, I am used to going through the treasures of the dead, but this time I was confronted with details that resonated with my life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/booming/traces-of-a-man-who-disappear