Al Nour, seen as a potential political kingmaker, said it was suspending its role in efforts to form an interim government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A party of ultraconservative Islamists that emerged as an unexpected political kingmaker in Egypt after the military’s ouster of President Mohamed Morsi said on Monday that it was suspending its participation in efforts to form an interim government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamist Party Backs Out of Negotiations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nour, Al-, Party (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T08:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15951369-630d-5a6e-9805-9a1140bcdcb3', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15951369-630d-5a6e-9805-9a1140bcdcb3'}, {'abstract': 'Can you calculate the number of bicycles in Amsterdam if you know the population and the bicycles-to-people ratio?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/test-yourself-math-july-8-2013/', 'snippet': 'Can you calculate the number of bicycles in Amsterdam if you know the population and the bicycles-to-people ratio?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question, created by Bobson Wong at Math for America from the article “The Dutch Prize Their Pedal Power, but a Sea of Bikes Swamps Their Capital.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, July 8, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T08:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc006826-9d5d-51ff-8639-2f2fd6fe4ef3', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc006826-9d5d-51ff-8639-2f2fd6fe4ef3'}, {'abstract': 'Arjun Abrol’s “fair price” shop is one of about 2500 stores in Delhi that sell subsidized grain to the poor under government’s public distribution program.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/a-grocer-to-delhis-poor/', 'snippet': 'Arjun Abrol’s “fair price” shop is one of about 2500 stores in Delhi that sell subsidized grain to the poor under government’s public distribution program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India runs one of the world’s largest subsidized food distribution programs, covering 330 million people, including 65.2 million families, with an annual household income below 24,200 rupees, or $405—the official poverty line.\xa0With a government-issued ration card, families below the poverty line are entitled to buy 35 kilograms of grain a month, including wheat and rice. Some Indian states also offer kerosene and small quantities of sugar at subsidized prices. Around 500,000 “fair price” stores participate in the program known as India’s Public Distribution System. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/world/asia/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk/08-rice-warehouse-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grocer to Delhi’s Poor', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'majo