tions', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Asset Management', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efea0e85-fc76-544e-b2c2-c39400c73e5d', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efea0e85-fc76-544e-b2c2-c39400c73e5d'}, {'abstract': 'Your smartphone can be an important tool in an emergency. Here are apps that can help.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/app-smart-extra-emergency/', 'snippet': 'Your smartphone can be an important tool in an emergency. Here are apps that can help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week my App Smart column was about apps that can help you prepare for and deal with all sorts of different emergency situations. Since they’re portable and we tend to take them almost everywhere with us, smartphones can be an incredibly useful emergency tool because even if you’re not using them to call for help, they can carry apps packed with useful data.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: Emergency!', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9854e512-ed37-5c00-a939-57ef9e533884', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9854e512-ed37-5c00-a939-57ef9e533884'}, {'abstract': 'Asiana Flight 214, which crashed at San Francisco International Airport on Saturday, was “a training flight” for the pilot, the airline’s president said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/world/asia/asiana-airlines-san-francisco-plane-crash.html', 'snippet': 'Asiana Flight 214, which crashed at San Francisco International Airport on Saturday, was “a training flight” for the pilot, the airline’s president said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — It was Lee Kang-guk’s first attempt to land a Boeing 777 at San Francisco International Airport, and it ended in disaster. The crash of Asiana Airlines Flight 214 on Saturday killed two passengers, injured 180 others and tarnished the reputation of South Korea’s aviation industry, whose leaders had thought it was leaving a poor safety record behind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asiana President Says Pilot Was in Training', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asiana Airlines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:24:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2993d049-4918-5dfc-95fe-932202d0bac7', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2993d049-4918-5dfc-95fe-932202d0bac7'}, {'abstract': 'Russia has changed significantly in the past year and a half. The Kremlin’s position has become socially conservative, xenophobic and intolerant of any difference, political or otherwise.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/no-good-news-from-russia/', 'snippet': 'Russia has changed significantly in the past year and a half. The Kremlin’s position has become socially conservative, xenophobic and intolerant of any difference, political or otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW\xa0 — “So tell me some good news,” Nadya kept demanding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Good News From Russia', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolokonnikova, Nadezhda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df7b76ea-d57f-5d4f-ac5b-10947c383504', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df7b76ea-d57f-5d4f-ac5b-10947c383504'}, {'abstract': 'Even though polls have shown little desire among voters for Eliot Spitzer to return to public office, he is ready to ask for forgiveness and to make the case why he is again qualified to serve.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/spitzer-believes-voters-might-give-him-second-chance/', 'snippet': 'Even though polls have shown little desire among voters for Eliot Spitzer to return to public office, he is ready to ask for forgiveness and to make the case why he is again qualified to serve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even by the forgiving standards of New York City politics, it sounds improbable: a governor felled by a prostitution scandal entering a race for citywide office with just four days left until qualifying petitions are due.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spitzer Opens Up About His Decision to Return to Politics', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spitzer, Eliot L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9da601e-c0b9-5962-8375-950497bdade8', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9da601e-c0b9-5962-8375-950497bdade8'}, {'abstract': 'After a week of tense negotiations, Greece and its foreign lenders agreed on a new round of austerity measures that must be taken by the country to unlock the crucial rescue funds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/business/global/greece-and-lenders-near-deal-on-new-austerity-measures.html', 'snippet': 'After a week of tense negotiations, Greece and its foreign lenders agreed on a new round of austerity measures that must be taken by the country to unlock the crucial rescue funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Euro zone finance ministers meeting in Brussels decided Monday to continue drip-feeding payments of emergency aid to Greece, pressuring Athens to keep its promises to restructure the economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/business/09greece-web1/09greece-web1-thumbLarge.