ook.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/chinese-insurer-buys-lloyds-building-in-london/', 'snippet': 'The $388 million purchase is indicative of the growing appetite by Chinese buyers of commercial and residential real estate abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The Ping An Insurance Group of China agreed on Monday to buy the headquarters building of the insurance giant Lloyd’s of London, a landmark in the city’s financial district, for about $388 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Insurer Buys Lloyd’s Building in London', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b6b5c95-c159-54e4-b940-3a9b2f20c660', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b6b5c95-c159-54e4-b940-3a9b2f20c660'}, {'abstract': 'Institutional Shareholder Services recommends that Dell investors accept a buyout offer. | The government has a range of possible avenues in the SAC Capital Advisors insider trading investigation. | Thomson Reuters is suspending the practice of providing select clients with an early look at an index. | The future of mostly automated cars looks attractive to a group of investors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/a-vote-of-confidence-for-dell-buyout/', 'snippet': 'Institutional Shareholder Services recommends that Dell investors accept a buyout offer. | The government has a range of possible avenues in the SAC Capital Advisors insider trading investigation. | Thomson Reuters is suspending the practice of pr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The influential proxy advisory firm Institutional Shareholder Services recommended on Monday that Dell Inc. investors accept Michael S. Dell’s $24.4 billion leveraged buyout offer. The recommendation is something of a surprise. Advisers to both the buyers and to a special committee of Dell’s board had expected the report would likely be unfavorable to the deal, DealBook writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vote of Confidence for Dell Buyout', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T11:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d70ad47-0e22-57a1-9138-262a55c1fe71', 'word_count': 1880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d70ad47-0e22-57a1-9138-262a55c1fe71'}, {'abstract': 'Beware the fees on Europe’s budget airlines, how to make a perfect summer feast, skin cancer is on the rise in young women and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/monday-reading-beware-fees-on-europes-budget-airlines/', 'snippet': 'Beware the fees on Europe’s budget airlines, how to make a perfect summer feast, skin cancer is on the rise in young women and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Beware Fees on Europe’s Budget Airlines', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T13:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cabd859e-63ed-542e-9ae4-0741cfe35de6', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cabd859e-63ed-542e-9ae4-0741cfe35de6'}, {'abstract': 'Where the economy is headed in seven charts. Hiring beats the forecasts. A start-up has 30 days to live. Can you explain what a Bitcoin is?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/this-week-in-small-business-the-employer-mandate/', 'snippet': 'Where the economy is headed in seven charts. Hiring beats the forecasts. A start-up has 30 days to live. Can you explain what a Bitcoin is?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week In Small Business: The Employer Mandate', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T13:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08764507-7947-54f9-97c4-4582dadfee8c', 'word_count': 1389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08764507-7947-54f9-97c4-4582dadfee8c'}, {'abstract': 'In your heart you know she isn’t Dwight.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/not-like-ike/', 'snippet': 'In your heart you know she isn’t Dwight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Warsh has a meditation on the possibilities of a Hillary Clinton presidency, suggesting that she might be — of all things — the next Dwight Eisenhower. That’s an interesting thought, although I believe it’s quite wrong. But the good thing about Warsh’s suggestion is that it forces me to ask why, exactly, I think it’s so wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Like Ike', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T13:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b107d967-319c-521d-97a8-5eb4cdf0c21e', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b107d967-319c-521d-97a8-5eb4cdf0c21e'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray’s Wimbledon title on Sunday was portrayed in the news media as a victory over doubt and public negativity, one made more appealing by past defeats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/sports/murray-sheds-britains-burden-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray’s Wimbledon title on Sunday was portrayed in the news media as a victory over doubt and public negativity, one made more appealing by past defeats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This was a victory borne in tears, those Andy Murray shed a year ago into the same blades of grass. You could not even begin to comprehend how Murray finally won Wimbledon on Sunday, how he finally bore the pressure of a faded tennis empire, an entire country hoping for him to win but expecting him to fail, without those tears. It was that day in 2012 when Murray let the world see how much he cared, how much of his heart was invested in winning this. It was as if he shared his burden with the rest of us and somehow that made it lighter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murray Sheds Britain’s Burden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durant, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Dwight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T13:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c283e40d-6674-543a-b307-c0e80af73e46', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c283e40d-6674-543a-b307-c0e80af73e46'}, {'abstract': 'Hawks, but only when a Dem is in power.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/political-inflationistas/', 'snippet': 'Hawks, but only when a Dem is in power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing the ongoing attempt to characterize the economists and economist wannabes who keep warning about inflation from the Fed’s efforts to do something about a weak economy, Noah Smith suggests that none of the inflationistas really believe what they’re saying. Instead, he writes, they’re either trying to defend economic models that defined their careers, but failed; lashing out because they personally have been made to look like fools; or playing to a lucrative audience of grumpy old rich white men, who are natural goldbugs:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Inflationistas', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T13:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0f7116e-39eb-5d1b-aee7-5675c19b79f5', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0f7116e-39eb-5d1b-aee7-5675c19b79f5'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens were killed in Cairo after Egyptian soldiers opened fire on supporters of ousted President Mohamed Morsi on Monday, outside the facility where he was believed to be detained.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000002325343/raw-footage-aftermath-of-cairo-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens were killed in Cairo after Egyptian soldiers opened fire on supporters of ousted President Mohamed Morsi on Monday, outside the facility where he was believed to be detained.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dozens were killed in Cairo after Egyptian soldiers opened fire on supporters of ousted President Mohamed Morsi on Monday, outside the facility where he was believed to be detained.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/08/multimedia/video-tc-130708-cairo-shooting/video-tc-130708-cairo