': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3581c198-0a1b-5cdd-bf69-6cce2ae5d597', 'word_count': 1811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3581c198-0a1b-5cdd-bf69-6cce2ae5d597'}, {'abstract': 'Did Grant win the siege, or did Pemberton lose it?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/rashomon-at-vicksburg/', 'snippet': 'Did Grant win the siege, or did Pemberton lose it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall of Vicksburg, Miss., on July 4 sent a shock wave through both North and South – it split the Confederacy in two and gave the Union nearly unfettered control of the Mississippi River. Less clear was what brought about the surrender. Indeed, the principal players in the surrender drama — John C. Pemberton for the South and Ulysses S. Grant for the North — insisted on very different accounts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rashomon at Vicksburg', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vicksburg (Miss)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T16:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Bassett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bassett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4af49ed0-60a4-5ebe-9129-ff4dbd6699f0', 'word_count': 1520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4af49ed0-60a4-5ebe-9129-ff4dbd6699f0'}, {'abstract': 'George Lucas, Herb Alpert, Allen Toussaint, Renée Fleming and Tony Kushner are among this year’s recipients of the National Medal of Arts. National Humanities Medals will go to Marilynne Robinson, Kay Ryan, Anna Deavere Smith and Joan Didion, among others.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/obama-to-present-arts-and-humanities-medals-on-wednesday/', 'snippet': 'George Lucas, Herb Alpert, Allen Toussaint, Renée Fleming and Tony Kushner are among this year’s recipients of the National Medal of Arts. National Humanities Medals will go to Marilynne Robinson, Kay Ryan, Anna Deavere Smith and Joan Didion, amon...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may not lead to the creation of a science-fiction saga with a great jazz and R&B score, or an operatic aria about the life of America’s 16th president, but George Lucas, Herb Alpert, Allen Toussaint, Renée Fleming and Tony Kushner will be among the artistic dignitaries invited to gather on Wednesday at the White House to receive the National Medal of Arts, it was announced on Monday. The award,\xa0 managed by the National Endowment for the Arts, is regarded as the nation’s highest honor for artistic excellence, and its winners are selected annually “based on their contributions to the creation, growth, and support of the arts in the United States,” the organization said in a news release.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Present Arts and Humanities Medals on Wednesday', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALPERT, HERB', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deavere Smith, Anna', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Didion, Joan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Renee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Ellsworth', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kushner, Tony', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, George', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Elaine', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Marilynne', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Kay', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toussaint, Allen', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Humanities', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T16:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5208bac3-4c34-556b-b237-01c7aef7a2e0', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5208bac3-4c34-556b-b237-01c7aef7a2e0'}, {'abstract': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/weekend-gun-report-july-4th-edition/', 'snippet': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a holiday weekend, which, as we’ve sadly learned in the months since we began the Gun Report, means an even more gruesome list of gun deaths and injuries than usual. Here is the one we want to highlight, however: On the evening of July 4, in Midlothian, Va., Brendon Mackey was walking with his father in the parking lot of a local restaurant where they had gone to see the fireworks. He suddenly fell to the ground. Nobody understood why at first; even after they saw blood, they thought he must have hit his head from the fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Gun Report: July 4th Edition', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T16:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa1353a-7d3d-5b19-bbee-1d439a2cf408', 'word_count': 4485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa1353a-7d3d-5b19-bbee-1d439a2cf408'}, {'abstract': 'Two ultra-Orthodox men were arrested on suspicion of throwing objects at the women in an activist group, in the latest clash at one of Judaism’s holiest sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/world/middleeast/new-prayer-confrontation-at-western-wall.html', 'snippet': 'Two ultra-Orthodox men were arrested on suspicion of throwing objects at the women in an activist group, in the latest clash at one of Judaism’s holiest sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Thousands of ultra-Orthodox teenage girls and adults flooded the Western Wall early Monday, forcing a group of activist women to hold their monthly service farther from the wall than usual. It was the latest chapter of a bitter struggle over the nature of public prayer at one of Judaism’s holiest sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/09israel_inline/09israel_inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/09/world/09israel_inline/09israel_inline-articl