r': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T16:34:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab1fe98d-224e-5270-9ddf-f25f526d20f3', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab1fe98d-224e-5270-9ddf-f25f526d20f3'}, {'abstract': 'Victoire de Castellane has whipped up a lovely, delicate collection of new designs for Dior that puts attention on brilliant colors', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/victoire-de-castellane-designs-jewelry-for-dior/', 'snippet': 'Victoire de Castellane has whipped up a lovely, delicate collection of new designs for Dior that puts attention on brilliant colors', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a fashion sensibility changes, so do the jewels. Victoire de Castellane has whipped up a lovely, delicate collection of new designs for Dior that puts attention on brilliant colors. In the past, her calling card was the crazy and sensational, as befitting the decade of John Galliano. But now, closer to the spirit of Raf Simons, her work emphasizes different values. The jewels in her Cher Dior collection seem drenched in pure color: pink, yellow, blue and purple sapphires, rubies, diamonds, garnets and Paraiba tourmalines. “There is certainly a red for everyone,” Christian Dior wrote in his “Little Dictionary of Fashion.” In stones, Ms. de Castellane makes that abundantly clear. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Dior Jewels from Victoire de Castellane', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dior, Christian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T16:38:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f1ae33-c23b-549a-a03d-dcd503415716', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f1ae33-c23b-549a-a03d-dcd503415716'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray unsuccessfully tried to convert three match points in a row, then saved three break points before nailing the Wimbledon victory he coveted on his fourth attempt.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/title-matchs-final-points-leave-murray-sapped/', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray unsuccessfully tried to convert three match points in a row, then saved three break points before nailing the Wimbledon victory he coveted on his fourth attempt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Murray had to endure an 11 1/2-minute nightmare before realizing the greatest dream of his life at Wimbledon on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Title Match’s Final Points Leave Murray Sapped', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T16:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'pers