name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donnelly, Brian', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seibert, Fred', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays Center (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T17:21:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/706f0110-f3a4-5ac7-94bc-8ff6bab9e958', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/706f0110-f3a4-5ac7-94bc-8ff6bab9e958'}, {'abstract': 'Our chief national correspondent discusses what he learned from being “on the other side” of a reporter’s notebook and whether he felt guilty about his involvement in the firing of Kurt Bardella, former press secretary to Representative Darrell Issa.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/behind-the-cover-story-mark-leibovich-on-being-part-of-a-washington-scandal/', 'snippet': 'Our chief national correspondent discusses what he learned from being “on the other side” of a reporter’s notebook and whether he felt guilty about his involvement in the firing of Kurt Bardella, former press secretary to Representative Darrell Is...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Leibovich, chief national correspondent for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story about Kurt Bardella, who was fired as Representative Darrell Issa’s press secretary after sharing work e-mails with Leibovich. (Bardella has since returned as an adviser to Issa.) Leibovich’s new book, “This Town: Two Parties and a Funeral — Plus, Plenty of Valet Parking! — in America’s Gilded Capital,” comes out next week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/19/magazine/19-mark-leibovich/19-mark-leibovich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/19/magazine/19-mark-leibovich/19-mark-leibovich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/19/magazine/19-mark-leibovich/19-mark-leibovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/19/magazine/19-mark-leibovich/19-mark-leibovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/19/magazine/19-mark-leibovich/19-mark-leibovich-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Mark Leibovich on Being Part of a Washington ‘Scandal’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bardella, Kurt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T17:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c103dab-7b89-5e2e-8e29-7bd1fabf9ddd', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c103dab-7b89-5e2e-8e29-7bd1fabf9ddd'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, it can be done.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/safer-sweatshops/', 'snippet': 'Yes, it can be done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A long, long, long time ago I used to believe that the central political and economic debate facing our nation was going to be about globalization — not realizing that it would instead revolve around a powerful movement to roll back the clock here at home, and bring back the Gilded Age. (As I once said, I think to Robert Kuttner, while he and I were arguing about tariffs, Sauron was gathering his forces at Mordor). Anyway, back then, as a columnist for Slate, I wrote a piece arguing that low wages and poor working conditions by Western standards were necessary and inevitable in poor countries — provoking the predictable outrage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safer Sweatshops', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T17:32:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa277363-72e9-5484-a130-a7cbdda1be8c', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa277363-72e9-5484-a130-a7cbdda1be8c'}, {'abstract': 'The tennis star and his girlfriend wore head-to-toe Burberry at the Champion’s Dinner last night.', 'web_url': 'https://tmaga