f Song to Honor Ned Rorem', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rorem, Ned', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Festival of Song', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T17:33:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91748e3b-1739-54cc-aab3-c399aa7c936d', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91748e3b-1739-54cc-aab3-c399aa7c936d'}, {'abstract': 'Auto racing is often derided as a nonsport, but new physiological research shows that driving stock cars is tough on the human body.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/research-shows-the-physiological-stresses-of-stock-car-racing/', 'snippet': 'Auto racing is often derided as a nonsport, but new physiological research shows that driving stock cars is tough on the human body.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIDDEFORD, Maine — For anyone who does not think that the Nascar drivers sweltering inside their cars at Daytona over the weekend were participating in a real sport, there’s new research that supports racing’s athletic cred.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/Oxford-Nascar-Research-AHRENS-1/Oxford-Nascar-Research-AHRENS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/Oxford-Nascar-Research-AHRENS-1/Oxford-Nascar-Rese