 press for the prompt restoration of a democratic government and to head off further violence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Administration Rules Out Suspension of Aid to Egypt in Near Term', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T19:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7cf1580-7b65-512b-b6c7-8ab4156f5540', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7cf1580-7b65-512b-b6c7-8ab4156f5540'}, {'abstract': 'Widespread coal use in the north has led in recent decades to an average decrease in life span of more than five years, research indicates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/world/asia/pollution-leads-to-drop-in-life-span-in-northern-china-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Widespread coal use in the north has led in recent decades to an average decrease in life span of more than five years, research indicates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Southern Chinese on average have lived at least five years longer than their northern counterparts in recent decades because of the destructive health effects of pollution from the widespread use of coal in the north, according to a study released Monday by a prominent American science journal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge