, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48117546-ae05-5377-bfe1-adf3530e9342', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48117546-ae05-5377-bfe1-adf3530e9342'}, {'abstract': 'When I want to get out of the office, I go to Ladakh, India.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/my-monthly-trip-to-ladakh/', 'snippet': 'When I want to get out of the office, I go to Ladakh, India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever I’m feeling too rooted, which is most of the time, the only antidote usually at hand is clicking on a video posted on Vimeo: “Trip to Ladakh, India 2009.” It’s not my trip. I don’t know the people in the video, who, I think, are a group of seven friends from Singapore. I probably watch it once a month, and it always has the odd effect of making me tear up. Maybe there’s a name for that feeling. Projected nostalgia? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydog