yt://article/6ef3f23d-0187-5c73-a3fc-fde26af324ce'}, {'abstract': 'Todd Park, a former Silicon Valley entrepreneur, spoke to John Harwood about how the government is using data and the “lean start-up” model.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/10-questions-for-obamas-chief-technology-officer/', 'snippet': 'Todd Park, a former Silicon Valley entrepreneur, spoke to John Harwood about how the government is using data and the “lean start-up” model.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Todd Park, a former Silicon Valley entrepreneur, serves as President Obama’s chief technology officer. His role has taken on heightened importance after several recent developments, including the implementation of the new health care law, efforts to reduce the backlog in Department of Veterans Affairs claims processing, and privacy issues raised by disclosures about data collection by the National Security Agency. Mr. Park spoke with John Harwood of The Times and CNBC at the White House as Mr. Obama publicly challenged his administration to improve the government’s innovation and efficiency in his second term.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '10 Questions for Obama’s Chief Technology Officer', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T21:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organi