h in Soldotna, Alaska, with much less reaction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than 24 hours after a plane crash at San Francisco International Airport killed two people and injured 180 others, 10 people died in a plane crash in Soldotna, Alaska. But while the accident in hyperconnected San Francisco instantly drew global attention through social media postings, video from dedicated plane-spotters and extensive news coverage, the crash in a town on Alaska’s Kenai peninsula has barely bubbled into national consciousness hours after it occurred.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plane Crash in Alaska Kills 10, but Draws Scant Attention', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T22:19:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Roston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c6a83b9-263d-5352-a305-f54bbda70bb2', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c6a83b9-263d-5352-a305-f54bbda70bb2'}, {'abstract': 'In a sharp escalation of tensions Monday, Egyptian soldiers opened fire on hundreds of supporters of Mohamed Morsi, the ousted president.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/07/09/world/middleeast/20130709-EGYPT.html', 'snippet': 'In a sharp escalation of tensions Monday, Egyptian soldiers opened fire on hundreds of supporters of Mohamed Morsi, the ousted president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a sharp escalation of tensions Monday, Egyptian soldiers opened fire on hundreds of supporters of Mohamed Morsi, the ousted president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i