//thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/projections-show-u-s-budget-deficit-will-shrink/', 'snippet': 'The deficit will fall to $759 billion for the fiscal year that ends this September, a $214 billion improvement from the projection made in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The federal budget deficit will fall to $759 billion for the fiscal year that ends this September, a $214 billion improvement from the projection made in March, as spending cuts, tax increases and an improving economy begin to tame the government’s red ink, the White House budget office said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Projections Show U.S. Budget Deficit Will Shrink', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T22:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03741321-2a1d-5e86-b5f9-e71b6784b001', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03741321-2a1d-5e86-b5f9-e71b6784b001'}, {'abstract': 'Erasmo Ponce’s sentencing to 90 days in jail was a sobering change of fortune for a man who was once considered a success story among Mexican immigrants in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/nyregion/tortilla-factory-owner-gets-jail-time-for-violating-payroll-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Erasmo Ponce’s sentencing to 90 days in jail was a sobering change of fortune for a man who was once considered a success story among Mexican immigrants in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The owner of a Brooklyn tortilla factory where a worker died in 2011 after falling into a mixing machine was sentenced on Monday to 90 days in jail, after pleading guilty to labor law violations for failing to pay his workers adequate wages, the New York State attorney general’s office said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tortilla Factory Owner Gets Jail Time for Violating Payroll Laws', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponce, Erasmo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tortilleria Chinantla', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baten, Juan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Workers' Compensation Insurance", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T22:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. C. Gogolak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gogolak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e9f6234-cd1c-5e4a-ab81-2f5769c781af', 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e9f6234-cd1c-5e4a-ab81-2f5769c781af'}, {'abstract': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/triple-play-week-14-results/', 'snippet': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The crack baseball committee of the Bats blog had a heated debate over the correct answer to Question No. 1 but eventually agreed that Austin Jackson’s seven runs scored, .313 average and four runs batted in trumped Chris Carter’s two homers and six R.B.I. Carter’s .222 average did him in. (O.K., it wasn’t very heated, but there was debate.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triple Play: Week 14 Results', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-08T22:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d5e1b3d-17ca-5252-8c14-63bfd574f3f4', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d5e1b3d-17ca-5252-8c14-63bfd574f3f4'}, {'abstract': 'Manager Joe Girardi said that Curtis Granderson’s broken pinkie was “not healing as quickly as” Girardi would like.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/08/granderson-still-a-few-weeks-at-least-from-return/', 'snippet': 'Manager Joe Girardi said that Curtis Granderson’s broken pinkie was “not healing as quickly as” Girardi would like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Derek Jeter and Alex Rodriguez seem to make steady progress in their rehabilitation in the Yankees’ farm system, another of the club’s missing mainstays remains at least a few weeks away from any thought of returning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Granderson Still a Few Weeks, at Least, From Return', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, David L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Luis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granderson, Curtis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'per