ead_paragraph': 'Next Monday, in a courtroom in downtown Manhattan, the Securities and Exchange Commission will begin what is likely to be its most prominent case stemming from the financial crisis: its case against Fabrice Tourre, a former Goldman Sachs trader who is accused of misleading clients by selling a mortgage securities investment that the government said was designed to fail.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trader’s Day in Court May Lack Some Details', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trader’s Day In Court May Lack Some Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Laura', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACA  Financial Guaranty Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T00:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c89019-73bd-5560-8362-2f8bf40d2b77', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c89019-73bd-5560-8362-2f8bf40d2b77'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Weeks, a government witness, gave testimony in the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, recounting how Mr. Bulger killed two men in South Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/us/former-protege-of-bulger-recounts-1982-double-murder-and-its-code-words.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Weeks, a government witness, gave testimony in the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, recounting how Mr. Bulger killed two men in South Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Brian Halloran had a head so big he was known as Balloonhead to South Boston hoodlums like Kevin Weeks. So when Mr. Halloran got up to leave a restaurant one day in 1982 — and the alleged crime boss James (Whitey) Bulger sat in a souped-up 1975 Chevy Malibu outside waiting to kill him — Mr. Weeks and Mr. Bulger had a code.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/us/BULGER/BULGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/09/us/BULGER/BULGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/us/BULGER/BULGER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/us/BULGER/BULGER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1097, 'width': 1646, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/us/BULGER/BULGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/09/us/BULGER/BULGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'