itorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffdf6ff-692a-5fc8-9b20-8b5b7a4bac7f', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffdf6ff-692a-5fc8-9b20-8b5b7a4bac7f'}, {'abstract': 'Eliot Spitzer’s bid to run for New York City comptroller is unnerving on many levels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/opinion/spitzer-redux.html', 'snippet': 'Eliot Spitzer’s bid to run for New York City comptroller is unnerving on many levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There will always be candidates for public office who are ethically compromised, temperamentally unsuitable and politically incompetent, but if they insist on running anyway, who has the right to tell them not to? Campaigns sort out the good public servants from the bad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spitzer Redux', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spitzer Redux', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spitzer, Eliot L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Comptrollers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T01:31:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a94fafcb-aecb-5716-9ed0-a29ca602984d', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a94fafcb-aecb-5716-9ed0-a29ca602984d'}, {'abstract': 'The suit, brought by 19 former students at Yeshiva University High School for Boys, in Manhattan, names Rabbi George Finkelstei