were trapped on the upper level of a double-decker commuter train for about four hours before the Toronto police marine unit arrived in boats. Motorists fled from cars that had become inundated on expressways. More rain was expected through the night, and there were fears that the banks of at least one river in the city might collapse. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Storm Floods Toronto', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | the Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Storm Floods Toronto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T02:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/48eceedb-23d9-5ce8-a2e4-14fdb761ef39', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48eceedb-23d9-5ce8-a2e4-14fdb761ef39'}, {'abstract': 'Senate Democrats plan to force confirmation votes on appointments by President Obama, and to threaten rules changes to thwart Republican tactics like the filibuster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/us/politics/democrats-plan-challenge-to-gops-filibuster-use.html', 'snippet': 