188-a574-44cc52446a7a', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7569cd03-d48b-5188-a574-44cc52446a7a'}, {'abstract': 'Winning House candidates spent an average of $1.6 million in 2012, two times what it cost in 1986, according to newly released data.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/how-much-does-a-house-seat-cost/', 'snippet': 'Winning House candidates spent an average of $1.6 million in 2012, two times what it cost in 1986, according to newly released data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Winning a House seat in 2012 cost the victor on average twice as much as it did a quarter-century ago: about $1.6 million, compared with about $753,000 in 1986.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Much Does a House Seat Cost?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Enterprise Institute for Public Policy Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T10:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad44afb7-1a32-5c41-ae9c-7457944a686b', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad44afb7-1a32-5c41-ae9c-7457944a686b'}, {'abstract': 'In an effort to avoid the huge storage tank that natural gas-powered cars usually use, a company turned to an unusual approach: burning gasoline and natural gas together.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/carlab-mixes-natural-gas-and-gasoline-for-more-efficient-vehicle/', 'snippet': 'In an effort to avoid the huge storage tank that natural gas-powered cars usually use, a company turned to an unusual approach: burning gasoline and natural gas together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When engineers convert gasoline cars to run on natural gas as well, they typically install a large pressurized tank and figure that the driver will go 100 miles or more, use up the gas and then switch back to gasoline. But for cars in the United States, the idea hasn’t caught on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/carlab-2/carlab-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/carlab-2/carlab-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/carlab-2/carlab-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 950, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/carlab-2/carlab-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 950, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/carlab-2/carlab-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/05/automobiles/wheels/carlab-2/carlab-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio