ain were each trying to improve themselves, through vastly different books.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Couple, Getting Better', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carew, Rod', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T13:19:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Sanchez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanchez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c96f0d17-f804-5536-bb70-3adde9a7323f', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96f0d17-f804-5536-bb70-3adde9a7323f'}, {'abstract': 'In Japan, prospective adoptive parents need their family’s permission to adopt — and my father-in-law did not want to give his.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/in-japan-seeking-a-father-in-laws-permission-to-adopt/', 'snippet': 'In Japan, prospective adoptive parents need their family’s permission to adopt — and my father-in-law did not want to give his.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asking your partner’s parents for his hand in marriage is rare these days, but getting permission from your in-laws to have a child is unheard of. Yet that’s exactly what I did in Japan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Japan, Seeking a Father-in-Law’s Permission to Adopt', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T13:28:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leza Lowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leza', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50e5ffb4-0252-5607-858f-16bc4c0a408a', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50e5ffb4-0252-5607-858f-16bc4c0a408a'}, {'abstract': 'They’re spending more than $1 million to (yet again) discredit President Obama’s health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/the-koch-brothers-advertising-campaign/', 'snippet': 'They’re spending more than $1 million to (yet again) discredit President Obama’s health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David and Charles Koch, the immensely rich industrialists, presumably have health insurance, though they don’t really need it. More than 25 million Americans don’t have it and really do need it, however, and the Koch brothers are working hard to make sure the government doesn’t give it to them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Koch Brothers’ Advertising Campaign', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Charles G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 4,