ry-entertainment-said-to-be-near-deal-to-move-to-universal.html', 'snippet': 'If the deal happens, the fast-growing movie financing and production company behind “Man of Steel” and “The Hangover” franchise would leave Warner Brothers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Legendary Entertainment, the fast-growing movie financing and production company involved in hits like “Man of Steel” and “The Hangover” franchise, is nearing a deal with Comcast that would move its operations to Universal from Warner Brothers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Legendary Entertainment Said to Be Near Deal to Move to Universal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legendary Entertainment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tull, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinov, Jeff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T14:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba72bbac-20f8-55f9-9879-0bf987a96297', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba72bbac-20f8-55f9-9879-0bf987a96297'}, {'abstract': 'The candidates’ daily campaign schedule at a glance.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/july-9-where-the-candidates-are-today/', 'snippet': 'The candidates’ daily campaign schedule at a glance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Planned events for the mayoral candidates, according to the campaigns and organizations they are affiliated with. Times are listed as scheduled but frequently change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July 9: Where the Candidates Are Today', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T14:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Leigh Cowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bced6b3-5460-5bdb-99ed-3baedaed6a6e', 'word_count': 1703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bced6b3-5460-5bdb-99ed-3baedaed6a6e'}, {'abstract': 'In a video edition of Leading Off, Jets Coach Rex Ryan visits Pamplona; a Browns fan has the final word; and the Yankees have an on-again, off-again relationship with their tarp.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/sports/rex-ryan-climbs-with-the-bulls.html', 'snippet': 'In a video edition of Leading Off, Jets Coach Rex Ryan visits Pamplona; a Browns fan has the final word; and the Yankees have an on-again, off-again relationship with their tarp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sports news has officially taken a turn for the absurd. Not that this is a bad thing, mind you, particularly in the N.F.L., where it desperately needed a turn from the Aaron Hernandez murder charges. Even baseball could use a little silliness this time of year, just to get you through the All-Star Game break without resorting to checking Alex Rodriguez’s Twitter feed for entertainment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rex Ryan Climbs With the Bulls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kraft, Robert K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valverde, Jose', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Robert III', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Urban', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T14:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff7f8560-8c4a-5783-803d-1bbfb2918112', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff7f8560-8c4a-5783-803d-1bbfb2918112'}, {'abstract': 'How new communication technology actually made Southern news reporting worse during the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/lies-damned-lies-and-the-telegraph/', 'snippet': 'How new communication technology actually made Southern news reporting worse during the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first few days of July 1863 were a time of unmatched excitement for Richmond journalists. In the east, the Army of Northern Virginia invaded Pennsylvania and fought a mammoth battle near the town of Gettysburg; in the west, the long, tense siege of Vicksburg had finally ended with a head-on confrontation between Union and Confederate armies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lies, Damned Lies and the Telegraph', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Richmond (Va)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T15:22:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yael A. Sternhell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yael', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Sternhell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de9dea65-3014-5c18-8473-6c2966397b9b', 'word_count': 1610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de9dea65-3014-5c18-8473-6c2966397b9b'}, {'abstract': 'The six-count indictment accuses a Bonanno soldier and an associate of assisting in the 2010 election of another crime family associate as the president of a Teamsters union on Long Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/nyregion/new-charges-against-bonanno-family-suggest-it-controlled-a-union.html', 'snippet': 'The six-count indictment accuses a Bonanno soldier and an associate of assisting in the 2010 election of another crime family associate as the president of a Teamsters union on Long Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An organized crime indictment unsealed in Manhattan on Tuesday had its share of well-worn mob enterprises: extortion, loan-sharking and union control, to name a few. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/nyregion/y-mob1/y-mob1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width