aeli soldier doesn’t get the recognition he deserves because he wasn’t Jewish enough by Orthodox standards.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/the-ultimate-conversion/', 'snippet': 'A fallen Israeli soldier doesn’t get the recognition he deserves because he wasn’t Jewish enough by Orthodox standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNT HERZL, Israel — Private Evgeny Tuluzko is buried in the military graveyard on Mount Herzl, area A, plot 23, row 1, grave 2. He died in February during basic training, and when Israel celebrated its Memorial Day, on April 9, he was the latest of its soldiers to have fallen. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ultimate Conversion', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorial Day', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gantz, Benny', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T16:25:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c7537d6-0451-5659-8b2c-70da9eefdf52', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c7537d6-0451-5659-8b2c-70da9eefdf52'}, {'abstract': 'To celebrate the launch of its updated version of a classic moccasin, the womenswear designer Wren commissioned a video from the indie band Guards, on view exclusively at T.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/perfect-pairing-wren-pays-tribute-to-the-iconic-minnetonka-moccasin/', 'snippet': 'To celebrate the launch of its updated version of a classic moccasin, the womenswear designer Wren commissioned a video from the indie band Guards, on view exclusively at T.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If I think about Coachella, I think about people wearing Minnetonkas,” said Melissa Coker, the designer behind Wren, the Los Angeles-based line of feminine, festival-chic womenswear. Coker, who has previously partnered with brands like Claire Vivier and The Lake & Stars, recently unveiled a collaboration with the Minnesota-based moccasin brand — in which she riffs on the company’s classic thunderbird style, reimagining the iconic beaded toe detail in a range of solid metallics. To celebrate the collaboration, she also tapped the director Maximilla Lukacs to film the Brooklyn indie band Guards performing an acoustic rendition of their song “Not Supposed To” while traipsing around the sort of sun-dappled field that mocs are made for. “Their style is very vintage inspired,” Coker said of the band, which happened to play the Coachella festival in April. “I think of them as sort of sixties Americana, free spirit vibe. It just seemed perfect.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wren Pays Tribute to the Iconic Minnetonka Moccasin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T16:32:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Felsenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felsenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dce359dd-9890-5b3a-82e2-225431ad74b4', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dce359dd-9890-5b3a-82e2-225431ad74b4'}, {'abstract': 'A list of wines to take to your summer rental.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/wines-for-savory-pungent-sausages/', 'snippet': 'A list of wines to take to your summer rental.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What wine goes with sausages? What wine doesn’t? Savory, pungent sausages seem to bond instantly with countless wines. Simply look for ones that are as elemental, casual and juicy as the sausages themselves. With Italian sausages, you’ll most likely want a red, and for warm-weather grilling it ought to enjoy a light chill. Translation: avoid tannins and oaky flavors. What does that leave? Only much of the low-priced red wine universe. Allow me to make a list, beginning in Italy: barbera, dolcetto, Valpolicella, Chianti, Montepulciano d’Abruzzo, to name a few. If grilling French sausages, you might start with Beaujolais, or an easygoing Chinon or Bourgueil. But no need to get hung up on ethnicities. Look for an American gamay noir, or one of the good reds from the Canary Islands, or a dry rosé. For summer rentals, don’t rely on local selections — B.Y.O.B.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wines for Savory, Pungent Sausages', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sausages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T16:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e79248-6d92-533d-ab31-f453404b5dc4', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e79248-6d92-533d-ab31-f453404b5dc4'}, {'abstract': 'Health care workers have a new tool to ease needle anxiety in children: a talking robot.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/using-a-robot-to-ease-a-childs-pain/', 'snippet': 'Health care workers have a new tool to ease needle anxiety in children: a talking robot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Health care workers have a new tool to ease needle anxiety in children: a talking robot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using a Robot to Ease a Child’s Pain', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T16:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophie Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cec6adf6-5e84-5595-926e-069e23dc4c8a', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cec6adf6-5e84-5595-926e-069e23dc4c8a'}, {'abstract': 'The high-tech 700-car garage will sit beneath the down