 who tire of local flavors in the Czech capital, new restaurants are serving global fare that can reset the palate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doff hats to the invincible dumpling. All due respect to the noble spud. But for those accustomed to more flavorful fare, the traditional dishes of Central Europe —\xa0and especially the Czech Republic —\xa0can turn quite tiresome even just halfway through a trip, at which point the plates of meat and starchy vegetables really start to stack up. Fortunately, the Czech capital of Prague is now home to an unexpected variety of new restaurants, including authentic Japanese, Mexican, Vietnamese and even dressed-up American-style joints, providing plenty of flavors beyond potatoes.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-sf/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-sf/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-sf/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-sf/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-sf/14PRAGUETABLES-SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_n