open this spot in March. Here’s an early take on what it’s like to eat there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has taken only four generations for the Arzaks to expand beyond Spain’s Basque Country, where the family opened a tavern in 1897. Since the 1970s, the three-Michelin-starred restaurant Arzak, in San Sebastián, run by the father and daughter team of Juan Mari and Elena Arzak, has been a center of modern Basque cooking. In March, with a team from their consultancy Arzak Instruction and the chef Sergio Sanz, the pair oversaw the opening of Ametsa — Basque for “dream” — in London’s sleek Halkin hotel.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14BITES_SPAN/14BITES_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14BITES_SPAN/14BITES_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14BITES_SPAN/14BITES_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14BITES_SPAN/14BITES_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1511, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14BITES_SPAN/14BITES_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/travel/14BITES_SPAN/14BITES_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thu