 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/vietnamese-marinated-flank-steak/', 'snippet': 'Vary the marinade, and you can serve flank steak in endless variation all summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In What’s for Dinner?, a column appearing every other week on Diner’s Journal, Melissa Clark answers that universal question, offering recipes for simple, relatively quick dishes that use ingredients you can pick up on the way home. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vietnamese Marinated Flank Steak', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T18:39:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2392a4e-4aa3-5a91-9324-12c5c62b1115', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2392a4e-4aa3-5a91-9324-12c5c62b1115'}, {'abstract': 'The State Department said doctors in Boston have ruled out a heart attack, stroke or brain tumor as the cause of a seizure-like episode she had over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/heinz-kerrys-condition-continues-to-improve/', 'snippet': 'The State Department said doctors in Boston have ruled out a heart attack, stroke or brain tumor as the cause of a seizure-like episode she had over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Teresa Heinz Kerry, the wife of Secretary of State John Kerry, is improving in a Boston hospital and doctors have ruled out a heart attack, stroke or brain tumor, the State Department said Tuesday. Mrs. Heinz Kerry experienced a seizure-like episode over the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heinz Kerry’s Condition Continues to Improve', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T18:40:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45c1a21e-1209-5252-b2e2-1a2f70d8b255', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45c1a21e-1209-5252-b2e2-1a2f70d8b255'}, {'abstract': 'At Segera, a 50,000-acre ranch on Kenya’s Laikipia Plateau, guests can relax in style — while giving back to the place they’re visiting.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/check-in-an-african-eco-resort-with-a-greater-sense-of-purpose/', 'snippet': 'At Segera, a 50,000-acre ranch on Kenya’s Laikipia Plateau, guests can relax in style — while giving back to the place they’re visiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Puma C.E.O. Jochen Zeitz is dining under the stars at Segera, his 50,000-acre ranch in the middle of central Kenya’s Laikipia Plateau, when he pauses over his steak and squints out into the sprawling savanna. “Sometimes you think there nothing’s there, but take a minute,” he says. “See how the bush comes to life.” Sure enough, as we peer through the inky blue twilight, what had appeared to be tall tree trunks start to move, and soon we can make out the silhouettes of giraffes grazing amid the shadowy acacia trees, and hear the elephants lumbering through the undergrowth toward the nearby river.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An African Eco-Resort With a Greater Sense of Purpose', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eco-Tourism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T18:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Sessa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sessa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9257c0ab-851c-597a-aea0-ec0293c19299', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9257c0ab-851c-597a-aea0-ec0293c19299'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the poems in Roberto Bolaño’s “Unknown University” were written when he was in his 20s, the sound of a promising young writer seeking his way in the world of words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/books/roberto-bolanos-unknown-university-collects-his-poems.html', 'snippet': 'Many of the poems in Roberto Bolaño’s “Unknown University” were written when he was in his 20s, the sound of a promising young writer seeking his way in the world of words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great Chilean writer Roberto Bolaño liked to argue, plausibly enough, that poetry is a higher calling than fiction.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/books/10book-SUB/10book-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/10/books/10book-SUB/10book-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 706}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/books/10