-744639658406', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4c4fd70-0f4a-5114-ae9c-744639658406'}, {'abstract': 'Many readers commented on the usefulness of self-employment in balancing work and family responsibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/on-working-for-yourself-for-more-flexible-hours/', 'snippet': 'Many readers commented on the usefulness of self-employment in balancing work and family responsibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve gotten a lot of e-mails in response to my article about how middle-class mothers balance work and family, raising many interesting and important issues: What about the challenges for working fathers? What about single parents who don’t have much of a support network? Are companies demanding more from childless employees to accommodate employees with children? Should men be encouraged to be more active co-parents so it’s not so challenging for women to remain in the work force?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Working for Yourself, for More Flexible Hours', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T19:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dcbc879-4224-5842-b69e-72e0c15520c4', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dcbc879-4224-5842-b69e-72e0c15520c4'}, {'abstract': 'The Interpublic Group of Companies has long sought a United States hub for Lowe. Its new plan is to enlist the firm Campbell Ewald.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/business/media/after-four-years-lowe-agency-gets-a-new-us-partner.html', 'snippet': 'The Interpublic Group of Companies has long sought a United States hub for Lowe. Its new plan is to enlist the firm Campbell Ewald.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For almost two decades, the Interpublic Group of Companies has tried to figure out the right way to beef up the United States operations of one of its global agency networks, Lowe & Partners. On Tuesday, Interpublic announced that it would go back to the drawing board again, undoing one alignment and forming another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Four Years, Lowe Agency Gets a New U.S. Partner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interpublic Group of Companies Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lowe & Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T19:06:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8330ea73-b8a5-5014-a004-94c7c7d7ca99', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8330ea73-b8a5-5014-a004-94c7c7d7ca99'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Vincent Di Maio, an expert in forensic pathology, testified that Trayvon Martin was leaning over George Zimmerman during their altercation last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/us/teenager-was-over-zimmerman-as-he-was-shot-expert-says.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Vincent Di Maio, an expert in forensic pathology, testified that Trayvon Martin was leaning over George Zimmerman during their altercation last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANFORD, Fla. — With the defense a day away from wrapping up its case, a widely known expert in forensic pathology, Dr. Vincent Di Maio, testified on Tuesday that Trayvon Martin’s injuries suggest he was on top of and leaning over George Zimmerman when Mr. Zimmerman fired his gun last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/ZIMMERMAN/ZIMMERMAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Martin Was Shot as He Leaned Over Zimmerman, Court Is Told', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zimmerman Fired From Beneath Victim, Pathologist Testifies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Di Maio, Vincent', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T19:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49636419-0d62-5d45-905a-ecd68c75fb70', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49636419-0d62-5d45-905a-ecd68c75fb70'}, {'abstract': 'Because of violence in Egypt, the United States and Britain have advised against traveling to the country, and one luxury tour operator has canceled tours.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/travel-warnings-on-egypt/', 'snippet': 'Because of violence in Egypt, the United States and Britain have advised against traveling to the country, and one luxury tour operator has canceled tours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rising tensions and violence in Egypt over the ouster of Mohamed Morsi, the country’s deposed president, have compelled some tour operators to cancel their scheduled trips and foreign governments to advise their citizens against traveling to the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel Warnings on Egypt', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABERCROMBIE & KENT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Tourism Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEXANDRIA (EGYPT)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Said (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T19:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a57d266-5562-534d-8a01-ea67ec20b452', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a57d266-5562-534d-8a01-ea67ec20b452'}, {'abstract': 'The missing whites that weren’t.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/a-whiter-shade-of-fail/', 'snippet': 'The missing whites that weren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aha. In my last post, I wrote about the claims that there were a lot of missing white voters, which are emboldening those calling for “libertarian populism”; as I pointed out, this supposed populism is actually just the same old economic royalism, wrapped in different rhetoric — and “downscale” whites very much need the safety net the GOP is tearing down. I also wondered, however, how much I should trust Sean Trende’s claim that missing white voters are a real, important thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Whiter Shade of Fail', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-09T19:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c90deb17-7448-5e31-8b89-104136379a96', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c90deb17-7448-5e31-8b89-104136379a96'}, {'abstract': 'Meredith Vieira, former host on “The View” and “Today,” will begin her syndicated show in fall 2014 for NBCUniversal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/business/media/meredith-vieira-to-return-to-daytime-tv-as-talk-show-host.html', 'snippet': 'Meredith Vieira, former host on “The View” and “Today,” will begin her syndicated show in fall 2014 for NBCUniversal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meredith Vieira will return to daytime television as the host of a syndicated talk show in the fall of 2014, Comcast’s NBCUniversal unit announced on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 