is expected to take up a measure against discrimination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The federal government is moving quickly to extend benefits like health care and life insurance to gay and lesbian married couples in response to the Supreme Court decision that struck down the Defense of Marriage Act.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Effects of Ruling on Same-Sex Marriage Start Rippling Out Through Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Effects of Ruling on Same-Sex Marriage Start Rippling Out Through Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T00:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82ea3e8c-2ed3-510b-8965-7f376827800c', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82ea3e8c-2ed3-510b-8965-7f376827800c'}, {'abstract': 'For Fabrice Tourre, an unfavorable verdict could yield a fine, or a ban from the securities industry. For the S.E.C., the trial is a defining moment that follows one courtroom disappointment after another.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/09/s-e-c-seeks-validation-in-gold