l': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/25543ee1-77fa-5cf3-97a6-04fdcd54a45d', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25543ee1-77fa-5cf3-97a6-04fdcd54a45d'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans are systematically dismantling the state’s reputation for progress and tolerance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/opinion/the-decline-of-north-carolina.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans are systematically dismantling the state’s reputation for progress and tolerance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Monday since April, thousands of North Carolina residents have gathered at the State Capitol to protest the grotesque damage that a new Republican majority has been doing to a tradition of caring for the least fortunate. Nearly 700 people have been arrested in the “Moral Monday” demonstrations, as they are known. But the bad news keeps on coming from the Legislature, and pretty soon a single day of the week may not be enough to contain the outrage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Decline of North Carolina', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Decline of North Carolina', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T01:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c927d75-8f70-596e-8040-180fb38ae6d7', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c927d75-8f70-596e-8040-180fb38ae6d7'}, {'abstract': 'The austerity demanded by the agreement for continued bailout payments in a country already in critical condition will only make things worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/opinion/wrong-prescription-for-greece.html', 'snippet': 'The austerity demanded by the agreement for continued bailout payments in a country already in critical condition will only make things worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greece and its financial overseers agreed on terms for continued bailout payments on Monday. The agreement is cause for relief — without it Greece would go bankrupt. But, at the same time, it is no cause for celebration — indeed, quite the opposite. Greece must eventually carry out painful reforms. But the precondition for these reforms is not the austerity demanded by the agreement but economic revival. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong Prescription for Greece', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wrong Prescription for Greece', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T01:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/87e7113c-ff5e-56cc-b107-c42bfa0a9619', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87e7113c-ff5e-56cc-b107-c42bfa0a9619'}, {'abstract': 'James Comey says most of the right things before the Senate Judiciary Committee, but questions remain about his commitment to civil liberties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/opinion/a-new-leader-for-the-fbi.html', 'snippet': 'James Comey says most of the right things before the Senate Judiciary Committee, but questions remain about his commitment to civil liberties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s nominee for F.B.I. director, James Comey, faced a mostly friendly Senate Judiciary Committee on Tuesday, and he is almost assured confirmation given strong bipartisan support. But his tenure as deputy attorney general in the George W. Bush administration raises important questions about his commitment to civil liberties and his independence in an office that demands unstinting devotion to both principles. As has been made all too clear in recent weeks, the relationship between American citizens and the government’s law-enforcement and intelligence agencies remains deeply damaged. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Leader for the F.B.I.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Leader for the F.B.I.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T01:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/28397b8a-8441-53ed-a230-5ef0cf8e06b3', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28397b8a-8441-53ed-a230-5ef0cf8e06b3'}, {'abstract': 'In remarks at a workshop, a judge who served on the secret Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court said the country needed a more open debate on surveillance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/us/nation-will-gain-by-discussing-surveillance-expert-tells-privacy-board.html', 'snippet': 'In remarks at a workshop, a judge who served on the secret Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court said the country needed a more open debate on surveillance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A retired federal judge, who formerly served on the secret Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court, on Tuesday praised the growing public discussion about government surveillance fostered by the leaks of classified information by Edward J. Snowden, the former National Security Agency contractor whom the Obama administration has charged with espionage and who remains a fugitive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/NSA/NSA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/10/us/NSA/NSA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/NSA/NSA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/us/NSA/NSA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nation Will Gain by Discussing Surveillance, Expert Tells Privacy Board', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nation Will Gain by Discussing Surveillance, Expert Tells Privacy Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons',