and among Asian consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/k-k-r-raises-6-billion-in-new-asia-fund/', 'snippet': 'The private equity group’s second regional fund ranks as the largest such fund to date and will seek to capitalize on rising demand among Asian consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG – Kohlberg Kravis Roberts said on Wednesday that it had closed a $6 billion fund for the Asia-Pacific region, the biggest such fund to date.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'K.K.R. Raises $6 Billion Asian Fund', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T06:02:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62900c2a-5303-5dc3-8bf7-2c4c8498ab31', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62900c2a-5303-5dc3-8bf7-2c4c8498ab31'}, {'abstract': 'There is a strange mix of great amounts of transparency and very little accountability when it comes to surveillance and intelligence agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/how-surveillance-works-in-india/', 'snippet': 'There is a strange mix of great amounts of transparency and very little accountability when it comes to surveillance and intelligence agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Indian government announced it would start a Centralized Monitoring System in 2009 to monitor telecommunications in the country, the public seemed unconcerned. When the government announced that the system, also known as C.M.S., commenced in April, the news didn’t receive much attention. After a colleague at the Centre for Internet and Society wrote about the program and it was lambasted by Human Rights Watch, more reporters started covering it as a privacy issue. But it was ultimately the revelations by Edward J. Snowden about American surveillance that prompted Indians to ask questions about its own government’s surveillance programs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-internet-IndiaInk/09-internet-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Surveillance Works in India', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court of India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T06:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pranesh Prakash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pranesh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prakash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26d23391-a51e-54ec-8b2b-ddf5ab33a386', 'word_count': 1351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26d23391-a51e-54ec-8b2b-ddf5ab33a386'}, {'abstract': 'Development of the drug, aleglitazar, was discontinued after Roche cited concerns about safety and effectiveness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/business/roche-abandons-new-diabetes-drug.html', 'snippet': 'Development of the drug, aleglitazar, was discontinued after Roche cited concerns about safety and effectiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roche, the Swiss pharmaceutical giant, has discontinued development of a potentially important diabetes drug, a move that could raise safety questions about the entire category of drugs, which includes the controversial medicine Avandia.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roche Stops Developing a New Drug for Diabetes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roche Stops Developing A New Drug For Diabetes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roche Holding AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T07:21:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e521392-48ec-53bc-baf0-83022e4b1f98', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e521392-48ec-53bc-baf0-83022e4b1f98'}, {'abstract': 'Can you identify the number that cannot represent the possible total number of votes at a recent Stuyvesant High School election?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/test-yourself-math-july-10-2013/', 'snippet': 'Can you identify the number that cannot represent the possible total number of votes at a recent Stuyvesant High School election?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question, created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the article “At Stuyvesant High School, a Presidency Is Won, and Quickly Revoked.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, July 10, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T08:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9601fb24-a70f-5e72-a8f9-49811817955b', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9601fb24-a70f-5e72-a8f9-49811817955b'}, {'abstract': 'Two crab recipes for summer — one rich, one light. No bait required.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/magazine/crab-without-a-net.html', 'snippet': 'Two crab recipes for summer — one rich, one light. No bait required.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two ways to get crab this season. One is beautiful, hard work. It requires only a chicken neck, string, a net and access to coastal Atlantic waters. Tie the string to the neck and dangle it into the shallows where you can see the bait. Here comes Mr. Crab. Here comes Mr. Net. Repeat until you’ve got enough for dinner. Children can do this — and will — until you’ve got enough crabs for two dinners. Steam them and start picking.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14eat_span/14eat_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 332, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14eat_span/14eat_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 332}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14eat_span/14eat_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 1024, 'su