ract': 'Social innovation rarely comes from “eureka” moments; it’s much more deliberate. It’s something that can be studied and learned.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/summer-reading-how-to-shake-up-the-status-quo/', 'snippet': 'Social innovation rarely comes from “eureka” moments; it’s much more deliberate. It’s something that can be studied and learned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you write a weekly column that examines creative responses to social problems, you begin to spot patterns. One of the things I’ve noticed is that, unlike the bursts of creativity that are depicted in children’s books or Hollywood movies, social innovation rarely comes from “eureka” moments; it’s much more deliberate. It’s something that can be studied and learned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Reading: How to Shake Up the Status Quo', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T11:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f23594fc-e399-5227-8db5-20ca78c2bd1e', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f23594fc-e399-5227-8db5-20ca78c2bd1e'}, {'abstract': 'A business owner’s reflections on a first job, the meaning of hard work and missed opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/a-not-to-do-list-for-recent-college-graduates/', 'snippet': 'A business owner’s reflections on a first job, the meaning of hard work and missed opportunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College graduation: lofty commencement speeches are given, bright futures anticipated and, for some lucky college graduates, new jobs await. While commencement addresses may be inspiring, I wish someone would take the opportunity to deliver a more practical message to new college graduates who are about to enter the work force. It would go something like this:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Not-to-Do’ List for Recent College Graduates', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commencement Speeches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Callidus Software', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T11:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burkhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burkhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d343fde4-76cb-5ad5-a9ed-0f5ccf2828f5', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d343fde4-76cb-5ad5-a9ed-0f5ccf2828f5'}, {'abstract': 'The flooding, coupled with frequent earthquakes and soil erosion, has called into question efforts to populate areas along rivers that snake through deep canyons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/asia/rainstorms-flood-chinas-sichuan-province-killing-at-least-40.html', 'snippet': 'The flooding, coupled with frequent earthquakes and soil erosion, has called into question efforts to populate areas along rivers that snake through deep canyons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Rainstorms that are said to be the worst in five decades have flooded large areas of southwest China, washing out bridges, setting off a landslide that buried dozens of people and destroying a memorial to victims of the 2008 earthquake in Sichuan Province that flattened large parts of the same area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11china2/11china2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11china2/11china2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11china2/11china2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11china2/11china2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11china2/11china2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail'