ally.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/obama-and-bush-promote-benefits-of-immigration/', 'snippet': 'President Obama and former President George W. Bush found themselves on the same side of a public policy debate on Wednesday as they promoted the virtues of immigration at a time when Congress is considering rewriting the rules to accept millions ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and former President George W. Bush found themselves on the same side of a public policy debate on Wednesday as they promoted the virtues of immigration at a time when Congress is considering rewriting the rules to accept millions here illegally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Bush Promote Benefits of Immigration', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T14:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1877de1-6e8b-5cd1-a4e3-f896bdbf6e58', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1877de1-6e8b-5cd1-a4e3-f896bdbf6e58'}, {'abstract': 'A series of award-winning photographs chronicle the ethnic violence that broke out in the Kokrajhar district of Assam in the summer of 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/remains-of-the-day-in-kokrajhar/', 'snippet': 'A series of award-winning photographs chronicle the ethnic violence that broke out in the Kokrajhar district of Assam in the summer of 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I began my career as a photojournalist in 2006 in the Kokrajhar district of the northeastern state of Assam on the India-Bhutan border. Six years later, I was back there to cover the aftermath of the violence that broke out in June and July 2012 between the indigenous Bodos and the Bengali-speaking Muslims, whose ancestors had immigrated from the parts of undivided Bengal, which now form Bangladesh. It was a war between the poorest of the Indians. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remains of the Day in Kokrajhar', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bodos (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Assam State (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T14:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivek Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/802b6afb-0f40-5418-a1cf-4dba8d68834a', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/802b6afb-0f40-5418-a1cf-4dba8d68834a'}, {'abstract': 'Germany’s resistance to sharing risk with its European Union brethren is at odds with the unified approach to problem-solving that Brussels wants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/business/global/european-union-proposes-plan-for-failing-banks.html', 'snippet': 'Germany’s resistance to sharing risk with its European Union brethren is at odds with the unified approach to problem-solving that Brussels wants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — European Union officials presented long-awaited 