ood, drink and tobacco from dawn to dusk. Traffic is thin in my downtown neighborhood but I can hear televisions blaring the latest developments. People are talking about Egypt’s new interim government, amid a general feeling that, at least today, the first day of Ramadan, everyone can relax.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong About Tamarrod?', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fasting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beblawi, Hazem el-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mansour, Adli', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freedom and Justice Party (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nour, Al-, Party (Egypt)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T16:28:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Golia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename