: 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f29abb91-85ee-51ae-a106-18b70077f9f5', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f29abb91-85ee-51ae-a106-18b70077f9f5'}, {'abstract': 'Everywhere you look, pink is this summer’s standout color.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/were-having-a-pink-wave/', 'snippet': 'Everywhere you look, pink is this summer’s standout color.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is pink the official color of summer? Tables at street cafes are peppered with glasses of blush-colored rosé (is it more popular than ever?), cheeks are flushed from the heat (and maybe the wine), and at the European fashion shows just ended, a slew of stylish showgoers worked pink shades into their looks. At the men’s shows, the blogger Linda Tol wore a raw-edged pink maxidress with a matching camera case, no less; and the model Jamie Bochert wore a grungy pink Saint Laurent cardigan to the SL show. At couture, the stylist Natalia Alaverdian was quirky in her boxy pink jacket and dangling earrings; Jennifer Lawrence was daring in a cropped pink lace top from the Dior resort collection; and Natalia Vodianova was terribly correct in pink Chanel. And doesn’t the pale pink bag carried by Leighton Meester, in Los Angeles for a premiere, look fresh? As these pack leaders prove, a little pink, styled in nuanced ways, is just the right amount of sweet.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re Having a Pink Wave', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We’re Having A Pink Wave', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ee0cfe2-e3f6-5ddf-92bd-75b71018686a', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ee0cfe2-e3f6-5ddf-92bd-75b71018686a'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese government’s response to weak economic data will be a test of the nation’s new leadership, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/chinas-growth-woes-could-force-government-response/', 'snippet': 'The Chinese government’s response to weak economic data will be a test of the nation’s new leadership, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, China enters the “sanfu days” of the lunar calendar, similar to what are known in the west as the dog days of summer. Some areas of the country are battling huge floods, and the weather will most likely get worse before it gets better.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Growth Woes Could Force Government Response', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Keqiang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 