, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc909bd4-ed31-5d3e-8f3c-0f11f6fa7169', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc909bd4-ed31-5d3e-8f3c-0f11f6fa7169'}, {'abstract': 'A bipartisan Senate coalition blocked a Democratic proposal to retroactively cut interest rates on higher education loans in half, leaving any student loan rescue in doubt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/us/politics/democratic-rifts-stymie-senate-bill-on-student-loan-rates.html', 'snippet': 'A bipartisan Senate coalition blocked a Democratic proposal to retroactively cut interest rates on higher education loans in half, leaving any student loan rescue in doubt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A bipartisan Senate coalition on Wednesday blocked a Democratic proposal to retroactively cut interest rates on higher education loans in half, leaving any student loan rescue in doubt and laying bare divisions among Democrats about how to resolve the dispute.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rift Among Democrats Stalls Effort to Reverse Rise in College Loan Rates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rift Among Democrats Stalls Effort to Reverse Rise in College Loan Rates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manchin, Joe III', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Angus Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carper, Thomas R', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burr, Richard M', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a186b924-b1f3-5b9f-ac42-06dc55c13a75', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a186b924-b1f3-5b9f-ac42-06dc55c13a75'}, {'abstract': 'The acquisition of America’s largest pork producer by Shuanghui International could result in the transfer of food-production technologies that endanger the United States economy and, perhaps, national security, two experts tell the Senate Agriculture Committee.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/lawmakers-have-concerns-over-chinese-takeover-of-smithfield/', 'snippet': 'The acquisition of America’s largest pork producer by Shuanghui International could result in the transfer of food-production technologies that endanger the United States economy and, perhaps, national security, two experts tell the Senate Agricul...', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Members of the Senate Agriculture Committee raised questions on Wednesday about the economic and national security implications of a Chinese company’s proposed acquisition of Smithfield Foods, the nation’s largest pork producer.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senators Question Chinese Takeover of Smithfield', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senators Question Chinese Takeover of Smithfield', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, '