 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/travel/11orient/11orient-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Travel Boom in Myanmar', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cruises: Travel Takes off in Myanmar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yangon (Myanmar)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c5a381e-5836-50bc-8db9-45222d54e948', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c5a381e-5836-50bc-8db9-45222d54e948'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s shaky state should not be an insurmountable obstacle to foreign investment, the author writes. Foreign deal makers just need to find ways to coax Italy’s aging entrepreneur-owners to the table.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/why-italy-could-be-fertile-ground-for-deal-makers/', 'snippet': 'Italy’s shaky state should not be an insurmountable obstacle to foreign investment, the author writes. Foreign deal makers just need to find ways to coax Italy’s aging entrepreneur-owners to the table.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overseas buyers should look again at Italy. It is hardly surprising that deal-making is slow east of the Alps. But Italian firms excel in fields from fashion to engineering. The country’s parlous state is not an insurmountable obstacle to foreign investment. Foreigners just need to find ways to coax Italy’s aging entrepreneur-owners to the table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Italy Could Be Fertile Ground for Deal Makers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ducati Motor Holding SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Loro Piana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:35:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Webb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3472555-25c0-5bb2-90e0-9c962efdfef3', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3472555-25c0-5bb2-90e0-9c962efdfef3'}, {'abstract': 'Shopping to celebrate the French national day.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/theyll-be-storming-the-pop-up/', 'snippet': 'Shopping to celebrate the French national day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fleur du Mal, the lingerie and ready-to-wear label from Jennifer Zuccarini, a founder of Kiki de Montparnasse, is going all out to celebrate Bastille Day. For two weeks, starting July 10, the company will honor the French national day with a pop-up shop inside Clic Gallery in SoHo. Among the treats you’ll find there are these flirty lace bits (bra, $148; high-waist panties; $138, and bodysuit, $295); chic striped knit underpinnings, $120 to $145; and a ruffled white lace jumpsuit, $1,250 — not to mention custom tulle panties embroidered with Eiffel Towers and phrases like “plat du jour” by LQQK Studio in Brooklyn. There is also jewelry from the Parisian designer Yazbukey and vintage goods, including Jane Birkin records and French photography magazines. Francophiles and lingerie nuts: this one is for you. Check the Web site, fleurdumal.com, for news of special events at the pop-up.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pop-Up Shop in Honor of Bastille Day', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’ll Be Storming The Pop-Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lingerie and Underwear', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop-Up Stores and Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:36:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/246db9b4-317f-5b9a-81f9-4a1db62c5f2c', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/246db9b4-317f-5b9a-81f9-4a1db62c5f2c'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Kazee’s show at 54 Below featured original, mostly downbeat alt-country material, performed with his band, the Shiny Liars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/arts/music/steve-kazee-sings-about-his-reflections-on-ex-girlfriends.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Kazee’s show at 54 Below featured original, mostly downbeat alt-country material, performed with his band, the Shiny Liars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Kazee is a far more complicated musical personality than Guy, the ingenuous Irish busker he portrayed in the Broadway musical “Once.” Bitter, tormented, and ruthlessly self-scrutinizing, he comes across on a nightclub stage as a performer struggling against insecurity. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11KAZEE/11KAZEE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 's