013/07/11/sports/cycling/11iht-tour11.html', 'snippet': 'Tony Martin won Stage 11 of the Tour de France. Christopher Froome, who finished second in the stage, is still wearing the yellow jersey as the overall leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONT SAINT-MICHEL, France — When he mounted an attack on the final climb of Stage 8 on Saturday, a move that gave him a commanding lead in the Tour de France, many of Christopher Froome’s rivals were caught by surprise. It was too early in the three-week race, they thought, to take the yellow jersey.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/11tour/11tour-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Froome Loses Time Trial but Not His Yellow Jersey', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Losing Time Trial, Not Yellow Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cycling, Road', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Froome, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Tony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:54:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Brand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb860995-f75a-50b6-ab54-d01fe87b1169', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb860995-f75a-50b6-ab54-d01fe87b1169'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of jewelry handmade from glass with bursts of color.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/ronni-kappos-turns-vintage-glass-into-jewelry/', 'snippet': 'A collection of jewelry handmade from glass with bursts of color.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest collection from the Los Angeles jeweler I. Ronni Kappos is handmade from a cache of vintage German glass edged with 24-karat gold, which she fashions into clean, modern shapes with summery bursts of color. These aqua and coral double drop earrings, $127, would be a great accent for a white beach dress, a striped work dress or a tank and jeans shorts. Think of them as an easy way to spruce up without breaking the bank. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ronni Kappos Turns Vintage Glass Into Jewelry', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Few Drops Of Color', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:57:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/385b95e9-f7fb-5235-985f-117709368ae2', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/385b95e9-f7fb-5235-985f-117709368ae2'}, {'abstract': 'Ayad Akhtar’s “The Who and the What” and “Stop Hitting Yourself,” devised by the Rude Mechs, will be staged at the Claire Tow Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/new-play-by-pulitzer-winner-to-be-part-of-lct3-season/', 'snippet': 'Ayad Akhtar’s “The Who and the What” and “Stop Hitting Yourself,” devised by the Rude Mechs, will be staged at the Claire Tow Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ayad Akhtar, whose “Disgraced” won this year’s Pulitzer Prize for drama, will be back at Lincoln Center Theater next year with a new offering, “The Who and the What.” Scheduled for the spring, the play is part of LCT3, a programming initiative aimed at introducing newer artists, and which presented “Disgraced” as well. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Play by Pulitzer Winner To Be Part of LCT3 Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AKHTAR, AYAD', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Senior, Kimberly', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rude Mechs', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T18:58:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60756dd7-4a63-5f3d-9dfd-8c1703eb1a73', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60756dd7-4a63-5f3d-9dfd-8c1703eb1a73'}, {'abstract': 'Every season, players emerge from under the radar to become key contributors on fantasy football rosters, especially at the running back position. Here are some candidates for 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/sports/football/fantasy-football-sleeper-and-breakout-candidates-at-running-back.html', 'snippet': 'Every season, players emerge from under the radar to become key contributors on fantasy football rosters, especially at the running back position. Here are some candidates for 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Players often emerge from under the radar to become key contributors on fantasy football rosters, especially at running back. Whether a player is returning from an injury or outshining the competition in a running-back-by-committee, it happens every season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/football/11fantasy1/11fantasy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 457, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/football/11fantasy1