y Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c39ee1eb-b391-567a-a2bc-5c4f9f068061', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c39ee1eb-b391-567a-a2bc-5c4f9f068061'}, {'abstract': 'It is astounding, the author writes, how little risk the markets are pricing into public companies that have poured shareholder money into emerging markets over the last several years through acquisitions and start-up projects.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/adventures-abroad-could-hurt-u-s-companies/', 'snippet': 'It is astounding, the author writes, how little risk the markets are pricing into public companies that have poured shareholder money into emerging markets over the last several years through acquisitions and start-up projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carson C. Block is the director of research for Muddy Waters, an investment firm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adventures Abroad Could Hurt U.S. Companies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Block, Carson C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Muddy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T19:06:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carson C. Block', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carson', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Block', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/935522f7-760f-5748-8826-40cb7e50ac58', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/935522f7-760f-5748-8826-40cb7e50ac58'}, {'abstract': 'Now a group of Web developers in Austria has introduced Data Dealer, a game that aims to make the business of consumer profiling more transparent.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/a-game-that-deals-in-personal-data/', 'snippet': 'Now a group of Web developers in Austria has introduced Data Dealer, a game that aims to make the business of consumer profiling more transparent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All kinds of companies and services – social networks, data brokers, loyalty card programs to name just a few – amass and analyze details about millions of consumers’ activities and preferences. But the inner workings of this surveillance economy remain largely opaque to the public despite the recent revelations of widespread government data-mining of people’s phone and e-mail records.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 1072, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/technology/10bits-datadeal/10bits-datadeal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Game That Deals in Personal Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Video Game\r\nThat Deals\r\nIn Personal Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brill, Julie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vienna (Austria)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T19:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a36bec5e-963c-5956-8a87-8ba74d2a9df6', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a36bec5e-963c-5956-8a87-8ba74d2a9df6'}, {'abstract': 'In an online video, the rapper and actor turns a spotlight on the controversial procedure of force-feeding detainees on hunger strike at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/mos-def-video-puts-force-feeding-in-spotlight/', 'snippet': 'In an online video, the rapper and actor turns a spotlight on the controversial procedure of force-feeding detainees on hunger strike at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an online video this week, the rapper and actor Yasiin Bey, also known as Mos Def, is shown in a baggy orange prison uniform with shackles around his wrists and ankles, and strapped into a medical chair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mos Def Video Puts Force-Feeding in Spotlight', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kessler, Gladys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mos Def', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T19:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/985aa4b2-887f-5a3c-9a84-633d8ae491c4', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/985aa4b2-887f-5a3c-9a84-633d8ae491c4'}, {'abstract': 'A new study foresees declining demand for oil both through thriftier use and new fuel options.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/more-signs-of-peak-us-in-new-study-of-peak-oil-demand/', 'snippet': 'A new study foresees declining demand for oil both through thriftier use and new fuel options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2010, I asked this question: “Which Comes First – Peak Everything or Peak Us?” My focus was whether humans could use the gift of foresight to curb resource appetites in ways that would avoid having the peak imposed on us by shortages or human-induced environmental shifts like climate disruption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/blogs/dotpeakdemand/dotpeakdemand-jumbo.gif', 'height': 285, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/blogs/dotpeakdemand/dotpeakdemand-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 285, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/blogs/dotpeakdemand/dotpeakdemand-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/10/blogs/dotpeakdemand/dotpeakdemand-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/blogs/dotpeakdemand/dotpeakdemand-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Signs of ‘Peak Us’ in New Study of ‘Peak Oil Demand’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub':