ee44f02'}, {'abstract': 'His album has held up better than Kanye West’s “Yeezus,” reaching the top of the chart with sales of 58,000 copies.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/j-cole-reaches-no-1-finally/', 'snippet': 'His album has held up better than Kanye West’s “Yeezus,” reaching the top of the chart with sales of 58,000 copies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, if an album makes it to No. 1, it usually does so right out of the gate. When one reaches the top after having started lower down the chart, it is often because the album has held strong against its competition, or because sales have sunk all around. In the case of J. Cole’s “Born Sinner” (Roc Nation/Columbia), both scenarios apply.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'J. Cole Reaches No.1, Finally', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'J. Cole Scales Top 100', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'J Cole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thicke, Robin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T19:45:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/122c4beb-2c7c-5ad5-800a-0ce41f554e9f', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/122c4beb-2c7c-5ad5-800a-0ce41f554e9f'}, {'abstract': 'A new Quinnipiac poll has found a significant shift in public opinion on the trade-off between civil liberties and national security.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/public-opinion-shifts-on-security-liberty-balance/', 'snippet': 'A new Quinnipiac poll has found a significant shift in public opinion on the trade-off between civil liberties and national security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new Quinnipiac poll has found a significant shift in public opinion on the trade-off between civil liberties and national security. In the new survey, released on Wednesday, 45 percent of the public said they thought the government’s antiterrorism policies have “gone too far in restricting the average person’s civil liberties” — as compared with 40 percent who said they have “not gone far enough to adequately protect the country.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Opinion Shifts on Security-Liberty Balance', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T19:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb96f31-a765-53fd-b37d-c1b57326b627', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb96f31-a765-53fd-b37d-c1b57326b627'}, {'abstract': 'The work of Theadora Van Runkle, a costume designer, is featured in an exhibition; Andy Warhol’s Polaroids will be on view in Sag Harbor, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/fashion/new-shops-and-sales-for-the-week-of-july-11.html', 'snippet': 'The work of Theadora Van Runkle, a costume designer, is featured in an exhibition; Andy Warhol’s Polaroids will be on view in Sag Harbor, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Openings', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':