uliar items. Wednesday’s selections include photos taken by the Transportation Security Administration when employees met people who just couldn’t stand ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Instagrams From the T.S.A., and Facebook Father', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T20:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdb060fb-86b2-5467-a607-46fd5a657db2', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdb060fb-86b2-5467-a607-46fd5a657db2'}, {'abstract': 'In Gabriel Roth’s “Unknowns,” the narrator knows more about writing code than he does about women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/books/the-unknowns-is-gabriel-roths-debut-novel.html', 'snippet': 'In Gabriel Roth’s “Unknowns,” the narrator knows more about writing code than he does about women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If only all social misfits were as stealthily charming as Eric Muller, the nerdy narrator of Gabriel Roth’s sparkling debut novel. If Eric means to make himself sound unappealing to the reader, he fails miserably in his mission. Who could resist the kind of tech-oriented guy who calculates his exact reasons for arriving at a party at 10:32 p.m., because at that relatively early stage “it’s possible to imagine that this party will live up to the promise inherent in the notion of a party”? Or who would notice, a little later, that “the population has increased, but not to the Malthusian degree it would take to make the party memorable”? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11BOOKROTH/11BOOKROTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 946, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11BOOKROTH/11BOOKROTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 946}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11BOOKROTH/11BOOKROTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11BOOKROTH/11BOOKROTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11BOOKROTH/11BOOKROTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail