}, {'abstract': 'Susanne Bartsch, the Swiss Miss of New York night life since the Koch era, presides over four parties every week as part of a late-career flowering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/fashion/not-going-gentle-into-that-good-night.html', 'snippet': 'Susanne Bartsch, the Swiss Miss of New York night life since the Koch era, presides over four parties every week as part of a late-career flowering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susanne Bartsch frowned into a ceiling-high mirror, lifting her left breast with her palm. “This one looks droopy,” she said, in her Swiss-German accent. She turned and examined her svelte profile, adding proudly, “They’re only a year old.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/fashion/11BARTSCH_SPAN/11zBARTSCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Going Gentle Into That Good Night', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Going Gentle Into That Good Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schulman, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartsch, Susanne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T21:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c40226-fad4-5155-8226-d30ab8640ac2', 'word_count': 2052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c40226-fad4-5155-8226-d30ab8640ac2'}, {'abstract': 'Pilobolus, the dance company founded in the early ’70s, opened its summer season at the Joyce Theater with works ranging from 1972 to this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/arts/dance/pilobolus-puts-4-decades-of-dance-on-display.html', 'snippet': 'Pilobolus, the dance company founded in the early ’70s, opened its summer season at the Joyce Theater with works ranging from 1972 to this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pilobolus, long a popular institution, is now 42. The publicity for the company’s current New York season says it wouldn’t be summer without Pilobolus at the Joyce Theater. Sure enough, on Tuesday’s opening night the Joyce audience stood to cheer through the curtain calls. At this rate, who knows? Pilobolus may be with us for another 42 years. This is an amazement to those of us who loved the first generation of Pilobolus in the 1970s. It was popular then, too. But it didn’t feel like an enduring institution. It was its own species, and seemed set to be fabulously ephemeral. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 568}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 970, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1929, 'width': 2036, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/subpilobolus1/subpilobolus1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg