ne': {'original': 'By Bridget Huber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bridget', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c00ce38-9248-5d7b-91ff-8237e403ce6c', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c00ce38-9248-5d7b-91ff-8237e403ce6c'}, {'abstract': 'Listening to “Beach House 2,” a new mixtape from Ty Dolla Sign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/arts/music/hes-acting-out-its-on-purpose.html', 'snippet': 'Listening to “Beach House 2,” a new mixtape from Ty Dolla Sign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s inevitable that we’ll have to get to a definition of “ratchet,” so let’s dispense with it quickly. To act ratchet is to act foolish, or trashy, to behave in a way that makes others shield their eyes. It is the opposite of decorous. There are plenty of places one can act ratchet — in the club, in the bedroom — but it’s always about behavior that’s dubious at best, that makes people point fingers in slack-jawed astonishment and discomfort.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11TYDOLLA/11TYDOLLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 251, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11TYDOLLA/11TYDOLLA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 251, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11TYDOLLA/11TYDOLLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11TYDOLLA/11TYDOLLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11TYDOLLA/11TYDOLLA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s Acting Out; It’s on Purpose', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s Acting Out; It’s On Purpose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-10T21:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efe7f8e0-5e72-5d1f-8179-e69762f2592e', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efe7f8e0-5e72-5d1f-8179-e69762f2592e'}, {'abstract': 'The Complicite production of “Shun-kin” uses puppetry, traditional performance, music and design to convey coolly a steamy Japanese tale at the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/theater/reviews/shun-kin-japanese-intrigue-at-lincoln-center-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Complicite production of “Shun-kin” uses puppetry, traditional performance, music and design to convey coolly a steamy Japanese tale at the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A distant world of ceremony, secrets and furtive sexual desire is conjured with shadow-strewn grace in “Shun-kin,” the latest production from Complicite and the director Simon McBurney. An adaptation of a 1933 short story by Junichiro Tanizaki, the production blends puppetry, traditional performance, music and design with the combination of daring and delicacy that Complicite has become known for in its previous visits to the Lincoln Center Festival. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/11SHUN/11SHUN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Manipulating Perverse Love', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manipulating Perverse Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 