ing the fab in prefab, ’50s style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a prefab dwelling made of porcelain-enamel steel and sold to Americans after World War II as a cheap housing solution, the Lustron has become quite celebrated. In 2008, a Lustron home was erected inside the Museum of Modern Art for a show on factory-produced architecture. Now, the same home is the star attraction of “1950s: Building the American Dream,” an exhibition at the Ohio History Center in Columbus. \xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/garden/11SHOWS_SPAN/11CURR3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 't