 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa20193e-9c06-5e3b-9d03-d5299fcc6aa3', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa20193e-9c06-5e3b-9d03-d5299fcc6aa3'}, {'abstract': 'The police reported that the remains of 20 people had been found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/americas/railroad-chairman-blames-engineer-in-quebec-crash.html', 'snippet': 'The police reported that the remains of 20 people had been found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — The death toll in the fiery derailment of a train in a Quebec town over the weekend rose Wednesday, with the police reporting that the remains of 20 people had been found. The police also said that 30 more people were still missing, and it is widely assumed that they are dead. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deaths Climb From Disaster in Quebec', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deaths Climb From Disaster In Quebec', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lac-Megantic (Quebec)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkhardt, Edward', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69cf1293-981f-562a-bdc6-8bae4a38b23d', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69cf1293-981f-562a-bdc6-8bae4a38b23d'}, {'abstract': 'Improvements in prison life for Amir Hekmati, incarcerated for nearly two years on spying accusations, strengthened his family’s hope that Iran’s judiciary would favorably review an appeal for his release.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/middleeast/hopes-rise-for-appeal-of-ex-marine-held-in-iran.html', 'snippet': 'Improvements in prison life for Amir Hekmati, incarcerated for nearly two years on spying accusations, strengthened his family’s hope that Iran’s judiciary would favorably review an appeal for his release.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prison life has markedly improved in recent weeks for Amir Hekmati, the former Marine incarcerated for nearly two years in Iran on spying accusations. His sister said he was now allowed weekly visits from three Iranian relatives, books, daily exercise and a regular correspondence of letters with family in the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hopes Rise for Appeal of Ex-Marine Held in Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hopes Rise For Appeal Of Ex-Marine Held in Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hekmati, Amir Mirzaei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/390b77e8-dfae-5362-8206-d87b888f599e', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/390b77e8-dfae-5362-8206-d87b888f599e'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge commuted the sentence of Joseph C. Massino, a former Bonanno crime family leader who broke the code of silence, and he will be released from federal custody in 60 days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/nyregion/Judge-Commutes-2-Life-Sentences-for-Mob-Boss-Joseph-Massino-Who-Became-Informer.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge commuted the sentence of Joseph C. Massino, a former Bonanno crime family leader who broke the code of silence, and he will be released from federal custody in 60 days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Joseph C. Massino took the witness stand in 2011, becoming the first official boss of one of New York’s five crime families to break the code of silence and testify against a former confederate, he offered a succinct explanation for his departure from mob tradition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/nyregion/MOB-city/MOB-city-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 199, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/nyregion/MOB-city/MOB-city-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 199, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/nyregion/MOB-city/MOB-city-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '