uld never know if I might have been infected with H.I.V. or not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up in a Modern Orthodox Jewish family in New Jersey, where my “sex talk,” at 13, came in the form of my mother handing me a book of anatomical comics. Inside it, she placed post-it notes to indicate her feelings. In the masturbation section: “God does not approve of this.” In the gay sex section: “Definitely not.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Life, Post Exposure', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isaac Lobel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isaac', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1937efb-826a-5746-b92d-3680c9239325', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1937efb-826a-5746-b92d-3680c9239325'}, {'abstract': 'A hunger strike over solitary confinement and other conditions that continued for a third day Wednesday could become the largest in state history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/us/hunger-strike-by-california-inmates-already-large-is-expected-to-be-a-long-one.html', 'snippet': 'A hunger strike over solitary confinement and other conditions that continued for a third day Wednesday could become the largest in state history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Nearly 29,000 inmates in California state prisons refused meals for the third day Wednesday during a protest of prison conditions and rules. The protest extended to two-thirds of the 33 prisons across the state and all 4 private out-of-state facilities where California sends inmates, corrections officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/PRISON/PRISON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunger Strike by California Inmates, Already Large, Is Expected to Be Long', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hunger Strike by California Inmates, Already Large, Is Expected to Be a Long One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solitary Confinement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pelican Bay State Prison', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:32:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b83dd5c-f182-56f8-a33d-3b0df8104fcb', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b83dd5c-f182-56f8-a33d-3b0df8104fcb'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli police on Wednesday agreed to re-investigate the 2009 injury of an American activist during a clash between Israeli security forces and protesters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/middleeast/israel-reopens-inquiry-into-activists-injury.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli police on Wednesday agreed to re-investigate the 2009 injury of an American activist during a clash between Israeli security forces and protesters.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Israeli police on Wednesday agreed to re-investigate the 2009 injury of an American activist during a clash between Israeli security forces and protesters against the extension of Israel’s separation barrier in the West Bank. The activist, Tristan Anderson of Oakland, Calif., then 38, was hit in the head by a tear-gas canister in the village of Nilin, and remains partly paralyzed and blind in one eye. Yesh Din, an Israeli human rights organization, appealed to Israel’s High Court of Justice after the police closed the investigation without indicting any of the soldiers involved, and the court’s justices urged the police to reopen the case. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Reopens Inquiry Into Activist’s Injury', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Inquiry Into Activist’s Injury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Myra Noveck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Myra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Noveck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8f5e82c-ee40-5f03-855a-30fae6bbd93d', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8f5e82c-ee40-5f03-855a-30fae6bbd93d'}, {'abstract': 'A senior North Korean diplomat said Wednesday that his country was willing to have “any kind of talks” to ease tensions on the Korean Peninsula.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/asia/north-korea-repeats-call-for-talks.html', 'snippet': 'A senior North Korean diplomat said Wednesday that his country was willing to have “any kind of talks” to ease tensions on the Korean Peninsula.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A senior North Korean diplomat said Wednesday that his country was willing to have “any kind of talks” to ease tensions on the Korean Peninsula, while at the same time repeating its call for the United States to dismantle its military command in South Korea. In the second news conference on the subject staged by the North’s senior diplomats in less than three weeks, So Se-pyong, North Korea’s ambassador to the United Nations in Geneva, called for the dissolution of the United Nations military command led by the United States as a prerequisite for calming the situation on the peninsula. The alliance is called the United Nations Command, although the United Nations plays no role. If the United States made a “bold decision” on the issue, the North would also be in favor of taking confidence-building measures, Mr. So said, setting out the same case presented by North Korea’s ambassador to the United Nations in New York last month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Repeats Call for Talks', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea: Repeat Call for Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/66b6026a-9e55-5963-9e13-620e1a669595', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66b6026a-9e55-5963-9e13-620e1a669595'}, {'abstract': 'A bill would require Wal-Mart to pay a starting wage that is several dollars above the city’s minimum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/business/dc-council-passes-wage-bill-despite-wal-marts-threats.html', 'snippet': 'A bill would require Wal-Mart to pay a starting wage that is several dollars above the city’s minimum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in urban areas where Wal-Mart has faced stiff opposition, little has slowed its expansion. But the City Council in the District of Columbia is trying to do so, as its passage of a bill that would require the world’s largest retailer to pay a starting wage that is several dollars above the city’s minimum on Wednesday showed. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/business/Walmart/Walmart-thumbLarge