protests and government ministers are on the run or in jail, but since the military ousted President Mohamed Morsi, life has somehow gotten better for many people across Egypt: Gas lines have disappeared, power cuts have stopped and the police have returned to the street.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/jp-plot1/jp-plot1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudden Improvements in Egypt Suggest a Campaign to Undermine Morsi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudden Improvements in Egypt Suggest a Campaign to Undermine Morsi', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:51:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e68b6365-03f1-5002-bbe2-e34eeb784096', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e68b6365-03f1-5002-bbe2-e34eeb784096'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s decision to delay until 2015 a major provision of the law was the subject of a House Ways and Means subcommittee hearing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/us/politics/democrats-shrug-off-delays-and-affirm-support-for-health-law.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s decision to delay until 2015 a major provision of the law was the subject of a House Ways and Means subcommittee hearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Congressional Democrats said Wednesday that they expected to see more delays and snags in President Obama’s efforts to carry out the new health care law, but they affirmed their strong support for the overarching goal of expanded coverage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 1954, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Shrug Off Delays and Affirm Support for Health Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democrats Shrug Off Delays and Affirm Support for Health Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:51:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f44ed6-1872-5b1f-ab54-8bc3bca26b0f', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f44ed6-1872-5b1f-ab54-8bc3bca26b0f'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration’s hopes of persuading Chinese leaders to crack down on the daily barrage of theft and espionage over the Internet are likely to be difficult.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/asia/differences-on-cybertheft-complicate-china-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration’s hopes of persuading Chinese leaders to crack down on the daily barrage of theft and espionage over the Internet are likely to be difficult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. opened annual strategic talks with senior Chinese leaders here on Wednesday by repeating the United States’ accusation that the electronic theft of American intellectual property could undermine the relationship between the world’s two largest economies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Differences on Cybertheft Complicate China Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Differences On Cybertheft Complicate China Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Industrial Espionage', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:56:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c97a3ef-36e5-518d-9b55-2ad15de48a81', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c97a3ef-36e5-518d-9b55-2ad15de48a81'}, {'abstract': 'A stop in Mali on this year’s win-a-trip journey showed just how crucial it is to promote breast-feeding in poorer countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/opinion/kristof-a-free-miracle-food.html', 'snippet': 'A stop in Mali on this year’s win-a-trip journey showed just how crucial it is to promote breast-feeding in poorer countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOPTI, Mali — Can you name a miracle food that is universally available, free and can save children’s lives and maybe even make them smarter?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Free Miracle Food!', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Free Miracle Food!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malnutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T00:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6077aacf-7097-5771-992c-485e724283c8', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6077aacf-7097-5771-992c-485e724283c8'}, {'abstract': 'Parliamentary rule would force Islamists to reach across the aisle and govern with secularists. It could have averted the current crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/opinion/to-save-egypt-drop-the-presidency.html', 'snippet': 'Parliamentary rule would force Islamists to reach across the aisle and govern with secularists. It could have averted the current crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — AS violence escalates, Egypt’s military is trying to bridge a widening political gap by promising a rapid return to civilian rule. But its gesture of accommodation does not get to the heart of the problem: the presidential system, inherited from the Mubarak era, virtually guarantees a repetition of the tragic events of the past year. A democratic breakthrough requires a more fundamental constitutional redesign, in which the contending sides compete for power in a European-style parliamentary system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Save Egypt, Drop the Presidency', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Save Egypt, Drop the Presidency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T01:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Ackerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ackerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/11c23d57-db11-5e1c-9b38-ecc0cdd80a1e', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11c23d57-db11-5e1c-9b38-ecc0cdd80a1e'}, {'abstract': 'Accommodation in the pursuit of unanimity on the Supreme Court can be perilous.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/10/the-cost-of-compromise/', 'snippet': 'Accommodation in the pursuit of unanimity on the Supreme Court can be perilous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his 2011 memoir, “Five Chiefs,” the retired Supreme Court Justice John Paul Stevens offered a mildly eyebrow-raising reflection on Brown v. Board of Education. The landmark school desegregation decision is celebrated not only for its outcome but also for the unanimity that Chief Justice Earl Warren extracted from his wary colleagues. But the price of unanimity may have been too high, Justice Stevens suggested. He observed that the court’s compromise order to desegregate “with all deliberate speed,” rather than immediately, turned into a recipe for hardly any speed at all. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cost of Compromise', 'kicker': 'Linda Greenhouse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsburg, Ruth Bader', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, John Paul', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T01:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a880e5dc-3f3a-5336-9ebd-7d5e619e5adb', 'word_count': 1690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a880e5dc-3f3a-5336-9ebd-7d5e619e5adb'}, {'abstract': 'The George Zimmerman trial has started a valuable discussion about race and justice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/opinion/blow-beyond-the-courtroom.html', 'snippet': 'The George Zimmerman trial has started a valuable discussion about race and justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whatever happens in the George Zimmerman trial, it has produced a valuable and profound dialogue in America about some important issues surrounding race and justice, fear and aggression, and legal guilt and moral culpability.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption'