3/07/11/opinion/clouds-darken-over-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The military is pushing the country toward dangerous instability and a possible civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The military proved disastrously inept when it tried to govern Egypt after the overthrow of Hosni Mubarak in 2011. Now, a week after ousting Mohamed Morsi, the first freely elected president, the military is orchestrating an even more dangerous maneuver. We are deeply fearful that Egypt could devolve into civil war, which would add new trauma to a region already in turmoil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clouds Darken Over Egypt', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clouds Darken Over Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T01:11:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ce9f879-fc46-5301-992d-949366f4a6b5', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ce9f879-fc46-5301-992d-949366f4a6b5'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-Claude Juncker of Luxembourg bowed Wednesday to outrage over revelations of a litany of abuses by his tiny country’s wayward intelligence service and declared that he would step down as prime minister.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/europe/luxembourg-spy-scandal-forces-exit-of-premier.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-Claude Juncker of Luxembourg bowed Wednesday to outrage over revelations of a litany of abuses by his tiny country’s wayward intelligence service and declared that he would step down as prime minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The longest-serving government leader in the European Union, Jean-Claude Juncker of Luxembourg, bowed Wednesday to outrage over revelations of a litany of abuses by his tiny country’s wayward intelligence service and declared that he would step down as prime minister. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Luxembourg Spy Scandal Forces Exit of Premier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Luxembourg Spy Scandal Forces Exit Of Premier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juncker, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higgins, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luxembourg', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T01:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd475bec-c5a8-502e-83b2-ddd56b3543b6', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd475bec-c5a8-502e-83b2-ddd56b3543b6'}, {'abstract': 'A new program succeeds in preventing sexual assault in the Navy, but it is also an anomaly in the midst of a crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/opinion/one-drop-in-military-sexual-violence.html', 'snippet': 'A new program succeeds in preventing sexual assault in the Navy, but it is also an anomaly in the midst of a crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Navy is reporting surprising success in a program to get sailors at Naval Station Great Lakes, near Chicago, to stop raping their comrades. Sexual assaults have been epidemic at the station, where about 40,000 recruits complete boot camp each year. But crimes at the station’s Training Support Center, where about 16,000 sailors receive specialized training, and where most of the assaults occur, have fallen about 60 percent over two years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Drop in Military Sexual Violence', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Drop in Military Sexual Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T01:14:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfea75cc-c3d4-5c84-8d62-ad0521c64ebf', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfea75cc-c3d4-5c84-8d62-ad0521c64ebf'}, {'abstract': 'New rules from the S.E.C. will expose investors to more fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/opinion/youve-been-warned.html', 'snippet': 'New rules from the S.E.C. will expose investors to more fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With two bad rules adopted on Wednesday, the Securities and Exchange Commission has all but invited hucksters, rip-off artists and other bad actors to prey on individual investors. The new rules are another disturbing sign that under the leadership of the new chairwoman, Mary Jo White, the S.E.C. will pursue deregulation at the expense of investor protection. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You’ve Been Warned', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You’ve Been Warned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Mary Jo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Placements (Non-Public Offerings) and Mini IPOs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T01:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bc6252d-42dc-5029-8feb-313b4b642182', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bc6252d-42dc-5029-8feb-313b4b642182'}, {'abstract': 'Why it’s so hard for consumers to fix faulty credit reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/opinion/to-catch-a-creditor.html', 'snippet': 'Why it’s so hard for consumers to fix faulty credit reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1999, Judy Ann Thomas of Elyria, Ohio, applied for a loan. But the bank mixed up her record with the file of a Utah woman named Judith Kendall — their Social Security 