s-it-two-dominating-starts-in-a-row.html', 'snippet': 'Ivan Nova allowed one run in eight innings, and the offense came alive with home runs by Robinson Cano and Lyle Overbay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ivan Nova was coming off perhaps the game of his life. Last week, with his future in the Yankees’ rotation less than certain, he pitched a complete game and struck out 11 Baltimore Orioles in a spot start. He had earned another start, another chance to prove himself, which came Wednesday night against the Kansas City Royals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/CITY-YANKEES-1/CITY-YANKEES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/CITY-YANKEES-1/CITY-YANKEES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/CITY-YANKEES-1/CITY-YANKEES-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/CITY-YANKEES-1/CITY-YANKEES-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/CITY-YANKEES-1/CITY-YANKEES-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/sports/CITY-YANKEES-1/CITY-YANKEES-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur