rticle/5f6749b9-6b3c-5852-a292-f078253410cc'}, {'abstract': 'Ban Ki-moon made his strongest criticism to date of how the Buddhist-majority country has handled the growing problem of mob violence against Muslims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/world/un-secretary-general-warns-myanmar-on-religious-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Ban Ki-moon made his strongest criticism to date of how the Buddhist-majority country has handled the growing problem of mob violence against Muslims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — The secretary general of the United Nations, Ban Ki-moon, warned the Myanmar government on Wednesday of “dangerous polarization” between Buddhists and Muslims and urged the leaders of the Buddhist-majority country to resolve the question of citizenship for the nearly one million stateless Muslims near the border with Bangladesh.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Secretary General Warns Myanmar on Religious Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Leader Warns Myanmar\r\nAbout Religious ‘Polarization’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T05:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/591f2cf3-7a58-5355-90d8-108a95d09106', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/591f2cf3-7a58-5355-90d8-108a95d09106'}, {'abstract': 'The Global Poverty Project benefit in September will include Alicia Keys, Kings of Leon, John Mayer and Stevie Wonder.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/poverty-benefit-concert-set-for-central-park/', 'snippet': 'The Global Poverty Project benefit in September will include Alicia Keys, Kings of Leon, John Mayer and Stevie Wonder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a second year in a row, the Global Poverty Project is mounting a benefit concert in Central Park, on Sept. 28, to urge world leaders at the United Nations to do more to raise the living standards among the world’s poor. This time the show will feature Alicia Keys, Kings of Leon, John Mayer and Stevie Wonder.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poverty Benefit Concert Set for Central Park', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concert for World’s Poor to Return to Central Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Poverty Project', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T06:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b71644-3d47-560b-8a00-8994f19560ee', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b71644-3d47-560b-8a00-8994f19560ee'}, {'abstract': 'The Juvenile Justice Board in Delhi has deferred its verdict against the youngest of the accused in the Delhi gang rape case till July 25.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/verdict-on-juvenile-accused-in-delhi-gang-rape-deferred/', 'snippet': 'The Juvenile Justice Board in Delhi has deferred its verdict against the youngest of the accused in the Delhi gang rape case till July 25.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI – Seven months after six men, including a teenager, allegedly carried out an assault and rape that led to the death of a 23-year-old paramedical student on Dec. 16, the Juvenile Justice Board in Delhi has deferred its verdict against the youngest of the accused till July 25. A magistrate at the Juvenile Justice Board was expected to declare the judgement today, but has delayed the verdict against the accused who was 17 at the time of the crime.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/world/asia/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk/11-rape-protest-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r