he New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, July 11, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T08:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98ce3680-6c3a-5380-a3d8-2aa5e70b5112', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98ce3680-6c3a-5380-a3d8-2aa5e70b5112'}, {'abstract': 'Why do you think Aristides de Sousa Mendes was willing to risk his career and family to help so many people escape Nazi atrocities?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/6-qs-about-the-news-paying-tribute-to-diplomat-who-saved-thousands-from-nazi-persecution/', 'snippet': 'Why do you think Aristides de Sousa Mendes was willing to risk his career and family to help so many people escape Nazi atrocities?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the article, “In Portugal, a Protector of a People Is Honored,” Raphael Minder writes about an effort to honor a diplomat who saved thousands from Nazi persecution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/10/world/0710PORTUGAL-LN/0710PORTUGAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | Paying Tribute to a Diplomat Who Saved Thousands from Nazi Persecution', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a7a5ba-2f38-5de3-b686-52c9f6822cd1', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a7a5ba-2f38-5de3-b686-52c9f6822cd1'}, {'abstract': 'How a country that banned golf has become an unlikely incubator for the wunderkinds of the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/magazine/golf-in-china-is-younger-than-tiger-woods-but-growing-up-fast.html', 'snippet': 'How a country that banned golf has become an unlikely incubator for the wunderkinds of the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Xie Chengfeng had a fever. Otherwise, the Chinese golfer would have been driving his orange coupe to the practice range on this June morning rather than languishing in bed, cold towel on his forehead, in his four-story mansion. Five years ago, Xie (pronounced “shee-eh”) and his family uprooted themselves and moved to Mission Hills, a sprawling golf resort in the southern Chinese city of Shenzhen for just one purpose: so he could become the next Tiger Woods.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 763}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 806, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1784, 'width': 1403, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/magazine/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP/14golf_ss-slide-RQQP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type