 government tax fraud, died four years ago in a Russian prison after being denied proper medical care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The steel cage reserved for the defendants was empty Thursday, which was not surprising since one of them is dead and the other lives in London. As the judge, his voice nearly inaudible, read out his verdict, one of the main defense lawyers paid no attention, tapping nonchalantly on his tablet computer instead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/europe/12magnitsky/12magnitsky-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dead Lawyer, a Kremlin Critic, Is Found Guilty of Tax Evasion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dead Lawyer, a Kremlin Critic, Is Found Guilty of Tax Evasion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magnitsky, Sergei L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzenhorn, David M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T12:46:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17abc9cf-f328-5a14-b0d6-72707657e1e3', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17abc9cf-f328-5a14-b0d6-72707657e1e3'}, {'abstract': 'The giant software company is creating four new divisions and reassigning nearly every senior executive as it tries to create timely products that consumers want.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/technology/microsoft-revamps-structure-and-management.html', 'snippet': 'The giant software company is creating four new divisions and reassigning nearly every senior executive as it tries to create timely products that consumers want.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — A couple of years ago, a satirical set of diagrams depicting the organization of Amazon, Apple, Facebook and other technology companies made the rounds on the Internet. The chart for Microsoft showed several isolated pyramids representing its divisions, each with a cartoon pistol aimed at the other.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/business/MICROSOFT/MICROSOFT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft Overhauls, the Apple Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Microsoft Overhauls, the Apple Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T13:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64490d92-5e2a-5066-8cea-729e9dc1799f', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64490d92-5e2a-5066-8cea-729e9dc1799f'}, {'abstract': 'Any educational institution at the post-high school/university level should emphasize the importance of the humanities in terms of expanding a student’s intellect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/global/humanities-and-the-intellect.html', 'snippet': 'Any educational institution at the post-high school/university level should emphasize the importance of the humanities in terms of expanding a student’s intellect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regarding “Resilience of the humanities” (July 5): Scott Saul states that, “Many of our students struggle to think and write with precision, and we struggle to teach them the mechanics of good writing.” I respectfully suggest that any educational institution at the post-high school/university level in any country should emphasize the importance of the humanities in terms of expanding a student’s intellect, by reference to the study of philosophy in particular, and the application of philosophical methods to any academic discipline, be it the study of medicine or law or business, indeed any faculty that requires critical and analytical thinking and the forensic critique of information. Perhaps such an approach would be helpful to students, and also assist educators in their attempts to successfully teach students how to think and write with precision?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humanities and the Intellect', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T13:16:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaef643e-c86b-5645-b9d0-7dff34bf8235', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaef643e-c86b-5645-b9d0-7dff34bf8235'}, {'abstract': 'Online file storage services like Dropbox let you share files with people who do not have an account with the company.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/qa-sharing-files-with-dropbox/', 'snippet': 'Online file storage services like Dropbox let you share files with people who do not have an account with the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Sharing Files With Dropbox', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dropbox Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T13:19:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bb82d75-2114-538f-ae40-3a5c6cc57377', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bb82d75-2114-538f-ae40-3a5c6cc57377'}, {'abstract': 'On a party-line vote, the House forced through a stalled farm bill, despite Democratic objections that stripping the food stamp program would leave poor Americans without a safety net.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/us/politics/house-bill-would-split-farm-and-food-stamp-programs.html', 'snippet': 'On a party-line vote, the House forced through a stalled farm bill, despite Democratic objections that stripping the food stamp program would leave poor Americans without a safety net.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Republicans muscled a pared-back agriculture bill through the House on Thursday, stripping out the food stamp program to satisfy recalcitrant conservatives but losing what little Democratic support the bill had when it failed last month. It was the first time food stamps had not been a part of the farm bill since 1973.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/us/FARM/FARM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/us/FARM/FARM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/us/FARM/FARM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/us/FARM/FARM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legac