major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF COUNTRY MUSIC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T16:12:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf14e52-207a-58f1-bbad-bf111e2d6140', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf14e52-207a-58f1-bbad-bf111e2d6140'}, {'abstract': 'It has been a vertigo-inducing baseball season so far, with the Biogenesis scandal, the rise of the Pirates, the fall of the Giants and the excitement over Yasiel Puig.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/sports/baseball-needs-its-break-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'It has been a vertigo-inducing baseball season so far, with the Biogenesis scandal, the rise of the Pirates, the fall of the Giants and the excitement over Yasiel Puig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The coming All-Star break could not come at a better time for baseball. For the ruling cabal, its corporate-sponsored bacchanalia cannot come often enough, particularly with that nasty Biogenesis scandal percolating in the background and Alex Rodriguez still trying to swing a bat somewhere (in Tampa, in, ahem, rehab). But even the rest of us need a chance to stop and look around. After all, the first half has been downright disorienting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/12leading/12leading-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Baseball Needs Its Break', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Puig, Yasiel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valenzuela, Fernando', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaudin, Chad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortiz, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Marshall', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donaldson, Josh (1985- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T16:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa2b714-9c9b-5751-badd-3aa68f256b19', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa2b714-9c9b-5751-badd-3aa68f256b19'}, {'abstract': 'New evidence explains why the Netherlands tried to get freedmen to colonize Suriname.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/hollands-plan-for-americas-slaves/', 'snippet': 'New evidence explains why the Netherlands tried to get freedmen to colonize Suriname.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1863, American blacks were not the only enslaved people with emancipation on the mind. On the northeastern coast of South America, in the Dutch colony of Suriname, some 30,000 slaves also prepared for their day of freedom, which would arrive with the government’s emancipation mandate of July 1, 1863, six months after Lincoln issued the Emancipation Proclamation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holland’s Plan for America’s Slaves', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hague (Netherlands)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Suriname', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T16:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. Douma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Douma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89381a22-7d12-5001-a446-ff5a01f7254d', 'word_count': 1361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89381a22-7d12-5001-a446-ff5a01f7254d'}, {'abstract': 'Though he had previously said that stage projects required him to turn down the offer, Mr. Mendes said that the Bond producers had given him “the time I need to honor all my theater commitments.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/sam-mendes-will-direct-new-james-bond-movie-after-all/', 'snippet': 'Though he had previously said that stage projects required him to turn down the offer, Mr. Mendes said that the Bond producers had given him “the time I need to honor all my theater commitments.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As they say in the movies, James Bond will return — and so, too, will the director Sam Mendes, who will oversee that long-lived secret agent’s next cinematic adventure, despite a previous declaration that he had passed on the film project. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/mendes/mendes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/mendes/mendes-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/mendes/mendes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/11/arts/mendes/mendes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna