ta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6a69c3e-6e06-54c0-b30f-0b4673a144fd', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6a69c3e-6e06-54c0-b30f-0b4673a144fd'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/the-gun-report-july-11-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember “The Ex,” a mannequin shooting target in the likeness of a bleeding woman who bleeds fake blood when shot? Zombie Industries, an N.R.A. convention vendor also famous for marketing a target that resembles President Obama, has now rolled out a target in the likeness of a zombie gun lobbyist. Each “zombie” comes with a back story and a reason to shoot at them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: July 11, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T16:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbd08229-d58a-5757-b7c7-c4a441ac4f25', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbd08229-d58a-5757-b7c7-c4a441ac4f25'}, {'abstract': 'With lighter textures and and layers, a selection of summer pieces that can work with warm days and cool nights.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/market-report-prints-and-textures-elevate-surfer-separates/', 'snippet': 'With lighter textures and and layers, a selection of summer pieces that can work with warm days and cool nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taking cues from the surfer girls of summer, designers are offering easy-to-wear pieces that transition from sweltering daytime highs to cool nights. The clever combinations of texture (lace slip-on sneakers, calf hair backpacks) and graphic prints — on everything from sunnies to hoodies — will appeal to the California beach brigade and city dwellers alike.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | Prints and Textures Elevate Surfer Separates', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T16:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/254e6672-6a78-5bdf-b208-3e731099075c', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/254e6672-6a78-5bdf-b208-3e731099075c'}, {'abstract': 'At 29, she is reaching new career heights, less than a decade after she got a foothold in television as an intern on “Saturday Night Live.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/movies/aubrey-plaza-is-dangerously-funny.html', 'snippet': 'At 29, she is reaching new career heights, less than a decade after she got a foothold in television as an intern on “Saturday Night Live.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hudson, N.Y. — “If anyone asks,” Aubrey Plaza said, “you’re my cousin Nina.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/