nyt://video/a597c3ef-82fb-5952-81a3-dfb95d0f13cb'}, {'abstract': 'A cleverly designed jewelry and lifestyle shop comes to the eastern end of Long Island for the summer.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/in-store-montauks-new-one-stop-lifestyle-shop/', 'snippet': 'A cleverly designed jewelry and lifestyle shop comes to the eastern end of Long Island for the summer.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’ve always wanted to do a little hotel store with cool things that you need and things you didn’t know you need,” explained Lori Leven of her latest venture, Love Adorned: Summer Session, a pop-up shop at Ruschmeyer’s, the summer-camp-like hotel in Montauk, N.Y. While she’d flirted with the idea of opening a location of Love Adorned, her thoughtfully curated jewelry and lifestyle shop, on the eastern tip of Long Island for a while, Leven admitted that the spot posed challenges she hadn’t faced at her Amagansett or Manhattan locations — namely, finding a way to secure the merchandise when the shop was closed but the lobby was still bustling. “We came up with the idea of making cabinets reminiscent of old train cases that we could completely close down and lock at night and easily open to reveal the goods in the morning,” she said. Those goods run the gamut from basic necessities (toothpaste and Tylenol) to RTH sweatshirts, leather bandannas from Japan, children’s moccasins, one-of-a-kind vintage objects like compasses and hand-carved penknives, and, of course, jewelry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | Montauk’s New One-Stop Lifestyle Shop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T17:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 