tml', 'snippet': 'The three tales in “Pawn Shop Chronicles” involve robbery, meth and an Elvis impersonator.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hee Haw” meets “Pulp Fiction” at the meth lab: That describes the style of “Pawn Shop Chronicles,” a hillbilly grindhouse yawp of a movie that belches in your face and leaves a sour stink. The heart of this carny show posing as a film is General Lee’s Pawn Shop, whose proprietor (Vincent D’Onofrio) and his pal (Chi McBride) while away the afternoons arguing about the possibility of an African-American Santa Claus. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/PAWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/PAWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/PAWN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/PAWN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/12PAWN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/12PAWN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12PAWN_SPAN/12PAWN_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Simple Swap or Sale? Not Here', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Simple Swap or Sale? Not Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pawn Shop Chronicles (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kramer, Wayne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Onofrio, Vincent", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T19:35:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c51faba0-3984-507f-8058-8134e445e90c', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c51faba0-3984-507f-8058-8134e445e90c'}, {'abstract': 'In “Crystal Fairy,” two young Americans attend a coke-and-pot-fueled party and go on a road trip with three Chilean brothers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/movies/in-crystal-fairy-young-ustourists-aim-for-the-mystical.html', 'snippet': 'In “Crystal Fairy,” two young Americans attend a coke-and-pot-fueled party and go on a road trip with three Chilean brothers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title character of “Crystal Fairy,” Sebastián Silva’s small, lovely road movie, is the assumed name of a free-spirited latter-day hippie visiting Chile. She attaches herself to another American tourist, Jamie (Michael Cera), after he casually invites her to join him and his friends. Perfectly played by Gaby Hoffmann, Crystal Fairy has all the hallmarks of a professed earth mother holding the keys to truth, peace, love and wisdom. She has her charms, but like many such know-it-alls, she can be overbearing and preachy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CRYSTAL_SPAN/12CRYSTAL_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Psychedelic Euphoria Wears Off in the Desert', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Psychedelic Euphoria Wears Off in the Desert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cera, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Crystal Fairy (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silva, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T19:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/431757b2-5901-502f-b30e-611280dd2bd9', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/431757b2-5901-502f-b30e-611280dd2bd9'}, {'abstract': 'The prolific English literary critic Terry Eagleton follows well-worn paths in “Across the Pond: An Englishman’s View of America” and “How to Read Literature.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/books/in-across-the-pond-terry-eagleton-explains-the-us.html', 'snippet': 'The prolific English literary critic Terry Eagleton follows well-worn paths in “Across the Pond: An Englishman’s View of America” and “How to Read Literature.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several years I worked under a literary editor who, whenever he encountered a new volume he thought had little reason to exist, would hold it aloft and announce, his voice bright with sarcasm, “Well, here’s a necessary book.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 546}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 932, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1864, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America for Dummies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America For Dummies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eagleton, Terry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T19:40:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/42538f48-0721-504f-8d7b-7dd1261810d7', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42538f48-0721-504f-8d7b-7dd1261810d7'}, {'abstract': 'The latest maneuver by the activist investor Carl Icahn to try to get a higher payout for his shares in Dell Inc. may not work out. But don’t write him off just yet.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/in-battle-over-dells-fate-dont-underestimate-carl-icahn/', 'snippet': 'The latest maneuver by the activist investor Carl Icahn to try to get a higher payout for his shares in Dell Inc. may not work out. But don’t write him off just yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Negotiation gurus say that if you think your opponent is foolish or stupid, it may well be you who is out-negotiated. I generally shrug off this type of pop business advice, but when we are talking about Carl C. Icahn, the investor whom I have likened to a Wile E. Coyote, it may be a wise adage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Battle Over Dell’s Fate, Don’t Underestimate Carl Icahn', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Asset Management', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T19:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8936a7c-483f-5a1a-ab05-de06ec3a3b4e', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8936a7c-483f-5a1a-ab05-de06ec3a3b4e'}, {'abstract': 'Questions about  favoritism among friends, competitive behavior and other social situations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/fashion/when-a-finders-fee-is-mia.html', 'snippet': 'Questions about  favoritism among friends, competitive behavior and other social situations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An acquaintance promised my friend $20,000 in cash if my friend found her a house to buy in our neighborhood without using a broker. After some effort, my friend came through and found a house. The acquaintance will be closing on it soon, having negotiated a much better price with the seller in the absence of a broker’s fees. She thanked my friend with a Bundt cake and three dozen cookies. But the acquaintance hasn’t mentioned the $20,000 in months, and my friend hasn’t, either. Any tips on getting this woman to live up to her promise?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail