e country on Thursday by calling for a new coalition government and early elections, rather than maintaining the administration of Prime Minister Pedro Passos Coelho, which has been strained by differences over its austerity policies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portugal’s President Calls for Early Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Portugal: A Call for Early Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Passos Coelho, Pedro', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T19:55:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8965975-d053-51e6-8d7b-077cf29e8813', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8965975-d053-51e6-8d7b-077cf29e8813'}, {'abstract': 'Nemcatacoa Teatro, a troupe of Colombian street performers, paraded through a Pelham Bay Park playground on Wednesday with stilts and striking makeup, and the children followed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/arts/dance/nemcatacoa-teatro-brings-stilts-to-a-playground.html', 'snippet': 'Nemcatacoa Teatro, a troupe of Colombian street performers, paraded through a Pelham Bay Park playground on Wednesday with stilts and striking makeup, and the children followed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They came for our children. The strange, tall creatures paraded through the playground, accompanied by panpipes. First the children screamed. Then they followed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12CIRCUS1_SPAN/CIRCUS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pied Pipers of Bogotá Cast a Spell in the Bronx', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pied Pipers of Bogotá Cast a Spell in the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pelham Bay Park (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nemcatacoa Teatro', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Parks Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T19:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/db882748-4629-56bf-a67a-4b65404d68a2', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db882748-4629-56bf-a67a-4b65404d68a2'}, {'abstract': '“Julius Caesar,” a calypso “Taming of the Shrew” and short plays by Bertolt Brecht are among the free theater productions being presented outdoors this weekend in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/nyregion/free-theater-in-the-parks-and-parking-lot.html', 'snippet': '“Julius Caesar,” a calypso “Taming of the Shrew” and short plays by Bertolt Brecht are among the free theater productions being presented outdoors this weekend in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When even air-conditioning can’t beat the city heat, outdoor activities are essential to staying sane. Spurred by a younger, baseball-crazed housemate, the Miser has been frequenting the ballparks of the Brooklyn Cyclones and Staten Island Yankees. But for those more interested in soliloquies and social criticism than in balks and bunts, and lacking the time or energy to wait in line for Shakespeare in the Park tickets, plays from both the classical and modern canons are available in affordable outdoor productions all over the city this weekend.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Theater in the Park