tempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soho House', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Nicholas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cachay, Sylvie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T21:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3453e04e-7c62-57b9-adab-6a7d245671e3', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3453e04e-7c62-57b9-adab-6a7d245671e3'}, {'abstract': '“Grown Ups 2” features many of the same former “Saturday Night Live” stars as “Grown Ups,” but they’ve moved to New England from Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/movies/adam-sandler-and-snl-alumni-return-in-grown-ups-2.html', 'snippet': '“Grown Ups 2” features many of the same former “Saturday Night Live” stars as “Grown Ups,” but they’ve moved to New England from Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The party’s over, fellas,” says Adam Sandler’s character, Lenny, to his buddies in “Grown Ups 2.” “We’re irrelevant.” And though the box office may disagree, his words aren’t far from the truth. The first “Grown Ups,” in 2010, grossed more than $271 million worldwide; the sequel will probably rival that amount, reaping lavish dividends for Mr. Sandler and his co-stars, many of them his fellow “Saturday Night Live” alumni. Once again Mr. Sandler milks middle age for lucre, nostalgia and clunky, ham-fisted humor. But he has cause for concern. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cr