ndy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3e71e1a-9e2e-556a-b960-5bb2f5c0fc61', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3e71e1a-9e2e-556a-b960-5bb2f5c0fc61'}, {'abstract': 'The National Transportation Safety Board is looking at the flight crew’s inputs into the autopilot and other cockpit automation systems during Asiana Flight 214’s final minutes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/us/safety-board-reconstructing-crew-actions-shortly-before-crash.html', 'snippet': 'The National Transportation Safety Board is looking at the flight crew’s inputs into the autopilot and other cockpit automation systems during Asiana Flight 214’s final minutes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — In a critical period of nearly 30 seconds shortly before impact, none of the three pilots in the cockpit of the Asiana jet that crashed here on Saturday mentioned the airspeed of their Boeing 777, the chairwoman of the National Transportation Safety Board said Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safety Board Reconstructs Crew Actions Before Crash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safety Board Reconstructs Crew Actions Before Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asiana Airlines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco International Airport', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T21:13:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a18f9b3-fc31-57c2-afb1-d39d9e5b7742', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a18f9b3-fc31-57c2-afb1-d39d9e5b7742'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Hot Flashes,” a group of plucky middle-aged Texas women form a basketball team to raise money for breast cancer prevention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/movies/in-the-hot-flashes-brooke-shields-leads-a-team.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Hot Flashes,” a group of plucky middle-aged Texas women form a basketball team to raise money for breast cancer prevention.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Hot Flashes,” an agreeably silly buddy comedy with a positive message, belongs to the chipper school of Southern-fried entertainment in which can-do gals of a certain age band together for community service and self-empowerment. In the fictional town of Burning Bush, Tex., Beth (Brooke Shields), who is experiencing early signs of menopause, forms a women’s basketball team to raise money for a mobile breast-screening unit. She pressures her out-of-shape friends to compete with the town’s championship high school team in a charity tournament.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12HOT_SPAN/HOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/12HOT_SPAN/HOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty