'nyt://article/089c41c8-572b-5cd1-a759-50512e4f72e8'}, {'abstract': 'Jefferson R. Burdick collected 30,000 baseball cards from the sport’s early years to take his mind off his arthritis. Now, 600 of them are on display at the Met.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/arts/design/metropolitan-museum-opens-huge-show-of-baseball-cards.html', 'snippet': 'Jefferson R. Burdick collected 30,000 baseball cards from the sport’s early years to take his mind off his arthritis. Now, 600 of them are on display at the Met.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE annual All-Star Game is scheduled to take place on Tuesday at that crime scene in Queens known as Citi Field, where the New York Mets routinely commit misdemeanor assaults on the heart. A night of celebrity baseball, neatly wrapped in red, white and blue bunting, might be just the thing to clean the slate and help the Mets see the light, and maybe a fastball or two.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/design/12legends_337/12legends_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/arts/design/12legends_337/12legends_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rascals and Heroes, Before the Babe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rascals and Heroes, Before the Babe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trading Cards', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 6, 'major'