rom around the world and fills the town with music, dancing and merriment. It is the subject of “Brasslands,” a 2013 documentary by the Meerkat Media Collective, an American group, that will be screened at 8:30 p.m. at a free event at Brookfield Place Plaza, 220 Vesey Street, near West Street, Lower Manhattan. (Below, Demiran Cerimovic, a Roma trumpeter, in a scene from the movie.) Presented by Arts Brookfield and Rooftop Films as part of the River to River festival, the evening — also called “Brasslands” — begins at 6:30 p.m. with music by four American brass bands, including Zlatne Uste, which also appears in the film. (In an event, above, featured in the movie, fans surround musicians at a Balkan music festival last year at a Brooklyn ballroom.) Doors open at 6 p.m. Although some seating will be available, spectators are encouraged to provide their own. More details can be found at rooftopfilms.com. There is sure to be dancing in the aisles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for July 12-18', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T22:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso and Lori Holcomb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf847b0a-fd67-5519-9e1d-ad4780ec3121', 'word_count': 3015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf847b0a-fd67-5519-9e1d-ad4780ec3121'}, {'abstract': 'T