ne reason to visit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few things are more pleasant than a water view while dining, especially in summertime. And at the new Rive Bistro in Westport, it’s almost impossible not to have a water view, no matter where you are seated. Not only does the restaurant face the Saugatuck River, with wide windows on three sides, but the screened patio, with a long banquette, also has a head-on river view. If you happen to be there in the early evening, you may have the pleasure of watching scullers skim past.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINECT2/14DINECT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'French Fare With Enticing Vistas', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French Fare With Enticing Vistas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westport (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rive Bistro (Westport, Conn, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T22:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f24f0a82-2a09-54fb-be0d-598862533d7f', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f24f0a82-2a09-54fb-be0d-598862533d7f'}, {'abstract': 'Working in the oil fields two weeks at a time isn’t conducive to a long-term relationship, but still men try, talking on their cellphones in their pickup trucks, and avoiding long goodbyes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/fashion/a-life-that-can-fracture-a-relationship.html', 'snippet': 'Working in the oil fields two weeks at a time isn’t conducive to a long-term relationship, but still men try, talking on their cellphones in their pickup trucks, and avoiding long goodbyes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We live in the world of hydraulic fracturing, the dozen of us, for two weeks at a time, 14 hours a day, shuffling the heavy iron in the Rube Goldberg maze of six-inch pipes connecting a two-acre artificial pond to eight natural gas wells. Five times a day the pond is drained by 10 huge diesel-powered pumps and then refilled by an endless line of water trucks.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 662}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 928, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1856, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/fashion/14MODERNLOVE/14MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life That Can Fracture a Relationship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Life That Can Fracture a Relationship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T22:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/def1a44d-c62c-525c-ab7d-38467372ecc9', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/def1a44d-c62c-525c-ab7d-38467372ecc9'}, {'abstract': 'The multi-hyphenate artist and the Buzzfeed founder chat about how people interact, share content and present themselves online.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/in-conversation-miranda-july-and-jonah-peretti-on-reading-other-peoples-e-mail/', 'snippet': 'The multi-hyphenate artist and the Buzzfeed founder chat about how people interact, share content and present themselves online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For her latest project, We Think Alone, the filmmaker, artist and author Miranda July took other people’s e-mail as her raw material. Earlier this month, she launched a service that compiles personal e-mails sent by noteworthy figures to other people in their lives. The e-mailers, all chosen by July, include the NBA legend Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, the “Girls” creator Lena Dunham, the actress Kirsten Dunst, the writer Sheila Heti, the Rodarte designers Kate and Laura Mulleavy and the photographer Catherine Opie. Their correspondence arrives in subscribers’ inboxes every Monday for 20 weeks, grouped around a single topic; so far, they’ve dealt with money and advice. Reading these one-sided missives one after the next offers a voyeuristic, occasionally enlightening portrait of the ways people use e-mail to communicate in 2013.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miranda July and Jonah Peretti on Reading Other People’s E-Mail', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Fashion: Couture Diary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'July, Miranda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peretti, Jonah H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BuzzFeed Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-11T22:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Ashlock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ashlock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3650553f-28e3-5699-876f-8e49a0e2f6af', 'word_count': 1843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3650553f-28e3-5699-876f-8e49a0e2f6af'}, {'abstract': 'Seven Israeli soldiers who detained a 5-year-old Palestinian boy for rock-throwing this week in the West Bank city of Hebron have been cleared of any wrongdoing by their superiors, after a review of video of the incident.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/israeli-army-clears-soldiers-who-detained-child-for-throwing-rock-at-settlers-car/', 'snippet': 'Seven Israeli soldiers who detained a 5-year-old Palestinian boy for rock-throwing this week in the West Bank city of Hebron have been cleared of any wrongdoing by their superiors, after a review of video of the incident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven Israeli soldiers who detained a 5-year-old Palestinian boy for rock-throwing this week in the West Bank city of Hebron have been cleared of any wrongdoing by their superiors, after a review of video of the incident published on Thu