ports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb3f0b44-2254-5218-a073-029cdcb36dbd', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb3f0b44-2254-5218-a073-029cdcb36dbd'}, {'abstract': 'Empanadas have become more and more popular, and New Jersey chefs are experimenting with dozens of different varieties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/nyregion/pastries-filled-every-which-way.html', 'snippet': 'Empanadas have become more and more popular, and New Jersey chefs are experimenting with dozens of different varieties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenny Candelaria of Hackensack recently vacationed in Greece. While there, he said, he ate tomatoes stuffed with feta and garlic, fava beans with tzatziki dipping sauce and several lamb dishes. And he never stopped thinking about how he might convert all those dishes into empanadas back home. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINENJ1/14DINENJ1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINENJ1/14DINENJ1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINENJ1/14DINENJ1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14DINENJ1/14DINENJ1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1248, 'w