es.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/the-charade-of-darrell-issa/', 'snippet': 'The California congressman is the monster that Washington has created for our times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, this guy who made a stink-pile of money in the car alarm business, and had some youthful trouble with the law over auto-related liberties, gets the break he’s been waiting for after Republicans win control of the House in 2010. He’s given the keys to the biggest Caddie in Congress: the main oversight committee. It’s loaded with everything — subpoena power, an overhead cam worth of auditors and investigators, a hyperkinetic staff devoted to keeping shine on the boss.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Charade of Darrell Issa', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b101c17-710c-5342-97a1-454e243b37bb', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b101c17-710c-5342-97a1-454e243b37bb'}, {'abstract': 'The federal judge, Royce C. Lamberth, portrayed the procedure as unnecessary and intended to “actively discourage” meetings between detainees and their lawyers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/us/judge-halts-groin-searches-at-guantanamo-calling-them-abhorrent-to-muslims.html', 'snippet': 'The federal judge, Royce C. Lamberth, portrayed the procedure as unnecessary and intended to “actively discourage” meetings between detainees and their lawyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A federal judge on Thursday ordered the military to stop touching the groins of detainees at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, when they are moved from their cells to speak with lawyers. The procedure had led some prisoners to stop meeting with or calling their lawyers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Halts Groin Searches at Guantánamo, Calling Them Abhorrent to Muslims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Orders Halt to Groin Searches at Guantánamo, Citing Offense to Muslims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamberth, Royce C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb0709b-d293-5392-9550-2319d8de15b9', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb0709b-d293-5392-9550-2319d8de15b9'}, {'abstract': 'Faulty urban policies, shoddy construction and unchecked real-estate speculation are to blame for recent building collapses in Mumbai.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/boom-and-bust-at-the-same-time.html', 'snippet': 'Faulty urban policies, shoddy construction and unchecked real-estate speculation are to blame for recent building collapses in Mumbai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI, India — A RECENT wave of building collapses has brought attention to this city’s large number of poorly built structures. It feels as if every week brings fresh reports of a new disaster. The death toll is expected to rise with the monsoons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 754}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1935, 'width': 1539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/opinion/0712OPEDholder/0712OPEDholder-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boom and Bust at the Same Time', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boom and Bust At the Same Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Echanove, Matias', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Srivastava, Rahul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matias Echanove and Rahul Srivastava', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matias', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Echanove', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rahul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Srivastava', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc23cdf-f85e-56a9-9bc1-7b08d237a5f8', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc23cdf-f85e-56a9-9bc1-7b08d237a5f8'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Elizabeth Warren and Senator John McCain are sponsoring a 21st-century version of the Glass-Steagall Act from the 1930s, to break up large banks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/11/senators-introduce-bill-to-separate-trading-activities-from-big-banks/', 'snippet': 'Senator Elizabeth Warren and Senator John McCain are sponsoring a 21st-century version of the Glass-Steagall Act from the 1930s, to break up large banks.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:32 a.m. | Updated Senator Elizabeth Warren on Thursday introduced an aggressive piece of legislation that intends to take the financial industry back to an era when there was a strict divide between traditional banking and speculative activities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senators Introduce Bill to Separate Trading Activities From Big Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senators Introduce Bill to Separate Trading Activities From Big Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4178e140-e9df-51a2-96bc-422b838e02ca', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4178e140-e9df-51a2-96bc-422b838e02ca'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t dismiss the military unit that brings families closure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/missing-in-action-but-not-forever.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t dismiss the military unit that brings families closure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — THE American military’s commitment to “leave no man behind” is unmatched in the world. Few countries make an organized effort to find the remains of their long-lost troops, and on battlefields like Peleliu, an island in the Pacific, the skeletons of Japanese soldiers still crouch at the mouths of caves with their helmets and boots half-buried in seven decades of mud. Yet since World War I, our military has worked to locate every fallen service member and to bring their remains — along with some closure — back home to mourning families.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing in Action, but Not Forever', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missing in Action, but Not Forever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hylton, Wil S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missing in Action', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint POW/MIA Accounting Command', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wil S. Hylton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wil', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Hylton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d422d5d-7ae5-5e81-aa95-83f9a8d3445d', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d422d5d-7ae5-5e81-aa95-83f9a8d3445d'}, {'abstract': 'The baseball tradition of keeping a scorecard is facing increasing competition from ballpark attractions and hand-held electronic devices, but it has persisted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/sports/baseball/who-scores-games-by-hand-anymore.html', 'snippet': 'The baseball tradition of keeping a scorecard is facing increasing competition from ballpark attractions and hand-held electronic devices, but it has persisted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing Bruce Levy did upon recent entry into Yankee Stadium while accompanied by his in-laws and teenage son was to purchase a program in the area of the concourse behind home plate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/sports/Y-SCORECARD-1/Y-SCORECARD-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Scores Games by Hand Anymore?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who’s Keeping Score?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chadwick, Henry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:06:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12b8cdd8-a176-5617-97c6-53a1cffa907e', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12b8cdd8-a176-5617-97c6-53a1cffa907e'}, {'abstract': 'The likelihood that House Republicans will block immigration reform counteracts the four biggest conservative objectives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/brooks-pass-the-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The likelihood that House Republicans will block immigration reform counteracts the four biggest conservative objectives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s beginning to look as though we’re not going to get an immigration reform law this year. House Republicans are moving in a direction that will probably be unacceptable to the Senate majority and the White House. Conservative commentators like my friends Bill Kristol and Rich Lowry are arguing that the status quo is better than the comprehensive approach passed by the Senate. The whole effort is in peril. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pass the Bill!', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pass The Bill!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:07:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b9fe232-4010-581a-a1ab-3553e1a4db07', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b9fe232-4010-581a-a1ab-3553e1a4db07'}, {'abstract': 'Scientifically, it is very unlikely that marijuana use caused aggression in the Trayvon Martin case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/reefer-madness-an-unfortunate-redux.html', 'snippet': 'Scientifically, it is very unlikely that marijuana use caused aggression in the Trayvon Martin case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Was Trayvon Martin aggressive and paranoid from smoking marijuana, and did that lead him to attack George Zimmerman? That’s what lawyers for Mr. Zimmerman are arguing. He is on trial for killing Mr. Martin, but claims he acted in self-defense, and the judge in the racially charged, nationally followed case decided earlier this week that the jury could be presented with Mr. Martin’s toxicology report, which shows that he had marijuana in his system. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reefer Madness, an Unfortunate Redux', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reefer Madness, an Unfortunate Redux', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:08:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl L. Hart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Hart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/763e89f8-c76b-5187-9919-771d69e182f0', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/763e89f8-c76b-5187-9919-771d69e182f0'}, {'abstract': 'These are tough times for members of the conservative intelligentsia. And their latest idea for regaining power is bunk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/krugman-delusions-of-populism.html', 'snippet': 'These are tough times for members of the conservative intelligentsia. And their latest idea for regaining power is bunk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you heard about “libertarian populism” yet? If not, you will. It will surely be touted all over the airwaves and the opinion pages by the same kind of people who assured you, a few years ago, that Representative Paul Ryan was the very model of a Serious, Honest Conservative. So let me make a helpful public service announcement: It’s bunk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Delusions of Populism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delusions Of Populism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libertarianism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:10:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ff262b9-ce74-5be6-b3c1-1e7c721cea80', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ff262b9-ce74-5be6-b3c1-1e7c721cea80'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement by Senator David Vitter to drop his threat of a filibuster of Gina McCarthy is good news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/the-epa-may-get-a-boss-after-all.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement by Senator David Vitter to drop his threat of a filibuster of Gina McCarthy is good news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, Senator David Vitter, a Louisiana Republican, said that he would drop his threat of a filibuster and allow an up-or-down vote on Gina McCarthy, President Obama’s nominee to lead the Environmental Protection Agency. This is welcome news, not just for the agency but for the planet. More than any other federal official, Ms. McCarthy will be responsible for carrying out Mr. Obama’s promise to confront the threat of climate change. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The E.P.A. May Get a Boss After all', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The E.P.A. May Get a Boss After all ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Gina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitter, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9552c03b-3412-5b8a-9168-4dd99820267e', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9552c03b-3412-5b8a-9168-4dd99820267e'}, {'abstract': 'The wheels of the machinery of death in Georgia keep turning, greased by a strict federal law that prevents prisoners from filing multiple appeals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/last-chance-for-warren-hill.html', 'snippet': 'The wheels of the machinery of death in Georgia keep turning, greased by a strict federal law that prevents prisoners from filing multiple appeals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justice Harry Blackmun surely would have confronted the case of Warren Lee Hill Jr. — whom the state of Georgia plans to execute Monday evening — by recalling perhaps his most famous dissent. “From this day forward,” he wrote in a 1994 Supreme Court case, “I no longer shall tinker with the machinery of death.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Chance for Warren Hill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Chance for Warren Hill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Warren Lee Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Retardation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:13:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/04b8a6cd-ee6c-5840-aeeb-bb2a73605d2d', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b8a6cd-ee6c-5840-aeeb-bb2a73605d2d'}, {'abstract': 'The Guardian reports the company provided the National Security Agency with up-to-date access to its customer data whenever it changed its encryption and related technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/us/report-indicates-more-extensive-cooperation-by-microsoft-on-surveillance.html', 'snippet': 'The Guardian reports the company provided the National Security Agency with up-to-date access to its customer data whenever it changed its encryption and related technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Microsoft has collaborated with the National Security Agency more extensively than it previously acknowledged, providing the spy agency with up-to-date access to its customer data whenever the company changes its encryption and related software technology, according to a new report based on disclosures by the former N.S.A. contractor Edward J. Snowden. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/us/NSA/NSA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/us/NSA/NSA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 769}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/us/NSA/NSA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/us/NSA/NSA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Indicates More Extensive Cooperation by Microsoft on Surveillance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Indicates More Extensive Cooperation by Microsoft on Surveillance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T01:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Risen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Risen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19486e58-42de-58b9-87a3-05d344cda8fb', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19486e58-42de-58b9-87a3-05d344cda8fb'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans resist compromising their extreme positions and retreat further and further from the national mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/opinion/in-the-house-a-refusal-to-govern.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans resist compromising their extreme positions and retreat further and further from the national mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On two crucial issues this week, the extremists who dominate the Republican majority in the House of Representatives made it clear how little interest they have in the future prosperity of their country, or its reputation for fairness and decency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the House, a Refusal to Govern', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the H