ment_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Hoinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b66509cc-4355-5903-8cf4-ec92f2271c7e', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b66509cc-4355-5903-8cf4-ec92f2271c7e'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bob Filner refused to resign in response to sexual harassment accusations leveled by prominent allies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/us/mayor-of-san-diego-apologizes-over-treatment-of-women.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bob Filner refused to resign in response to sexual harassment accusations leveled by prominent allies.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Mayor Bob Filner of San Diego apologized Thursday for his treatment of women who had worked in his office, but he refused to resign in response to sexual harassment accusations leveled by prominent allies. “I am embarrassed to admit that I have failed to fully respect the women who work for me and with me, and that at times I have intimidated them,” Mr. Filner, 70, a Democrat in his first year in office, said in a video statement. “I have begun to work with professionals to make changes in my behavior and approach,” he said, adding that he and his staff will participate in training about sexual harassment. Donna Frye, a former city councilwoman who worked for Mr. Filner until April, had asked him to resign, saying she had credible evidence he had sexually harassed numerous women. KPBS, a public radio affiliate, reported that women in Mr. Filner’s office said they had been groped, kissed and grabbed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor of San Diego Apologizes Over Treatment of Women', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Mayor of San Diego Apologizes Over Treatment of Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filner, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T03:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/696e6d61-91aa-58f3-a2f2-6539c24df185', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/696e6d61-91aa-58f3-a2f2-6539c24df185'}, {'abstract': 'International students make up 70 percent of the full-time electrical engineering graduate students, according to a new report by the National Foundation for American Policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/education/foreign-students-fill-science-ranks-at-universities-in-united-states.html', 'snippet': 'International students make up 70 percent of the full-time electrical engineering graduate students, according to a new report by the National Foundation for American Policy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' International students make up 70 percent of the full-time electrical engineering graduate students in the United States, 63 percent of those in computer science, and more than half in industrial engineering, economics, chemical engineering, materials engineering and mechanical engineering, according to a new report by the National Foundation for American Policy. The report said the American economy would benefit from welcoming such students and allowing them to remain in the United States when they complete their studies. Stuart Anderson, the executive director of the foundation, said policy makers spend “too much time talking about who we don’t want to come to this country” and not enough about who should be welcomed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foreign Students Fill Science Ranks at Universities in United States', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Foreign Students Fill Science Ranks at Universities In United States', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T03:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef409dd2-04b5-5d4a-9980-00fdbde0a480', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef409dd2-04b5-5d4a-9980-00fdbde0a480'}, {'abstract': 'The robot is seen as a new tool that can come to the aid of humanity in natural and man-made disasters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/science/modest-debut-of-atlas-may-foreshadow-age-of-robo-sapiens.html', 'snippet': 'The robot is seen as a new tool that can come to the aid of humanity in natural and man-made disasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WALTHAM, Mass. — Moving its hands as if it were dealing cards and walking with a 