ronmental Protection Agency has set in drinking water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Nearly two years after an outcry about arsenic in apple juice touched off by a segment on “The Dr. Oz Show,” the federal Food and Drug Administration is proposing a new limit on acceptable levels.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Limits for Arsenic Proposed by F.D.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Limits For Arsenic Proposed By F.D.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARSENIC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oz, Mehmet C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juices', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T04:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f53c27-83a7-5477-9cce-9d6660560418', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f53c27-83a7-5477-9cce-9d6660560418'}, {'abstract': 'Silence has become a luxury in New York that scant few can truly afford, and cultural, technological and economic changes  have added to the city’s din, creating not one culprit but many.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/nyregion/behind-citys-painful-din-culprits-high-and-low.html', 'snippet': 'Silence has become a luxury in New York that scant few can truly afford, and cultural, technological and economic changes  have added to the city’s din, creating not one culprit but many.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first helicopter thundered overhead at 8:05 a.m., as Christine Reekie was sipping her morning coffee. Another one came a minute later, and another, and another, and yet another, swooping so low she feared it would not clear the transmission lines. Ms. Reekie had suffered a small stroke two years earlier, and now she shakily began noting each flyover in writing. By noon, she had counted 14, as they jetted to and from the Hamptons right over her home in Floral Park, just over the border from Queens on Long Island.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/nyregion/NOISE1/NOISE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind City’s Painful Din, Culprits High and Low', 'kicker': 'What? | Outdoor Roar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Behind City’s Painful Din, Culprits High and Low', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T04:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Series', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd42cd14-8c63-592c-8875-3e7b8eb358d3', 'word_count': 3307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd42cd14-8c63-592c-8875-3e7b8eb358d3'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:30 A.M. (Showtime 2) LIBERAL ARTS (2012) Josh Radnor (“How I Met Your Mother”), who wrote and directed this film, stars as Jesse, a 35-year-old admissions counselor at a New York City university who returns to his Ohio alma mater, where he encounters his two favorite teachers. The first is Judith (Allison Janney), a bitter, cynical professor of romantic literature, who seduces him, then throws him out of her bed. “You didn’t think we were going to cuddle while I read you Wordsworth,” she says. “Put some armor around that gooey little heart.” The second is Peter (Richard Jenkins), who is ending a 37-year career at the place he describes as a prison. Then Peter introduces Jesse to Zibby (Elizabeth Olsen, above with Mr. Radnor), an intellectually precocious 19-year-old drama student, and something clicks over the strains of Beethoven, Wagner, Vivaldi and Massenet. “\xa0‘Liberal Arts’ is a much stronger, more deeply felt film than Mr. Radnor’s debut, ‘Happythankyoumoreplease,’\xa0” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times, but, “to quote the hard-boiled Judith, Mr. Radnor’s Jesse is gooey. The harder Mr. Radnor strains to make you love his alter ego, the more resistant you become. The last thing in the world you want to hear is Jesse congratulating himself for growing up, but toward the end of the movie that’s exactly what he does, with a gooey happy ending in sight.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7215a3d3-181e-5e15-91b1-f9d19ee68647', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7215a3d3-181e-5e15-91b1-f9d19ee68647'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, July 12, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-july-12-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, July 12, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It wa