er Mao — rare admissions in a country that shuns its past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — He beat his teachers, terrorized his neighbors, spat on his enemies. But last month, nearly four decades later, the former Red Guard Liu Boqin published in a progressive magazine an apology to nine of his victims. Liu was in junior high school at the start of the 1966-76 Cultural Revolution and, like the rest of the nation’s youth, was encouraged by Mao’s government to turn on intellectuals, teachers and others in positions of authority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions From the Cultural Revolution', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T11:36:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clarissa Sebag-Montefiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clarissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sebag-Montefiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65073ed6-d111-524d-bc17-7eeab7aacc37', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65073ed6-d111-524d-bc17-7eeab7aacc37'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Therrien’s solo exhibition at the Albright-Knox Art Gallery in Buffalo surveys his surreal and understated works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/arts/design/robert-therrien-gets-a-solo-show-at-the-albright-knox.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Therrien’s solo exhibition at the Albright-Knox Art Gallery in Buffalo surveys his surreal and understated works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buffalo — On a recent afternoon at the Albright-Knox Art Gallery here, workers were struggling to mount a huge metal sculpture high on a wall. The piece looked like a Looney Tunes black cloud, with oversize spigots poking out of its sides. You’d imagine it raining bad luck on Porky Pig. It seemed to be jinxing its installers as well, as time and again their forklift refused to heave it to the right spot. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14THERRIEN1_SPAN/14THERRIEN1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge',