times.com/2013/07/12/as-promised-icahn-adds-to-his-bid-for-dell/', 'snippet': 'In a letter to Dell shareholders, Carl C. Icahn and his partner, Southeastern Asset Management, proposed giving shareholders a warrant to buy a share in the struggling computer company at $20 apiece for every four shares that they tender, in addit...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl C. Icahn lived up to his word on Friday, offering a sweetener to his alternative to a $24.4 billion leveraged buyout of Dell Inc. by adding a warrant to his stock buyback plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Promised, Icahn Adds to His Bid for Dell', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Asset Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T15:59:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bbea1df-6c40-5907-956b-52d303f29454', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bbea1df-6c40-5907-956b-52d303f29454'}, {'abstract': 'For one writer, inspiration began between pulpy pages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/arts/a-writer-found-lifes-inspiration-in-thor-and-the-hulk.html', 'snippet': 'For one writer, inspiration began between pulpy pages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comic books were just comic books once upon a time — humble 10-cent gateways to the fantastic, the astonishing. They weren’t paper-and-ink scaffolds for the multibillion-dollar entertainment franchises that some characters have become, franchises (and would-be franchises) that will be celebrated this week in San Diego at the annual multimedia orgy that’s Comic-Con International. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14SECRET-ORIGIN1_SPAN/14SECRET-ORIGIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14SECRET-ORIGIN1_SPAN/14SECRET-ORIGIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14SECRET-ORIGIN1_SPAN/14SECRET-ORIGIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14SECRET-ORIGIN1_SPAN/14SECRET-ORIGIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1431, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14SECRET-ORIGIN1_SPAN/14SECRET-ORIGIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14SECRET-ORIGIN1_SPAN/14SECRET-ORIGIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts