, 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T16:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/347e022f-d120-58e9-b16b-cb3736e49860', 'word_count': 1637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/347e022f-d120-58e9-b16b-cb3736e49860'}, {'abstract': 'The Intiman Theater in Seattle has reconstituted itself as a far smaller enterprise — the Intiman Theater Festival, with a mission of producing four shows every summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/theater/intiman-theater-in-seattle-downsizes-into-a-summer-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Intiman Theater in Seattle has reconstituted itself as a far smaller enterprise — the Intiman Theater Festival, with a mission of producing four shows every summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — During a recent rehearsal here of the new musical “Stu for Silverton,” the director, Andrew Russell, asked the people in the room to introduce themselves. Several of the actors were students and recent alumni of Cornish College of the Arts, while crew members described themselves as interns. Mr. Russell himself was boyish at 30, tying his long black hair into a knotted ball, and offering zippy superlatives after each scene: “Nice nice nice nice” and “Good good good” and “High five high five.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14INTINMAN2_SPAN/14INTINMAN2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'im