le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59222bea-d673-5825-be4a-ab72f3f32476', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59222bea-d673-5825-be4a-ab72f3f32476'}, {'abstract': 'The actress and writer Michelle Morgan talks about the arc of her career and how “Bridesmaids,” starring Kristen Wiig, paved the way for her new film, “Girl Most Likely.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/movies/kristen-wiig-helped-greenlight-michelle-morgans-script.html', 'snippet': 'The actress and writer Michelle Morgan talks about the arc of her career and how “Bridesmaids,” starring Kristen Wiig, paved the way for her new film, “Girl Most Likely.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been a lot of debate over the last two years about what the blockbuster “Bridesmaids” did for films written and driven by women. That discussion was less theoretical for the actress and writer Michelle Morgan. The film’s box office blowout simply meant that her script “Imogene,” which Kristen Wiig had expressed an interest in starring in years earlier, was about to benefit from the overnight minting of Ms. Wiig as a woman who could get a movie greenlighted.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14MMORGAN1_SPAN/14MMORGAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14MMORGAN1_SPAN/14MMORGAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/arts/14MMORGAN1_SPAN/14MMORGAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred