y-july-12-2/', 'snippet': 'Muslims offering prayers at a mosque in Allahabad, Uttar Pradesh, on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/world/asia/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk/12-Ramadan-POD-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: July 12', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T16:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3dd651a-9b62-5a6a-bf69-6872e0e6aec2', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3dd651a-9b62-5a6a-bf69-6872e0e6aec2'}, {'abstract': 'Ian Doescher, whose mashup of Shakespeare and “Star Wars” is at No. 12 on the hardcover fiction list, says the sci-fi epic is “partly a history, like ‘Henry V,’ and partly a fantasy, like ‘The Tempest.’ ”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Ian Doescher, whose mashup of Shakespeare and “Star Wars” is at No. 12 on the hardcover fiction list, says the sci-fi epic is “partly a history, like ‘Henry V,’ and partly a fantasy, like ‘The Tempest.’ ”', 'lead_paragraph': 'USETH THE FORCE: A couple of weeks ago in this space, I wrote about Jeffrey Brown’s “Star Wars”-based parenting books, which were enjoying a run on the advice, how-to and miscellaneous list. Now another “Star Wars” spinoff is making noise: “William Shakespeare’s Star Wars,” by Ian Doescher, is new at No. 12 on the hardcover fiction list. The book recasts the story of Luke and Leia and Darth Vader as a five-act play in iambic pentameter — because why not? — and it’s more entertaining than you might guess. (Here’s a sample couplet from the prologue: “In time so long ago begins our play / In star-crossed galaxy far, far away.”) In a phone interview, Doescher told me he came up with the idea last year, after watching the original “Star Wars” trilogy and attending the Oregon Shakespeare Festival in quick succession. “People ask me whether I see ‘Star Wars’ as a comedy or a tragedy,” he said, “but it’s really neither — it’s partly a history, like ‘Henry V,’ and partly a fantasy, like ‘The Tempest.’ ” He added that he was gratified, but not entirely surprised, by the book’s success: “Shakespeare is a popular market, and ‘Star Wars’ is a popular market,” he said. “It’s not like I was writing ‘Geoffrey Chaucer’s Ishtar.’ ”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/books/review/12Doescher/12Doescher-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 449, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/books/review/12Doescher/12Doescher-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 449, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/books/review/12Doescher/12Doescher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/12/books/review/12Doescher/12Doescher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/12/books/review/12Doescher/12Doescher-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TBR: Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T16:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75a28097-8778-5517-be4d-708ca0bba167', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75a28097-8778-5517-be4d-708ca0bba167'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s fiendishly complicated system of proportional representation is keeping small parties out of power.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/of-the-dhondt-method-with-a-barrier/', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s fiendishly complicated system of proportional representation is keeping small parties out of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Demonstrations across Turkey over the past couple of months have sparked a debate over what democracy here should look like. The prime minister seems to think that, because he was elected and re-elected, he now has the authority to override objections to, say, his plans to destroy a park or build a mosque in the center of Istanbul. The opposition calls this “majoritarianism” and argues that democracy creates an obligation for the government to consult the minority, not a license to trample it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Of the D’Hondt Method With a Barrier', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Martial Law', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice and Development Party (