x at the Abingdon in the West Village with five bedrooms, two wood-burning fireplaces and a formal gallery designed with large art in mind was the most expensive residential sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/big-ticket-at-23-4-million-a-condo-with-space-for-big-art/', 'snippet': 'A triplex at the Abingdon in the West Village with five bedrooms, two wood-burning fireplaces and a formal gallery designed with large art in mind was the most expensive residential sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A striking West Village triplex at the Abingdon, a 10-unit luxury condominium conversion of a six-story 1906 building on Abingdon Square Park that had been used as a nursing home, sold for $23,419,750 and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. The 9,600-square-foot dwelling, No. 2, has its own entry west of the main lobby at 320 West 12th Street, at Hudson Street.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/realestate/14TICKET_SPAN/Ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/realestate/14TICKET_SPAN/Ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/realestate/14TICKET_SPAN/Ticket-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/realestate/14TICKET_SPAN/Ticket-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i