/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'German Fairytale Route, Germany Germany is celebrating the 200th anniversary of “Children’s and Household Tales,” folk tales collected by Jacob and Wilhelm Grimm. Events are planned throughout 2013. Many are along the German Fairytale Route, stretching some 375 miles from Hanau in the south to Bremen in the north, winding through villages where the Brothers Grimm lived and worked, and passing settings — a castle where Sleeping Beauty may have awakened or a house fit for Little Red Riding Hood — that inspired the stories. Travelers can relive their favorites at open-air plays, puppet shows, festivals, concerts, exhibitions, guided walking tours and medieval feasts. A musical Grimm fairy tale will be performed in a park in Kassel July 18 to Aug. 18.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Germany and Norway', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T17:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ea60df2-d756-55d4-80c8-cbd47ed543bd', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ea60df2-d756-55d4-80c8-cbd47ed543bd'}, {'abstract': 'With two of the car’s former drivers in attendance at the auction, the 1954 Mercedes-Benz W196 racer sold for nearly $30 million.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/mercedes-grand-prix-car-smashes-auction-records/', 'snippet': 'With two of the car’s former drivers in attendance at the auction, the 1954 Mercedes-Benz W196 racer sold for nearly $30 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'C