least 160 people are still missing from the flooding afflicting a mountainous stretch of Sichuan Province.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Five days of torrential rain in China’s southwest has killed 31 people and left more than 160 others missing, the state news media reported on Friday. Most of those affected are in a mountainous stretch of Sichuan Province that only recently recovered from the 2008 earthquake that left 87,000 people dead or missing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Toll at 31 From Flooding in Southwest China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Storm Deaths Are Tallied', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sichuan Province (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T18:12:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f3f543-f5a5-5ec8-9a9d-8ea58db5ba3b', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f3f543-f5a5-5ec8-9a9d-8ea58db5ba3b'}, {'abstract': 'The identity of @RuthBourdain, a Twitter avatar created to poke fun at the pretensions of the culinary elite, is revealed.', 'web_url': 'https://www