t': 1761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2faa4f10-5f89-5197-904b-e386bef4646d'}, {'abstract': 'Rich Donnelly, manager of the Brooklyn Cyclones, a Mets farm team, said his job was like that of a plate spinner, including before and long after games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/nyregion/a-long-day-at-the-diamond.html', 'snippet': 'Rich Donnelly, manager of the Brooklyn Cyclones, a Mets farm team, said his job was like that of a plate spinner, including before and long after games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Managing a baseball team, says Rich Donnelly, is like being the plate spinner on the old “Ed Sullivan Show” — running from one precariously wobbly plate to the next, trying to avert the crash of china. What better way to spend a summer Sunday? Mr. Donnelly, 66, is in his third year as the manager of the Brooklyn Cyclones. They are a farm team for the Mets, who will host the Major League Baseball All-Star Game on July 16 at Citi Field. Before joining the Cyclones, Mr. Donnelly, a former minor league catcher, worked 28 years in the major leagues, mainly coaching third base. He is, he said, a creature of habit. From June to early September, Mr. Donnelly leaves behind his family in Steubenville, Ohio, for temporary accommodations in Gravesend, Brooklyn, and the delights of baseball in Coney Island.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE3_SPAN/14ROTINE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Long Day at the Diamond', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Long Day at the Diamond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Cyclones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Coney Island (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T18:33:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cb532f4-8dcd-58b9-a51e-819be0b24c47', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cb532f4-8dcd-58b9-a51e-819be0b24c47'}, {'abstract': 'If the policy don’t fit, you must exit.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/the-monetary-debate-enter-chewbacca/', 'snippet': 'If the policy don’t fit, you must exit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debate over monetary policy has grown increasingly surreal as time goes by. Initially, it was about a fairly straightforward and — crucially — falsifiable position: the claim by monetary hawks like Allan Meltzer and Martin Feldstein that quantitative easing would lead to a major acceleration of inflation. If that inflation had happened, I like to imagine that doves like me would have conceded that we got it wrong, and reconsidered our position.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Monetary Debate: Enter Chewbacca', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T18:37:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a7a7ff8-15a7-54b5-97ac-17f8e753d196', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a7a7ff8-15a7-54b5-97ac-17f8e753d196'}, {'abstract': 'Questions that chief executives — and others — ought to regularly ask themselves, not just to be good citizens, but as a powerful way to build competitive advantage.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/what-it-takes-to-fully-engage-your-employees/', 'snippet': 'Questions that chief executives — and others — ought to regularly ask themselves, not just to be good citizens, but as a powerful way to build competitive advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the 15 years I’ve been consulting in the corporate world, I’ve only met a handful of senior leaders who had as a primary goal for their companies making a positive difference i