com/2013/07/12/health-sites-under-scrutiny-over-mining-of-data/', 'snippet': 'Lisa Madigan, the attorney general of Illinois, has opened an inquiry into the data-mining practices of some popular health sites in an effort to increase the industry’s transparency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of people rely on Web sites like WebMD and Health.com for information about depression, sexually transmitted diseases, cancer and other sensitive personal health issues. But it can be difficult for consumers to understand how health sites may capture, analyze and share information about user searches and other activities — even the small minority of people who manage to slog all the way through the privacy policies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/business/13bits-health/13bits-health-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 897, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/13/business/13bits-health/13bits-health-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 897}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/business/13bits-health/13bits-health-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/business/13bits-health/13bits-health-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1371, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/business/13bits-health/13bits-health-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/13/business/13bits-health/13bits-health-thumbStandard.jpg