 in the regulation, inviting an onslaught of lobbying from banks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/u-s-regulators-approve-stricter-trading-rules-abroad/', 'snippet': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission voted 3-1 to rein in lucrative trading by American banks doing business overseas, but the agency also afforded Wall Street additional time to comment on the plan to phase in the regulation, inviting an onsl...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal regulators reached a last-minute compromise on Friday to expand their oversight far beyond American shores, overcoming internal squabbles and Wall Street lobbying to rein in some of the overseas trading that imploded during the financial crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Regulators Approve Stricter Trading Rules Overseas', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Regulators Approve Stricter Trading Rules Overseas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gensler, Gary S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wetjen, Mark P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T21:53:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59e29c2a-a16f-5523-97a5-39fc0a12f937', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59e29c2a-a16f-5523-97a5-39fc0a12f937'}, {'abstract': 'Emile Charlap, 95, is the host of a weekly, brass-heavy jam session in a Times Square office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/nyregion/an-ageless-music-man-and-his-makeshift-ensemble.html', 'snippet': 'Emile Charlap, 95, is the host of a weekly, brass-heavy jam session in a Times Square office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A trombone was first. A couple of French horns filed in. Here came the bass. The drums were late, but the group waited on no instrument.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 508}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1735, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/nyregion/14MUSIC1_SPAN/14MUSIC1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Music Man, Merry Band', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Music Man, Merry Band', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kleinfield, N R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charlap, Emile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T22:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By N. R. Kleinfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'N.', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Kleinfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c17bc04b-c861-55a1-aedc-5b2f9f7d1045', 'word_count': 1344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c17bc04b-c861-55a1-aedc-5b2f9f7d1045'}, {'abstract': 'The illustrator Konstantin Kakanias and his fictional alter ego, Mrs. Tependris, report back from the haute couture shows earlier this month — in pictures.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/the-diary-of-mrs-tependris-complicated-coats-and-cabinets-of-curiosities-at-paris-couture/', 'snippet': 'The illustrator Konstantin Kakanias and his fictional alter ego, Mrs. Tependris, report back from the haute couture shows earlier this month — in pictures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the couture shows this season, T sent Mrs. Tependris, the high-society doyenne who is the fictional alter ego of the artist and T contributing editor Konstantin Kakanias, to Paris. “She hadn’t been for years,” Kakanias said. “Things have changed, so she was a bit confused when she arrived.” But she got her bearings soon enough and soaked up the weeklong high-fashion parade. Here, Kakanias shares some of the things that his heroine saw and did.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Diary of Mrs. Tependris | Complicated Coats and Cabinets of Curiosities at Paris Couture', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T22:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Konstantin Kakanias', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Konstantin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakanias', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9d3ce11-a14f-5a30-8443-144aaab5b55f', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9d3ce11-a14f-5a30-8443-144aaab5b55f'}, {'abstract': 'With the acquisition, AT&T would gain five million new customers and acquire Leap’s network, licenses and retail stores, as well as the Cricket brand.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/12/att-to-buy-leap-wireless-for-1-2-billion/', 'snippet': 'With the acquisition, AT&T would gain five million new customers and acquire Leap’s network, licenses and retail stores, as well as the Cricket brand.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:37 a.m. | Updated AT&T, thwarted by regulators nearly two years ago on a planned $39 billion acquisition of T-Mobile USA, is back in the merger hunt, albeit with a much smaller target. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'AT&T to Buy Leap Wireless for $1.2 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At&t To Buy Leap Wireless International', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-12T22:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a089bbb-6d6f-556d-b6a7-070af01b83a0', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a089bbb-6d6f-556d-b6a7-070af01b83a0'}, {'abstract': 'John Malkovich, who starred in a film version of “Les Liaisons Dangereuses,” has directed a French-language production of the English-language play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/13/theater/reviews/les-liaisons-dangereuses-opens-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'John Malkovich, who starred in a film version of “Les Liaisons Dangereuses,” has directed a French-language production of the English-language play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sexual temperature rarely rises above a simmer in the listless French-language production of Christopher Hampton’s play “Les Liaisons Dangereuses,” which runs through Sunday at the Gerald Lynch Theater as part of the Lincoln Center Festival. Directed with a fussy hand by John Malkovich, who starred in the delectable Stephen Frears film version of the play, the production vigorously seeks to freshen familiar material with unexpected flourishes. But even Mr. Malkovich’s supposed innovations have a stale feeling. As a result, attending to the manipulations of the Vicomte de Valmont (Yannik Landrein) and his ex-lover, the Marquise de Merteuil (Julie Moulier), feels a bit like observing a chess game — spanning nearly three hours — that can barely hold the attention of its players, let alone any spectators. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1442, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/arts/13LIASONS/13LIASONS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steamy Epistles, Updated for the Sexting Era', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steamy Epistles, Updated for the Sexting Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkovich, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hampton, Christopher', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landrein, Yannik', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {