, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/688877e5-7909-5891-8417-bc39083c1cc7', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/688877e5-7909-5891-8417-bc39083c1cc7'}, {'abstract': 'Southern California air quality regulators voted to establish buffer zones, to keep fire rings — and the harmful particulate matter that rises from them — away from beachfront homes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/13/us/california-regulators-in-south-restrict-fire-rings-on-beaches.html', 'snippet': 'Southern California air quality regulators voted to establish buffer zones, to keep fire rings — and the harmful particulate matter that rises from them — away from beachfront homes.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Southern California air quality regulators voted Friday to restrict fire rings on the beaches in Orange County and parts of Los Angeles County. The 7-to-6 vote by the South Coast Air Quality Management District’s board will establish buffer zones, to keep fire rings — and the harmful particulate matter that rises from them — away from beachfront homes, where residents complained about the smoke. A proposal to outlaw fire rings entirely was modified, after protests from local residents who considered them a cultural tradition. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Board Restricts Fire Rings ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Board Restricts Fire Rings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orange County (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T01:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea43e516-4c51-55cf-a82d-ff012376bd93', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea43e516-4c51-55cf-a82d-ff012376bd93'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Yevgeny R. Urlashov’s supporters say his prosecution is political, but government evidence that includes tapped phone calls and videos suggests otherwise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/13/world/europe/retribution-corruption-or-both-in-russia-mayors-bribery-case.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Yevgeny R. Urlashov’s supporters say his prosecution is political, but government evidence that includes tapped phone calls and videos suggests otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YAROSLAVL, Russia — Just last week, Mayor Yevgeny R. Urlashov’s political career seemed as bright as the generous summer light that drenches this ancient citadel of onion-domed churches and stone-walled monasteries. Elected last year as one of the few anti-establishment leaders of a major Russian city, he was preparing to head an opposition slate in regional parliamentary elections in September. There were also stirrings about a future run for governor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/13/world/russia/russia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/13/world/russia/russia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':