ocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T16:34:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61427e3f-815f-5c1f-a3dd-ddb7a75faefe', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61427e3f-815f-5c1f-a3dd-ddb7a75faefe'}, {'abstract': 'I never said what I said, I said something else that also isn’t true.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/13/fish-in-a-barrel-rick-santelli-edition/', 'snippet': 'I never said what I said, I said something else that also isn’t true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tale of Monetary Hawks Down continues to get ever more interesting, although it makes one ever less sanguine about human nature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish in a Barrel, Rick Santelli Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T16:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b56a858-8ba5-5981-9b66-86d85eb49a5f', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b56a858-8ba5-5981-9b66-86d85eb49a5f'}, {'abstract': 'On Saturday, the support men had their day in the sun. Matteo Trentin, who usually works for Cavendish on the Omega Pharma-Quick Step team, won Stage 14.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytime