cle', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51412ba1-a1c7-50e6-8059-8082ff4fcf48', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51412ba1-a1c7-50e6-8059-8082ff4fcf48'}, {'abstract': 'The free-agent center Dwight Howard is a superb fit in Houston’s offense, if he buys in to playing at the quick pace the Rockets prefer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/sports/basketball/recasting-a-dream-is-howards-goal.html', 'snippet': 'The free-agent center Dwight Howard is a superb fit in Houston’s offense, if he buys in to playing at the quick pace the Rockets prefer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Dwight Howard joined the Los Angeles Lakers in a complex four-team trade that sent him and two other stars, Andrew Bynum and Andre Iguodala, to different corners of the N.B.A. map, it seemed that Howard, the N.B.A.’s most dominant big man, had found a home. Many people instantly picked the aging Lakers as championship contenders. Howard called it “a dream come true.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1454, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/sports/DOG-DRIBBLE/DOG-DRIBBLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recasting a Dream Is Howard’s Goal', 'kicker': 'Off The Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recasting a Dream Is Howard’s Goal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Beckley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Rockets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Dwight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T16:52:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64d3f854-7301-5995-9b19-d456615579e7', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64d3f854-7301-5995-9b19-d456615579e7'}, {'abstract': 'How New York’s African-American leadership dealt with, and suffered from, the violence of 1863.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/13/black-elites-and-the-draft-riots/', 'snippet': 'How New York’s African-American leadership dealt with, and suffered from, the violence of 1863.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the 1850s, New York’s black leaders tended to congregate in the backroom of Dr. James McCune Smith’s pharmacy at 55 West Broadway. Many of them, including Philip Bell, Henry Highland Garnet and Albro Lyons, my great-great-granduncle — had attended the Mulberry Street School, an institution for teaching African-American children, in the late 1820s, and remained close friends. Some of the men were ministers, others doctors and pharmacists; still others ran newspapers or operated boarding houses. But despite their material comfort, they staunchly stood at the vanguard of the fight for black civil rights. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Elites and the Draft Riots', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T16:54:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carla Peterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_o