 from newcomers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/opinion/sunday/forgive-the-interruption.html', 'snippet': 'Panhandlers’ rounds are so ingrained that a New Yorker learns to appreciate innovative twists from newcomers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The old reliables are still hard at work panhandling: The polite fellow in the bus terminal with his hand out and a very precise plea, “I just need 78 cents more to get to Jersey.” The man who works the subways with a showy bag of groceries, announcing with a first responder’s concern: “Is there anyone here hungry? I have sandwiches and fruit!” He works quickly with his beggar’s cup among riders who are never seen to accept his free foodstuffs. He pockets donations as he works his way into the next car.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "‘Forgive the Interruption ... '", 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "‘Forgive the Interruption ... '", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beggars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2b02eb8-71c8-5aec-95d7-2bd0bfd2d33a', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2b02eb8-71c8-5aec-95d7-2bd0bfd2d33a'}, {'abstract': 'There are risks wherever Republicans look.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/opinion/sunday/douthat-the-houses-i