, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-13T19:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5c61c204-e368-5b6f-b24f-946424bb0248', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5c61c204-e368-5b6f-b24f-946424bb0248'}, {'abstract': 'Erich Spangenberg often sues companies, contending patent infringement. So it was a surprise when he took the side of a small company facing such a suit over a new phone app.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/business/how-a-typical-patent-battle-took-an-unexpected-turn.html', 'snippet': 'Erich Spangenberg often sues companies, contending patent infringement. So it was a surprise when he took the side of a small company facing such a suit over a new phone app.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT would the country’s “most notorious patent troll” advise a guy under attack from a patent troll? Or, put more judiciously, a company that bears the outward appearance of a patent troll?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/business/14-PATENT-JP2/14-PATENT-JP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/14/business/14-PATENT-JP2/14-PATENT-JP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/business/14-PATENT-JP2/14-PATENT-JP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/14/business/14-PATENT-JP2/14-PATENT-JP2-superJumbo.jpg', 'heig