013/07/15/us/george-zimmerman-verdict-trayvon-martin.html', 'snippet': 'A six-woman jury accepted self-defense as justification for the fatal shooting of Trayvon Martin, 17, by George Zimmerman in Sanford, Fla., last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANFORD, Fla. — George Zimmerman, the neighborhood watch volunteer who fatally shot Trayvon Martin, an unarmed black teenager, igniting a national debate on racial profiling and civil rights, was found not guilty late Saturday night of second-degree murder. He was also acquitted of manslaughter, a lesser charge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zimmerman Is Acquitted in Killing of Trayvon Martin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zimmerman Is Acquitted In Trayvon Martin Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Self-Defense', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T05:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez and Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4adcfdeb-acf5-560f-a185-31692c0e93b6', 'word_count': 2121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4adcfdeb-acf5-560f-a185-31692c0e93b6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/arts/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:05 A.M. (Showtime 2) THE WAY OF THE GUN (2000) Ryan Phillippe and Benicio Del Toro, above from left, play a pair of career criminals looking for the score of a lifetime and find it in the form of Robin (Juliette Lewis), a pregnant woman who is the surrogate for a wealthy couple (Scott Wilson and Kristin Lehman) in this noir written and directed by Christopher McQuarrie. The crooks kidnap Robin and hold the baby for ransom, but her bodyguards (Taye Diggs and Nicky Katt) and the bagman (James Caan) won’t part with the money without the requisite number of gunfights and double crosses. Writing in The New York Times, Elvis Mitchell said: “Mr. McQuarrie is smart about moviemaking in ways that show his respect for the genre, and he doesn’t force the material on audiences. He knows that part of the enjoyment they will get is in knowing they’ve seen movies like this before that weren’t so direct and intense.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T05:47:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/559b356c-ae6c-5b0b-a260-0d97d6884a46', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/559b356c-ae6c-5b0b-a260-0d97d6884a46'}, 