 which cost Legendary Entertainment and Warner Brothers at least $180 million to make, took in $38.3 million between Friday and Sunday, according to studio estimates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the third weekend in a row, a big-budget nonsequel sputtered in North America: “Pacific Rim,” which cost Legendary Entertainment and Warner Brothers at least $180 million to make, took in $38.3 million between Friday and Sunday, according to studio estimates. That result is a humiliation for Legendary, a young company that has been eager to prove that it can produce blockbusters on its own; Warner was a minority partner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Pacific Rim’ Has a Slow Start at Theaters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Toro, Guillermo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandler, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legendary Pictures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers Pictures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T16:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ee832dc-356f-58f8-8c3e-770a55ac096c', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ee832dc-356f-58f8-8c3e-770a55ac096c'}, {'abstract': 'Just indicators.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/there-is-no-true-unemployment-rate/', 'snippet': 'Just indicators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my last post I compared food stamp use with U6, a broad definition of unemployment — and I saw some commenters claiming that U6 is the “true” unemployment rate, even that I was for the first time admitting this fact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There Is No “True” Unemployment Rate', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T17:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b56aeac-4432-57e6-812f-9c808554bf25', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b56aeac-4432-57e6-812f-9c808554bf25'}, {'abstract': 'While the promise of huge paydays exists for both movies and tech start-ups, the safest bet is in more mundane markets.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/disruptions-hollywood-or-silicon-valley-wheres-the-money/', 'snippet': 'While the promise of huge paydays exists for both movies and tech start-ups, the safest bet is in more mundane markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, “The Dark Knight Rises” was one of the top-grossing films of 2012, racking up $1 billion in worldwide box-office sales. That same year, Instagram, the photo-sharing site based in Silicon Valley, was also one of the top-grossing commercial tech deals of the year;  Facebook bought it for $1 billion. So which was a better return on investment, the Hollywood hit or the Silicon Valley wonder?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/technology/15disruptions/15disruptions-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: Hollywood, or Silicon Valley: Where’s the Money?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Movies or Technology: Where’s the Money?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T18:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': No