ng part in the protest at the prison in Cuba, an American military spokesman said, accelerating an apparent downward trend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — An American military spokesman said Sunday that 15 detainees at the military prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, who had been listed as having gone on hunger strike had quit participating in the protest, accelerating an apparent downward trend since the start of Ramadan last week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '15 Held at Guantánamo Are Said to Quit Hunger Strike ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '15 Held at Guantánamo Are Said to Quit Hunger Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T19:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/815d049e-f7aa-5654-b8e8-28b2ef095823', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/815d049e-f7aa-5654-b8e8-28b2ef095823'}, {'abstract': 'The candidates’ daily campaign schedule at a glance.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/july-14-where-the-candidates-are-today/', 'snippet': 'The candidates’ daily campaign schedule at a glance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Planned events for the mayoral candidates, according to the campaigns and organizations they are affiliated with. Times are listed as schedule