’s “Great Gatsby,” commissioned by the Met in the 1990s, was revived on Thursday at Tanglewood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LENOX, Mass. — One thing that can be said for John Harbison, the composer of an operatic version of “The Great Gatsby” that was revived in concert at Tanglewood on Thursday, is that he was well ahead of the current “Gatsby” craze.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rich Are Different: They Can Sing', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Rich Are Different: They Can Sing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbison, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tanglewood Music Festival (Lenox, Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T19:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba2d3a69-7d6c-5cdb-8acb-0d42d7f779e0', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba2d3a69-7d6c-5cdb-8acb-0d42d7f779e0'}, {'abstract': 'On Twitter and around the Web, an impassioned debate about race and justice follows the acquittal of George Zimmerman in the shooting death of Trayvon Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/social-medias-reaction-to-the-acquittal-of-george-zimmerman/', 'snippet': 'On Twitter and around the Web, an impassioned debate about race and justice follows the acquittal of George Zimmerman in the shooting death of Trayvon Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague, Michael Schwirtz reports, the acquittal of George Zimmerman in the shooting death of Trayvon Martin prompted an impassioned debate on Sunday about race and the judicial system, amid calls for more protests to be held across the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Media’s Reaction to the Acquittal of George Zimmerman', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-14T19:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82ac2857-9aaf-573c-a8df-d1542bcabd90', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82ac2857-9aaf-573c-a8df-d1542bcabd90'}, {'abstract': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 