ata about their behavior.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/business/video-retailnext-surveillance/video-retailnext-surveillance-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/05/business/video-retailnext-surveillance/video-retailnext-surveillance-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/business/video-retailnext-surveillance/video-retailnext-surveillance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/05/business/video-retailnext-surveillance/video-retailnext-surveillance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/05/business/video-retailnext-surveillance/video-retailnext-surveillance-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Data Hits Real Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T01:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Erica Berenstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7409f88c-e6e3-5144-8936-39fd63a8c6f1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7409f88c-e6e3-5144-8936-39fd63a8c6f1'}, {'abstract': 'In its recent, unanimous decision that human genes cannot be patented, the Supreme Court gave a rare victory to the cause of economic fairness.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/14/how-intellectual-property-reinforces-inequality/', 'snippet': 'In its recent, unanimous decision that human genes cannot be patented, the Supreme Court gave a rare victory to the cause of economic fairness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the war against inequality, we’ve become so used to bad news that we’re almost taken aback when something positive happens. And with the Supreme Court having affirmed that wealthy people and corporations have a constitutional right to buy American elections, who would have expected it to bring good news? But a decision in the term that just ended gave ordinary Americans something that is more precious than money alone — the right to live.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Intellectual Property Reinforces Inequality', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Myriad Genetics Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T01:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph E. Stiglitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stiglitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a96d350-e030-545d-8811-df53275d7d86', 'word_count': 2030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a96d350-e030-545d-8811-df53275d7d86'}, {'abstract': 'With the farm bill vote in the House, policy turns outright sadistic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/opinion/krugman-hunger-games-usa.html', 'snippet': 'With the farm bill vote in the House, policy turns outright sadistic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something terrible has happened to the soul of the Republican Party. We’ve gone beyond bad economic doctrine. We’ve even gone beyond selfishness and special interests. At this point we’re talking about a state of mind that takes positive glee in inflicting further suffering on the already miserable.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandar