 an impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best prospects in the world had gathered on the same field, so naturally, Pat Gillick was there. Gillick, the Hall of Fame executive, works for the Philadelphia Phillies but lives in Seattle. He never misses a Futures Game, and there he was, up in the stands, in the shade, watching batting practice on Sunday morning at sweltering Citi Field.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1282, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Future Is Now for Young Stars', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Future Is Now for Top Young Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillick, Pat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL STAR GAMES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Jose', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Machado, Manny', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Segura, Jean', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T01:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414b2d64-f7a5-5579-8383-172925559db1', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414b2d64-f7a5-5579-8383-172925559db1'}, {'abstract': 'The United States and New Zealand have put forward excellent proposals to create two major marine reserves in Antarctica.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/opinion/further-protection-for-antarctica.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and New Zealand have put forward excellent proposals to create two major marine reserves in Antarctica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antarctica is this planet’s only continent wholly protected from mining and other economic activity, save tourism — a place where nature, not commerce, rules. But protection ends at the water’s edge. While the land mass itself is pretty much a biological desert, Antarctic waters are full of life, especially krill, which has drawn the attention of international fishing fleets over the past decade. In fact, the Antarctic Ocean is one of the most intact marine ecosystems on the planet, and one of the most fragile. Now is the time to protect it for good.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Further Protection for Antarctica', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Further Protection for Antarctica', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T01:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/33f97b44-c6b9-59d7-a137-903cd7918480', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33f97b44-c6b9-59d7-a137-903cd7918480'}, {'abstract': 'The acquittal of George Zimmerman should be a call to reform laws that make it easier to kill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/opinion/trayvon-martins-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'The acquittal of George Zimmerman should be a call to reform laws that make it easier to kill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may not be possible to consider the case of George Zimmerman, who was acquitted Saturday of all charges in the killing of Trayvon Martin, as anything but a sad commentary on the state of race relations and the battle over gun rights in America today.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trayvon Martin’s Legacy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trayvon Martin’s Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T01:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6697dc12-fa81-517d-a810-f9b9bdc5bff6', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6697dc12-fa81-517d-a810-f9b9bdc5bff6'}, {'abstract': 'A mayor who was long on vision, though often short on consensus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/opinion/keller-the-bloomberg-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'A mayor who was long on vision, though often short on consensus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A DOZEN years ago I wrote a column not exactly endorsing Michael Bloomberg for mayor (columnists don’t endorse) but endorsing the idea of Michael Bloomberg. If a guy who built a wildly successful business wants to offer his services to the city, I argued, we shouldn’t let our prejudice against the rich stand in his way. Since then the idea, the C.E.O. as aspiring public steward, has suffered some setbacks (Mitt Romney, for one), but I feel pretty well vindicated by the mayor. As he would be the first to tell you, he will be a very hard act to follow.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bloomberg Legacy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bloomberg Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T01:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c255dba-c318-5fdb-b236-2c4dd9421fd1', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c255dba-c318-5fdb-b236-2c4dd9421fd1'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets prospects Noah Syndergaard and Rafael Montero each threw a scoreless inning in the Futures Game, giving the organization hope that more help is on the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/sports/baseball/syndergaard-and-montero-offer-a-vision-the-mets-could-love.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets prospects Noah Syndergaard and Rafael Montero each threw a scoreless inning in the Futures Game, giving the organization hope that more help is on the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Piazza was back behind the plate Sunday, catching softballs from Jennie Finch in a celebrity game at Citi Field. The Mets announced that Piazza would join their Hall of Fame in September, and Piazza, who carried the team to the 2000 World Series, has a keen sense of their patterns.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/SYNDERGAARD/SYNDERGAARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/sports/SYNDERGAARD/SYNDERGAARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, '