rsons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T06:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce McClure', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McClure', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb6a32cc-6e65-543e-81a2-8b76a575795a', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb6a32cc-6e65-543e-81a2-8b76a575795a'}, {'abstract': 'Summer temperatures may have you avoiding the stove, but with a five-minute burst of heat, stir-frying can turn an array of greens and vegetables into a delicious meal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/health/summer-stir-fries.html', 'snippet': 'Summer temperatures may have you avoiding the stove, but with a five-minute burst of heat, stir-frying can turn an array of greens and vegetables into a delicious meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are trying to put dinner together in a hot apartment this summer you will appreciate the fact that stir-frying in a wok requires little more than a five-minute blast of heat. Some time is needed to prepare the ingredients while the stove is off, but once you begin cooking, be ready to eat. Yes, you have to cook the rice or noodles you will be eating with your stir-fries, but those can be cooked ahead, in the morning for example, before it gets too hot, or in a rice cooker, and then reheated in the wok.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1313, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Stir-Fries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T06:36:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ba40285-9889-52bf-a011-72f971384238', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ba40285-9889-52bf-a011-72f971384238'}, {'abstract': 'Extrajudicial killings in the name of counterinsurgency are corroding India’s democratic ideals.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/extrajudicial-killings-corrode-democracy-in-india/', 'snippet': 'Extrajudicial killings in the name of counterinsurgency are corroding India’s democratic ideals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India is grappling with an important question: at which point can a potential threat be reason enough to compromise on the right to life? India’s premier federal investigation agency, Central Bureau of Investigation has recently charged seven police officers in the western state of Gujarat for the killing of four individuals, including a 19-year-old woman named Ishrat Jahan. The police claimed they were shot in an armed exchange in June 2004 and that all four were terrorists conspiring to target Narendra Modi, the chief minister of Gujarat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/world/asia/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/world/asia/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/world/asia/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/world/asia/15-ishrat-jahan-protest-IndiaInk/15-