dia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate’s Leader Sets Showdown Over Changes to Filibuster', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate’s Leader Sets Showdown Over Filibuster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T14:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c0a9548-9ffd-5771-89b6-bf35458459f1', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c0a9548-9ffd-5771-89b6-bf35458459f1'}, {'abstract': 'Bangladesh’s streams made iridescent by factory pollution hark back to those of the Hudson River Valley in the 1950s.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/iridescent-rivers-then-hudson-valley-and-now-bangladesh/', 'snippet': 'Bangladesh’s streams made iridescent by factory pollution hark back to those of the Hudson River Valley in the 1950s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The parallels between development and pollution tracks in industrializing poor countries now and the United States half a century ago are remarkable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iridescent Rivers, Then (Hudson Valley) and Now (Bangladesh)', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fishkill (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River Valley (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T14:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b298c711-6430-5867-87f6-d24ae4c76028', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b298c711-6430-5867-87f6-d24ae4c76028'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian propaganda machine has not gotten this much mileage out of a U.S. citizen since the 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/snowden-and-a-cold-war-revival/', 'snippet': 'The Russian propaganda machine has not gotten this much mileage out of a U.S. citizen since the 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The greatest media event of the Cold War occurred on July 12, 2013. By all accounts, the scene at Moscow’s Sheremetyevo International Airport on Friday afternoon was like nothing those present had ever seen — and most were no strangers to media madness. One witness said she had feared she might be torn apart by the journalists. Her concerns were not baseless: Though there apparently were no human casualties, the mob of reporters did break an escalator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snowden and a Cold War Revival', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lokshina, Tanya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T14:36:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a271685f-a74c-53a8-bee7-85fd73452f21', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a271685f-a74c-53a8-bee7-85fd73452f21'}, {'abstract': 'The Home Run Derby may be the most popular part of baseball’s All-Star festivities, and the most coveted seats for Monday’s event at Citi Field are far from the action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/sports/baseball/at-home-run-derby-the-cheap-seats-are-anything-but.html', 'snippet': 'The Home Run Derby may be the most popular part of baseball’s All-Star festivities, and the most coveted seats for Monday’s event at Citi Field are far from the action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hottest seat in town this week might not be behind home plate for Tuesday night’s All-Star Game at Citi