umbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/nyregion/15cityroom-sign-1/15cityroom-sign-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/nyregion/15cityroom-sign-1/15cityroom-sign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/15/nyregion/15cityroom-sign-1/15cityroom-sign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/nyregion/15cityroom-sign-1/15cityroom-sign-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret Behind a Mysterious Traffic Code? It’s Made Up', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rule Is Real; Part of Its Sign Was Made Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Signals and Signs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Samuel I', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T14:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed0d7b19-8190-50fc-aea4-c9c8cb35651a', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed0d7b19-8190-50fc-aea4-c9c8cb35651a'}, {'abstract': 'About 218,000 cars from the 2008-9 model years are under investigation for a potential wiring problem that has led to smoke and melted wiring in a few cases.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/n-h-t-s-a-investigates-mercedes-c-class-for-potential-electrical-problems/', 'snippet': 'About 218,000 cars from the 2008-9 model years are under investigation for a potential wiring problem that has led to smoke and melted wiring in a few cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is investigating the possibility that faulty electrical wiring can cause fires on about 218,000 Mercedes-Benz C-Class models from 2008-9. The safety agency has received 21 complaints from owners, including three reports of small fires in the trunk, according to a report posted over the weekend on the N.H.T.S.A. Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/automobiles/wheels/mercedes-c-class/mercedes-c-class-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/automobiles/wheels/mercedes-c-class/mercedes-c-class-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/automobiles/wheels/mercedes-c-class/mercedes-c-class-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/automobiles/wheels/mercedes-c-class/mercedes-c-class-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1178, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/automobiles/wheels/mercedes-c