er, a new study suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/the-possible-cancer-toll-of-ct-scans/', 'snippet': 'Each year more than four million CT scans are performed on children, and they are increasing the risk for future cancer, a new study suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each year more than four million CT scans are performed on children, and they are increasing the risk for future cancer, a new study suggests.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Possible Cancer Toll of CT Scans', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childhood: CT Scans Raising Cancer Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computerized Axial Tomography (CAT Scans)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JAMA Pediatrics (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T17:45:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b738fed-914b-569a-8cb1-e3dc7650f2ee', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b738fed-914b-569a-8cb1-e3dc7650f2ee'}, {'abstract': 'Neither the Trayvon Martin trial nor the matter of Edward Snowden is easy to explain to children, and that’s exactly what makes both worth talking about.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/talking-truth-trials-and-trayvon-with-children/', 'snippet': 'Neither the Trayvon Martin trial nor the matter of Edward Snowden is easy to explain to children, and that’s exactly what makes both worth talking about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any parents who expected a clear lesson about race to emerge from the trial of George Zimmerman for the death of Trayvon Martin were surely disappointed by the complexities of the actual testimony, and the result. Discussion of what looked, to many observers, like decisions by Mr. Zimmerman made because of racial bias (his initial interpretation of Mr. Martin as “real suspicious;” his choice to disregard the suggestion by the 911 operator that “we don’t need you” to follow Mr. Martin) was complicated by the fact that those decisions were not on trial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Truth, Trials and Trayvon With Children', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T17:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a2017b3-bbab-5454-a614-6bab2f913e28', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a2017b3-bbab-5454-a614-6bab2f913e28'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Harvey will be the first pitcher to start the All-Star Game in his team’s home stadium since Roger Clemens did it in Houston in 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/sports/baseball/all-star-game.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Harvey will be the first pitcher to start the All-Star Game in his team’s home stadium since Roger Clemens did it in Houston in 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Mets cited a blister and a rising innings count as their reasons for manipulating Matt Harvey’s pitching schedule, the hope was that their showpiece pitcher would still be able to start in the showcase event at their home stadium.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/sports/Y-ALLSTAR/Y-ALLSTAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType':