on Practices Constitutional?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eighth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T20:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e10375f-b266-52bd-8b8c-fc484d92dd4d', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e10375f-b266-52bd-8b8c-fc484d92dd4d'}, {'abstract': 'Police officers in Union Square dealt with the extreme heat.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/union-square-324-p-m/', 'snippet': 'Police officers in Union Square dealt with the extreme heat.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Union Square, 3:24 P.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Union Square (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T21:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa59b30d-b68a-5914-8770-e37b506b7704', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa59b30d-b68a-5914-8770-e37b506b7704'}, {'abstract': 'Yoshiko Chuma presented a multidisciplinary work at La MaMa last weekend that incorporated dance, violin, electric guitar, trombone and the making of a daguerreotype.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/arts/dance/yoshiko-chuma-brings-her-exotic-blend-to-la-mama.html', 'snippet': 'Yoshiko Chuma presented a multidisciplinary work at La MaMa last weekend that incorporated dance, violin, electric guitar, trombone and the making of a daguerreotype.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before each performance of Yoshiko Chuma’s “π=3.14...Ramallah-Fukushima-Bogotá Endless Peripheral Border,” at La MaMa’s Galleria over the weekend, the Japanese artist Takashi Arai made a daguerreotype. That process from photography’s beginnings, in which an image is produced on a silvered copper plate, is far from instant. The exposure takes many minutes, as do the chemical dipping and spraying, the holding over a flame, the drying and the framing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/chuma/chuma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/chuma/chuma-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/chuma/chuma-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/chuma/chuma-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/chuma/chuma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda