.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/world/europe/spain-rajoy.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy has been forced to confront a rising tide of fraud accusations and calls from the opposition for him to resign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Confronted by an intensifying corruption scandal, Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy of Spain insisted on Monday that he would not yield to “blackmail” and resign, even as his former party treasurer reportedly acknowledged before a judge that he had made payments for years to Mr. Rajoy and other center-right politicians from a secret party slush fund.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/world/0716SPAIN/0716SPAIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain’s Premier Refuses to Resign in Fraud Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain’s Premier Refuses To Resign in Fraud Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajoy, Mariano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Popular Party (Spain)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barcenas, Luis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T21:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04439ef3-559c-55f1-9386-21f572b62cec', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04439ef3-559c-55f1-9386-21f572b62cec'}, {'abstract': 'Average cholesterol levels in Americans have stopped falling since 2008, a study finds, raising concerns about an increase in heart disease and the effectiveness of statins.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/15/cholesterol-levels-are-leveling-off/', 'snippet': 'Average cholesterol levels in Americans have stopped falling since 2008, a study finds, raising concerns about an increase in heart disease and the effectiveness of statins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pharmaceutical companies are racing to develop a new class of drugs that may lower blood levels of LDL cholesterol to a point few scientists had believed attainable, The New York Times reported last week. For many people with high cholesterol, the breakthrough can’t come soon enough.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16CHOL/16CHOL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cholesterol Levels Are Leveling Off', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cholesterol Levels Plateau', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholesterol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statins (Cholesterol-Lowering Drugs)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T21:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Tarkan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tarkan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e282601-3c59-5c2d-85db-25fb297958a1', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e282601-3c59-5c2d-85db-25fb297958a1'}, {'abstract': 'A new study suggests that the extinct little people known as hobbits were not just modern Homo sapiens with growth disorders but members of a distinct species.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/science/hobbits-size-not-likely-linked-to-growth-disorders.html', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that the extinct little people known as hobbits were not just modern Homo sapiens with growth disorders but members of a distinct species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much about the extinct little people nicknamed hobbits remains roundly contentious 10 years after their fossils were discovered on the Indonesian island of Flores. But a new study has weighed in with strong support for the original hypothesis about them: that they were remnants of a previously unknown distinct species of the genus Homo that lived as recently as 17,000 years ago.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16HOBB1/16HOBB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 947, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16HOBB1/16HOBB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 947}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/science/16HOBB1/16HOBB1-jumbo.jpg', 'he