iddlename': 'Rafael', 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindsay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Abe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sater', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Kriston', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7b71ab9c-1170-5b36-b875-da1ee2d933eb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7b71ab9c-1170-5b36-b875-da1ee2d933eb'}, {'abstract': 'Two experimental gonorrhea treatments are nearly 100 percent effective but have harsh side effects, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/health/caution-urged-on-gonorrhea-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'Two experimental gonorrhea treatments are nearly 100 percent effective but have harsh side effects, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two experimental gonorrhea treatments are nearly 100 percent effective but harsh side effects mean they should be reserved for patients allergic to current first-line therapy, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said Monday. Like current therapy, the new treatments involve use of two classes of oral and injected antibiotics. The new combinations of azithromycin with either gentacimin or gemifloxicin cured nearly all 400 gonorrhea victims in a clinical trial, but more than a third suffered nausea, diarrhea or abdominal pain. No patients had unusual strains of the disease. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caution Urged on Gonorrhea Drugs', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health',