anmar Admits to Political Prisoners, Pledging Their Freedom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar Admits to Political Prisoners, Pledging Their Freedom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T23:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1545f371-cb10-549a-b3a2-a0dda3ddbe7e', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1545f371-cb10-549a-b3a2-a0dda3ddbe7e'}, {'abstract': 'In Steven Levenson’s play “The Unavoidable Disappearance of Tom Durnin,” Mr. Denham plays James, the son of a disgraced former securities attorney who served a five-year prison sentence for fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000002337219/in-performance-christopher-denham.html', 'snippet': 'In Steven Levenson’s play “The Unavoidable Disappearance of Tom Durnin,” Mr. Denham plays James, the son of a disgraced former securities attorney who served a five-year prison sentence for fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Steven Levenson’s play “The Unavoidable Disappearance of Tom Durnin,” Mr. Denham plays James, the son of a disgraced former securities attorney who served a five-year prison sentence for fraud.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/arts/video-inperformance-denham/video-inperformance-denham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/15/arts/video-inperformance-denham/video-inperformance-denham-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/arts/video-inperformance-denham/video-inperformance-denham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/15/arts/video-inperformance-denham/video-inperformance-denham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/15/arts/video-inperformance-denham/video-inperformance-denham-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Christopher Denham', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denham, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levenson, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-15T23:36:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Poh Si Teng and Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Poh', 'middlename': 'Si', 'lastname': 'Teng', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/40732330-073a-55a2-a551-64b7d5eb4130', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/40732330-073a-55a2-a551-64b7d5eb4130'}, {'abstract': 'The death of a Frenchman held by Islamist fighters in northern Africa was confirmed on Monday after the recovery and examination of the man’s body in northern Mali.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/world/europe/france-captive-in-mali-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The death of a Frenchman held by Islamist fighters in northern Africa was confirmed on Monday after the recovery and examination of the man’s body in northern Mali.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The death of a Frenchman held by Islamist fighters in northern Africa was confirmed on Monday, President François Hollande announced, after the recovery and examination of the man’s body in northern Mali. The man, Philippe Verdon, 53, had been kidnapped in northeastern Mali in November 2011. Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb, the regional affiliate of Al Qaeda, said in March that Mr. Verdon had been killed, but the claim could not be confirmed, and his family suggested that he might have died of a heart ailment. His body will be returned to France, Mr. Hollande said. Mr. Verdon was kidnapped with another Frenchman, Serge Lazarevic, who remains a captive; the two were said to have been in the isolated town of Hombori, Mali, on business, but some French media outlets speculated that they might have been arms dealers or spies. At least six other French citizens are believed to be held by militants in the region. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Captive in Mali Is Dead', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Captive in Mali Is Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verdon, Philippe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T00:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b18587c0-fe0c-5d18-af02-df66ba34b541', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b18587c0-fe0c-5d18-af02-df66ba34b541'}, {'abstract': 'As the debate over immigration reform continues, more than 4.4 million legal immigrants languish in a broken visa system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/us/legal-immigrants-seek-reward-for-years-of-following-the-rules.html', 'snippet': 'As the debate over immigration reform continues, more than 4.4 million legal immigrants languish in a broken visa system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angeles P. Barberena has always tried to follow the United States’ immigration laws. She dutifully filed her petition to become a resident, complied with the requirements and paid her taxes and fees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/us/sub-IMMIG-2/sub-IMMIG-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/us/sub-IMMIG-2/sub-IMMIG-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlar