', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc6e3b3e-7609-5aa9-bcec-8982489e2d35', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc6e3b3e-7609-5aa9-bcec-8982489e2d35'}, {'abstract': 'A study suggests that a child’s gift for spatial reasoning may better predict future innovation than math or verbal skills, particularly in math and science fields.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/us/study-finds-early-signs-of-creativity-in-adults.html', 'snippet': 'A study suggests that a child’s gift for spatial reasoning may better predict future innovation than math or verbal skills, particularly in math and science fields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A gift for spatial reasoning — the kind that may inspire an imaginative child to dismantle a clock or the family refrigerator — may be a greater predictor of future creativity or innovation than math or verbal skills, particularly in math, science and related fields, according to a study published Monday in the journal Psychological Science.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Finds Spatial Skill Is Early Sign of Creativity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Finds Spatial Skill Is Early Sign Of Creativity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quenqua, Douglas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence and Intelligence Tests (IQ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Psychological Science (Journal)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T00:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccdb691d-eb9d-5224-a0d9-0951462ca8b6', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccdb691d-eb9d-5224-a0d9-0951462ca8b6'}, {'abstract': 'In exchange, the students were offered another gathering space and an invitation to join school leaders to seek a way out of the school’s financial crisis that would not require charging tuition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/nyregion/protesters-agree-to-vacate-top-office-at-cooper-union.html', 'snippet': 'In exchange, the students were offered another gathering space and an invitation to join school leaders to seek a way out of the school’s financial crisis that would not require charging tuition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 65 days, nightly light shows, one salon exhibition, a dozen or so guest lectures and a running debate about how to alter history, the occupation of Cooper Union has come to a peaceful and reportedly productive end. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters Vacate Cooper Union’s Top Office', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters Vacate Cooper Union’s Top Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaminer, Ariel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooper Union for the Advancement of Science and Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T00:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63962211-d395-5388-abf2-85e3b2060dbe', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63962211-d395-5388-abf2-85e3b2060dbe'}, {'abstract': 'Every July, the Finnish town of Seinajoki draws thousands of people to a four-day tango festival, and many say the dance’s blend of passion and brooding perfectly expresses the Finnish soul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/world/europe/finnish-tango-the-passion-and-the-melancholy.html', 'snippet': 'Every July, the Finnish town of Seinajoki draws thousands of people to a four-day tango festival, and many say the dance’s blend of passion and brooding perfectly expresses the Finnish soul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEINAJOKI, Finland — Every July, this modest Finnish town, population 59,000, transforms several square blocks downtown into a vast dance hall. Stages are erected, tents are put up, and thousands of Finns — along with Spaniards, Germans and even a smattering of Japanese and North and South Americans — gather to dance for four days to the smoldering rhythms of the tango. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finnish Tango: The Passion and the Melancholy', 'kicker': 'Seinajoki Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finnish Tango: The Passion and the Melancholy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tango', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tagliabue, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Finland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seinajoki (Finland)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T00:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Tagliabue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tagliabue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a6eb18d-3648-5811-ac75-d03af60ad012', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a6eb18d-3648-5811-ac75-d03af60ad012'}, {'abstract': 'Blocked political appointments have left the National Labor Relations Board without its full slate of five members throughout the Obama presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/us/politics/vacancies-and-partisan-fighting-put-labor-relations-agency-in-legal-limbo.html', 'snippet': 'Blocked political appointments have left the National Labor Relations Board without its full slate of five members throughout the Obama presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — At the heart of the rancorous showdown between Senate Republicans and Democrats over President Obama’s blocked political appointments is an unglamorous federal agency that polices labor practices and that has, for Republicans, become a reviled symbol of the Obama administration’s bureaucratic overreach.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/us/N