cations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T01:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/54701fe9-e034-51d4-af4f-9d7efdba6968', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54701fe9-e034-51d4-af4f-9d7efdba6968'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration announced tougher guidelines to protect the news media from federal investigators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/opinion/new-rules-protecting-news-media.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration announced tougher guidelines to protect the news media from federal investigators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Faced with intense criticism for trampling basic press freedoms while chasing government leakers, the Obama administration has announced tougher rules to protect the news media from federal criminal investigators. The new guidelines, if followed, would make it more difficult to secretly review a media organization’s e-mails, phone or business records or other communications. And Attorney General Eric Holder Jr.’s office promised on Friday that “members of the news media will not be subject to prosecution based solely on news-gathering activities.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Rules Protecting News Media', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rules Protecting News Media', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T01:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7f99fad-80aa-5511-ad17-a1bb76442fcf', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7f99fad-80aa-5511-ad17-a1bb76442fcf'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats should proceed with banning the filibuster for executive-branch appointments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/opinion/a-step-to-majority-rule-in-the-senate.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats should proceed with banning the filibuster for executive-branch appointments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of growing Republican obstruction — legislation blocked, judicial candidates forced to withdraw, presidential nominations left to languish, government agencies rendered powerless by denying them leaders — Senate Democrats say they are finally ready to take action. Barring a last-minute deal, Harry Reid, the majority leader, said he would move to change the Senate rules on Tuesday to ban the filibuster for executive appointments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Step to Majority Rule in the Senate', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Step to Majority Rule in the Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T01:14:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c9b5d75-d7e7-5327-be9f-59e3d39edd79', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c9b5d75-d7e7-5327-be9f-59e3d39edd79'}, {'abstract': 'Poor Joe Nocera, the Yankees fan of Randolph, N.J., has been getting some pretty insulting Twitter messages. But they weren’t meant for him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/opinion/nocera-a-case-against-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'Poor Joe Nocera, the Yankees fan of Randolph, N.J., has been getting some pretty insulting Twitter messages. But they weren’t meant for him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing you notice when you arrive at the home of the other Joe Nocera is the New York Yankees’ flag that hangs from his porch. Joe, 46, who lives with his family in Randolph, N.J., has rooted for the Yankees for as long as he can remember. A regional manager for a big fast-food franchisee, Joe is as passionate about the Bronx Bombers today as he was growing up in Queens. So passionate that, a few years ago, he decided to start writing about the Yankees on Twitter. His handle — is that what you call it? — is @joenocera.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Case Against Twitter', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Case Against Twitter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T01:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'a