its platforms, may finally be approaching extinction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/nyregion/mta-will-end-mystery-of-where-the-g-train-stops.html', 'snippet': 'The so-called G train sprint, wrought by a line whose trains are too short for its platforms, may finally be approaching extinction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is perhaps the most Darwinian corridor of the subway system, demanding either speed or cunning from riders hoping to evade the transit equivalent of captivity: waiting for a second G train.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/nyregion/subGTRAIN/subGTRAIN-