intense, enveloping, gratifyingly thorough screen adaptation of Mr. Turow’s story.” She added: “This version of ‘Presumed Innocent’ is notably more subdued than Mr. Turow’s, and at times its grimness and reserve risk becoming overwhelming. But this director’s best work (particularly ‘All the President’s Men’ and ‘Klute,’ both of which are powerfully recalled by ‘Presumed Innocent’) can make restraint a great virtue, turning it into a slow-burning fuse.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d2540a5-5b9c-5efd-982a-9f7a0170a660', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d2540a5-5b9c-5efd-982a-9f7a0170a660'}, {'abstract': 'In his final season, relief pitcher Mariano Rivera is taking a behind-the-scenes tour to meet some fans and employees, who drive the machinery of baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/sports/baseball/yankees-rivera-spends-his-goodbye-tour-saying-hello.html', 'snippet': 'In his final season, relief pitcher Mariano Rivera is taking a behind-the-scenes tour to meet some fans and employees, who drive the machinery of baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two and a half hours before the game, Mariano Rivera sat in the owner’s suite at Target Field in Minneapolis, wearing his batting practice uniform, sneakers and a dark blue Yankees cap. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'sourc