: 'nyt://article/bc7bf729-1512-529d-a001-c7bef151d678'}, {'abstract': 'Why is Fabrice Tourre, a former Goldman employee, the only person on trial for a 2007 scheme to defraud investors?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/the-s-e-c-s-fall-guy/', 'snippet': 'Why is Fabrice Tourre, a former Goldman employee, the only person on trial for a 2007 scheme to defraud investors?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jury selection was completed on Monday in the case of Fabrice Tourre, the former midlevel Goldman Sachs employee accused by the Securities and Exchange Commission of participating in a scheme to defraud investors in the run up to the financial crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street’s Fall Guy', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T13:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65d491a6-bfe0-5b08-9955-869a0580b2b6', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65d491a6-bfe0-5b08-9955-869a0580b2b6'}, {'abstract': 'Cutting wages: not a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/the-paradox-of-flexibility/', 'snippet': 'Cutting wages: not a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett’s latest has some interesting history from the 1930s that just so happens to bear on my mild chiding of Noah Smith (Smith has an answer that, frankly, I don’t understand — but he’s been such a good guy over time that I’m just going to let this one drop). Anyway, Bartlett focuses largely on the malign influence of Henry Hazlitt, who was among other things writing many editorials for the New York Times, always insisting that the answer to the Great Depression was to encourage big cuts in wages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Paradox of Flexibility', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T13:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12d5f641-dae4-5d39-907b-d5fd3fbfb8e5', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12d5f641-dae4-5d39-907b-d5fd3fbfb8e5'}, {'abstract': 'A royal carriage for a future heir to the throne.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/opinion/global/waiting-for-royal-baby.html', 'snippet': 'A royal carriage for a future heir to the throne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A royal carriage for a future heir to the throne.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/opinion/global/16iht-edchappatte16/16iht-edchappatte16-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/opinion/global/16iht-edchappatte16/16iht-edchappatte16-articleLarge.jpg', 'x