ps://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/holy-ambivalence/', 'snippet': 'I fast for Tisha B’av, but don’t ask me why: Like many Jews, I don’t know how to feel about Temple Mount.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — This Tuesday is a day of mourning for Jews. It is Tisha B’av, which commemorates the destruction of the First Temple by the Babylonians (586 B.C.) and of the Second Temple by the Romans (in A.D. 70). The day is supposed to be marked by fasting, a practice most Jewish Israelis don’t observe. I do, but don’t ask me why: Like many Jews, I’m not sure how I feel about this holiday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holy Ambivalence', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temple Mount (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Temple Mount (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western Wall (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T15:14:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/935844a1-00fa-506d-ad53-cfae00fba7b6', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/935844a1-00fa-506d-ad53-cfae00fba7b6'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers on Tuesday reached a deal to preserve the delaying tactic in exchange for Senate confirmation of President Obama’s long-sought nominee for consumer protection chief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/us/politics/senators-near-agreement-to-avert-fight-over-filibuster.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers on Tuesday reached a deal to preserve the delaying tactic in exchange for Senate confirmation of President Obama’s long-sought nominee for consumer protection chief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senate leaders reached an agreement on Tuesday to preserve the filibuster in exchange for confirmation votes on President Obama’s stalled nominees, ending, at least for now, months of partisan warfare that threatened the stability of several federal agencies and a generation of procedural traditions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/us/JP-FILIBUSTER/JP-FILIBUSTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/us/JP-FILIBUSTER/JP-FILIBUSTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/us/JP-FILIBUSTER/JP-FILIBUSTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/us/JP-FILIBUSTER/JP-FILIBUSTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/us/JP-FILIBUSTER/JP-FILIBUSTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/us/JP-FILIBUSTER/JP-FILIBUSTER-t