ow can his working parents find child care, and how can they find him a place to succeed?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s rare for us to label a child here at Motherlode. They’re children first, with the modifiers after — a child with Attention Deficient Hyperactivity Disorder; a child who uses a wheelchair. Language matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What if No Day Care Will Take Your A.D.H.D. Child?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Day Care Centers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T15:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e76d560-1c8a-54ea-852e-c75ae440b01e', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e76d560-1c8a-54ea-852e-c75ae440b01e'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/the-gun-report-july-16-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much attention has been paid, and rightly so, to the stalking and killing of 16-year-old Trayvon Martin, who was unarmed, in a residential neighborhood in Sanford, Fla., last year, as well as the disproportionate rate at which people (and children) of color are losing their lives to gun violence. And though the George Zimmerman trial has concluded, another is about to begin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: July 16, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T15:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b9d965-1868-538c-a6ce-f8cd0569b36a', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b9d965-1868-538c-a6ce-f8cd0569b36a'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Kidd, the Nets’ new coach, was placed on interim probation and agreed to speak to Long Island high school students about the dangers of drunken driving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/sports/basketball/kidd-expected-to-plead-guilty-to-drunken-driving-charge.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Kidd, the Nets’ new coach, was placed on interim probation and agreed to speak to Long Island high school students about the dangers of drunken driving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Kidd pleaded guilty to a drunken-driving charge on Tuesday, exposing him to a likely suspension from the N.B.A. that could postpone his coaching debut with the Nets this fall.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/SUB-KIDD/SUB-KIDD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/SUB-KIDD/SUB-KIDD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'