39e438a93ac6', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/887927d9-2029-51f1-b743-39e438a93ac6'}, {'abstract': 'The effortlessly elegant singer-songwriter and former First Lady of France shares her tips for formal dressing, healthy skin and more.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/rules-of-style-carla-bruni-sarkozy-on-the-allure-of-the-pantsuit-and-the-importance-of-staying-hydrated/', 'snippet': 'The effortlessly elegant singer-songwriter and former First Lady of France shares her tips for formal dressing, healthy skin and more.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My personal style’s never really changed,” Carla Bruni-Sarkozy explained recently. Wearing a striped pantsuit and worn brown leather men’s brogues, the former model and onetime first lady of France was sitting on a sofa in her suite at the London Hotel in New York City, puffing an e-cigarette. In town to promote her fourth album, the simple, easygoing “Little French Songs,” she showed no ill effects from a late night performing at the Royalton Hotel the previous night — her only American gig this year, though she does plan to tour the United States in 2014. Here, the effortlessly elegant 45-year-old shares a few of her timeless style maxims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rules of Style | Carla Bruni-Sarkozy on the Allure of the Pantsuit and the Importance of Staying Hydrated', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Carla', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T17:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b6fe1a8-af4e-57f2-8856-b5bfd141756c', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b6fe1a8-af4e-57f2-8856-b5bfd141756c'}, {'abstract': 'Although it is natural to think that having access to information that influences the markets before others is always wrong, the laws on fraud do not go that far.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/possibly-unfair-but-not-necessarily-fraudulent/', 'snippet': 'Although it is natural to think that having access to information that influences the markets before others is always wrong, the laws on fraud do not go that far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When someone has access to a service that is not equally available to others, the immediate response is often to say, “That’s not fair!” And when the securities markets are involved, the first thought seems to be that any informational advantage is not only unfair but potentially fraudulent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Possibly Unfair, but Not Necessarily Fraudulent', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Confidence (Economic Indicator)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thomson Reuters Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T17:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5625dba-6b26-59a6-80f5-e11cb536c701', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5625dba-6b26-59a6-80f5-e11cb536c701'}, {'abstract': 'Getting to know the weirder side of Sears.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/john-galt-and-the-theory-of-the-firm/', 'snippet': 'Getting to know the weirder side of Sears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via David Atkins at Digby’s place, Bloomberg Businessweek has a great piece about how an Ayn Rand-loving hedge fund guy is driving Sears into the ground. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Galt and the Theory of the Firm', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T17:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9cbba00-02d1-583b-819a-6caa949a7f4a', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9cbba00-02d1-583b-819a-6caa949a7f4a'}, {'abstract': 'Tiny craft-beer outfits, or nanos, stick to do-it-yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/dining/breweries-not-too-big-for-their-barrels.html', 'snippet': 'Tiny craft-beer outfits, or nanos, stick to do-it-yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every other Friday at 2 a.m., Rich Castagna walks out to the one-car garage behind his home in Maspeth, Queens, and fills a 55-gallon stainless-steel barrel with water. While his wife and three daughters are asleep inside the house, he fires up a burner and slowly brings the water to a boil, turning the 150-square-foot room into a sauna.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 254, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 254}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 866, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/dining/17NANO1_SPAN/17NANO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breweries Not Too Big for Their Barrels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breweries Not Too Big for Their Barrels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'