e, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8df2e298-5996-5f02-b3d3-95c7094605d6', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8df2e298-5996-5f02-b3d3-95c7094605d6'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Ohena Lembembe was found dead in his home in Yaoundé, shortly after he wrote about attacks on organizations that support gay rights. Cameroon is one of 38 African countries that criminalize homosexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/prominent-gay-rights-activist-is-found-dead-in-cameroon/', 'snippet': 'Eric Ohena Lembembe was found dead in his home in Yaoundé, shortly after he wrote about attacks on organizations that support gay rights. Cameroon is one of 38 African countries that criminalize homosexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Ohena Lembembe, a prominent activist in Cameroon for the rights of lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender and intersex people, was found dead in his apartment in the capital of Yaoundé, soon after he wrote about attacks in the country on organizations that support homosexuals, Human Rights Watch said in a statement on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prominent Gay Rights Activist Is Found Dead in Cameroon', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Wilson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gay and Lesbian Alliance Against Defamation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cameroon', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T18:24:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6169cafd-181e-596a-8e06-0730bd3d28be', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6169cafd-181e-596a-8e06-0730bd3d28be'}, {'abstract': 'The hedge fund manager William A. Ackman would have a pretty good shot at agitating for change at a company like ADT, according to an analysis. A company like FedEx would be a harder target.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/estimating-ackmans-odds-of-success-at-his-next-target/', 'snippet': 'The hedge fund manager William A. Ackman would have a pretty good shot at agitating for change at a company like ADT, according to an analysis. A company like FedEx would be a harder target.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the activist investor William A. Ackman hunts for his next target, a favorite guessing game on Wall Street is to see what company he will pick next to agitate for change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Estimating Ackman’s Odds of Success at His Next Target', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'p