//article/24750086-27ec-50b4-b23e-758dd603e5ff', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24750086-27ec-50b4-b23e-758dd603e5ff'}, {'abstract': 'Talking to the authors of “Wealth and Power: China’s Long March to the Twenty-First Century.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/q-and-a-orville-schell-and-john-delury-on-chinas-quest-for-rejuvenation/', 'snippet': 'Talking to the authors of “Wealth and Power: China’s Long March to the Twenty-First Century.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING – Last November, after ascending to the top position in the Chinese Communist Party, Xi Jinping led the other six members of the new Politburo Standing Committee to an outing at the National Museum, on the east side of Tiananmen Square. The men stood in dark jackets at an exhibition on modern Chinese history titled “The Road to Rejuvanation,” or 复兴之路. This was their first appearance together outside the Great Hall of the People, and so it was loaded with meaning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 659}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 933, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1821, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/books/18delury/18delury-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Orville Schell and John Delury on China’s Quest for Rejuvenation', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schell, Orville', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T18:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d8d8ec5-65dd-59ff-8262-2304a8e1d348', 'word_count': 2410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d8d8ec5-65dd-59ff-8262-2304a8e1d348'}, {'abstract': 'So much for the state’s public financing program for judicial elections.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/the-decline-of-north-carolina-continued/', 'snippet': 'So much for the state’s public financing program for judicial elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An editorial last week lamented North Carolina’s abandonment of progressive policies in the seven months since Republicans took control of both the executive and legislative branches in the Tar Heel State for the first time since reconstruction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Decline of North Carolina, Continued', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T18:52:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/930b909f-319c-5ff9-8946-cc2d3a501c5c', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/930b909f-319c-5ff9-8946-cc2d3a501c5c'}, {'abstract': 'Several digital initiatives promote reading and storytelling for children from preschool age to young adult.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/technology/personaltech/disney-encourages-readers-to-create-their-own-stories.html', 'snippet': 'Several digital initiatives promote reading and storytelling for children from preschool age to young adult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After decades of telling a wide variety of stories, like those about mice that pilot steamboats and monsters in college, Disney wants to give children and young adults the chance to create their own.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/GW-Disney-Apps/GW-Disney-Apps-articleLarge.png', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/business/GW-Disney-Apps/GW-Disney-Apps-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo',