e, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/GADGET4C/GADGET4C-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Capture the Hours With a Time-Lapse App', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Capture the Hours With a Time-Lapse App', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Furchgott, Roy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T19:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Web Log', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a171d7a-f956-5a43-8a51-b6c4b4506cf6', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a171d7a-f956-5a43-8a51-b6c4b4506cf6'}, {'abstract': 'After she shot the premiere of the new season of her TV show “Covert Affairs” in the South American metropolis, the actress thanked the folks who helped her out with an advanced outdoor screening.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/travel-diary-piper-perabo-throws-a-party-in-medellin/', 'snippet': 'After she shot the premiere of the new season of her TV show “Covert Affairs” in the South American metropolis, the actress thanked the folks who helped her out with an advanced outdoor screening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Piper Perabo landed in Medellín, Colombia, in March, to film the fourth season of the C.I.A. drama “Covert Affairs,” which premieres tonight on USA, she had never been to South America before and was surprised to be traveling to a city she knew only as the hometown of Pablo Escobar. But she was instantly impressed by Medellín, which has transformed itself from a battleground for warring drug cartels into a model of 21st-century urban planning. “The city itself is shaped like a bowl,” Perabo explained. “The downtown is on the flat part at the bottom, and then on the steep sides on the mountain rim are all what’s called the communas. Those are sort of ghettos or favelas, built in pretty steep tiers up the side of the mountain and numbered into districts.” One of Medellín’s recent innovations: a government-built escalator that safely carries passengers 1,300 feet from the communas down into the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Piper Perabo’s Party for the Residents of Medellín, Colombia', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perabo, Piper', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Medellin (Colombia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T19:16:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/598b2623-0a18-5a45-b441-fa77d5ee2e79', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/598b2623-0a18-5a45-b441-fa77d5ee2e79'}, {'abstract': 'Eliot Spitzer, who plans to finance his campaign for New York City comptroller using his family’s wealth, disclosed 2012 earnings of $4.2 million', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/nyregion/spitzer-reveals-income-but-not-the-tax-returns-a-rival-sought.html', 'snippet': 'Eliot Spitzer, who plans to finance his campaign for New York City comptroller using his family’s wealth, disclosed 2012 earnings of $4.2 million', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eliot Spitzer, who plans to finance his campaign for New York City comptroller using his family’s considerable wealth, disclosed on Tuesday that he earned more than $4.2 million in 2012 and paid about $2.1 million in federal, state and city taxes. The year before, he had an adjusted gross income of more than $3.7 million and paid about $1.5 million in combined taxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spitzer Reveals Income, but Not the Tax Returns a Rival Sought', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spitzer Reveals Income, but Stringer Wants His Tax Returns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spitzer, Eliot L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Comptrollers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T19:18:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc3bf815-8e8d-5db8-a54f-211f4d422a35', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc3bf815-8e8d-5db8-a54f-211f4d422a35'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Weiner, who has brain cancer, is facing a showdown with the commissioner’s office over players linked to the Biogenesis drug investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/sports/baseball/baseball-drug-suspensions-likely-delayed-until-next-season.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Weiner, who has brain cancer, is facing a showdown with the commissioner’s office over players linked to the Biogenesis drug investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Weiner wanted no sympathy when he met with the All-Stars this week at Citi Field. Weiner, the executive director of the players’ association, has brain cancer, and his symptoms have worsened in recent weeks. He cannot walk. He has lost the use of his right arm. His speech is slower.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/baseball-1/baseball-1374015183110-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/baseball-1/baseball-1374015183110-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/baseball-1/baseball-1374015183110-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/baseball-1/baseball-1374015183110-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1502, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/baseball-1/baseball-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/baseball-1/basebal