17/opinion/invitation-to-a-dialogue-the-myth-of-race.html', 'snippet': 'A reader says the idea of “race” is false and not supported by science. Readers are invited to reply.', 'lead_paragraph': ' ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/opinion/0717LETTERS/0717LETTERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/opinion/0717LETTERS/0717LETTERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/opinion/0717LETTERS/0717LETTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/opinion/0717LETTERS/0717LETTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/opinion/0717LETTERS/0717LETTERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Invitation to a Dialogue: The Myth of ‘Race’', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Invitation to a Dialogue: The Myth of ‘Race’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T19:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e2c954a-f533-5744-a051-fda7acf8f7bc', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e2c954a-f533-5744-a051-fda7acf8f7bc'}, {'abstract': 'A simple-majority vote to determine confirmation of executive appointments should be the rule, not a one-time deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/opinion/the-senate-clings-to-the-filibuster.html', 'snippet': 'A simple-majority vote to determine confirmation of executive appointments should be the rule, not a one-time deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Richard Cordray, who has waited for two years to be permanently appointed as director of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, the wait is over. He was confirmed on Tuesday,  after a deal was reached to avoid a ban on filibusters on presidential nominations. Senate Republicans agreed to allow the up-or-down vote on his nomination, as well as on six other appointments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Senate Clings to the Filibuster', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Senate Clings to the Filibuster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearce, Mark Gaston', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Richard F Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': '