 {'abstract': 'The brand’s latest slick, technologically sophisticated line of running shoes includes a special model that pays tribute to the Big Apple.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/feeling-for-nikes-limited-edition-free-flyknit-sneaker-celebrates-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'The brand’s latest slick, technologically sophisticated line of running shoes includes a special model that pays tribute to the Big Apple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Yorkers tend to wear their city pride on their sleeves, but only to a point. Proving that showing one’s affection for the Big Apple can be less conspicuous than donning an “I Love NY” T-shirt, Nike unveiled today a limited-edition New York City version of its new Free Flyknit running shoe, which comes with a subtle yet slick monogram of Gotham’s famous initials stretched across the laces. The Flyknit is a hybrid of the company’s ergonomic Nike Frees, which are favored by many dedicated runners, and the state-of-the-art, socklike Nike Flyknit Racer, which was introduced in April at the Salone Internazionale del Mobile in Milan. The black-soled New York City edition (all the better for pounding New York’s not-so-sanitary pavement) will be available in early August. Nike is also rolling out additional variations celebrating other international cities, including London, Tokyo, Paris, Shanghai and Rio de Janeiro. For specific availability dates for each city, please visit nikestadiums.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Nike’s Limited-Edition Free Flyknit Sneaker Celebrates New York City', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sneakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New 