', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Banco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/380e429e-bc49-5d73-aaa5-087c0b507dea', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/380e429e-bc49-5d73-aaa5-087c0b507dea'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s new national political correspondent about the issues he will be covering in his new job, with a special focus on Hillary Rodham Clinton.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/video-interview-with-jonathan-martin/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s new national political correspondent about the issues he will be covering in his new job, with a special focus on Hillary Rodham Clinton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard L. Berke talks with The New York Times’s new national political correspondent about the issues he will be covering in his new job, with a special focus on Hillary Rodham Clinton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Interview With Jonathan Martin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T22:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ede5a6a0-7a87-57cf-bfe1-9605f5584ac9', 'word_count': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ede5a6a0-7a87-57cf-bfe1-9605f5584ac9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Dealin’ With Idiots,” Jeff Garlin lampoons the obsessions of adults with children on a baseball team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/movies/in-dealin-with-idiots-jeff-garlin-lampoons-parents.html', 'snippet': 'In “Dealin’ With Idiots,” Jeff Garlin lampoons the obsessions of adults with children on a baseball team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Garlin, who plays Larry David’s affable manager-sidekick in “Curb Your Enthusiasm,” knows his own strengths: watching and listening patiently to more colorful performers and then responding with resigned, understated outrage. In “Dealin’ With Idiots,” which he also directed, Mr. Garlin surrounds himself with a quirky, seemingly improvisational ensemble of comic actors (in the manner of, say, Christopher Guest’s usual players) to lampoon the obsessions of adults with children on a baseball team. The results are amusing if predictably mild.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1214, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup1/17filmroundup1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Youth League Tantrums, but Not by the Kids', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dealin’ With Idiots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Dealin' With Idiots (Movie)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garlin, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T22:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7514b355-276f-52bd-824a-04f4e55d8dcc', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7514b355-276f-52bd-824a-04f4e55d8dcc'}, {'abstract': '“Les Coquillettes” follows the fictional exploits of the film director Sophie Letourneur and her two friends at the Locarno Film Festival in Switzerland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/movies/sophie-letourneur-directs-and-stars-in-les-coquilletes.html', 'snippet': '“Les Coquillettes” follows the fictional exploits of the film director Sophie Letourneur and her two friends at the Locarno Film Festival in Switzerland.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Les Coquillettes” could be described as an effervescent and pastel-colored version of John Cassavetes’s “Husbands.” Or it could be thought of as a French version of the “Girls” episode directed by Jody Lee Lipes, in which the women head to Bushwick, Brooklyn, for what promises to be “the best party ever.” But perhaps the most accurate comparison for this film, written, directed and also starring Sophie Letourneur, is to Renata Adler’s novel “Speedboat.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1054, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/arts/17filmroundup2/17filmroundup2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Girls Behaving Badly at a Film Festival', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Les Coquillettes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letourneur, Sophie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T23:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miriam Bale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miriam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd8b9d3f-11d5-5788-893d-156cc3052f02', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd8b9d3f-11d5-5788-893d-156cc3052f02'}, {'abstract': 'Images and video posted online by reporters and witnesses offered detailed views of clashes late Monday around a train station in central Cairo.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/images-of-latest-deadly-clashes-in-cairo/', 'snippet': 'Images and video posted online by reporters and witnesses offered detailed views of clashes late Monday around a train station in central Cairo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Kareem Fahim and David Kirkpatrick report from Cairo, hours before Egypt’s new interim government was sworn in, “at least seven people were killed and more than 200 were injured in overnight clashes between Islamists and Egyptian riot police, health officials said Tuesday.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Images of Latest Deadly Clashes in Cairo', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-16T23:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2df0d4aa-a63e-5f26-afa4-a606689d4d02', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2df0d4aa-a63e-5f26-afa4-a606689d4d02'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Tuesday’s selections include a woman’s bad experience with a Lyft driver, and an app that tries to teach foreign language with cat photos.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/16/todays-scuttlebot-dark-side-of-a-taxi-app-and-language-cats/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Tuesday’s selections include a woman’s bad experience with a Lyft driver, and an app that tries to teach foreign language with cat photos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'su