ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a4ef73-68a2-525f-b858-119fb3c9b71a', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a4ef73-68a2-525f-b858-119fb3c9b71a'}, {'abstract': 'Discrimination based on beauty rests on the same sexist principle as discrimination against the ugly. And both rest on the power of the male gaze.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/opinion/fired-for-being-beautiful.html', 'snippet': 'Discrimination based on beauty rests on the same sexist principle as discrimination against the ugly. And both rest on the power of the male gaze.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOST everyone knows by now about “lookism” — the preferential treatment given to those who conform to social standards of beauty. Research suggests that people who are judged physically attractive are seen as more competent and more socially graceful than those who aren’t; they have more friends and more sex; and they make more money. One economic study found a 5 percent bonus for being in the top third in the looks department (as assessed by a set of observers), and a 7 to 9 percent penalty for being in the bottom 9 percent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fired for Being Beautiful', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fired for Being Beautiful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmel, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Melissa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knight, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T01:06:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kimmel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kimmel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b72cf9-6cd0-51e8-9253-9aa943a370ce', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b72cf9-6cd0-51e8-9253-9aa943a370ce'}, {'abstract': 'The G.O.P. aversion to an immigration bill is costing us dearly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/opinion/friedman-if-churchill-could-see-us-now.html', 'snippet': 'The G.O.P. aversion to an immigration bill is costing us dearly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever we go into political drift as a country, optimists often quote Winston Churchill’s line that Americans will always do the right thing, after they’ve “exhausted all other possibilities.” I don’t think that’s true anymore. Churchill never met the Tea Party, and he certainly never met today’s House Republicans, a group so narrow-minded and uninterested in governing — and the necessary compromises that go with it — that they’re ready to kill an immigration bill that is manifestly in the country’s economic, social and strategic interests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If Churchill Could See Us Now', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Churchill Could See Us Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T01:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materi