final season. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Giddy Youngsters, Seeking Out Rivera With Pens and Pads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Giddy Youngsters, Seeking Out Rivera With Pens and Pads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL STAR GAMES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Machado, Manny', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Chris (1986- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T01:17:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c205cd11-171b-5bee-b5e7-0335a6c9875b', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c205cd11-171b-5bee-b5e7-0335a6c9875b'}, {'abstract': 'As the sun becomes almost predatory, the conversation this year suggests this may be more than a temporary discomfort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/opinion/summers-beast-is-loose.html', 'snippet': 'As the sun becomes almost predatory, the conversation this year suggests this may be more than a temporary discomfort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On clear, mild summer mornings, whatever those are, the sun rises fat and woozy out of the East, shimmering in a pool of its own rays. But this past month, here and across the country, there has been something blunt and almost predatory about the sun the moment it frees itself from the horizon. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer’s Beast Is Loose', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer’s Beast Is Loose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T01:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2ad4fc8-2d6e-575c-ae6e-41357069ffaf', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2ad4fc8-2d6e-575c-ae6e-41357069ffaf'}, {'abstract': 'The candidates aiming to succeed Mayor Michael Bloomberg seek pro-growth policies for uncertain times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/opinion/jobs-and-the-city.html', 'snippet': 'The candidates aiming to succeed Mayor Michael Bloomberg seek pro-growth policies for uncertain times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opportunity and prosperity in New York City are spread thickly but unevenly. For too many New Yorkers, paychecks are too small and the rent too high. Life is uneasy, and recent economic and natural disasters have made it feel only more perilous, even as a luxury-apartment boom and gentrification have turned parts of the city into enclaves of prosperity and graciousness. People want jobs they can live on, in neighborhoods they can live in, but they don’t know how that is supposed to happen — or how the next mayor is going to make sure that it does.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs and the City', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs and the City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T01:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0304e4-b91c-5688-8b5a-2a6f03a76307', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0304e4-b91c-5688-8b5a-2a6f03a76307'}, {'abstract': 'At 19, Jordan Spieth became the youngest PGA Tour winner in 82 years after winning the John Deere Classic. With the victory, Spieth became eligible to compete at Muirfield.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/sports/golf/unexpected-british-trip-for-spieth.html', 'snippet': 'At 19, Jordan Spieth became the youngest PGA Tour winner in 82 years after winning the John Deere Classic. With the victory, Spieth became eligible to compete at Muirfield.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GULLANE, Scotland — Where does the jet lag end and the emotional letdown from his breakout victory begin? The teenager Jordan Spieth had no answer. He knew only that his legs felt wobbly as he stood off the ninth green at Muirfield on Tuesday after playing nine practice holes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlar