.html', 'snippet': 'Four local officials are being investigated for “dereliction of duty” in two coal mine blasts that killed 53 people last spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four local officials are being investigated for “dereliction of duty” in two coal mine blasts that killed 53 people last spring, according to a report on Tuesday by Xinhua, the state news agency. The double blasts, in Jilin Province of northeast China, were among the worst recent coal mine accidents. The Xinhua report named the officials as Li Shijun and Zhang Yuzhong, both former officials with the Work Safety Bureau in Baishan City, and Xu Shengxue and Wang Yuxi, former officials with the Baishan branch of the provincial Bureau of Coal Mine Safety.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Four Officials Detained Over Mine Explosions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T02:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e521176a-ce25-5f1e-8a8a-a5b56e205c79', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e521176a-ce25-5f1e-8a8a-a5b56e205c79'}, {'abstract': 'The move to bring back Keith Olbermann, a former co-anchor at ESPN, was the result\xa0of 14 months\xa0of intense discussion\xa0within the network and its parent, the Walt Disney Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/sports/after-16-year-absence-olbermann-is-said-to-be-returning-to-espn-to-host-show.html', 'snippet': 'The move to bring back Keith Olbermann, a former co-anchor at ESPN, was the result\xa0of 14 months\xa0of intense discussion\xa0within the network and its parent, the Walt Disney Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ESPN is expected to announce on Wednesday that the former network mainstay Keith Olbermann, who contentiously departed in 1997, will return to host a one-hour, nightly show for ESPN2 later this year, according to three executives with knowledge of the\xa0deal\xa0but not authorized to speak about it publicly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olbermann Will Return to ESPN', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olbermann Will Return To ESPN', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, James Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olbermann, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN2', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T02:56:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Andrew Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8526528f-d36b-5ff9-a425-4fe166c848c4', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8526528f-d36b-5ff9-a425-4fe166c848c4'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Rodriguez played seven innings at third base with the Trenton Thunder, the Yankees’ Class AA affiliate, in a 6-3 loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/sports/baseball/rodriguez-trentons-vip-has-yet-to-visit.html', 'snippet': 'Alex Rodriguez played seven innings at third base with the Trenton Thunder, the Yankees’ Class AA affiliate, in a 6-3 loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'READING, Pa. — After he swung and missed at a first-inning strike, Alex Rodriguez unintentionally flung his bat into the stands along the third-base line on his follow-through. Everyone appeared to be safe, and it turned out to be the most eventful sequence of the night for Rodriguez at FirstEnergy Stadium.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/arod/arod-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/arod/arod-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/arod/arod-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/arod/arod-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/arod/arod-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/17/sports/arod/arod-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r