By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf069ea-8dd3-5865-ace7-c4233ce68a01', 'word_count': 2011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf069ea-8dd3-5865-ace7-c4233ce68a01'}, {'abstract': 'How a pro-women’s group used a strategy of “community conversations” to effectively end the practice of genital cutting in an Ethiopian village.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/talking-female-circumcision-out-of-existence/', 'snippet': 'How a pro-women’s group used a strategy of “community conversations” to effectively end the practice of genital cutting in an Ethiopian village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like every other girl of her era in her part of southern Ethiopia — and most girls in the country — Bogaletch Gebre was circumcised. In some regions girls are circumcised as infants, but in her zone it happened at puberty. It was around 1967, and she was about 12. A man held her from behind, blindfolded her and stuffed a rag in her mouth, and with his legs held her legs open so she could not move. A female circumciser took a razor blade and sliced off Gebre’s genitals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Female Circumcision Out of Existence', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Female Genital Mutilation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Development Program', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ethiopia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T12:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0c3452d-f623-5632-952c-675504f917f7', 'word_count': 2047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0c3452d-f623-5632-952c-675504f917f7'}, {'abstract': 'The buzzy British designer’s shoes will be available at the department store for the first time beginning today.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/in-store-rupert-sandersons-must-have-footwear-collection-for-barneys/', 'snippet': 'The buzzy British designer’s shoes will be available at the department store for the first time beginning today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barneys New York has quietly snapped up 13 styles by Rupert Sanderson, the British shoe designer whose sexy stilettos have graced the feet of Hollywood starlets like Jessica Chastain, Amanda Seyfried and Naomi Watts. To mark his debut, Sanderson — who has also designed architectural heels for Karl Lagerfeld’s collections — created four shoes exclusively for the retailer, including demure Chelsea boots with monk straps, hand-cut strappy stilettos and two pairs of textured flats like the calf-hair one pictured above.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | Rupert Sanderson’s Must-Have Footwear Collection for Barneys', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagerfeld, Karl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barneys New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T12:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59ede619-2cea-5f52-bf32-4542c997e616', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59ede619-2cea-5f52-bf32-4542c997e616'}, {'abstract': 'Starting in December, the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater’s season will include the world premiere of an untitled work by Aszure Barton.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/alvin-ailey-announces-new-season/', 'snippet': 'Starting in December, the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater’s season will include the world premiere of an untitled work by Aszure Barton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Alvin Ailey’s death in 1989, the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater, now directed by Robert Battle, has held true to the choreographer’s insistence that the company not be a showcase for his works alone, but that it provide a palette for other choreographers as well. The company’s plans for its new season at the New York City Center further that mandate with the world premiere of an untitled work by Aszure Barton and the company premiere of “Chroma” by the British choreographer Wayne McGregor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alvin Ailey Announces New Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T12:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe9440f6-7c5a-5296-bda1-6a52797904f0', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe9440f6-7c5a-5296-bda1-6a52797904f0'}, {'abstract': 'Bank of America posts second-quarter net income of $4 billion. | Michael S. Dell is engaged in last-minute maneuvers over the company he founded. | Hiring a company’s former executive as a buyout adviser can present problems, the Deal Professor writes. | Paolo Pellegrini gets testy on the witness stand in the trial of Fabrice Tourre.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/morning-agenda-bank-of-america-profit-surges/', 'snippet': 'Bank of America posts second-quarter net income of $4 billion. | Michael S. Dell is engaged in last-minute maneuvers over the company he founded. | Hiring a company’s former executive as a buyout adviser can present problems, the Deal Professor wr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bank of America reported on Wednesday that its second-quarter net income rose 63 percent to $4 billion, or 32 cents a share, compared with $2.5 billion, or 19 cents a share, in the period a year earlier. Revenue increased to $22.7 billion from $22 billion in the period a year earlier. A conference call to discuss the results is being held at 8:30 a.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of America Profit Surges', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T12:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e3a8e0-97ae-5439-b17f-b32dade048e9', 'word_count': 1689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e3a8e0-97ae-5439-b17f-b32dade048e9'}, {'abstract': 'Ben S. Bernanke said that the Federal Reserve expected the economy to gain strength in the coming months, potentially allowing the central bank to decelerate its stimulus campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/business/economy/fed-chairman-points-finger-at-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Ben S. Bernanke said that the Federal Reserve expected the economy to gain strength in the coming months, potentially allowing the central bank to decelerate its stimulus campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve’s chairman, Ben S. Bernanke, emphasized on Wednesday that the central bank remains committed to bolstering the economy, insisting that any deceleration in the Fed’s stimulus campaign will happen because it is achieving its goals, not because it has lowered its sights.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/Fedjp/Fedjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/business/Fedjp/Fedjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/Fedjp/Fedjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/Fedjp/Fedjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/Fedjp/Fedjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'