ty, there were suffocating moments of poverty and repression. But there were also moments of grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANGON — I delight at the sight of my 60-year-old mother gingerly taking her first rides up and down the escalators of the new glitzy shopping malls downtown. In a sarong, her face smeared with thanakha (a traditional cream-colored paste made from bark) she and other women walk with their young daughters in tight jeans or miniskirts, visiting expensive supermarkets and Mango and Prada stores. Most just window-shop, simply to bask among symbols of modernity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Smoke in the Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T14:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Swe Win', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Swe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Win', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04ff8393-bbba-5755-8c9f-1d2ee3111c0f', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04ff8393-bbba-5755-8c9f-1d2ee3111c0f'}, {'abstract': 'A scene from the documentary “The Act of Killing,” about an Indonesian death squad leader re-enacting his crimes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002340589/clip-the-act-of-killing.html', 'snippet': 'A scene from the documentary “The Act of Killing,” about an Indonesian death squad leader re-enacting his crimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A scene from the documentary “The Act of Killing,” about an Indonesian death squad leader re-enacting his crimes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/video-act-of-killing/video-act-of-killing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/video-act-of-killing/video-act-of-killing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/video-act-of-killing/video-act-of-killing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/video-act-of-killing/video-act-of-killing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/16/arts/video-act-of-killing/video-act-of-killing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clip: ‘The Act of Killing’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T14:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Drafthouse Films', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Drafthouse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Films', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/00b0f55a-9c49-5e12-a4a7-1bc8ae43b9f0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/00b0f55a-9c49-5e12-a4a7-1bc8ae43b9f0'}, {'abstract': '“Prototype: Opera/Theater/Now” will present five works in January.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/cutting-edge-chamber-opera-festival-to-offer-five-works/', 'snippet': '“Prototype: Opera/Theater/Now” will present five works in January.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Prototype: Opera/Theater/Now,” a festival that presents avant-garde chamber opera, will offer its second slate of productions at Here, the cozy arts center in Greenwich Village, in January. The festival, produced by Here and Beth Morrison Projects, will include five works, among them the world premiere of “Thumbprint,” a 90-minute work by the composer and singer Kamala Sankaram and the playwright Susan Yankowitz, and “Angel’s Bone,” a work-in-progress by Du Yun, with a libretto by Royce Vavrek. The festival runs Jan. 8 to 18.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cutting-Edge Chamber Opera Festival to Offer Five Works', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T14:20:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93c8ba17-a8eb-57d2-ba29-de71ba0ef567', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93c8ba17-a8eb-57d2-ba29-de71ba0ef567'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Stoker, a former midlevel Citigroup executive who beat a government fraud case, has joined the spectators at the trial of Fabrice Tourre.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/in-audience-at-tourre-trial-a-familiar-face/', 'snippet': 'Brian Stoker, a former midlevel Citigroup executive who beat a government fraud case, has joined the spectators at the trial of Fabrice Tourre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fabrice P. Tourre and Brian Stoker share a bond: The Securities and Exchange Commission accused both men of fraud. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Audience at Tourre Trial, a Familiar Face', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoker, Brian H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T14:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a736da0-0274-5841-8a63-ab11fd8c081d', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a736da0-0274-5841-8a63-ab11fd8c081d'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Smith, who writes a blog called Ask the Pilot, explains why he thinks air travel is so safe and offers tips for fliers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/travel/a-pilots-views-on-flight-safety.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick Smith, who writes a blog called Ask the Pilot, explains why he thinks air travel is so safe and offers tips for fliers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As details emerge from the investigation into what went wrong aboard Asiana Flight 214, which crashed at San Francisco International Airport on July 6, killing three passengers and injuring scores more, some travelers may find themselves thinking twice about boarding their next flight.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/travel/21QNA1/21QNA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/travel/21QNA1/21QNA1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/travel/21QNA1/21QNA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/21/travel/21QNA1/21QNA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/travel/21QNA1/21QNA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pilot’s Views on Flight Safety', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Air safety and anxieties: Patrick Smith on concerns about flying.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, Emily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patrick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T14:28:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/41cf562f-7dd8-5276-b969-820edcb57fa2', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41cf562f-7dd8-5276-b969-820edcb57fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Whether you want to split a hotel room, share a meal or meet up with friends of friends in a foreign city, these new social Web sites could help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/travel/making-travel-connections-online.html', 'snippet': 'Whether you want to split a hotel room, share a meal or meet up with friends of friends in a foreign city, these new social Web sites could help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taking their inspiration from Web sites like Facebook and OkCupid, a flourishing category of social sites is aiming to connect travelers and their friends — especially those going solo — to help them save money, stay safe and enjoy more authentic cultural experiences. Sites like Couchsurfing, Airbnb and Planely have led the way. Now add to the genre a handful of newcomers striving to make touring a city full of strangers a little more friendly and a little less costly. (All of the sites are free to join unless otherwise noted.)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/trave