A Console With Quirks, for Tinkerers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Console With Quirks, For Tinkerers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pogue, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ouya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Open-Source Software', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T16:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34d051d9-c995-5e71-804b-4e765ee32991', 'word_count': 1309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34d051d9-c995-5e71-804b-4e765ee32991'}, {'abstract': 'Stuart Holden and Landon Donovan are trying to show that they are worthy of a permanent elevation to the elite group in United States men’s soccer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/sports/soccer/every-us-game-counts-for-holden-and-donovan.html', 'snippet': 'Stuart Holden and Landon Donovan are trying to show that they are worthy of a permanent elevation to the elite group in United States men’s soccer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST HARTFORD, Conn. — In the litany of one-off exhibitions, charity games and assorted tournaments that make up soccer’s calendar, the Gold Cup is an especially strange affair. Staged every two years by the sport’s regional governing body, Concacaf, this month’s iteration has featured: allegations from Belize regarding a failed attempt at match-fixing; dispirited play, including another disastrous performance from Mexico; and one team, Martinique, nearly advancing to the knockout round despite being ineligible for the prize that goes to the tournament’s winner.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1249, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/sports/18soccer1/18soccer1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Every U.S. Game Is a Critical Audition for Holden and Donovan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Every U.S. Game Is a Critical Audition for Holden and Donovan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holden, Stuart', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T16:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f616e121-8b18-52fb-92af-b748dc1d7fcd', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f616e121-8b18-52fb-92af-b748dc1d7fcd'}, {'abstract': 'A critic recalls the first stirrings of his fascination with classical music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/arts/music/a-critics-ode-to-a-childhood-joy-in-classical-music.html', 'snippet': 'A critic recalls the first stirrings of his fascination with classical music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before I showed up, no one in my family was musical, played an instrument or even sang in a choir. I found music on my own. In a way, my eureka moment came early, when my parents bought me a little toy piano and, like Schroeder in “Peanuts,” I started picking out tunes on it. I campaigned to get a real piano. It wasn’t until I was 8 that, seeing that I was serious, my parents complied. One day a boxy old upright was hauled into our home on Long Island.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It All Started With a Toy Piano', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Boy and His Magic Ballade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, MARIAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serkin, Rudolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T16:12:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb089ad-c3e7-56b4-9258-d50516b896ef', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb089ad-c3e7-56b4-9258-d50516b896ef'}, {'abstract': 'Brad Minor had had it with living in a studio. He decided to buy a one-bedroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/realestate/in-soho-an-apres-studio-apartment.html', 'snippet': 'Brad Minor had had it with living in a studio. He decided to buy a one-bedroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his eight years living and working in Atlanta, Brad Minor constantly declared his intention to move to New York. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/realestate/Hunt-Main/Hunt-Main-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlar