}, {'abstract': 'I spent years denying the label of “woman composer.” Not any more.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/taking-off-my-pants/', 'snippet': 'I spent years denying the label of “woman composer.” Not any more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Season of My Denial and Evasion lasted nearly two decades — from the age of 18 to 36. During this season, I wore pants for premieres of my music, while performing as a pianist and teaching, for all important composerly things. I hated the “What’s it like to be a woman composer” question at pre-concert talks, on panels and in interviews. If I couldn’t evade this question, I rattled off something dismissive: How could I possibly know any different? That’s like asking me what if I had grown up in Alaska. I refused to enter any competitions exclusively for female composers or to have my music presented at women-only concerts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Off My Pants', 'kicker': 'The Score', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T19:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristin Kuster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdeb94ab-9745-58b1-bed1-14c6990bb399', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdeb94ab-9745-58b1-bed1-14c6990bb399'}, {'abstract': 'While no technological tool is perfect, there are ways to limit one’s digital footprint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/technology/personaltech/digital-tools-to-help-curb-online-eavesdropping.html', 'snippet': 'While no technological tool is perfect, there are ways to limit one’s digital footprint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Let’s be clear. Your personal information online is not always yours to control.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/TOOLKIT/TOOLKIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/business/TOOLKIT/TOOLKIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/TOOLKIT/TOOLKIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/business/TOOLKIT/TOOLKIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 1858, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Tools to Curb Snooping', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Digital Tools To Curb Snooping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RSA, The Security Division of EMC Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cryptography, Codes and Ciphers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:08:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b894771-6d51-531a-914c-c7214a83a4b2', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b894771-6d51-531a-914c-c7214a83a4b2'}, {'abstract': 'The British culture minister deferred approval of an export license for “Rembrandt Laughing,” leaving time for a British institution to raise money to keep it.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/getty-museums-rembrandt-acquisition-hits-a-snag/', 'snippet': 'The British culture minister deferred approval of an export license for “Rembrandt Laughing,” leaving time for a British institution to raise money to keep it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The J. Paul Getty Museum in Los Angeles knows when it comes to getting an export license from the British government, sometimes you win; other times you don’t.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getty Museum’s Rembrandt Acquisition Hits a Snag', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getty and Britain Vie for a Rembrandt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Rijn, Rembrandt Harmenszoon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:17:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d0c906-ab30-5d77-ba89-ba9d74150d62', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d0c906-ab30-5d77-ba89-ba9d74150d62'}, {'abstract': '“Fats Waller: A Handful of Keys,” a tribute to the pianist, opened the 92nd Street Y’s annual Jazz in July series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/arts/music/fats-waller-opens-the-jazz-in-july-series.html', 'snippet': '“Fats Waller: A Handful of Keys,” a tribute to the pianist, opened the 92nd Street Y’s annual Jazz in July series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As two formidable pianists, Bill Charlap and Rossano Sportiello, faced each other from behind grand pianos and played Fats Waller’s “Jitterbug Waltz” on Tuesday evening at the 92nd Street Y, their surprisingly delicate dual keyboards conjured a vision of music boxes on a seesaw. The sound was rollicking but refined, as the pianists, neither known for hammering the keyboard or for injecting unruly comedy into a performance, traded variations on the theme whose melody echoes the opening verse of “Star Dust.” The performance was a high point of the program, “Fats Waller: A Handful of Keys,” which opened the Y’s 29th annual Jazz in July series. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/waller/waller-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/waller/waller-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 231}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/waller/waller-jumbo.jpg', 'height'