zation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1d3ba07-5e0d-5361-bd1c-8ad002af09df', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1d3ba07-5e0d-5361-bd1c-8ad002af09df'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Opera presented Erin Morley, Isabel Leonard and Stephen Costello in its SummerStage recital in Central Park on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/arts/music/the-met-in-the-parks-arias-lush-to-sassy-under-the-stars.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Opera presented Erin Morley, Isabel Leonard and Stephen Costello in its SummerStage recital in Central Park on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the beginning of the second half of Tuesday evening’s Metropolitan Opera SummerStage recital, the soprano Erin Morley was wheeled out in a handcart. A stage worker maneuvered her rigid legs onto the floor, arranged her bent arms in front of her chest and adjusted the angle of her head so that she faced the audience. When he was satisfied with his work, he trudged off, pulling the empty cart behind him. Then the pianist Bradley Moore played the first whimsical bars of “Les oiseaux dans la charmille” from Offenbach’s “Contes d’Hoffmann” and Ms. Morley began to sing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/opera/opera-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/opera/opera-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/opera/opera-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/opera/opera-superJ