gy reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Wednesday’s selections include a decline in investment in social media from venture capitalists, and a mathematical comparison of new phone plans from AT&T and T-Mobile.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/todays-scuttlebot-social-media-cooling-and-expensive-upgrades/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Wednesday’s selections include a decline in investment in social media from venture capitalists, and a mathematical comparison of new phone ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Social Media Cooling, and Expensive Upgrades', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0d26ea2-252f-5a4c-955d-969971c3df20', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0d26ea2-252f-5a4c-955d-969971c3df20'}, {'abstract': 'Joel Harrison brought his ambitious blend of post-Minimimalist classical music, jazz and rock to Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/arts/music/the-joel-harrison-19-a-big-band-at-dizzys-club-coca-cola.html', 'snippet': 'Joel Harrison brought his ambitious blend of post-Minimimalist classical music, jazz and rock to Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In retrospect, it feels inevitable that Joel Harrison would make a big-band record. A guitarist and composer with an itch for blending timbres, Mr. Harrison, 55, has no problem putting familiar materials to unfamiliar use. His recent work has involved a chamber septet, a “string choir,” a quintet featuring sarod and tabla, and a trio with banjo and kora. Which may not be a symptom of restlessness so much as a sign of initiative in a playing field that privileges new concepts, new contexts, a new narrative. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grueling Mix for Stout Hearts', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Grueling Mix For Stout Hearts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, Joel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:24:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', '