l': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/fashion/jonathan-simkhai-coaxing-the-clothes-from-his-head.html', 'snippet': 'As Fashion Week approaches, Mr. Simkhai mines his archives and his myriad inspirations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Simkhai spends most of his waking hours chasing cool, an ineffable quality he might spy in a random pileup of deck chairs, their stripes meandering every which way, or in the image of a skateboard gang surfing the pavements of Venice Beach. Nothing is too crazy or far-fetched to escape his roving eye.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18COUNTDOWN_SPAN/18zCOUNTDOWN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Countdown to Fashion Week for Designer Jonathan Simkhai', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coaxing the Clothes From His Head', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simkhai, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a1faaa0-763f-506c-b189-0f68e4498011', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a1faaa0-763f-506c-b189-0f68e4498011'}, {'abstract': 'Staff Sgt. Joseph Chamblin said he had no regrets about the incident and would do it again out of revenge for the killing of American soldiers.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/marine-who-urinated-on-taliban-corpses-says-he-has-no-regrets/', 'snippet': 'Staff Sgt. Joseph Chamblin said he had no regrets about the incident and would do it again out of revenge for the killing of American soldiers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A United States Marine who was videotaped with several others urinating on the corpses of Taliban fighters in Afghanistan in 2011 said in remarks broadcast this week that he had no regrets about the incident and would do it again out of revenge for the killing of American soldiers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marine Who Urinated on Taliban Corpses Says He Has No Regrets', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dede631-e573-515a-9152-23fee173606b', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dede631-e573-515a-9152-23fee173606b'}, {'abstract': 'My obstetrician ignored my symptoms of postpartum depression, and told me to take more ‘me’ time. Just like that, I slipped through the cracks, and I’m not alone. There’s no universal screening for depression in women after giving birth.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/who-will-screen-for-postpartum-depression/', 'snippet': 'My obstetrician ignored my symptoms of postpartum depression, and told me to take more ‘me’ time. Just like that, I slipped through the cracks, and I’m not alone. There’s no universal screening for depression in women after giving birth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I attended the prestigious festival premier of my first documentary film in a fog. Zombielike, I answered audience questions, attended mixers, absorbed nothing. Then I returned to my hotel room and wept. As independent filmmakers, we (my husband and I) had worked hard to get to this point. And I was a mess. Frozen with worry, I watched myself squandering this great career opportunity and felt helpless to do anything about it. I was six months postpartum and felt like I was lying beneath a thick pile of sodden blankets and, in spite of my great drive to fight my way out, I remained pinned to the ground, gasping for air.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Will Screen for Postpartum Depression?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T20:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Gonser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8731dc9-1cf3-5ef8-9ae6-3b87d360bcae', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8731dc9-1cf3-5ef8-9ae6-3b87d360bcae'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s lower earnings reflect the trend of fewer personal computer sales worldwide and the trouble Intel has had moving to mobile devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/technology/revenue-falls-at-intel-as-pc-sales-sag.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s lower earnings reflect the trend of fewer personal computer sales worldwide and the trouble Intel has had moving to mobile devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After decades at the center of Silicon Valley, Intel is now struggling with one of the technology industry’s oldest lessons: beware the cheaper, “good enough” competitor.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': 