end $3 on coconut water when $10 buys a small bottle of kale-green goodness, cold-pressed and extracted from locally sourced vegetables? Not all juices are equal. Here’s a primer to the pulpy bounty:', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18zJUICE1B-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18zJUICE1B-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 281}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18zJUICE1B-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18zJUICE1B-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18JUICE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18JUICE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/fashion/18JUICE_SPAN/18JUICE_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Juice-Box Set Grows Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Juice-Box Set Grows Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortved, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T21:25:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Ortved', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ortved', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/819a4a0c-cbbe-5f9e-8486-ac1b18117e37', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/819a4a0c-cbbe-5f9e-8486-ac1b18117e37'}, {'abstract': 'With notably rare exceptions …', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/17/the-prophecies-of-maestrodamus/', 'snippet': 'With notably rare exceptions …', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oh, my. Brad Delong recalls to us Alan Greenspan’s lamentable 2010 op-ed on US debt and deficits. What’s notable about the piece is not just that Greenspan was wrong about everything that would happen over the next three years; he’s actually part of a substantial club on that point. Nor, I guess, is it notable that, to all appearances, he has learned nothing at all from his predictive failures — that the fact that he was wrong about everything, while the Keynesians got almost everything right, has made no dent in his faith that he has The Truth. Again, that makes him part of a substantial club.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Prophecies of Maestrodamus', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-17T21:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'las