e current negotiating team, which has been led by Saeed Jalili, a hard-line conservative who was among the presidential candidates defeated by Mr. Rowhani in the June 14 elections. Mr. Salehi was quoted by the Iranian Students’ News Agency as saying that the talks would restart but that first Mr. Rowhani — a former nuclear negotiator — “should assume the responsibility and appoint the negotiating team.” Iran has rejected demands by the so-called P5-plus-1 powers — the five permanent members of the Security Council plus Germany — to halt uranium enrichment. Iran asserts the enrichment is for peaceful purposes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nuclear Program Talks Could Resume, Iranian Official Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Nuclear Program Talks Could Resume, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salehi, Ali Akbar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowhani, Hassan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T00:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1693bc9e-b37a-5bd5-b60a-6d736b7054cf', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1693bc9e-b37a-5bd5-b60a-6d736b7054cf'}, {'abstract': 'Cutting the tax to 13 percent from 23 percent, effective Aug. 1, is seen as a way to aid small businesses and bolster the tourism sector.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/world/europe/greece-wins-concession-on-tax-for-restaurant-meals.html', 'snippet': 'Cutting the tax to 13 percent from 23 percent, effective Aug. 1, is seen as a way to aid small businesses and bolster the tourism sector.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — As Greek lawmakers prepared to vote on a package of new austerity measures, Prime Minister Antonis Samaras said Wednesday that the country’s lenders had agreed to a major concession, a sharp reduction in the sales tax on restaurant meals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Wins Concession on Tax for Restaurant Meals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Wins Concession on Tax for Restaurant Meals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T00:29:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edeacded-de68-5562-add8-5be3bb7380a0', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edeacded-de68-5562-add8-5be3bb7380a0'}, {'abstract': 'The leader of the R&A, which conducts the British Open, said the policy of men-only clubs was in no way comparable to racial or religious discrimination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/sports/golf/member-policy-of-men-only-clubs-will-be-reviewed-ra-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'The leader of the R&A, which conducts the British Open, said the policy of men-only clubs was in no way comparable to racial or religious discrimination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GULLANE, Scotland — The leader of the R&A, which conducts the British Open, said the matter of men-only clubs would be reviewed but added that the exclusionary policy was in no way comparable to racial or religious discrimination.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Member Policy of Men-Only Clubs Will Be Reviewed, R&A Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Member Policy To Get Review, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muirfield Golf Club (Gullane, Scotland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T00:41:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f345e2a-f2d6-597d-aadb-98d90b587021', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f345e2a-f2d6-597d-aadb-98d90b587021'}, {'abstract': 'As more and more Italians reach their 100th birthdays, younger generations are supporting a growing social safety net but have fewer job opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000002342205/italys-centenarian-generation.html', 'snippet': 'A