gration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strange, David N', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:06:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alberto R. Gonzales and David N. Strange', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alberto', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gonzales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Strange', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b223e0-012c-581e-a9c2-06bcc7e4cab6', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b223e0-012c-581e-a9c2-06bcc7e4cab6'}, {'abstract': 'The omnibus bill bundling together an overhaul of the civil service and a new tax code, along with other budget cuts, was endorsed by 153 lawmakers in the 300-seat House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/world/europe/greece-approves-new-austerity-measures.html', 'snippet': 'The omnibus bill bundling together an overhaul of the civil service and a new tax code, along with other budget cuts, was endorsed by 153 lawmakers in the 300-seat House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Following two days of intense debate, Greece’s Parliament narrowly approved a barrage of new austerity measures early Thursday, including a contentious plan for thousands of layoffs and wage cuts for civil service workers. The approval paved the way for the release of additional crucial financing from the country’s foreign creditors but raised questions about the stability of the fragile coalition that is to enforce the cuts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Approves New Austerity Measures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Approves New Austerity Measures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/794d894c-e7cd-56cc-8784-374ed6c15e25', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794d894c-e7cd-56cc-8784-374ed6c15e25'}, {'abstract': 'Why was a 16-year-old American citizen killed by a drone strike in Yemen?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/opinion/the-drone-that-killed-my-grandson.html', 'snippet': 'Why was a 16-year-old American citizen killed by a drone strike in Yemen?', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — I LEARNED that my 16-year-old grandson, Abdulrahman — a United States citizen — had been killed by an American drone strike from news reports the morning after he died.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Drone That Killed My Grandson', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Drone That Killed My Grandson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Nasser al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Abdulrahman al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:08:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nasser al-Awlaki', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f70a348e-dd5b-59ec-ac98-d9cbe7387dfe', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f70a348e-dd5b-59ec-ac98-d9cbe7387dfe'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate races aren’t until next year, but things are already heating up in a few states. Have you seen Liz’s video on YouTube?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/opinion/collins-the-cheney-in-waiting.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate races aren’t until next year, but things are already heating up in a few states. Have you seen Liz’s video on YouTube?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dick Cheney’s daughter wants to be a senator! To give Wyoming a conservative voice! Well, it’s about time somebody thought of that.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cheney in Waiting', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cheney In Waiting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Gail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Liz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Enzi, Michael B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/abf5fd8f-c75f-54de-be19-8e4a46a882dc', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abf5fd8f-c75f-54de-be19-8e4a46a882dc'}, {'abstract': 'It is time the public got a clear picture of what Wildlife Services is up to, and for the agency’s work to be brought into accord with sound biological practices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/opinion/agricultures-misnamed-agency.html', 'snippet': 'It is time the public got a clear picture of what Wildlife Services is up to, and for the agency’s work to be brought into accord with sound biological practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a unit within the Agriculture Department’s Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service called Wildlife Services. Its official mission, according to its Web site, is “to resolve wildlife conflicts to allow people and wildlife to coexist.” This has meant, since 2000, some two million dead animals. The list includes coyotes, beavers, mountain lions, black bears and innumerable birds. The agency’s real mission? To make life safer for livestock and game species.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agriculture’s Misnamed Agency', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agriculture’s Misnamed Agency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/facc2d5f-04cd-5ea5-9d9d-ab96d2ad6cac', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/facc2d5f-04cd-5ea5-9d9d-ab96d2ad6cac'}, {'abstract': 'It is essential for the Senate to approve a global treaty that would apply the principles of the Americans With Disabilities Act to the world at large.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/opinion/a-second-chance-for-the-worlds-disabled.html', 'snippet': 'It is essential for the Senate to approve a global treaty that would apply the principles of the Americans With Disabilities Act to the world at large.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a painful moment on Capitol Hill in December when former Senator Bob Dole, seated in a wheelchair, was greeted warmly by old Republican colleagues but then rebuffed by some of those very same members after he had urged Senate ratification of a United Nations treaty defending the rights of people with disabilities. The treaty drew a 61-to-38 vote that fell five votes short of the needed two-thirds majority after skittish Republicans bought into a nonsensical attack by right-wing critics that it would undermine national sovereignty.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Second Chance for the World’s Disabled', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Second Chance for the World’s Disabled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dole, Bob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES ACT', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treaties', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc09de9f-501d-5f7c-b222-ecdb4f6cfc27', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc09de9f-501d-5f7c-b222-ecdb4f6cfc27'}, {'abstract': 'The Government Communications Headquarters had been accused of accessing information from an American surveillance program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/world/europe/british-agency-is-cleared-of-illegal-data-gathering.html', 'snippet': 'The Government Communications Headquarters had been accused of accessing information from an American surveillance program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A parliamentary committee on Wednesday cleared Britain’s electronic intelligence-gathering agency of working with its American counterparts to bypass laws governing the collection of data about its citizens, but said new legislation might be needed to police electronic surveillance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Agency Is Cleared of Illegal Data Gathering', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Agency Is Cleared of Illegal Data Gathering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc05a106-9f1e-50af-8e62-5070434855c9', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc05a106-9f1e-50af-8e62-5070434855c9'}, {'abstract': 'A new law does not do enough to empower workers and improve workplace safety only a few months after the tragic collapse of a factory building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/opinion/halfhearted-labor-reform-in-bangladesh.html', 'snippet': 'A new law does not do enough to empower workers and improve workplace safety only a few months after the tragic collapse of a factory building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under increasing international pressure to address problems in its clothing industry, legislators in Bangladesh this week changed the country’s labor law to make it easier for workers to form unions. But the changes fall far short of what is needed and are unlikely to do much to prevent the fires, building collapses and other tragedies that have claimed hundreds of lives in recent years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Halfhearted Labor Reform in Bangladesh', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Halfhearted Labor Reform in Bangladesh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T01:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/57e77c1c-bd3a-5220-a222-3ca69222397e', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57e77c1c-bd3a-5220-a222-3ca69222397e'}, {'abstract': 'Statehouse politicians make it ever easier for constituents to carry guns at alarming rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/opinion/the-arms-race-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'Statehouse politicians make it ever easier for constituents to carry guns at alarming rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid all the furious debate generated by gun tragedies like the Trayvon Martin shooting in Florida, citizens in too many states have been quietly, legally arming themselves at alarming rates that offer scant optimism for reining in the nation’s runaway gun culture. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Arms Race at Home', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Arms Race at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'},