nt-loan-interest-rates.html', 'snippet': 'A Senate aide said that the new proposal, which had been the subject of tense negotiations since the rates doubled on July 1, would include a cap on federal Stafford and PLUS loans and a relatively low interest rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senators negotiating a bipartisan deal to keep student loan rates low reached a deal on Wednesday night that could end the partisan feud on Capitol Hill that has threatened to permanently double interest rates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Reaches Deal to End Fight Over Student Loan Interest Rates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Reaches Deal to End Fight Over Student Loan Interest Rates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T03:26:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/647cacb3-20a8-5831-9a30-f6c5b2431e23', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/647cacb3-20a8-5831-9a30-f6c5b2431e23'}, {'abstract': 'The government of Puerto Rico and the Justice Department’s Civil Rights division on Wednesday formalized a sweeping agreement meant to overcome a history of police discrimination, violence and corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/us/agreement-is-reached-on-police-reforms-in-puerto-rico.html', 'snippet': 'The government of Puerto Rico and the Justice Department’s Civil Rights division on Wednesday formalized a sweeping agreement meant to overcome a history of police discrimination, violence and corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government of Puerto Rico and the Justice Department’s Civil Rights division on Wednesday formalized a sweeping agreement meant to overcome a history of discrimination, violence and corruption in the commonwealth’s Police Department. The agreement is the result of a long investigation by the Justice Department and a consent decree announced in December to settle a federal civil rights lawsuit. Its implementation was delayed to give the new governor, Alejandro García Padilla, time to review it and it is subject to approval by Judge Gustavo Gelpi of Federal District Court. Among other things, it will require the Police Department to implement new policies on the use of force and specialized tactical units, domestic violence, interactions with transgender people, crowd control, police training and promotions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agreement Is Reached on Police Reforms in Puerto Rico', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Puerto Rico', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agreement Reached On Police Reforms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T03:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1872fbf9-418b-5603-b9eb-cef45b94038a', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1872fbf9-418b-5603-b9eb-cef45b94038a'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican candidate for mayor, who also stopped by a Jewish social service agency in Midwood on Wednesday, is making a significant effort to attract the Jewish vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/nyregion/lhota-visits-store-seeking-jewish-vote-not-those-kosher-skittles.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican candidate for mayor, who also stopped by a Jewish social service agency in Midwood on Wednesday, is making a significant effort to attract the Jewish vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph J. Lhota, the Republican candidate for mayor, was strolling the aisles of the Gourmet Glatt Market in Borough Park, Brooklyn, on Wednesday, stopping to admire a long row of kosher sorbets, and wondering aloud what made a vegetable kosher or not kosher. (The answer: bugs.)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/trailside-1/trailside-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/trailside-1/trailside-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype