icle “New Smokey Bear Gives Hugs, Not Just Warnings.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, July 18, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T08:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8e582ea-1b1f-5019-8737-fb96cf09bab7', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8e582ea-1b1f-5019-8737-fb96cf09bab7'}, {'abstract': 'The operator of the ravaged nuclear plant in Japan stood ready Thursday to inject boric acid into the reactor if temperature or radiation levels rose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/world/asia/steam-detected-at-damaged-fukushima-reactor.html', 'snippet': 'The operator of the ravaged nuclear plant in Japan stood ready Thursday to inject boric acid into the reactor if temperature or radiation levels rose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — A damaged reactor at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant suddenly began releasing steam again, but the operator of the plant said Thursday it did not appear to be a result of renewed nuclear reactions — a worst-case situation that could lead to a large new release of radioactive materials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steam Detected at Damaged Fukushima Reactor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Crippled Plant Emits Steam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T08:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5007080c-07f9-53f4-8ca1-e6250c7bd208', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5007080c-07f9-53f4-8ca1-e6250c7bd208'}, {'abstract': 'An avid chronicler not only of her native Staten Island but of New York City and beyond, Alice Austen pushed herself and Victorian boundaries.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/alice-austens-type-of-town/', 'snippet': 'An avid chronicler not only of her native Staten Island but of New York City and beyond, Alice Austen pushed herself and Victorian boundaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, Paul Moakley discovered the archives of the Staten Island photographer Alice Austen when he started curating shows at Clear Comfort, a museum that was once Ms. Austen’s home. That initial discovery began a long process that has pretty much taken over his life: he now lives at the museum and works as its caretaker. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alice Austen’s Type of Town', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Alice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16e8b633-d14c-5f93-a18a-c8fcf71d19e6', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16e8b633-d14c-5f93-a18a-c8fcf71d19e6'}, {'abstract': 'How does this article contrast the lives of the workers that make parts for iPhones with the lives of Apple executives in Silicon Valley?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/6-qs-about-the-news-the-off-hours-lives-of-young-workers-in-china/', 'snippet': 'How does this article contrast the lives of the workers that make parts for iPhones with the lives of Apple executives in Silicon Valley?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Demanding Off-Hour Escapes of China’s High-Tech Workers,” Dan Levin writes about young people who work making electronic devices in China, desperately trying to enjoy the present as they strive for a better future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | The Off-Hours Lives of Young Workers in China', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T09:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cd61b2b-3660-5b16-9bc1-370f2d6e8df6', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cd61b2b-3660-5b16-9bc1-370f2d6e8df6'}, {'abstract': 'A new Indian political party is running an electoral campaign over electricity bills.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/electoral-war-over-electricity-bills-in-delhi/', 'snippet': 'A new Indian political party is running an electoral campaign over electricity bills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI – On Oct. 7, 2012, Bana Ram, a laborer who lives with six family members in a modest two-room house in the slum-like Tigri Colony area of South Delhi, received an electricity bill of 15,116 rupees ($250) for the months of September and October. Mr. Ram, who earns 8,000 rupees ($130) a month after 12-hour days of hard labor, was stunned. If he paid what the electric company demanded, Mr. Ram would be left with 600 rupees ($10) to feed his family for two months. The company, BSES Rajdhani Pvt. Ltd., disconnected his power supply for non-payment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-press-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Electoral War Over Electricity Bills in Delhi', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kejriwal, Arvind', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T09:24:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sai Manish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5acd158e-cb0a-5388-984e-889d7e9a4b83', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5acd158e-cb0a-5388-984e-889d7e9a4b83'}, {'abstract': 'What you need to know for Thursday: Unusual places to cool off on another very hot day, Nelson Mandela’s 95th birthday and a lost chicken is rescued in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/new-york-today-be-cool/', 'snippet': 'What you need to know for Thursday: Unusual places to cool off on another very hot day, Nelson Mandela’s 95th birthday and a lost chicken is rescued in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 10:55 a.m. | We’ll not mention that we’re in the midst of a seven-day heat wave, ending only on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/nyregion/NYTTODAYcool4/NYTTODAYcool4-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: Be Cool', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T09:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d6b4e01-77b4-5562-81b4-217b971ed56d', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d6b4e01-77b4-5562-81b4-217b971ed56d'}, {'abstract': 'A Jaguar designer who has never owned a Jaguar, Ian Callum is rebuilding a 1962 Jaguar Mark 2. But not without a few modifications.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/a-jaguar-mans-jaguar-designer-ian-callum-does-the-mark-2-his-way/', 'snippet': 'A Jaguar designer who has never owned a Jaguar, Ian Callum is rebuilding a 1962 Jaguar Mark 2. But not without a few modifications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ian Callum, the design director of Jaguar, has — strangely enough — never actually owned one of his company’s cars. But he’s rebuilding one to his own specifications. Slowly taking shape at Classic Motor Cars in Bridgnorth, England, is a very special 1962 Jaguar Mark 2 that incorporates Mr. Callum’s subtle design upgrades. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/17/automobiles/wheels/ian-callum-jaguar/ian-callum-jaguar-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/17/autom