f4eb627f'}, {'abstract': 'Finance Minister Wolfgang Schäuble visited Athens and expressed “admiration” hours after Parliament approved a plan for laying off civil servants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/world/europe/germany-backs-greeces-austerity-measures.html', 'snippet': 'Finance Minister Wolfgang Schäuble visited Athens and expressed “admiration” hours after Parliament approved a plan for laying off civil servants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — On a quick visit here amid tight security just a few hours after Greek lawmakers narrowly approved a new barrage of austerity measures, Germany’s finance minister on Thursday backed Greece’s efforts to revive its battered economy, saying the German government could provide financing for Greek businesses but ruling out a restructuring of the country’s huge debt burden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/world/europe/19greece/19greece-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/world/europe/19greece/19greece-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/world/europe/19greece/19greece-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/world/europe/19greece/19greece-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/world/europe/19greece/19greece-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'