arenthood, both authentic and fictitious.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/emmy-nominees-vera-farmiga-of-bates-motel/', 'snippet': 'Vera Farmiga, who plays Norma Bates, mother of the future “Psycho” murderer Norman Bates, talks about her nomination and the joys of parenthood, both authentic and fictitious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vera Farmiga, a star of films like “Up in the Air,” “The Departed” and “Source Code,” was nominated on Thursday for an Emmy\xa0 for lead actress in a drama series for “Bates Motel.” On that A&E thriller, Ms. Farmiga plays Norma Bates, the mother of the troubled teenager Norman Bates, who we know will some day grow up to be the twisted murderer of “Psycho.” Here in excerpts from the conversation, Ms. Farmiga talks about her nomination and the joys of motherhood, both authentic and fictitious.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/18artsbeat-vera/18artsbeat-vera-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/18artsbeat-vera/18artsbeat-vera-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 812}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/18artsbeat-vera/18artsbeat-vera-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/18artsbeat-vera/18artsbeat-vera-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 995, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/arts/18artsbeat-vera/18artsbeat-vera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 