34fd', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63b96d75-bd6f-55d4-a6d4-f1cde6b834fd'}, {'abstract': 'Some lawmakers are demanding more information about the National Security Agency’s data-mining programs.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/congress-pushes-back/', 'snippet': 'Some lawmakers are demanding more information about the National Security Agency’s data-mining programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the years since Sept. 11, 2001, Congress has repeatedly allowed the executive branch to expand its power, even as it encroached upon American citizens’ civil liberties. It stood by or even cheered as President Obama claimed the power to order Americans killed abroad, without any independent review, and permitted extensive wiretapping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Pushes Back', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiff, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sensenbrenner, F James Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T16:19:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16b5c710-7d47-563e-b3a3-6e916d54e034', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16b5c710-7d47-563e-b3a3-6e916d54e034'}, {'abstract': 'The first television ad from the Quinn campa