words': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rebates and Refunds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T17:39:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45aab869-ef94-54db-9b1f-5fc92cc8aa1d', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45aab869-ef94-54db-9b1f-5fc92cc8aa1d'}, {'abstract': 'Russells, a firm known for its work in the entertainment industry, said on Thursday that one of its partners  had told his wife’s best friend that the book was actually written by J.K. Rowling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/business/media/another-rowling-mystery-solved-behind-the-tweet-that-identified-her.html', 'snippet': 'Russells, a firm known for its work in the entertainment industry, said on Thursday that one of its partners  had told his wife’s best friend that the book was actually written by J.K. Rowling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the literary leak heard around the world: a little-read detective novel called “The Cuckoo’s Calling,” by the debut author Robert Galbraith, was actually written by J.\u2009K. Rowling, one of the best-known authors in the world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Rowling Mystery Solved: Behind the Tweet That Identified Her', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rowling Leak Mystery:\r\nThe Lawyer Did It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T17:39:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e01d53f-8cab-5c56-b76e-51e6d607c60e', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e01d53f-8cab-5c56-b76e-51e6d607c60e'}, {'abstract': 'Louis C.K. talks about the unexpected success of “Louie” and when he expects that it will all inevitably end.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/emmy-nominees-louis-c-k-of-louie/', 'snippet': 'Louis C.K. talks about the unexpected success of “Louie” and when he expects that it will all inevitably end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After three seasons on FX, “Louie,” about the lovably curmudgeonly not-so-alter ego of the comedian Louis C.K., is more popular than ever in the eyes of the Emmy Awards: on Thursday morning “Louie” picked up six Emmy nominations, including lead comedy actor (for Louis C.K.), guest comedy actress (for Melissa Leo), comedy direction and comedy writing, and comedy series — the first time a basic-cable TV series has been recognized in that category. In these excerpts from the conversation, Louis C.K. talks about his unexpected success and when he expects that it will all inevitably end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi