e': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T17:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/540774f5-aa3d-57b1-bab4-4ccc9066ac9e', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/540774f5-aa3d-57b1-bab4-4ccc9066ac9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Financial Industry Regulatory Authority sent letters to 10 high-speed trading firms this week, asking for more information about their trading programs and the steps taken to avert “market disruptions.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/finra-scrutinizes-high-speed-trading-firms/', 'snippet': 'The Financial Industry Regulatory Authority sent letters to 10 high-speed trading firms this week, asking for more information about their trading programs and the steps taken to avert “market disruptions.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regulators are taking a closer look at whether high-frequency trading firms might represent a threat to the stability of financial markets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finra Scrutinizes High-Speed Trading Firms', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trading Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Industry Regulatory Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knight Capital Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T17:59:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad3af673-8743-5ee7-b385-f67832f94911', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad3af673-8743-5ee7-b385-f67832f94911'}, {'abstract': 'A newly discovered pandoravirus is 1,000 times the size of the flu virus and has nearly 200 times as many genes. And giant viruses turn out to be everywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/science/changing-view-on-viruses-not-so-small-after-all.html', 'snippet': 'A newly discovered pandoravirus is 1,000 times the size of the flu virus and has nearly 200 times as many genes. And giant viruses turn out to be everywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time not that long ago when it was easy to tell the difference between viruses and the rest of life. Most obviously, viruses were tiny and genetically simple. The influenza virus, for example, measures about 100 nanometers across, and has just 13 genes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/science/18zimmer/18zimmer-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing View on Viruses: Not So Small After All', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T18:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/834a1493-86bd-5e4b-89d8-b1c965a33c96', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/834a1493-86bd-5e4b-89d8-b1c965a33c96'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have found a genetic mutation that may help explain why some people can eat the same amount as others but gain more weight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/health/overweight-maybe-you-really-can-blame-your-metabolism.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers have found a genetic mutation that may help explain why some people can eat the same amount as others but gain more weight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mice were eating their usual chow and exercising normally, but they were getting fat anyway. The reason: researchers had deleted a gene that acts in the brain and controls how quickly calories are burned. Even though they were consuming exactly the same number of calories as lean mice, they were gaining weight.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 487}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/us/OBESITY/OBESITY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Overweight? Maybe You Really Can Blame Your Genes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overweight? Maybe