e seek first is what they’ll tend to find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I know Matt Yglesias is probably trolling, as the kids say, with his post on “the scourge of doomed campus relationships,” but I’ll rise to the bait and say something about his argument that a sexual culture of strings-free hookups is brilliantly suited to today’s socioeconomic landscape:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Love in the Time of Hookups', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirshman, Linda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T19:07:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac6198c8-71f9-5b0c-8132-8db2f129c4d5', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac6198c8-71f9-5b0c-8132-8db2f129c4d5'}, {'abstract': 'A search tool from Paraktweet allows users to find books recommended by the people they follow on Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/test-run-bookvibe-picks-up-the-buzz-on-books/', 'snippet': 'A search tool from Paraktweet allows users to find books recommended by the people they follow on Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A persistent problem faced by users of social networks like Facebook and Twitter is the flood of information they create. If you are connected to more than a handful of people on one of those platforms, you will be deluged with far more status updates, photos, likes, advertisements and videos than any human being could ever digest.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 573, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 573}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-jumbo.png', 'height': 962, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 962, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/18bits-testrun1/18bits-testrun1-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}