t an all-star team of adventurous filmmakers will have both marketing appeal and formal éclat. “Centro Histórico,” commissioned to promote the Portuguese city of Guimarães as a 2012 European Capital of Culture, groups short films from a deadpan Finnish director (Aki Kaurismaki), a Basque neighbor (Victor Erice, in documentary mode) and two native sons (Pedro Costa and Manoel de Oliveira) who happily continue to direct exactly as they wish.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1191, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19centro-span/19centro-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType