eaWorld.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/movies/blackfish-a-documentary-looks-critically-at-seaworld.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Blackfish” considers the story of Tilikum, a bull orca, in a scathing look at SeaWorld.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unapologetically designed both to inform and affect, Gabriela Cowperthwaite’s delicately lacerating documentary, “Blackfish,” uses the tragic tale of a single whale and his human victims as the backbone of a hypercritical investigation into the marine-park giant SeaWorld Entertainment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/BLACKFISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/BLACKFISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/BLACKFISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/BLACKFISH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/19BLACKFISH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/19BLACKFISH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BLACKFISH_SPAN/19BLACKFISH_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Six-Ton Captives Dream of Freedom?', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Do Six-Ton Captives Dream of Freedom?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowperthwaite, Gabriela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SeaWorld Adventure Parks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Blackfish (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9be52cb2-cc6e-5044-94ce-e0ecd455bdd2', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9be52cb2-cc6e-5044-94ce-e0ecd455bdd2'}, {'abstract': 'The spirited heroine of Jenni Fagan’s debut novel, “The Panopticon,” is sent to an imposing rehab facility for young offenders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/books/review/the-panopticon-by-jenni-fagan.html', 'snippet': 'The spirited heroine of Jenni Fagan’s debut novel, “The Panopticon,” is sent to an imposing rehab facility for young offenders.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’m a bit unconvinced by reality,” says Anais Hendricks, the heroine of Jenni Fagan’s debut novel, “The Panopticon.” “It’s fundamentally lacking in something, and nobody seems bothered.” When we first meet Anais she is handcuffed in the back of a police car, her school uniform covered in blood, on her way to an institution for young offenders. She has no family, and has never seen so much as a photograph of any relatives. Her hobbies include joy riding, tripping on school days, painting CCTV cameras fluorescent pink and hand-delivering the lights from police cars, covered with glitter, to the desk of her local constabulary. Now 15, she still feels “2 years old and ready tae bite.” She is, in summary, “totally and utterly” messed up — “but I like pillbox hats.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/books/review/0721-bks-SHONEcover/0721-bks-SHONEcover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/21/books/review/0721-bks-SHONEcover/0721-bks-SHONEcover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/books/review/0721-bks-SHONEcover/0721-bks-SHONEcover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/books/review/0721-bks-SHONEcover/0721-bks-SHONEcover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2027, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/books/review/0721-bks-SHONEcover/0721-bks-SHONEcover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/21/books/review/0721-bks-SHONEcover/0721