icle/a447dc0e-f665-5f02-8433-e219b6806e73', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a447dc0e-f665-5f02-8433-e219b6806e73'}, {'abstract': 'A group of Latin American countries succeeded in blocking Amazon.com’s request to use the domain name .amazon, citing its importance to the identity of the Amazon basin.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/amazon-rejected-as-domain-name-after-south-american-objections/', 'snippet': 'A group of Latin American countries succeeded in blocking Amazon.com’s request to use the domain name .amazon, citing its importance to the identity of the Amazon basin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of Latin American countries appears to have succeeded in an effort to block Amazon, the online retailer, from using .amazon as a new suffix for Internet addresses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/business/bits-amazonjungle/bits-amazonjungle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Rejected as Domain Name After South American Objections', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domain Names (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internet Corp for Assigned Names and Numbers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:21:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed7e7d23-186f-5fa4-acc8-4d6e5ec7e0d7', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed7e7d23-186f-5fa4-acc8-4d6e5ec7e0d7'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes art competes with nature, requiring you to be clear on what’s affecting you. Under the best circumstances, they become one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/arts/design/ideally-striving-for-an-organic-fusion.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes art competes with nature, requiring you to be clear on what’s affecting you. Under the best circumstances, they become one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days you can find almost as much contemporary art outdoors as in. This is the legacy of Earthworks, also known as land art; site-specific open-air installations; and monumental sculptures. And then there’s plop art, transplanted from concrete plazas to green lawns, or onto something in between, like the gardenish median strips of Park Avenue, which are regularly dotted with large desultory objects. There are also those strange, gallery-like arrangements known as outdoor sculpture gardens, which rank high among my least favorite art viewing conditions (the Museum of Modern Art’s excepted). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 311}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 531, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1062, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-LCBD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ideally, Striving for an Organic Fusion', 'kicker': 'Playing Outside the Box ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ideally, Striving for an Organic Fusion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e7fbfa4-3ac8-567e-b535-d798c4db513a', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e7fbfa4-3ac8-567e-b535-d798c4db513a'}, {'abstract': 'Shade, grass, iced tea: all essential ingredients, a critic says, for the ideal experience of summer reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/books/ah-the-trips-taken-by-just-sitting-still.html', 'snippet': 'Shade, grass, iced tea: all essential ingredients, a critic says, for the ideal experience of summer reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the professional hazards of being a book critic is the nap. Naps sneak up on you. They are beautiful but, like recreational drugs and termites, they can undermine the foundations of your existence. Comfortable armchairs are murderous traps. So I mostly read while sitting upright, at a desk, ballpoint pen in hand. If I’m working, it should feel at least slightly like work, right?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19JPOUTDOORS10/19JPOUTDOORS10-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ah, the Trips Taken by Just Sitting Still', 'kicker': 'Playing Outside the Box | Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ah, the Trips Taken by Just Sitting Still', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:24:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d3d1133-f70e-5c4b-807c-080d8868e1f8', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d3d1133-f70e-5c4b-807c-080d8868e1f8'}, {'abstract': '“Girl Most Likely,” directed by Shari Springer Berman and Robert Pulcini, sends Kristen Wiig on a downward spiral that leaves her living with her gaudily accented mom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/movies/in-girl-most-likely-kristen-wiig-has-to-go-home-again.html', 'snippet': '“Girl Most Likely,” directed by Shari Springer Berman and Robert Pulcini, sends Kristen Wiig on a downward spiral that leaves her living with her gaudily accented mom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s impossible not to root for Kristen Wiig, even while you wait in vain for the funny to pop in her latest. A forced, laugh-challenged comedy with an appealing if not terribly well-used cast, “Girl Most Likely” is the first movie that Ms. Wiig has taken the lead in since the 2011 runaway hit “Bridesmaids.” In that comedy, she played an amusingly self-involved singleton without a love life, bright prospects or a home to call her very own. (Mind you, she did have Jon Hamm on demand.) In “Girl Most Likely,” she again plays a single gal who, after being booted out of Manhattan (long story), dusts herself off and tries all over again, this time while flopping with family in New Jersey.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/19GIRL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/19GIRL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/19GIRL-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/19GIRL-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1178, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/GIRL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/GIRL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19GIRL/GIRL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Is Just So Embarrassing', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Jersey Is Just So Embarrassing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pulcini, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springer Berman, Shari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Girl Most Likely (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/00d39da9-4b48-5115-9253-7df4c2cd9a3b', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00d39da9-4b48-5115-9253-7df4c2cd9a3b'}, {'abstract': 'From band shells to spaces with roofs, there’s something heartening about mingling with people at an open-air classical concert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/arts/music/so-rhapsodic-that-the-birds-join-in.html', 'snippet': 'From band shells to spaces with roofs, there’s something heartening about mingling with people at an open-air classical concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Natural sound is one of the glories of classical music. In our increasingly overamplified world, the concert hall and the opera house are like nature preserves where you can hear orchestras and operas without any electronic enhancement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-HAOV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Rhapsodic That the Birds Join In', 'kicker': 'Playing Outside the Box ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Rhapsodic That the Birds Join In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e44099a8-0481-58ec-96b9-1279e44858fc', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e44099a8-0481-58ec-96b9-1279e44858fc'}, {'abstract': 'The fact of outdoor concerts is that the audience becomes a far more important part of the music. It’s not a performance, it’s an event.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/arts/music/communing-with-more-than-nature.html', 'snippet': 'The fact of outdoor concerts is that the audience becomes a far more important part of the music. It’s not a performance, it’s an event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Low-flying airplanes. Traffic noise. Squealing children. Oblivious vendors. Sun in your eyes. Rain on your head. And for festival die-hards, there’s that infamous shoe-sucking mud. Music outdoors is almost inevitably bundled with distractions and annoyances — enough, at many open-air shows, to make me long for the more controlled environment of a theater or a club, where architecture and habit help keep the focus on the performance. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19OUTDOORS3/19JPOUTDOORS8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Communing With More Than Nature', 'kicker': 'Playing Outside the Box ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Communing With More Than Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:29:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faefc53a-06b7-57eb-9212-de65dec9e785', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faefc53a-06b7-57eb-9212-de65dec9e785'}, {'abstract': 'My idea of moviegoing bliss can’t be found in a park or on a roof but in a theater, where most of the ambient light comes from the projector and the screen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/movies/an-unfortunate-return-to-reality.html', 'snippet': 'My idea of moviegoing bliss can’t be found in a park or on a roof but in a theater, where most of the ambient light comes from the projector and the screen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a lifelong believer in the sanctity of the Great Indoors, at least when it comes to movies, I have never been to a drive-in or a rooftop screening. One typically balmy Los Angeles night, some friends and I watched a movie projected on a parking lot wall, but other than this adventure and a youthful stint working for the filmmaker Jon Rubin — whose Floating Cinema projected movies alfresco on pontoon boats that we guided into waterways unannounced, delighting and sometimes startling onshore campers — I have spent most of my movie life inside. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4/20130719-OUTDOORS-slide-NTT4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unfortunate Return to Reality', 'kicker': 'Playing Outside the Box ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Unfortunate Return to Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd18d6dd-8b70-5275-babf-bd2b450d2c3f', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd18d6dd-8b70-5275-babf-bd2b450d2c3f'}, {'abstract': 'To pair with rosé, a layered casserole of macaroni, tomatoes and lobster, baked with a béchamel topping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/dining/a-pale-pink-wine-conjures-the-notion-of-a-greek-pastitsio.html', 'snippet': 'To pair with rosé, a layered casserole of macaroni, tomatoes and lobster, baked with a béchamel topping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I might have simply chosen salade niçoise or fish soup to serve with French rosés, and been done with it. But the notion of a Greek pastitsio, a layered casserole of macaroni, tomatoes and ground beef baked with a béchamel topping (using lobster in place of the meat), took hold, and there was no turning back. I also decided to base the topping on aioli instead of a thick white sauce. It was worth the effort and delightful with the wine.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24PAIRING_SPAN/24PAIRING_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pale Pink Wine Conjures the Notion of a Greek Pastitsio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobsters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5e1ddf4-b9e6-53a1-a52d-6c2992f0b8b6', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5e1ddf4-b9e6-53a1-a52d-6c2992f0b8b6'}, {'abstract': '“Broken,” a British feature from Rufus Norris, focuses on Skunk, a curious 11-year-old girl who bears a resemblance to Scout Finch in “To Kill a Mockingbird.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/movies/broken-brings-kitchen-sink-realism-to-todays-britain.html', 'snippet': '“Broken,” a British feature from Rufus Norris, focuses on Skunk, a curious 11-year-old girl who bears a resemblance to Scout Finch in “To Kill a Mockingbird.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kitchen-sink realism for the 21st century: that would describe the first three-quarters of “Broken,” the fine but unnecessarily convoluted first feature film by the British theater director Rufus Norris about the tensions in a grubby middle-class neighborhood of North London. The movie lacks the visual austerity and despairing tone of its forerunners in the late 1950s and early 1960s. These people are not poor. But most are unhappy, coarse and highly stressed, and the social climate is claustrophobic. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/mov