ion_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7e6a0f1-7513-5a4b-9747-fd3b4e6e867a', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7e6a0f1-7513-5a4b-9747-fd3b4e6e867a'}, {'abstract': 'As pleasant as both rosé the wine and rosé the idea can be, too many bottles are produced with the sole idea of exploiting the public’s desire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/dining/reviews/rose-in-demand-but-not-demanding.html', 'snippet': 'As pleasant as both rosé the wine and rosé the idea can be, too many bottles are produced with the sole idea of exploiting the public’s desire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you feel the need for a good, strong bath of cynicism, gather a few sommeliers in summer and discuss rosés. They could give teenagers a few lessons in eye-rolling, lip-curling and other facial displays of exasperation. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/dining/24WINE_SPAN/24WINE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosé: In Demand, but Not Demanding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Good Thing? Maybe Too Much', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:32:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/28be9a5e-54d2-5075-af26-a9efcc4b6110', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28be9a5e-54d2-5075-af26-a9efcc4b6110'}, {'abstract': 'The Encores! Off-Center series presented a concert performance of “Violet,” starring Sutton Foster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/theater/reviews/sutton-foster-in-violet-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Encores! Off-Center series presented a concert performance of “Violet,” starring Sutton Foster.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’d like a pair of Gene Tierney eyes and Ava Gardner’s eyebrows,” announces the title character of “Violet,” a facially disfigured young woman dreaming of a miracle at the hands of a faith healer. A modest success when first produced at Playwrights Horizons in 1997, this Jeanine Tesori-Brian Crawley musical was revived on Wednesday evening in a deeply stirring one-night concert performance starring Sutton Foster as part of the Encores! Off-Center program at City Center. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19VIOLETALT_SPAN/19VIOLETALT_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 