y on mobile ads? ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Results Show Struggle With Mobile', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Results Show Struggle With Mobile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Claire Cain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T21:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3395ebff-182b-55ae-bfde-eb1cfe9996eb', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3395ebff-182b-55ae-bfde-eb1cfe9996eb'}, {'abstract': 'The two leads in “Teen Beach Movie” are zapped across time and dimensions into a 1962 beach blanket film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/arts/television/teen-beach-movie-goes-back-to-the-future.html', 'snippet': 'The two leads in “Teen Beach Movie” are zapped across time and dimensions into a 1962 beach blanket film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Disney Channel’s movie musicals crested in 2007, when “High School Musical 2” drew 17.2 million viewers, and the numbers have been sinking since, down to 5.7 million for “Let It Shine” last year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/arts/19BEACH_SPAN/JPBEACH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, '