abstract': 'A listing of walking tours, cultural events and more in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/arts/spare-times-for-july-19-25.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, cultural events and more in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘Bronx Rising!’: Screening and Discussion (Friday) For those with ties to Puerto Rico, the pre-Lenten Carnival in Ponce, which is several centuries old, is as joyous a celebration as Mardi Gras in New Orleans. And while Carnival is not such a big deal in New York, the Puerto Rican Day Parade is. Scattered among the marchers at the annual parade in New York are devilish figures known as vejigantes, wearing colorful and often fierce-looking masks similar to those found in Ponce.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for July 19-25', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-18T22:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5a64d1f-73fe-549f-b691-bef2b5415b88', 'word_count': 2777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5a64d1f-73fe-549f-b691-bef2b5415b88'}, {'abstract': 'It’s called Tomato Battle, and it involves thousands of people paying for the chance to splatter one another with, yes, tomatoes. But the national park where it will be held has its own defenders.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/plans-for-a-messy-fight-spur-concern-of-harm-to-the-battlefield/', 'snippet': 'It’s called Tomato Battle, and it involves thousands of people paying for the chance to splatter one another with, yes, tomatoes. But the national park where it will be held has its own defenders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, 40,000 pounds of tomatoes will be delivered to Floyd Bennett Field, the old municipal-airport-turned-park by Jamaica Bay in Brooklyn. There are no plans for a giant salad or a record-setting pasta sauce; these tomatoes will meet a more violent end, when up to 5,000 people are expected to pay $50 for the chance to hurl the fruit of the Solanum lycopersicum at one another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/tomato/tomato-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150,