'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mayy', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'Sheikh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02e32209-a643-53dc-80a6-ee7037bf21e8', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02e32209-a643-53dc-80a6-ee7037bf21e8'}, {'abstract': 'Mississippi changed to a fast-paced offense like many other SEC teams, but it was forced to change its offense again after Alabama hired one of its staff members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/sports/ncaafootball/as-alabamas-opponents-raise-the-tempo-saban-remains-a-step-ahead.html', 'snippet': 'Mississippi changed to a fast-paced offense like many other SEC teams, but it was forced to change its offense again after Alabama hired one of its staff members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOOVER, Ala. — When an Alabama football player can straighten his helmet, snap his chin strap, make sure his pads are snug, take a deep breath and get comfortably set in his stance, there is a good chance that he will have no equal in the Southeastern Conference. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 857}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 717, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1434, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/sports/SUB-Y-SEC/SUB-Y-SEC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Alabama’s Opponents Raise the Tempo, Saban Remains a Step Ahead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Hurry to Keep Up With Alabama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glier, Ray', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saban, Nick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Mississippi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeze, Hugh', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T00:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffa62b0d-c314-5226-870a-af2e7c12f7bf', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffa62b0d-c314-5226-870a-af2e7c12f7bf'}, {'abstract': 'The number of patients at Brooklyn’s Long Island College Hospital has dwindled to 18 amid a legal stalemate between its owner, which wants to close it, and unions representing workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/nyregion/State-Prepares-Long-Island-College-Hospital-for-Its-Closing.html', 'snippet': 'The number of patients at Brooklyn’s Long Island College Hospital has dwindled to 18 amid a legal stalemate between its owner, which wants to close it, and unions representing workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Long Island College Hospital in Brooklyn, there are scores of doctors and nurses on duty around the clock at a cost of\xa0$3 million per week. But in the maternity ward, nurses sit and knit or idly watch afternoon television because there are no babies being delivered and most of the hospital is empty. It is meant to house 375 patients; it has 18.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/nyregion/lich/lich-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nurses Roam Empty Halls as Long Island College Hospital Is Prepared to Close', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doctors and Nurses Roam Empty Halls As Hospital Again Prepares for Its Closing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Island College Hospital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SUNY Downstate Medical Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T00:57:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ad41fe7-8dbd-5e8d-8943-3781cd3d2e93', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ad41fe7-8dbd-5e8d-8943-3781cd3d2e93'}, {'abstract': 'We are all cookies now. And to allay concerns about that, several companies involved in offline tracking have said that they would work with a research group based in Washington to develop a series of “best practices” for privacy controls.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/the-rules-of-in-store-surveillance/', 'snippet': 'We are all cookies now. And to allay concerns about that, several companies involved in offline tracking have said that they would work with a research group based in Washington to develop a series of “best practices” for privacy controls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can tell when a powerful new technology, like tracking people as they shop, is coming of age. It starts trying to persuade people it is a force for good, and it broadens its reach and capabilities. Take the the observation and data collection techniques used by online retailers that are now moving into the physical world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 540, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 540}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-jumbo.png', 'height': 870, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 870, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/18/technology/bits-euclid1/bits-euclid1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rules of In-Store Surveillance', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Loyalty Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Euclid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polonetsky, Jules', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Will', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Future of Privacy Forum', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T00:58:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7905ee6-3cb6-5469-937f-38a0e9d9588d', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7905ee6-3cb6-5469-937f-38a0e9d9588d'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Schweitzer of Montana isn’t running for Senate — and it’s hard to blame him.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/power-or-the-porch/', 'snippet': 'Brian Schweitzer of Montana isn’t running for Senate — and it’s hard to blame him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just now, the sweet Lambert cherries of the Flathead Valley in Montana are ripe with a midsummer blush, and trout rise to snap fresh-hatched bugs from the surface of the Blackfoot River. At night, a mountain breeze, the natural air-conditioning of the West, cools things down just enough to make for a deep sleep. There are pockets of snow, still, in the high, north-facing draws of the Rockies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Power or the Porch?', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12652dd3-7e17-565c-8c74-97c9fbe9f2b1', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12652dd3-7e17-565c-8c74-97c9fbe9f2b1'}, {'abstract': 'If migrant workers can be deported, they will be abused.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/the-lessons-of-belle-glade.html', 'snippet': 'If migrant workers can be deported, they will be abused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WILLIAMSBURG, Va. — IN 1965, the secretary of labor, Willard Wirtz, stood under a porch light in Belle Glade, Fla., facing a crowd of guest workers from the Caribbean. Mr. Wirtz could smell sweat and burned sugar cane on their clothes but couldn’t see them, which was how the workers wanted it. Guest workers were often deported and blacklisted for striking or simply questioning whether they had been paid what they were owed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 979, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 979}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 628, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/opinion/0719OPEDfreshwater/0719OPEDfreshwater-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lessons of Belle Glade', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lessons of Belle Glade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hahamovitch, Cindy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant Labor (Agriculture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belle Glade (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodlatte, Robert W', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cindy Hahamovitch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cindy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hahamovitch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e112f5e-43e9-5a68-80c2-21e8ffaec454', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e112f5e-43e9-5a68-80c2-21e8ffaec454'}, {'abstract': 'The Syrian regime would collapse without Hezbollah’s backing. Negotiating with Hezbollah’s patron, Iran, could end the group’s support for Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/to-oust-assad-pressure-hezbollah.html', 'snippet': 'The Syrian regime would collapse without Hezbollah’s backing. Negotiating with Hezbollah’s patron, Iran, could end the group’s support for Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWPORT, R.I. — SYRIA has put President Obama’s enlightened realism in international affairs to its stiffest test. Direct military intervention could immerse the United States in yet another open-end