810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a91ff674-dcfc-5f6e-95d4-73f004b630ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Native American Financial Services Association writes that tribes are turning to online financial services as an alternative to casinos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/native-american-initiative.html', 'snippet': 'The Native American Financial Services Association writes that tribes are turning to online financial services as an alternative to casinos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Native American Initiative', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Native American Initiative', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:03:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/43da9c76-d213-5a42-8b1e-f1c95fc3da62', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43da9c76-d213-5a42-8b1e-f1c95fc3da62'}, {'abstract': 'The suit was filed against former President Ernesto Zedillo by 10 anonymous plaintiffs who said they were survivors of a 1997 massacre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/world/americas/lawsuit-against-ex-president-is-dismissed-in-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'The suit was filed against former President Ernesto Zedillo by 10 anonymous plaintiffs who said they were survivors of a 1997 massacre.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A United States District Court judge in Connecticut on Thursday dismissed a civil lawsuit against former President Ernesto Zedillo of Mexico that was filed by 10 anonymous plaintiffs who said they were survivors of a 1997 assault. Judge Michael P. Shea said he was deferring to a request for immunity for Mr. Zedillo submitted by the State Department last year. The two-year-old lawsuit had sought $50 million in damages against Mr. Zedillo, who now leads a research institute at Yale University. Members of the indigenous group that was the target of the assault, known as Las Abejas, or the Bees, said they did not know the plaintiffs and disassociated themselves from the suit. Mr. Zedillo was president in 1997 when paramilitary gunmen fired on members of the group taking refuge from fighting in the southern state of Chiapas and killed 45 people, including 18 children. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawsuit Against Ex-President of Mexico Is Dismissed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Lawsuit Against Ex-President Is Dismissed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zedillo, Ernesto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cca8cd0-448e-5514-bfdf-583c84499511', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cca8cd0-448e-5514-bfdf-583c84499511'}, {'abstract': 'All the signs coming from the economic data show that China is in big trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/krugman-hitting-chinas-wall.html', 'snippet': 'All the signs coming from the economic data show that China is in big trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All economic data are best viewed as a peculiarly boring genre of science fiction, but Chinese data are even more fictional than most. Add a secretive government, a controlled press, and the sheer size of the country, and it’s harder to figure out what’s really happening in China than it is in any other major economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitting China’s Wall', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hitting China’s Wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c66cfa9a-834b-5261-811f-61e60abd0a87', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c66cfa9a-834b-5261-811f-61e60abd0a87'}, {'abstract': 'A political storm unleashed by the swift expulsion of a dissident Kazakh oligarch’s wife and daughter has further strained the already tense relations within three-month-old coalition government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/world/europe/deportation-of-kazakhs-frays-italys-government.html', 'snippet': 'A political storm unleashed by the swift expulsion of a dissident Kazakh oligarch’s wife and daughter has further strained the already tense relations within three-month-old coalition government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — A political storm unleashed by the whirlwind expulsion of a dissident Kazakh oligarch’s wife and daughter has further strained the tense relations within the coalition parties of Italy’s fragile government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deportation of Kazakhs Frays Italy’s Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deportation of Kazakhs Fray