nt_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b23972e-9b3b-55cf-8259-d4201656bd7e', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b23972e-9b3b-55cf-8259-d4201656bd7e'}, {'abstract': 'The Affordable Care Act will save money for many who buy their own policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/the-good-news-on-insurance-premiums.html', 'snippet': 'The Affordable Care Act will save money for many who buy their own policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Individuals and families who buy health insurance on their own will pay significantly lower premiums next year in New York and many other states. It is the most impressive evidence yet that the Affordable Care Act, through its mandates and competition-promoting health insurance exchanges, can hold previously rising premiums in check.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Good News on Insurance Premiums', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Good News on Insurance Premiums', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f2cb4e4-1764-52ef-a847-70bcdf7fd6ce', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f2cb4e4-1764-52ef-a847-70bcdf7fd6ce'}, {'abstract': 'Retailers must give shoppers a chance to opt out of being tracked in physical stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/you-and-your-cellphone-on-candid-camera.html', 'snippet': 'Retailers must give shoppers a chance to opt out of being tracked in physical stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anybody who shops at online stores like Amazon.com knows that those merchants track customers, what they look at, what they buy and how long they spend on the site. Perhaps it’s not all that surprising that traditional retailers — with little or no notice — have started tracking shoppers in stores, using security cameras and devices that can monitor the location of customer cellphones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You (and Your Cellphone) on Candid Camera', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You (and Your Cellphone) on Candid Camera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:13:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6b1ecff-203d-5a5c-b7a7-d02ce457896b', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6b1ecff-203d-5a5c-b7a7-d02ce457896b'}, {'abstract': 'The charges and heavy punishment for Aleksei Navalny were a retaliation for his campaign against President Vladimir Putin’s corrupt political machine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/mr-putin-tries-to-crush-another-rival.html', 'snippet': 'The charges and heavy punishment for Aleksei Navalny were a retaliation for his campaign against President Vladimir Putin’s corrupt political machine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though he has long cultivated an image as a strong man, President Vladimir Putin of Russia actually seems weak and insecure, a judgment reinforced every time he manipulates the system to crush a potential political rival. Mr. Putin did so again on Thursday. A Russian court convicted Aleksei Navalny, a lawyer and charismatic opposition leader who was running for mayor of Moscow, of stealing $500,000 from a state-controlled timber company and sentenced him to five years in prison. The charges and heavy punishment were a transparent retaliation for Mr. Navalny’s campaign against public corruption and Mr. Putin’s United Russia political machine as a party of “swindlers and thieves.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Putin Tries to Crush Another Rival', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Putin Tries to Crush Another Rival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ee68a2-ffef-5a03-9034-188b2edf98a0', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ee68a2-ffef-5a03-9034-188b2edf98a0'}, {'abstract': 'The criticism that the magazine is trying to turn Dzhokhar Tsarnaev into a rock star by putting him on the cover is going too far.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/opinion/judging-rolling-stone-by-its-cover.html', 'snippet': 'The criticism that the magazine is trying to turn Dzhokhar Tsarnaev into a rock star by putting him on the cover is going too far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe the hysteria about Rolling Stone’s August issue is heat-wave induced. That’s the only charitable explanation for the stampede of critics who have been accusing Rolling Stone editors of trying to turn Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, the man accused of the Boston Marathon bombing, into a rock star merely by putting him on the issue’s cover. (Never mind the word “monster” right there in big type.)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judging Rolling Stone by Its Cover', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judging Rolling Stone by Its Cover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc4d06c-bf23-526d-9ee2-9a85e1c7e128', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc4d06c-bf23-526d-9ee2-9a85e1c7e128'}, {'abstract': 'An arrest warrant was issued on Thursday for the wife of a prominent Syrian television commentator and analyst who was shot dead on Wednesday in southern Lebanon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/world/middleeast/no-political-motive-behind-killing-of-assad-supporter-lebanese-officials-say.html', 'snippet': 'An arrest warrant was issued on Thursday for the wife of a prominent Syrian television commentator and analyst who was shot dead on Wednesday in southern Lebanon.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Lebanese authorities issued an arrest warrant on Thursday for the wife of a prominent Syrian television commentator and analyst who was shot dead on Wednesday in southern Lebanon and they arrested her brother and nephew in connection with the killing, said a prosecutor, Samih al-Hajj. The motive for the killing of the commentator, Mohammed Darrar Jammo, was personal and not political, Mr. Hajj said. He said Mr. Jammo’s wife left the door to the couple’s home open so the killers could enter. Lebanese authorities forwarded the arrest warrant to Syria, where the wife is believed to have fled after the killing. Mr. Jammo’s public role as a defender of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria prompted suspicions that Mr. Assad’s opponents had killed him. But the Lebanese Army said in a statement that the killing was not politically motivated. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Political Motive Behind Killing of Assad Supporter, Lebanese Officials Say', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lebanon: No Political Motive Behind Killing of Assad Supporter, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jammo, Mohammed Darrar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T01:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hwaida Saad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hwaida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/77e30295-f986-554a-a2ad-855410d8b555', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77e30295-f986-554a-a2ad-855410d8b555'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street’s big banks have reported giant profits, but they are still opposing aspects of the Dodd-Frank financial reform law and do not like a proposal to set aside more capital to cover future losses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/18/big-banks-flooded-in-profits-fear-flurry-of-new-safeguards/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street’s big banks have reported giant profits, but they are still opposing aspects of the Dodd-Frank financial reform law and do not like a proposal to set aside more capital to cover future losses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s six largest banks reported $23 billion in profits in the second quarter, but they could end up victims of their own success.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Banks, Flooded in Profits, Fear Flurry of New Safeguards', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Banks, Flooded in Profits, Fear Flurry of New Safeguards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deposit Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall S