ancial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/sheik-sells-stake-in-barclays/', 'snippet': 'Sheik Mansour bin Zayed al-Nahyan was part of a group of Middle Eastern investors who helped Barclays avoid a government bailout at the height of the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – More than four years after helping Barclays avoid a government bailout at the height of the financial crisis, Sheik Mansour bin Zayed al-Nahyan of Abu Dhabi has sold his stake in the bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheik Sells Stake in Barclays', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9ab5603-9740-52ea-b2b8-2d0bbfe4a45c', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9ab5603-9740-52ea-b2b8-2d0bbfe4a45c'}, {'abstract': 'Banks’ strong earnings could end up undercutting their arguments against more regulation. | As it prepares to settle with JPMorgan, an energy regulator is expected to spare a top bank lieutenant. | Dell bought itself six more days to drum up support for the proposed buyout. | A former colleague of Fabrice Tourre was in the spotlight on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/morning-agenda-banks-could-be-victims-of-their-own-success/', 'snippet': 'Banks’ strong earnings could end up undercutting their arguments against more regulation. | As it prepares to settle with JPMorgan, an energy regulator is expected to spare a top bank lieutenant. | Dell bought itself six more days to drum up suppo...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANKS COULD BE VICTIMS OF THEIR OWN SUCCESS \xa0|\xa0The nation’s six biggest banks reported $23 billion of profit in the second quarter, strong earnings that could end up undercutting their arguments against more regulation, DealBook’s Peter Eavis writes. With regulators and lawmakers recently stepping up efforts intended to make the largest banks safer, those banks have warned that more regulations could hurt their ability to compete and curtail their lending. The most pressing concern for banks is a relatively tough new rule that could force banks to build up more capital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Could Be Victims of Their Own Success', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T12:13:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16eacfd5-a06b-54c4-a740-699d11ad1d7f', 'word_count': 1663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16eacfd5-a06b-54c4-a740-699d11ad1d7f'}, {'abstract': 'Two former brokers at RP Martin Holdings made their first court appearance in London on Friday in connection to charges tied to the manipulation of global benchmark interest rates.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/ex-brokers-appear-in-court-in-libor-case/', 'snippet': 'Two former brokers at RP Martin Holdings made their first court appearance in London on Friday in connection to charges tied to the manipulation of global benchmark interest rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Two former brokers at RP Martin Holdings made their first court appearance in London on Friday in connection to charges tied to the manipulation of global benchmark interest rates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Brokers Appear in Court in Libor Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T12:17:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afd64035-8552-522b-b55b-d88d8f191f74', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afd64035-8552-522b-b55b-d88d8f191f74'}, {'abstract': 'The plan aims at corporations only and, if widely adopted, would shift some of the global tax burden away from small businesses and individuals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/business/global/g-20-nations-back-plan-to-curb-corporate-tax-evasion.html', 'snippet': 'The plan aims at corporations only and, if widely adopted, would shift some of the global tax burden away from small businesses and individuals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The world’s richest economies for the first time endorsed a blueprint on Friday to curb widely used tax avoidance strategies that allow some multinational corporations to pay only a pittance in income taxes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/business/GLOBALTAX/GLOBALTAX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/20/business/GLOBALTAX/GLOBALTAX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre