 second round of the 2013 British Open from Muirfield', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a steamy first round left players muttering about Muirfield’s linoleum-hard fairways and greens, British Open organizers ordered the greens watered and the pin placements adjusted. But they couldn’t do anything about the shifting wind, and by the end of the day, the course was just as hard and even more misery-inducing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Open Second Round: Jimenez Weathers Conditions Best', 'kicker': 'Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Zach', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T12:31:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e594da-e3dc-558d-b9f9-ea5b65029b09', 'word_count': 4145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e594da-e3dc-558d-b9f9-ea5b65029b09'}, {'abstract': 'No matter how earth-shattering that new research study looks, it probably doesn’t have much to do with being a parent.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/dear-parents-please-ignore-the-latest-research/', 'snippet': 'No matter how earth-shattering that new research study looks, it probably doesn’t have much to do with being a parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime soon—today, this week, this month—there will be a new and sensational study about small humans. There always is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear Parents: Please Ignore the Latest Research', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T12:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Day', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Day', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a60a3ac8-cf73-5e80-b644-1fb77a56ae34', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a60a3ac8-cf73-5e80-b644-1fb77a56ae34'}, {'abstract': 'The officials said the city’s bankruptcy filing gave Detroit “breathing room” to continue operating as it copes with its long-term debts and obligations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/us/breadth-of-bankruptcy-fight-detroit-faces-becoming-clear.html', 'snippet': 'The officials said the city’s bankruptcy filing gave Detroit “breathing room” to continue operating as it copes with its long-term debts and obligations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Gov. Rick Snyder of Michigan on Friday defended his decision to force Detroit into bankruptcy as a necessary step to halt its decades-long decline and resolve its spiraling debt crisis. But even as he was pleading for patience during the lengthy process ahead to fix the city’s finances, a state judge was ruling that the governor had overstepped his authority by approving the city’s bankruptcy filing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':