tes.html', 'snippet': 'The measure, passed largely along party lines, faces significant challenges from Senate Democrats and a veto threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in a dozen years, the House of Representatives passed a significant education bill on Friday, rewriting No Child Left Behind, President George W. Bush’s signature law governing how federal funds are spent in public schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Votes to Shift ‘No Child Left Behind’ Oversight to States', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Votes to Shift School Oversight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kline, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T16:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c082e769-8065-5905-b1aa-1214f3af68ef', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c082e769-8065-5905-b1aa-1214f3af68ef'}, {'abstract': 'The church of a pastor facing drug charges may sound like a plot device in a stoner movie, but Hawai’i Cannabis THC Ministry raises serious issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/us/marijuana-infused-faith-challenges-the-definition-of-religion.html', 'snippet': 'The church of a pastor facing drug charges may sound like a plot device in a stoner movie, but Hawai’i Cannabis THC Ministry raises serious issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixty-four-year old Roger Christie, a resident of Hawaii’s Big Island, although most recently of Cell 104 at the Honolulu Federal Detention Center, is a Religious Science practitioner, a minister of the Universal Life Church, ordained in the Church of the Universe (in Canada), an official of the Oklevueha Native American Church of Hilo, Hawaii, and the founder of the Hawai’i Cannabis THC Ministry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1528, 'width': 2047, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As a Religion, Marij