nyt://interactive/7823c4e5-4ca2-5105-b411-58007220e92d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/7823c4e5-4ca2-5105-b411-58007220e92d'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Francis has established a committee of seven lay experts and one cleric to help carry out “the simplification and rationalization” of the Vatican’s departments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/world/europe/panel-to-study-vaticans-finances-and-transparency.html', 'snippet': 'Pope Francis has established a committee of seven lay experts and one cleric to help carry out “the simplification and rationalization” of the Vatican’s departments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — As he forges ahead with reforming the Vatican’s troubled bureaucracy, Pope Francis has established a committee of international experts to help improve its finances and transparency, the Vatican said Friday. The committee of seven lay experts and one cleric will answer directly to the pope and a panel of cardinals he appointed to help coordinate reforms. The new committee will help carry out “the simplification and rationalization” of the Vatican’s departments, the Vatican said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel to Study Vatican’s Finances and Transparency', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: A Monitor for Vatican Finances', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'ori