um of the Moving Image’s sweetly coercive injunction to “See It Big!”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/movies/a-grand-ole-opus-from-altman.html', 'snippet': '“Nashville” is too much movie for your TV, so you might want to obey the Museum of the Moving Image’s sweetly coercive injunction to “See It Big!”', 'lead_paragraph': '“We must be doing something right to last 200 years,” sings Haven Hamilton (Henry Gibson), the pint-size star who rules country music in “Nashville” (1975), Robert Altman’s ramble through those twin peaks of American obsession, entertainment and politics. “Nashville” both undermines Haven’s optimism and upholds it: A country that produces a movie this vibrant and layered must be doing something right, right?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grand Ole Opus From Altman', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Grand Ole Opus From Altman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00e774d0-e697-5ae0-9cad-46c150f9c954', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00e774d0-e697-5ae0-9cad-46c150f9c954'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Dylan’s “AmericanaramA” tour is so much the summation and apotheosis of dad-rock that no experience of dad-rock may ever match it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/arts/music/young-and-hip-old-and-hip.html', 'snippet': 'Bob Dylan’s “AmericanaramA” tour is so much the summation and apotheosis of dad-rock that no experience of dad-rock may ever match it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A neat split in the popular-music audience goes down this week. Over here, the young cool of the New York area; over there, the more, uh, seasoned version. Bob Dylan’s “AmericanaramA” tour is so much the summation and apotheosis of dad-rock that no experience of dad-rock may ever match it. The tour, which includes Wilco, Beck and My Morning Jacket, visits Pier A Park in Hoboken, N.J., on Friday, and the Nikon at Jones Beach Theater on Long Island on Saturday. (5:30 p.m., bobdylan.com; $75.50 in Hoboken, $65 and up at Jones Beach .)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young and Hip, Old and Hip', 'kicker': 'Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young and Hip, Old and Hip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f954f62-5ca6-5562-9dee-f3f672caa534', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f954f62-5ca6-5562-9dee-f3f672caa534'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Dendy likes bringing people together in celebration — young people, old people, little people, big people, people of all kinds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/arts/dance/the-movement-of-time.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Dendy likes bringing people together in celebration — young people, old people, little people, big people, people of all kinds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Dendy likes bringing people together in celebration — young people, old people, little people, big people, people of all kinds. The movements he gives his dancers in these festivities are always appropriate to the space in which they’re placed. There will be 80 of them in his new “Ritual Cyclical,” a production with the American Dance Festival, which is celebrating its 80th anniversary at Lincoln Center Out of Doors. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Movement of Time', 'kicker': 'Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Movement Of Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dendy, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:13:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc5042fa-fdf5-5a6e-a4d4-497d49bb8611', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc5042fa-fdf5-5a6e-a4d4-497d49bb8611'}, {'abstract': 'After distinguished careers, some prominent string quartets disband. Others, like the Emerson String Quartet, replenish their ranks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/arts/music/a-new-guy-after-34-years.html', 'snippet': 'After distinguished careers, some prominent string quartets disband. Others, like the Emerson String Quartet, replenish their ranks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After distinguished careers, some prominent string quartets disband. Others, like the Emerson String Quartet, replenish their ranks. In its first change of membership since 1979, the cellist Paul Watkins replaces David Finckel (who joined the group that year). On Sunday, the Emerson makes its American debut with Mr. Watkins, who is also music director of the English Chamber Orchestra. It will demonstrate its mettle with a new member with two of Beethoven’s “Razumovsky” string quartets and Britten’s String Quartet No. 3. (4:30 p.m., Venetian Theater, 149 Girdle Ridge Road, Katonah, N.Y., 914-232-1252, caramoor.org; $15 to $40.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Guy After 34 Years', 'kicker': 'Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Guy After 34 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emerson String Quartet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watkins, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Attacca Quartet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jofre, J P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87216734-0ac8-5216-8164-df7c67122f87', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87216734-0ac8-5216-8164-df7c67122f87'}, {'abstract': 'When the cupboard is bare, as television’s often is in July, there’s apparently always a haunted house somewhere that needs exploring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/arts/television/haunted-houses-for-the-dog-days.html', 'snippet': 'When the cupboard is bare, as television’s often is in July, there’s apparently always a haunted house somewhere that needs exploring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the cupboard is bare, as television’s often is in July, there’s apparently always a haunted house somewhere that needs exploring.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haunted Houses for the Dog Days', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haunted Houses For the Dog Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Haunted Houses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca6e2b9c-7a27-5542-8ed1-e30d7f621076', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca6e2b9c-7a27-5542-8ed1-e30d7f621076'}, {'abstract': 'The gilded sculpture “Leonine Goddess” will be on public view for the first time in the Brooklyn Museum’s show “Divine Felines: Cats of Ancient Egypt.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/arts/design/a-big-litter-of-ancient-cats.html', 'snippet': 'The gilded sculpture “Leonine Goddess” will be on public view for the first time in the Brooklyn Museum’s show “Divine Felines: Cats of Ancient Egypt.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lion-headed female crouches on a papyrus-shaped base. The gilded sculpture, “Leonine Goddess” (770-412 B.C.), will be on public view for the first time in the Brooklyn Museum’s show “Divine Felines: Cats of Ancient Egypt,” which opens on Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big Litter of Ancient Cats', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Big Litter Of Ancient Cats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T18:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d2b2e37-48b6-5431-ac80-197195b8556e', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d2b2e37-48b6-5431-ac80-197195b8556e'}, {'abstract': 'A poet and an English teacher, who both also enjoy reality TV shows, marry in Maine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/fashion/weddings/starting-a-new-verse-with-i-do.html', 'snippet': 'A poet and an English teacher, who both also enjoy reality TV shows, marry in Maine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jackie McLean and Shawn Strack can discuss with equal passion the philosophical implications of “The Aeneid” by Virgil and “Jersey Shore,” which starred Snooki. Somewhere between a Latin epic poem for the ages and a reckless reality TV show in reruns lies a comfortable balance struck by Ms. McLean, a 23-year-old aspiring author and poet, and Mr. Strack, a 27-year-old English teacher.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/weddings/21VOWS1_SPAN/21VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/weddings/21VOWS1_SPAN/21VOWS1-artic