': 'The East Hampton designer Lorraine Kirke is attracted to throw beds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/fashion/utility-and-looks-in-bed-together.html', 'snippet': 'The East Hampton designer Lorraine Kirke is attracted to throw beds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The simplest fantasies are often the most complicated. That humble little cottage you saw in Elle Décor? It has a $2.4 million mortgage. That rambling Queen Anne on Corcoran.com? It’s a 3.5 hour drive — without traffic. And those people in glass houses? They need storage. And curtains. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/fashion/21POSSESSED2_SPAN/21POSSESSED2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Utility and Looks, in Bed Together', 'kicker': 'Possessed ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Utility and Looks, In Bed Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirke, Lorraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beds and Bedding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T20:34:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Colman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Colman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a583b6a9-2131-57de-bc93-c1831741e815', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a583b6a9-2131-57de-bc93-c1831741e815'}, {'abstract': 'The young-adult fiction writer Brittany Geragotelis spends her Sundays with her husband and their cats in a combination of work and play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/nyregion/reveling-in-a-bookstores-smell.html', 'snippet': 'The young-adult fiction writer Brittany Geragotelis spends her Sundays with her husband and their cats in a combination of work and play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 10 years of rejection by the publishing industry, Brittany Geragotelis, a writer of young-adult fiction, turned to the Internet. In 2011 she uploaded her paranormal action novel, “Life’s a Witch,” to the writing site Wattpad, and things started looking up. The book generated 19 million reads, which led to a deal for a book series with Simon & Schuster. It published the first book in the series in January; the second, a retooled version of “Life’s a Witch,” was released this month. For Ms. Geragotelis, 34, Sundays involve gluten-free foods, books, television and one-on-one time with her husband, Matt Gielen, 30. The couple share an apartment on the Upper East Side with their cats, Murray and Cohen. They are newlyweds, married this year on April Fools’ Day.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE3_SPAN/21ROUTINE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reveling in a Bookstore’s Smell', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reveling in a Bookstore’s Smell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geragotelis, Brittany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T20:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kara Mayer Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kara', 'middlename': 'Mayer', 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8be9488d-8b71-5f36-8581-be43ae3528e5', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8be9488d-8b71-5f36-8581-be43ae3528e5'}, {'abstract': 'Like Sylvia Plath and Joan Didion before her, Meg Wolitzer spent the summer as a guest editor at Mademoiselle. A look back at a time both heady with promise and tinged with the sadness of an era about to end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/fashion/my-mademoiselle-summer.html', 'snippet': 'Like Sylvia Plath and Joan Didion before her, Meg Wolitzer spent the summer as a guest editor at Mademoiselle. A look back at a time both heady with promise and tinged with the sadness of an era about to end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I lay drowsing in bed at the Barbizon Hotel for Women, the maid began slamming her fist against my door like a D.E.A. agent, and I popped up, briefly disoriented, taking in the grim, narrow room, the orange and yellow bedspread, the clothes I’d laid out on the armchair the night before. Slowly, I rose from my bed and took my shower caddy down the hall, nodding to a few of the other girls — or were we women now? I wasn’t