tract': 'The president’s powerful speech addressed the nation’s racial fault lines by laying bare his personal experiences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/opinion/president-obamas-anguish.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s powerful speech addressed the nation’s racial fault lines by laying bare his personal experiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama did something Friday that he hardly ever does — and no other president could ever have done. He addressed the racial fault lines in the country by laying bare his personal anguish and experience in an effort to help white Americans understand why African-Americans reacted with frustration and anger to the acquittal of George Zimmerman in the shooting of Trayvon Martin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama’s Anguish', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Obama’s Anguish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T20:57:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6cd586-30f2-5b18-afa3-ec7628fd924c', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6cd586-30f2-5b18-afa3-ec