om of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T21:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f9fe4a8c-51c9-5a7d-84b0-5fa234ac980b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f9fe4a8c-51c9-5a7d-84b0-5fa234ac980b'}, {'abstract': 'In addition to taking portraits of Hova, the photographer has documented the worlds of art, sports and street culture for a generation. Here, he shares some of his biggest personal inspirations.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/19/under-the-influence-ari-marcopoulos-the-man-behind-jay-zs-new-album-cover/', 'snippet': 'In addition to taking portraits of Hova, the photographer has documented the worlds of art, sports and street culture for a generation. Here, he shares some of his biggest personal inspirations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ari Marcopoulos has been documenting youth subcultures for a quarter of a century, but at 56 his work has suddenly achieved a new ubiquity thanks to the celebrity of his latest subject, Jay Z. His portraits and cover image for the rapper’s new album, “Magna Carta Holy Grail,” have popped up all over the urban landscape, wheat-pasted onto walls and digitized onto screens in Times Square. You can spot Marcopoulos hobnobbing with Jay Z and the producers Rick Rubin, Swizz Beatz and Pharrell Williams in the three-minute Samsung-sponsored promo commercial for the album.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ari Marcopoulos, the Man Behind Jay Z’s New Album Cover', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T22:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_nam