rce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/nyregion/21ARTSWE1_SPAN/21ARTSWE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes From Maine, and an Artist’s Life', 'kicker': 'Arts Review | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scenes From Maine, and an Artist’s Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Church, Frederic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sharp, Evelyn and Maurice, Gallery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olana State Historic Site', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T23:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd7b024b-befc-53a7-8cd0-c2bfdb45cb01', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd7b024b-befc-53a7-8cd0-c2bfdb45cb01'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s justice minister protested saying that the request for the extradition of the former C.I.A. officer, Robert Seldon Lady, based on an Interpol warrant, “has been disregarded without plausible explanations.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/world/americas/panama-former-spy-returns-to-us.html', 'snippet': 'Italy’s justice minister protested saying that the request for the extradition of the former C.I.A. officer, Robert Seldon Lady, based on an Interpol warrant, “has been disregarded without plausible explanations.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' A former Central Intelligence Agency officer who was detained in Panama on Thursday in connection with a criminal conviction in Italy was released and flew to the United States on Friday, American officials said. Italy’s justice minister, Anna Maria Cancellieri, protested, saying in a statement that Italy’s request for the extradition of the former C.I.A. officer, Robert Seldon Lady, based on an Interpol warrant, “has been disregarded without plausible explanations.” Mr. Lady is a former chief of the agency’s station in Milan, and one of 26 agency employees and contractors charged in the 2003 abduction in Milan of a radical Muslim cleric, Hassan Mustafa Osama Nasr, also known as Abu Omar. The cleric was taken to Egypt, where, he said, he was tortured, and the case fueled a public debate over the American practice of extraordinary rendition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panama: Former Spy Returns to U.S.', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panama: Former Spy Returns to U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady, Robert Seldon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraordinary Rendition', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasr, Hassan Mustafa Osama', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-19T23:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/574e56cc-079c-5819-ba30-e47df2b035ed', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/574e56cc-079c-5819-ba30-e47df2b035ed'}, {'abstract': 'The strong performance of a Republican in a district where Hispanics make up the majority and registered Republicans trail Democrats by 22 percentage points is seen as a road map to a turnaround.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/us/politics/california-republicans-all-but-endangered-see-hope-in-local-race.html', 'snippet': 'The strong performance of a Republican in a district where Hispanics make up the majority and registered Republicans trail Democrats by 22 percentage points is seen as a road map to a turnaround.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANFORD, Calif. — California Republicans hold no statewide office. They are ignored in the Legislature, where Democrats enjoy overwhelming majorities. Hispanic voters, who are expected to outnumber whites in California within the next several months, strongly back Democrats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/CALIFORNIA-1/CALIFORNIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/20/us/CALIFORNIA-1/CALIFORNIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/CALIFORNIA-1/CALIFORNIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/CALIFORNIA-1/CALIFORNIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/CALIFORNIA-1/CALIFORNIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/20/us/CALIFORNIA-1/CALIFORNIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight':