ents of the calls. The original order disclosed last month by Edward J. Snowden, an N.S.A. contractor, expired Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surveillance Court Renews Order for Phone Call Data', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surveillance Court Renews Order For Phone Call Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T00:22:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/57810bba-d2d9-5f1a-83fb-9328e31466f1', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57810bba-d2d9-5f1a-83fb-9328e31466f1'}, {'abstract': 'The remains of a man who confessed he was the Boston Strangler match the DNA profile of bodily fluids found at the last of the crime scenes attributed to the serial killer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/us/massachusetts-dna-match-made-in-strangler-case.html', 'snippet': 'The remains of a man who confessed he was the Boston Strangler match the DNA profile of bodily fluids found at the last of the crime scenes attributed to the serial killer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Law enforcement officials in Boston on Friday announced that the remains of a man who confessed he was the Boston Strangler match the DNA profile of seminal fluid found at the last of the crime scenes attributed to the serial killer. Although Albert DeSalvo, a convicted rapist, confessed to the strangler murders, he was killed in prison and never prosecuted for them. Scientists recently extracted a DNA profile from seminal fluid found on and near the body of Mary Sullivan, who was strangled in 1964. After finding a familial match between that sample and one taken from a nephew of Mr. DeSalvo, investigators last week exhumed Mr. DeSalvo’s body to confirm the match. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: DNA Match Made in Strangler Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: DNA Match Made In Strangler Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeSalvo, Albert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T00:27:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/50c2584a-747d-5b27-98d4-f63f4933ce3e', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50c2584a-747d-5b27-98d4-f63f4933ce3e'}, {'abstract': 'Judge Rosemary M. Collyer said she was “troubled” by the government’s assertion that it could kill American citizens it designated as dangerous with no role for judicial review.', '