 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/20/us/jp-LAND-2/jp-LAND-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 845}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/jp-LAND-2/jp-LAND-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 728, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/jp-LAND-2/jp-LAND-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1455, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/jp-LAND-2/jp-LAND-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/20/us/jp-LAND-2/jp-LAND-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/20/us/jp-LAND-2/jp-LAND-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bulger Trial, Old Partners Meet, on Opposite Sides', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Bulger Trial, Old Partners Meet, on Opposite Sides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flemmi, Stephen J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T03:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44995c5a-80ce-5ca0-91b8-34ee4ad02e31', 'word_count': 1342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44995c5a-80ce-5ca0-91b8-34ee4ad02e31'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) THE BOURNE LEGACY (2012) Jeremy Renner (above), replacing Matt Damon as the lead in this fourth installment, stars as the superspy Aaron Cross, on the run when the secret intelligence campaign (code name: Outcome) that produced him is compromised, leaving Cross and his fellow operatives to be eliminated under orders from a retired Air Force Colonel (Edward Norton). Rachel Weisz plays the geneticist who helped to create Cross and who may be his only hope for staying alive. While the director Tony Gilroy “retains some of the Bourne bequest, he’s also created a tricky parallel universe with a new agency that has its own clenched-jawed, closed-door complications and a hero who nearly becomes lost among them,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about these films inspired by the Robert Ludlum novels. But while some of the action here flows nicely, she added, the three previous movies “conveyed a sense of urgency that mirrored Bourne’s shattered being and his propulsive, convulsive journey from unenlightened self-interest to accountability, from the existential question mark of his identity to a hard moral reckoning.” Jason Bourne “was still trying to find the answers,” she said. “Now with Bourne gone, Mr. Gilroy needs to find other questions worth asking.” “The Bourne Identity” (2002), the first film in the series, will be shown on A&E at 8; “The Bourne Supremacy” (2004), the second, will be shown on Starz at 7:05.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfbc4dfa-dae0-5311-8e59-81ee5e93ceb7', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfbc4dfa-dae0-5311-8e59-81ee5e93ceb7'}, {'abstract': 'A form of sustainable agriculture that has attracted gardeners, tinkerers and futurists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2010/02/17/garden/20100218-aquaponics-slideshow_index.html', 'snippet': 'A form of sustainable agriculture that has attracted gardeners, tinkerers and futurists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A form of sustainable agriculture that has attracted gardeners, tinkerers and futurists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/02/17/garden/20100218-aquaponics-slideshow-S.JPG', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/02/17/garden/20100218-aquaponics-slideshow-S.JPG', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aquaponics 101', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Ga