e': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a39e7798-9e95-5bd9-af78-83875c77eecf', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a39e7798-9e95-5bd9-af78-83875c77eecf'}, {'abstract': 'A Fred Piscop Diagramless with feeling.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/20/variety-a-sensible-diagramless/', 'snippet': 'A Fred Piscop Diagramless with feeling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — If you’re going to say anything about me, say that I am filled with hope (among other things). I am always hopeful that after putting in the work necessary to build a Diagramless crossword puzzle, the theme will just pop out at me and reward me for counting correctly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: A Sensible Diagramless', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2acf30cf-8a6e-5261-9bb3-734e29766b97', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2acf30cf-8a6e-5261-9bb3-734e29766b97'}, {'abstract': 'An unusually loud outcry followed the vendor’s death in a squabble with urban management agents, who for many Chinese are the most visible face of the authoritarian impulses of the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/world/asia/death-in-china-stirs-anger-over-urban-rule-enforcers.html', 'snippet': 'An unusually loud outcry followed the vendor’s death in a squabble with urban management agents, who for many Chinese are the most visible face of the authoritarian impulses of the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — It started Wednesday morning as a squabble between an unlicensed watermelon vendor and the widely despised urban management agents who prowl China’s streets looking for scofflaws. Words were exchanged, blows were landed and in the end, the vendor, Deng Zhengjia, 56, lay dead on the pavement in Linwu, a city in central Hunan Province, as angry bystanders photographed his body with their cellphones. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/world/sub-china/sub-china-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/21/world/sub-china/sub-china-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/world/sub-china/sub-china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/world/sub-china/sub-china-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/21/world/sub-china/sub-china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/21/world/sub-china/sub-china-thumbStandard.jp