ations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro International Trade Services', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T17:59:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kocieniewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kocieniewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e5b6a84-cb72-56bf-8b50-f6d87039eb44', 'word_count': 3630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e5b6a84-cb72-56bf-8b50-f6d87039eb44'}, {'abstract': 'When the body wants the skin of someone else, it knows how to behave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/opinion/sunday/life-without-sex.html', 'snippet': 'When the body wants the skin of someone else, it knows how to behave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — FOR a period of my life, from my 27th to my 39th years, I slept alone: I had no sex. I wasn’t unhappy. Or frustrated. In fact, I found no sex preferable to disappointing sex. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Without Sex', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life Without Sex', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T18:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophie Fontanel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fontanel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6081f1f2-4fe7-5fe8-bc9c-dd33418638f8', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6081f1f2-4fe7-5fe8-bc9c-dd33418638f8'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers should have a simple and effective way to opt out of online monitoring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/opinion/sunday/dont-track-us.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers should have a simple and effective way to opt out of online monitoring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hardly a secret that Amazon, Facebook and Google monitor what their users do online and show them targeted ads based on that data. But many users do not fully appreciate that this is also done by dozens of obscure online advertising networks. These companies place small files known as cookies on the computers and phones of people who visit Web sites that display ads they bought. These cookies allow them to serve up ads for, say, shoes that a consumer looked at on one site even as he moves to other sites. Such tracking is pervasive now, and the data is often put into detailed profiles that can also include information from public records and other sources like cash registers at physical stores. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Track Us', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Track Us', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T18:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f5ea9b-89f2-5829-b1be-ce346c8fb061', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f5ea9b-89f2-5829-b1be-ce346c8fb061'}, {'abstract': 'Washington’s automatic budget-cutting is hurting the courts and imperiling the federal public defender program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/opinion/sunday/justice-sequestered.html', 'snippet': 'Washington’s automatic budget-cutting is hurting the courts and imperiling the federal public defender program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The madness of Washington’s across-the-board budget cuts known as sequestration is causing real damage to the American justice system — undermining the sound functioning of the courts and particularly imperiling the delivery of effective legal representation to poor people accused of federal crimes. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Sequestered', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice Sequestered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Courts (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T18:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/406a24b7-2d09-508e-9947-43901caa54e0', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/406a24b7-2d09-508e-9947-43901caa54e0'}, {'abstract': 'The United States and its allies must work diplomatically with Iran on its nuclear program, not push for military action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/opinion/sunday/next-steps-with-iran.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and its allies must work diplomatically with Iran on its nuclear program, not push for military action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The closer the world gets to serious diplomatic engagement with Iran on its nuclear program, the more hard-liners in Washington and abroad will push military action if the effort fails. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel, for one, has tried to goad the Obama administration to show Hassan Rowhani, Iran’s newly elected president, that “the military option which is on the table is truly on the table.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Next Steps With Iran', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Next Steps With Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowhani, Hassan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T18:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/88ac1dfb-5d14-51aa-bdda-e9209534c363', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88ac1dfb-5d14-51aa-bdda-e9209534c363'}, {'abstract': 'Is a protest against a writer’s comments a form of blacklisting?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/opinion/sunday/the-enders-game-boycott.html', 'snippet': 'Is a protest against a writer’s comments a form of blacklisting?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The film “Ender’s Game” tells the story of a gifted child sent to a military academy in space to prepare for an alien invasion. It’s catnip for the Comic-Con crowd, and Lionsgate Entertainment wants to position it as November’s big-budget blockbuster. But the studio is encountering an unexpected publicity nightmare: an activist group called Geeks Out is pushing a boycott of the film, claiming that anyone who pays to see it will effectively be subsidizing antigay “fear-mongering.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Ender’s Game’ Boycott', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The ‘Ender’s Game’ Boycott', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapidos, Juliet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Ender's Game (Movie)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Card, Orson Scott', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-20T18:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'midd