ion Domination High-Def, a late-night programming block overseen by Nick Weidenfeld, an alumnus of Adult Swim, begins with this adaptation of the Internet comic created by the brothers Malachai and Ethan Nicolle when they were 5 and 29, respectively, about an ax-wielding hero, above, (voiced by Nick Offerman) who sleeps two minutes a night, subsists on birthday cake and battles villains. “It’s a nonsensical but inventive and purely entertaining takeoff on superhero tales ,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. “The animation is serviceable, and the show gets a vital boost from the voice performance of Nick Offerman, whose mock solemnity works as well for a mildly fascistic superhero as it did for a middle-American bureaucrat in ‘Parks and Recreation.’\xa0” “High School USA!,” at 9:45, “a broad and dull spoof of the Archie gang” created and written by Dino Stamatopoulos, best known for playing Star-Burns on “Community,” “slides down the wall quickly,” Mr. Hale added. The block moves to Saturdays at 11 p.m. on July 27.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T06:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/543f43d6-13c1-5416-afc6-8dcb65048a99', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/543f43d6-13c1-5416-afc6-8dcb65048a99'}, {'abstract': 'Myanmar’s president U Thein Sein washes his dirty linen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/opinion/global/heng-cartoon-sectarian-violence-i