, 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8de3bcd5-ba07-562a-9851-11bdabcc967b', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8de3bcd5-ba07-562a-9851-11bdabcc967b'}, {'abstract': 'Two TV movies based on the Jack Irish mystery novels will begin streaming online Monday from Acorn TV.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/arts/television/hero-on-the-page-moves-doggedly-to-the-screen.html', 'snippet': 'Two TV movies based on the Jack Irish mystery novels will begin streaming online Monday from Acorn TV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To Americans, Guy Pearce is a movie star, known for playing a crusading cop in “L.A. Confidential,” an obsessive amnesiac in “Memento” and a villain in “Iron Man 3.” At home in Australia, he’s also that guy who used to be on television — a regular in popular soap operas in the 1980s and ’90s and a star of the frontier story “Snowy River: The McGregor Saga” (in which his cast mates included Josh Lucas, Hugh Jackman, Wendy Hughes and Olivia Newton-John).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/jackirish/jackirish-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hero on the Page Moves Doggedly to the Screen', 'kicker': 'Watch List', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hero on the Page Moves Doggedly to the Screen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearce, Guy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Temple, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Acorn TV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T22:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fcfa419-a7a8-530e-97d6-a1c57fbc96e5', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fcfa419-a7a8-530e-97d6-a1c57fbc96e5'}, {'abstract': 'Theatreworks USA’s production of “The Civil War” is a musical that gives personal faces to some of the hundreds of thousands of casualties in America’s bloodiest war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/theater/reviews/the-civil-war-from-theatreworks-usa-at-lucille-lortel.html', 'snippet': 'Theatreworks USA’s production of “The Civil War” is a musical that gives personal faces to some of the hundreds of thousands of casualties in America’s bloodiest war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first soldier who dies in “The Civil War” doesn’t crumple in agony or reel dramatically backward. After the crack of a gunshot, he stands immobile as a spotlight illuminates his face. He intones a few facts: “Michael O’Malley. 18. Born in County Clare. Got off the boat five months ago — just me and me ma.” Turning with military precision, the soldier (Michael Thomas Walker) quietly exits.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/civilwar/civilwar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Many Sons: The Faces of a Nation’s Slaughter', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Many Sons: The Faces of a Nation’s Slaughter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graeber, Laurel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theaterworks/USA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverstein, Jonathan (Theater Director)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T22:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc879317-cb84-5333-b5af-8e6708493432', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc879317-cb84-5333-b5af-8e6708493432'}, {'abstract': 'In the Bollywood film “Ramaiya Vastavaiya,” at a wedding celebration, the bride’s playful cousin falls in love with a poor village girl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/movies/in-ramaiya-vastavaiya-a-wealthy-man-pursues-a-poor-girl.html', 'snippet': 'In the Bollywood film “Ramaiya Vastavaiya,” at a wedding celebration, the bride’s playful cousin falls in love with a poor village girl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is something for everyone in Prabhudheva’s ambitious Bollywood film “Ramaiya Vastavaiya” — comedy, romance, action and the obligatory music-and-dancing numbers — but hardly any of it is convincing, and the proceedings are rife with clichés. (The film, a remake of his own “Nuvvostanante Nenoddantana,” from 2005, seems to have been made anew for the big-screen debut of Girish Kumar, the son of the music and film producer Kumar S. Taurani.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/arts/RAMA/RAMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hate at First Sight, With Love and Its Hurdles to Follow', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hate at First Sight, With Love and Its Hurdles to Follow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T22:17:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Herrington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d804bf41-a977-5540-b2e9-19cb5c59d8e7', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d804bf41-a977-5540-b2e9-19cb5c59d8e7'}, {'abstract': 'Carolyn Lynch, Mike Passell, Roger Bates, Garey Hayden, Marc Jacobus and Eddie Wold will be the USA-2 team in the d’Orsi Senior Trophy world championship in Bali, Indonesia, in September.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/crosswords/bridge/surviving-a-5-1-trump-break-at-usa-trials.html', 'snippet': 'Carolyn Lynch, Mike Passell, Roger Bates, Garey Hayden, Marc Jacobus and Eddie Wold will be the USA-2 team in the d’Orsi Senior Trophy world championship in Bali, Indonesia, in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carolyn Lynch, Mike Passell, Roger Bates, Garey Hayden, Marc Jacobus and Eddie Wold will be the USA-2 team in the d’Orsi Senior Trophy world championship in Bali, Indonesia, in September.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/crosswords/22card/22card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 251, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/crosswords/22card/22card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 251, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/crosswords/22card/22card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/crosswords/22card/22card-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/crosswords/22card/22card-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surviving a 5-1 Trump Break at USA Trials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T22:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c85b1d8-d5bc-5b43-a150-1578c4275ffc', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c85b1d8-d5bc-5b43-a150-1578c4275ffc'}, {'abstract': 'The Guggenheim Museum has announced the fall season of its Works & Process series, which offers audiences access to creators and performers of coming works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/arts/fall-season-announced-for-guggenheim-series.html', 'snippet': 'The Guggenheim Museum has announced the fall season of its Works & Process series, which offers audiences access to creators and performers of coming works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guggenheim Museum has announced the fall season of its Works & Process series, which offers audiences access to creators and performers of coming works. The New York City Opera and the Brooklyn Academy of Music are to kick off the season on Sept. 9 with excerpts from “Anna Nicole,” the opera by Mark-Anthony Turnage based on the life and death of Anna Nicole Smith. Other scheduled events include Juilliard Dance performances of excerpts from Pina Bausch’s “Wind von West” on Sept. 29 and 30; a preview of the Metropolitan Opera’s staging of Nico Muhly’s true-crime opera, “Two Boys,” on Oct. 14; and Prokofiev’s “Peter and the Wolf,” narrated by the fashion designer Isaac Mizrahi with music performed by the Juilliard Ensemble, in December.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fall Season Announced for Guggenheim Series', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fall Season Announced For Guggenheim Series', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T22:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d274bdc-e10d-5a19-9010-54d3aa58611e', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d274bdc-e10d-5a19-9010-54d3aa58611e'}, {'abstract': 'Let’s put an end to the misuse of quantum physics to validate outlandish metaphysical claims.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/21/nothing-to-see-here-demoting-the-uncertainty-principle/', 'snippet': 'Let’s put an end to the misuse of quantum physics to validate outlandish metaphysical claims.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You’ve observed the robbers. They know it. That will change their actions,” says Charlie Eppes, the math savant who helps detectives on television’s “Numbers.” Eppes claims that this insight follows from quantum physics, in particular, Werner Heisenberg’s infamous “uncertainty principle.” Not all mischaracterizations of Heisenberg’s principle are as innocent as Eppes’s. The film “What the Bleep Do We Know!?” uses it to justify many articles of faith in New Age philosophy. Asserting that observing water molecules changes their molecular structure, the film reasons that since we are 90 percent water, physics therefore tells us that we can fundamentally change our nature via mental energy. Fundamentally inaccurate uses of the principle are also common in the academy, especially among social theorists, who often argue that it undermines science’s claims to objectivity and completeness. As Jim Holt has written, “No scientific idea from the last century is more fetishized, abused and misunderstood — by the vulgar and the learned alike — than Heisenberg’s uncertainty principle.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nothing to See Here: Demoting the Uncertainty Principle', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bohr, Niels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heisenberg, Werner', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T23:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Callender', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Callender', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8401be9-e70c-5536-a1c1-86c4c31b01c1', 'word_count': 1476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8401be9-e70c-5536-a1c1-86c4c31b01c1'}, {'abstract': 'The market is surging, with digital sales of comic books almost tripling in a year’s time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/business/media/comic-books-cash-in-on-a-digital-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'The market is surging, with digital sales of comic books almost tripling in a year’s time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — The comic book industry, after years of struggling to bolster sales, appears to have found a way to draw new readers, thanks in part to its push into the digital realm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 813}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 756, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1798, 'width': 1327, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/22comic/22comic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Embracing Tablets, Comic Book Publishers Cash In on a Digital Revolution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Embracing Tablets, Comic Book Publishers Cash In on a Digital Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ComiXology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-21T23:28:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9d34932-6b18-56fc-902f-09443093a980', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9d34932-6b18-56fc-902f-09443093a980'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jan Brewer’s decision to push a Medicaid expansion through the Arizona Legislature has caused deep splits within her state’s Republican party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/us/arizona-republicans-are-at-odds-on-medicaid.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jan Brewer’s decision to push a Medicaid expansion through the Arizona Legislature has caused deep splits within her state’s Republican party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — For Gov. Jan Brewer, the passage last month of a Medicaid expansion was a major coup. Despite a Republican majority in the Legislature, where she faced significant opposition from Tea Party members, she rallied the entire Democratic delegation to her side and made a progressive issue palatable to just enough conservatives, casting the expansion as the right decision for the state, morally and monetarily.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-img/22medicaid1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-img/22medicaid1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 709}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-img/22medicaid1-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 867, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-img/22medicaid1-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1734, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-img/22medicaid1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-img/22medicaid1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/us/22medicaid1-