s on whether “more of the same” was about all Hollywood had.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/business/media/clones-rule-as-hollywood-beats-drum-at-comic-con.html', 'snippet': 'Many of the movies offered to fans in San Diego were sequels or retreads, raising questions on whether “more of the same” was about all Hollywood had.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Legendary Entertainment came to Comic-Con last year promoting “Pacific Rim” with all the attending buzz, hype and chatter. Then, a week and a half ago, came the release.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/media/comiccon/comiccon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clones Rule as Hollywood Beats Drum at Comic-Con', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clones Rule As Hollywood Beats Drum At Comic-Con', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Convention)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science Fiction', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twentieth Century Fox', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Pictures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legendary Pictures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lions Gate Entertainment Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers Pictures', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T01:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes and Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82356f58-8083-517b-8cad-f0b4d0ac234a', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82356f58-8083-517b-8cad-f0b4d0ac234a'}, {'abstract': 'The water will soon flow more freely on the Penobscot River, another step in the nationwide movement to restore native ecosystems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/opinion/down-comes-another-dam.html', 'snippet': 'The water will soon flow more freely on the Penobscot River, another step in the nationwide movement to restore native ecosystems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, a demolition crew will begin removing the Veazie Dam on the Penobscot River just above Bangor, Me. The Veazie is the lowest of the Penobscot dams and closest to the river’s mouth on the Maine coast. It is also critical to the entire Penobscot River watershed, which covers nearly a third of the state. Thanks to the work of the Penobscot River Restoration Trust and its partners, the lower river will be free-flowing once again, allowing the revival of a complex migratory ecosystem once teeming with fish working their way up from the sea.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Down Comes Another Dam', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Down Comes Another Dam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Penobscot River (Me)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Rivers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T01:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0d675de-3894-581c-b581-aeb16dce3050', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0d675de-3894-581c-b581-aeb16dce3050'}, {'abstract': 'With a confirmed director, the federal consumer bureau can move forward on its agenda to crack down on abusive tactics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/opinion/the-good-guy-wins.html', 'snippet': 'With a confirmed director, the federal consumer bureau can move forward on its agenda to crack down on abusive tactics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the deal that broke the filibuster logjam in the Senate, Richard Cordray was confirmed last week as director of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau — two years after his nomination by President Obama. Republicans had blocked a vote in an attempt to weaken the portion of the Dodd-Frank law that established the bureau. In explaining why 12 of them finally joined 54 Democrats to approve Mr. Cordray, Senator Bob Corker, Republican of Tennessee, told The Wall Street Journal that some Republicans had realized that “maybe” it wasn’t right to hold up a qualified nominee because you don’t like the law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Good Guy Wins', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Good Guy Wins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T01:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/413ea032-5ca0-53f4-868b-a52b0fd0355f', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/413ea032-5ca0-53f4-868b-a52b0fd0355f'}, {'abstract': 'Local and federal law enforcement authorities searched a