igher in New York and Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/business/in-climbing-income-ladder-location-matters.html', 'snippet': 'The odds of rising to another income level are notably low in certain cities, like Atlanta and Charlotte, and much higher in New York and Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA – Stacey Calvin spends almost as much time commuting to her job — on a bus, two trains and another bus — as she does working part-time at a day care center. She knows exactly where to board the train and which stairwells to use at the stations so that she has the best chance of getting to work on time in the morning and making it home to greet her three children after school.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/mobility-map/mobility-map-articleLarge.png', 'height': 317, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/business/mobility-map/mobility-map-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 317}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/mobility-map/mobility-map-jumbo.png', 'height': 500, 'width': 945, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/business/mobility-map/mobility-map-superJumbo.png', 'height': 500, 'width': 945, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Climbing Income Ladder, Location Matters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Geography Seen as Barrier To Climbing Class Ladder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonhardt, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subje