tname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfe3b763-653d-5739-8cd0-7aeee3273330', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfe3b763-653d-5739-8cd0-7aeee3273330'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, July 22.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-july-22.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, July 22.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Where you grow up matters. There is tremendous variation across the U.S. in the extent to which kids can rise out of poverty.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, July 22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T04:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/b380546d-5b11-53b9-a3d0-ff129fa52156', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b380546d-5b11-53b9-a3d0-ff129fa52156'}, {'abstract': 'Scranton still stands out as one of the American cities where poor people have among the best odds of climbing into the middle class, according to a large new study.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/snapshots-of-upwardly-mobile-areas/', 'snippet': 'Scranton still stands out as one of the American cities where poor people have among the best odds of climbing into the middle class, according to a large new study.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scranton, Pa., may not be anybody’s idea of a boom town. A year ago, with the industrial city in northeastern Pennsylvania on the verge of bankruptcy, the mayor cut city workers’ pay to the minimum wage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snapshots of Upwardly Mobile Areas', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T04:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Siddons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siddons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9afac67-9fe3-57d0-9917-755eebf8cbae', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9afac67-9fe3-57d0-9917-755eebf8cbae'}, {'abstract': 'Family structure was one of the four factors with a clear relationship to upward mobility in a new study comparing mobility across metropolitan areas.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/a-steeper-climb-for-single-parents/', 'snippet': 'Family structure was one of the four factors with a clear relationship to upward mobility in a new study comparing mobility across metropolitan areas.', 'lead_paragraph': ' For single parents, every step on the climb up the income ladder can come with additional complications. Taking a job with a long commute can be impossible, because it leaves no back-up plan when a child gets sick. Working late can be similarly difficult. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Steeper Climb for Single Parents', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T04:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/492092b7-791a-55ec-ab52-cd8f38884582', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/492092b7-791a-55ec-ab52-cd8f38884582'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Lifetime) SUPERMARKET SUPERSTAR Food entrepreneurs compete to have their creations sold by a major grocery chain in this new series hosted by Stacy Keibler. Three mentors — Debbi Fields of Mrs. Fields Cookies; Michael Chiarello, the owner of Coqueta restaurant in San Francisco and Bottega in the Napa Valley; and the brand expert Chris Cornyn (above from left, with Ms. Keibler) — help the contestants in preparing their products for mass production. The development chef Andrew Hunter helps them with their recipes to impress consumer focus groups. The players must then design packaging to present their products to Tom Dahlen, the supermarket buyer for A.&P., who will choose the winner of each episode. The last cook standing receives $10,000 in cash and $100,000 worth of professional product development with which to create samples. Three winners will be invited in the finale to introduce their products to Sam Martin, the chief executive of A.&P., for the possibility of national distribution. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T04:19:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/052d3b52-4510-5f96-8f6e-270a71220dba', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/052d3b52-4510-5f96-8f6e-270a71220dba'}, {'abstract': 'The state news media reported that 22 people had been confirmed dead after a series of temblors, one with a 6.6 magnitude, shook parts of Gansu Province.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/world/asia/earthquakes-hit-area-of-northwestern-china.html', 'snippet': 'The state news media reported that 22 people had been confirmed dead after a series of temblors, one with a 6.6 magnitude, shook parts of Gansu Province.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A series of earthquakes shook mountainous areas of Gansu Province in western China\xa0on\xa0Monday\xa0morning, triggering landslides across a wide area. State 