y, who is now third in line to the throne, was delivered at 4:24 p.m. local time on Monday, weighing 8 pounds, 6 ounces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/europe/royal-baby.html', 'snippet': 'Kensington Palace announced that the baby, who is now third in line to the throne, was delivered at 4:24 p.m. local time on Monday, weighing 8 pounds, 6 ounces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The news, when it finally came, was hardly a surprise. But after the days of fruitless speculation, of webcams showing live scenes of inactivity, of bystanders photographing one another and of wilting reporters straining for new ways to say that nothing was happening, the arrival of the newest royal heir on Monday afternoon turned out to be as much a relief as a joy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Duchess of Cambridge Gives Birth to a Boy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Royal Baby Arrives to Both Traditional Pomp and Modern Circumstance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'William, Duke of Cambridge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T07:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '',