 about Peggy Battin, a bioethicist who must confront her beliefs about a person’s right to die when her own husband suffers a grave accident. Henig’s latest book, “Twentysomething: Why Do Young Adults Seem Stuck?” was based on the article “What Is It About 20-Somethings?” that appeared a few years ago in the magazine, where she is a contributing writer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Robin Marantz Henig on Making End-of-Life Decisions (and Changing Your Mind)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battin, Margaret Pabst', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henig, Robin Marantz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T10:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb19ecd9-52ef-50bc-bd04-a493deaa72d2', 'word_count': 1360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb19ecd9-52ef-50bc-bd04-a493deaa72d2'}, {'abstract': 'An effort led by Britain brought a unanimous decision against the group’s military wing. Sanctions are expected to include asset freezes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/middleeast/european-union-adds-hezbollah-wing-to-terror-list.html', 'snippet': 'An effort led by Britain brought a unanimous decision against the group’s military wing. Sanctions are expected to in