ap, simple “feature phones” that have largely disappeared in America and Europe but are still the norm in developing countries like India and Brazil, Vindu Goel reports in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: A Mobile Facebook for Phones in the Developing World', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T11:26:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b6e9a0d-aee6-5ca2-ab58-c0fc8eeb4a00', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b6e9a0d-aee6-5ca2-ab58-c0fc8eeb4a00'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators argue that Steven A. Cohen knew about and took part in suspicious trading activity at SAC. | A maneuver by financial players adds a fraction of a penny to the price of aluminum cans. | The governing Liberal Democrats in Japan secured a landslide victory in parliamentary elections. | A revelation in Detroit illustrates a broader debate over pension math.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/morning-agenda-cohen-of-sac-in-the-spotlight/', 'snippet': 'Regulators argue that Steven A. Cohen knew about and took part in suspicious trading activity at SAC. | A maneuver by financial players adds a fraction of a penny to the price of aluminum cans. | The governing Liberal Democrats in Japan secured a ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defenders of the billionaire hedge fund manager Steven A. Cohen have argued that the unusual structure of his firm, SAC Capital Advisors, shielded him from any illegal trading by his employees. But in a legal filing on Friday, federal regulators argued that Mr. Cohen was not only aware of suspicious trading activity at SAC but participated in it, DealBook’s Peter Lattman writes. “Faced with red flags of potentially unlawful conduct by employees under his supervision, Cohen allowed his traders to execute the recommended trades and stood by,” the Securities and Exchange Commission said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cohen of SAC in the Spotlight', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T11:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57bd9ef4-d237-5880-9357-48e265cfaf51', 'word_count': 1763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57bd9ef4-d237-5880-9357-48e265cfaf51'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian authorities take on the anti-corruption blogger Alexei Navalny and his supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/that-blunt-russian-force/', 'snippet': 'The Russian authorities take on the anti-corruption blogger Alexei Navalny and his supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — In the versatile Russian vocabulary of obscenities, there is a single word that means “I am fed up with what they are doing and I can’t take it anymore.” On Wednesday night my partner, Darya, who does not usually speak in obscenities, used it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Blunt Russian Force', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T11:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37441617-0052-5b3a-b8be-aa18734f3004', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37441617-0052-5b3a-b8be-aa18734f3004'}, {'abstract': 'It certainly correlates.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/did-sprawl-kill-horatio-alger/', 'snippet': 'It certainly correlates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honest truth: I wrote yesterday’s post suggesting that sprawl may have killed Detroit without knowing either about David Leonhart’s forthcoming article on how sprawl seems to hurt social mobility or the study on which it is based — a study, by the way, not yet available at David’s link, although the underlying data are there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did Sprawl Kill Horatio Alger?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35c70866-c422-50b3-acf0-61c5eb697154', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35c70866-c422-50b3-acf0-61c5eb697154'}, {'abstract': 'Sergey V. Lavrov, the foreign minister, blamed rebels for stalling and asked the United States for help in the negotiations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/middleeast/russia-says-assad-is-ready-for-peace-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Sergey V. Lavrov, the foreign minister, blamed rebels for stalling and asked the United States for help in the negotiations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Russian foreign minister, Sergey V. Lavrov, said on Monday that the government of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria was ready to engage in peace negotiations without preconditions and he urged the United States and other Western nations to bring Syrian opposition groups to the table for a new round of talks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Says Assad Is Ready for Peace Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bc8c86d-9582-5238-a6d3-6faa78b1e1fe', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc8c86d-9582-5238-a6d3-6faa78b1e1fe'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede will have dispatches from reporters in London and news of the reaction online, where professional and amateur royal watchers have been engaged in the Internet’s version of nervous pacing in the hall for more than a week.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/live-video-of-royal-baby-watch-in-london/', 'snippet': 'The Lede will have dispatches from reporters in London and news of the reaction online, where professional and amateur royal watchers have been engaged in the Internet’s version of nervous pacing in the hall for more than a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 12:54 p.m. As our colleague Alan Cowell reports, the Duchess of Cambridge, the former Kate Middleton, entered St. Mary’s Hospital in London early on Monday to prepare for the birth of her first child and was “in the early stages of labor,” the royal family announced in a brief message. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of the Royal Baby Watch in London', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St Mary's Hospital", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaabdb84-d664-5b72-b7a8-5dca88fed190', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaabdb84-d664-5b72-b7a8-5dca88fed190'}, {'abstract': 'A dispatch from the royal-baby watch outside the Lindo Wing of St. Mary’s hospital in central London, where journalists have dutifully waited for more than two weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/the-five-stages-of-the-royal-baby-wait/', 'snippet': 'A dispatch from the royal-baby watch outside the Lindo Wing of St. Mary’s hospital in central London, where journalists have dutifully waited for more than two weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — On royal-baby watch outside the Lindo Wing of St. Mary’s Hospital in central London, where journalists have dutifully been waiting, one was tempted to think of the past two and a half weeks as the five stages of boredom: denial (“It might be born early?”), anger (“I wish this baby would hurry up!”), bargaining (there was plenty of betting in the hospital yard on anything from the baby’s sex to its name, likely godparents and birth weight), depression (“This is soul-destroying,” one photographer remarked darkly after yet another day without news) — and finally, going into Week 3, acceptance mixed with a good dose of British wit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Five Stages of the Royal Baby Wait', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b98ce9a-4657-50a7-becb-0dc33bad958d', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b98ce9a-4657-50a7-becb-0dc33bad958d'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time in the history of the British monarchy the issue of the baby’s sex is constitutionally irrelevant, too, at least in terms of succession.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/whether-a-boy-or-a-girl-third-in-line-to-the-throne/', 'snippet': 'For the first time in the history of the British monarchy the issue of the baby’s sex is constitutionally irrelevant, too, at least in terms of succession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Asked by a 10-year-old schoolgirl whether she wanted her great-grandchild to be a boy or a girl, Queen Elizabeth II last week said that she would not mind either.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whether a Boy or a Girl, Third in Line to the Throne', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:55:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d123265-1e06-5d02-aea2-247bcf77897a', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d123265-1e06-5d02-aea2-247bcf77897a'}, {'abstract': 'The foundation stone of the 1984 Sikh massacre memorial was laid in Delhi in June. A novelist who survived the pogrom looks back.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/thomas-bernhard-in-new-delhi/', 'snippet': 'The foundation stone of the 1984 Sikh massacre memorial was laid in Delhi in June. A novelist who survived the pogrom looks back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Bernhard, the great Austrian author, created several curious characters in his short play “The German Lunch Table.” An ordinary extended family sits down for a meal around a “natural oak” table, but somewhere down the line they find Nazis in the soup. Nazis in the soup. Nazi soup. The mother complains: When I open packages of noodles in the kitchen, I find Nazis inside the packages and they always enter the soup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas Bernhard in New Delhi', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Indira', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Sajjan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jaspreet Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaspreet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba83b392-9f75-5c90-b086-944dbeb9ca3a', 'word_count': 2122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba83b392-9f75-5c90-b086-944dbeb9ca3a'}, {'abstract': 'The tortuous but real path toward a more perfect union can be gleaned from the president’s response to the verdict in the Trayvon Martin case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/booming/president-obama-race-and-the-ku-klux-klan.html', 'snippet': 'The tortuous but real path toward a more perfect union can be gleaned from the president’s response to the verdict in the Trayvon Martin case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1986, as the suburban columnist for The Times, I interviewed the head of the Ku Klux Klan. The man lived in Shelton, Conn., and until then, the national news stories had talked about what a social commentary it was, that the new imperial wizard came from the North — the idea being that racism wasn’t just a Southern problem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/booming/22winerip-booming-race1/22winerip-booming-race1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama, Race and the Ku Klux Klan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ku Klux Klan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:57:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65626a50-78db-5387-b66d-f1b421d3cb0a', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65626a50-78db-5387-b66d-f1b421d3cb0a'}, {'abstract': 'The big Swiss bank said it had reached an agreement in principle with the Federal Finance Housing Agency to settle claims related to mortgage-backed securities issued between 2004 and 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/ubs-reaches-settlement-on-mortgage-securities/', 'snippet': 'The big Swiss bank said it had reached an agreement in principle with the Federal Finance Housing Agency to settle claims related to mortgage-backed securities issued between 2004 and 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UBS, the Swiss banking giant, said on Monday that it had reached an agreement in principle with a United States regulator to settle claims related to mortgage-backed securities issued between 2004 and 2007.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'UBS Reaches Settlement on Mortgage Securities', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mortgage Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T12:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a561f90-3358-549a-a4cd-db5c29879402', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a561f90-3358-549a-a4cd-db5c29879402'}, {'abstract': 'It is hard not to be struck by the frantic enthusiasm the monarchy still seems to inspire in 21st-century Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/wait-for-royal-baby-lets-a-nation-revel-in-nostalgia/', 'snippet': 'It is hard not to be struck by the frantic enthusiasm the monarchy still seems to inspire in 21st-century Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It is hard not to be struck by the frantic enthusiasm the monarchy still seems to inspire in 21st-century Britain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wait for Royal Baby Lets a Nation Revel in Nostalgia', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T13:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19043591-b6f7-5be9-953b-c9964a6381a3', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19043591-b6f7-5be9-953b-c9964a6381a3'}, {'abstract': 'Royal officials plan to make the birth public with a framed proclamation mounted on a gold-trimmed wooden easel outside Buckingham Palace.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/how-the-royal-birth-will-be-announced/', 'snippet': 'Royal officials plan to make the birth public with a framed proclamation mounted on a gold-trimmed wooden easel outside Buckingham Palace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Too sniffy, too hidebound, too fusty? Or just the right touch for the birth of a child destined one day to inherit the crown of one of the world’s longest-surviving monarchies?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Royal Birth Will Be Announced', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buckingham Palace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T13:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}]