ed on Monday for an initial public offering. The I.P.O. would be the latest deal to test investors’ willingness to bet on a recovery in real estate.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/extended-stay-america-aims-to-go-public/', 'snippet': 'Extended Stay, a hotel chain owned by three investment firms, filed on Monday for an initial public offering. The I.P.O. would be the latest deal to test investors’ willingness to bet on a recovery in real estate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than three years after leaving bankruptcy, Extended Stay America has made plans to sell its shares to the investing public.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extended Stay America Aims to Go Public', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.P.O. Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centerbridge Partners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paulson & Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Blackstone Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T14:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae18695e-c6b2-5ba1-a4ea-12fe9657fe7e', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae18695e-c6b2-5ba1-a4ea-12fe9657fe7e'}, {'abstract': 'The company Intrepid Travel will offer new sailing trips to islands in the Myeik Archipelago in Burma.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/new-cruises-to-remote-burmese-islands/', 'snippet': 'The company Intrepid Travel will offer new sailing trips to islands in the Myeik Archipelago in Burma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November, Intrepid Travel will begin two\xa0 sailing trips to the’s Myeik Archipelago of Burma, a little-explored area of roughly 800 islands in the Andaman Sea off the Malay Peninsula.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Cruises to Remote Burmese Islands', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T14:26:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08c43c71-663a-5adc-a3bd-b689598d4921', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08c43c71-663a-5adc-a3bd-b689598d4921'}, {'abstract': 'Fort Hamilton is a vestige of New York Harbor’s rich military history and a top housing choice for service members looking for a slice of military suburbia about 40 minutes from Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/nyregion/money-wont-help-land-a-place-in-this-oasis-but-a-uniform-may.html', 'snippet': 'Fort Hamilton is a vestige of New York Harbor’s rich military history and a top housing choice for service members looking for a slice of military suburbia about 40 minutes from Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take the R train as far south as possible, to 95th Street in Bay Ridge, Brooklyn. Walk down Fourth Avenue toward the water and make the last left. The Verrazano-Narrows Bridge looms eerily overhead and a shady stretch of road leads to freshly manicured gardens, stately gates and 19th-century cannons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/22/nyregion/23APPRAISAL-span/23APPRAISAL-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Live in This Oasis, Money Won’t Help, but a Uniform May', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Live in This Oasis, Money Won’t Help, But a Uniform May', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gogolak, E C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Hamilton (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T14:26:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. C. Gogolak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gogolak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82822b3b-1f68-5a9d-be07-247c5cd8a4f5', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82822b3b-1f68-5a9d-be07-247c5cd8a4f5'}, {'abstract': 'Phil Mickelson’s first victory at the British Open was an athletic achievement more than a psychological one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/sports/mental-breakdowns-all-around-at-british-open-but-not-by-mickelson.html', 'snippet': 'Phil Mickelson’s first victory at the British Open was an athletic achievement more than a psychological one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About the only thing anyone knew going into Sunday’s final round of the British Open was that demons would be cleared out of someone’s closet. Every single one of the contenders carried some serious issues around Muirfield. Collectively, they had enough baggage to open a Louis Vuitton outlet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mental Breakdowns All Around at British Open, but Not by Mickelson', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickelson, Phil', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Froome, Christopher', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T14:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f045019-d272-5c2c-a534-a7c40192da54', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f045019-d272-5c2c-a534-a7c40192da54'}, {'abstract': 'If a customer says something offensive to an employee, is your first concern for your customer or your employee?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/when-the-customer-is-not-right/', 'snippet': 'If a customer says something offensive to an employee, is your first concern for your customer or your employee?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have a friend who has an 18-year-old son. He is a big kid, with a friendly disposition and a kind and respectful demeanor. He has a very good part-time job at a respected restaurant in an affluent suburb of Chicago. He works at the carryout counter where he reviews customer orders, asks the customers if there is anything else he can get for them, and then asks if they need help carrying their food to their cars. He has worked there for more than a year, and I’m sure the training and support he has received will serve him well in future jobs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When 