st each week of the baseball season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oakland’s Yoenis Cespedes was not among the top 10 home run hitters before the All-Star break, but his batting practice exhibitions are legendary. Perhaps that was why “someone else” received nearly 23 percent of the vote in Question No. 1, trailing Baltimore’s Chris Davis and Detroit’s Prince Fielder. Cespedes, of course, delivered the Home Run Derby victory. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triple Play: Week 16 Results', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T20:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cc79d74-b15f-5496-9868-40539da5f9d5', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cc79d74-b15f-5496-9868-40539da5f9d5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Nelson, the newly appointed music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra, will be unable to conduct his first scheduled performance in his new job.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/andris-nelsons-withdraws-from-tanglewood-performance-after-concussion/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Nelson, the newly appointed music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra, will be unable to conduct his first scheduled performance in his new job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andris Nelsons, the newly appointed music director of the Boston Symphony Orchestra, has withdrawn from his Saturday evening performance at Tanglewood with his new orchestra – his first since his new position was announced – because of a household accident that has left him with a concussion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Andris Nelsons Withdraws From Tanglewood Performance After Concussion', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tanglewood Music Festival (Lenox, Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelsons, Andris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T20:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03a43a4c-765e-5e1e-85ca-b2e862412034', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03a43a4c-765e-5e1e-85ca-b2e862412034'}, {'abstract': 'Yahoo’s repurchase of a large chunk of Daniel Loeb’s stake sucks up most of the cash the company reserved for buybacks. It also heralds the departure of three Third Point-approved directors, robbing Yahoo of some much-needed advisers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/loeb-wins-and-shareholders-lose-out-at-yahoo/', 'snippet': 'Yahoo’s repurchase of a large chunk of Daniel Loeb’s stake sucks up most of the cash the company reserved for buybacks. It also heralds the departure of three Third Point-approved directors, robbing Yahoo of some much-needed advisers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Loeb’s Yahoo exit hurts investors twice over. The Internet company is buying back two-thirds of the hedge fund mogul’s stake, owned by his firm, Third Point, for $1.2 billion. That sucks up most of the cash Yahoo reserved for repurchases. It also heralds the departure of three Third Point-approved directors, robbing Yahoo of some much-needed advisers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loeb Wins and Shareholders Lose Out at Yahoo', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T20:18:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b370200-77ce-5faf-b344-4f925f7c0089', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b370200-77ce-5faf-b344-4f925f7c0089'}, {'abstract': '“The Telling Room,” by Michael Paterniti, focuses on the passions and disappointments of an artisanal cheesemaker in the highlands of Castile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/books/michael-paternitis-telling-room-set-in-rural-spain.html', 'snippet': '“The Telling Room,” by Michael Paterniti, focuses on the passions and disappointments of an artisanal cheesemaker in the highlands of Castile.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Telling Room” has a subtitle so hyperbolic that it’s a tall tale in its own right. This is Michael Paterniti’s second nonfiction book, 13 years after “Driving Mr. Albert” recounted his quality time with a Tupperware container that held part of Albert Einstein’s brain. Now his new, less exotic book, “Telling Room,” is billed as “A Tale of Love, Betrayal, Revenge, and the World’s Greatest Piece of Cheese.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/book-1374515804095-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/book-1374515804095-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 961}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/book-1374515804095-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/book-1374515804095-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1279, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/23book-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/23book-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23book-1/23book-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fable Fermented From a Tin of Cheese', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fable Fermented From a Tin Of Cheese', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterniti, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T20:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of