: 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f0b8fc3b-5222-55db-84e7-4518137df902', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f0b8fc3b-5222-55db-84e7-4518137df902'}, {'abstract': 'Ayatollah Ali Khamenei said such talks would not have a positive result for Iran because of what he called a lack of honesty by American officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/middleeast/iran-leader-not-optimistic-about-talks-with-us.html', 'snippet': 'Ayatollah Ali Khamenei said such talks would not have a positive result for Iran because of what he called a lack of honesty by American officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran’s supreme leader, Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, threw some cold water on recent efforts to reinvigorate diplomatic contacts between Iran and the United States, saying he was not optimistic that any agreement would be reached, though he does not oppose talks “on certain issues.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Leader Not Optimistic About Talks With U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowhani, Hassan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T21:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bf76d23-ab35-52cf-b6e6-79feaece6e3f', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bf76d23-ab35-52cf-b6e6-79feaece6e3f'}, {'abstract': 'These backpacks, found not far from Tucson, were discarded by Mexican migrants who used them to carry the clean clothes they would need after they crossed the border into the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/unpacking-a-new-life/', 'snippet': 'These backpacks, found not far from Tucson, were discarded by Mexican migrants who used them to carry the clean clothes they would need after they crossed the border into the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend’s Look featured a wall of backpacks. But they were more than schoolbags or knapsacks, despite all the Adidas and Puma and Nike branding, the cartoon decorations (Bart Simpson, the Tasmanian Devil), the soccer insignia, the corporate trademarks (Levitra, HSBC). They were used by Mexican migrants crossing into the United States to carry the clean clothes in which they hoped to start new lives in America. And, as the photographer\xa0Richard Barnes puts it: “Metaphorically, they were a vessel to help get these people across the border, where they strip them away and become new people. They’re also a potent example of globalization. You can see all the logos — like Ralph Lauren and a lot of knockoffs that are sold on the border — and you realize what a small world we live in.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/magazine/backpack2/backpack2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/19/magazine/backpack2/backpack2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/19/magazine/backpack2/backpack2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024,