ews_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25529845-ceda-543d-87ec-5a24402a2e4a', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25529845-ceda-543d-87ec-5a24402a2e4a'}, {'abstract': 'Fun in the sun with Jean O’Conor.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/22/packing-up-the-answers/', 'snippet': 'Fun in the sun with Jean O’Conor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — Here’s a puzzle to fit the season if ever there was one. If only we’d remembered to pack a cool drink as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Packing Up the Answers', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T22:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/997a2eae-4525-5543-9c90-60d1cb9777cc', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/997a2eae-4525-5543-9c90-60d1cb9777cc'}, {'abstract': 'At this year’s Glimmerglass Festival, a production of “The Flying Dutchman” is the most conventional of the offerings, a sign of Francesca Zambello’s boldness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/arts/music/glimmerglass-offers-an-ambitious-spread-of-works.html', 'snippet': 'At this year’s Glimmerglass Festival, a production of “The Flying Dutchman” is the most conventional of the offerings, a sign of Francesca Zambello’s boldness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COOPERSTOWN, N.Y. — Ambition has never been in short supply at the Alice Busch Opera Theater, the cozy 900-seat auditorium that long housed the Glimmerglass Opera, and now is the principal setting for its successor, the Glimmerglass Festival. But even measured by the high standard this annual affair has sustained, this year’s festival — which runs through Aug. 24 here — rises to new levels of innovation, curiosity and, yes, chutzpah.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/glimmer-2/glimmer-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bold Strokes in the Country', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bold Strokes In the Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glimmerglass Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zambello, Francesca', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T22:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81df71ea-e34c-513c-add3-c8bcf4584b79', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81df71ea-e34c-513c-add3-c8bcf4584b79'}, {'abstract': 'The Pitchfork Music Festival, sponsored by the taste-making culture Web site, took place in Union Park in Chicago last weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/arts/music/dancing-under-the-sky.html', 'snippet': 'The Pitchfork Music Festival, sponsored by the taste-making culture Web site, took place in Union Park in Chicago last weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Late Saturday afternoon, just as the stubborn, gummy heat was beginning to lift off Union Park here, the Canadian D.J.-producer Ryan Hemsworth took to the small stage in the southwest corner of the park and finally kicked this year’s edition of the Pitchfork Music Festival into gear. At one point, he played a remix of a new song by Kanye West, one of this city’s hometown heroes, and for the first time since early Friday afternoon, when the festival began under conditions of extreme heat, bodies got to moving. They didn’t stop for the rest of the weekend — not just because the weather remained mostly tolerable, but also because the second half of this festival served as a reminder of how dance music has become the most exciting emergent narrative in pop. This was true, not only in the mainstream but also in the connoisseur’s corners documented by Pitchfork, the forward-thinking and taste-shaping Web site that has sponsored this festival every year since 2006.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/pitchfork1/pitchfork1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge'