he most stringent limits on abortion in the country, calling them “invalid and unconstitutional.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Monday blocked enforcement of North Dakota’s recently enacted ban on most abortions, calling it “invalid and unconstitutional.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Blocks North Dakota Abortion Restrictions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abortion Restrictions Go Too Far, Judge Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hovland, Daniel L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalrymple, John (1948- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Reproductive Rights', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T23:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2242f41e-b7c0-52c8-9630-6913af03d7c0', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2242f41e-b7c0-52c8-9630-6913af03d7c0'}, {'abstract': 'Though Afghan-American relations have been badly strained, Gen. Martin E. Dempsey said he would like to see a long-term security agreement between the two countries signed by October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/asia/joint-chiefs-head-hopeful-on-afghan-security-pact.html', 'snippet': 'Though Afghan-American relations have been badly strained, Gen. Martin E. Dempsey said he would like to see a long-term security agreement between the two countries signed by October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Though Afghan-American relations have been badly strained, Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, expressed optimism on Monday about the prospects for a long-term security agreement between the two countries, saying he would like to see it signed no later than October.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joint Chiefs’ Head Hopeful on Afghan Security Pact', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joint Chiefs Chairman Hopeful on Afghan Pact', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T23:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b286a34f-7365-5e76-9ca8-e6f32f840d21', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b286a34f-7365-5e76-9ca8-e6f32f840d21'}, {'abstract': 'A review commissioned by the university found that administrators involved in searching faculty e-mail accounts did not believe they were violating privacy rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/education/no-evidence-harvard-officials-read-faculty-e-mails-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'A review commissioned by the university found that administrators involved in searching faculty e-mail accounts did not believe they were violating privacy rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A review commissioned by Harvard University and released on Monday concluded that administrators who searched some faculty members’ e-mail accounts last year did so in good faith, and it found no evidence that they had actually read any e-mails.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Evidence Harvard Officials Read Faculty E-Mails, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Says Harvard Officials Didn’t Think E-Mail Search Violated Privacy Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keating, Michael B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T23:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4fc88d9-4aad-5483-b903-3001295baf8c', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4fc88d9-4aad-5483-b903-3001295baf8c'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Flemmi, in his third day on the stand in the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, said Mr. Bulger 