ion': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Cites Extradition as Sore Point With U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Cites Extradition As Sore Point With U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T23:51:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6b6d8f1-3e9a-596c-b7f8-6fcc0d489b08', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6b6d8f1-3e9a-596c-b7f8-6fcc0d489b08'}, {'abstract': 'At least two people were killed Monday as supporters and opponents of former President Mohamed Morsi battled near Tahrir Square in Cairo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/middleeast/egypt-4-killed-in-political-clashes.html', 'snippet': 'At least two people were killed Monday as supporters and opponents of former President Mohamed Morsi battled near Tahrir Square in Cairo.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least two people were killed Monday as supporters and opponents of former President Mohamed Morsi battled near Tahrir Square in Cairo using firearms and rocks, according to witnesses and the Interior Ministry. In similar clashes in the Qalyubia governorate, north of Cairo, at least two people were killed, according to a ministry spokesman. The threat of violence has intensified over the past week as Mr. Morsi’s supporters have escalated their protests against Egypt’s military, which deposed Mr. Morsi on July 3 after mass protests against his rule. Mr. Morsi has not been seen since his ouster, when he was taken into military custody, along with several of his aides. At a news conference on Monday in Cairo, Mr. Morsi’s children, claiming that he had been “abducted,” said they intended to take legal action against the military to challenge his nearly three-week detention. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: 4 Killed in Political Clashes', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: 4 Killed in Political Clashes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-22T23:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/78143bdd-3d0a-5444-988c-a26eecd6bc23', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78143bdd-3d0a-5444-988c-a26eecd6bc23'}, {'abstract': 'The operator of the stricken Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant said Monday that contaminated water had been seeping from damaged reactors into the Pacific.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/world/asia/japan-nuclear-plant-admits-leaks.html', 'snippet': 'The operator of the stricken Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant said Monday that contaminated water had been seeping from damaged reactors into the Pacific.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The operator of the stricken Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant said Monday that contaminated water had been seeping from damaged reactors into the Pacific, reversing its previous denials. Increased levels of radioactive contaminants were found weeks ago in nearby seawater, leading regulators to conclude that the plant has been leaking into the sea since an earthquake and tsunami caused a triple meltdown in 2011. The operator, the Tokyo Electric Power Company, said it now believed that highly contaminated water had been leaking into groundwater, which flows into the sea. It said the contaminants appeared to be gathering in a man-made harbor near the plant, and not flowing into the open ocean. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: Nuclear Plant Admits Leaks', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Nuclear Plant Admits Leaks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Electric Power Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T00:04:08+0000', '