', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/e983be4e-6a63-5858-8678-7c28b2b94d95', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e983be4e-6a63-5858-8678-7c28b2b94d95'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Black was a cabaret singer known for her sprightly rendition of the Chock Full o’Nuts song in radio and television ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/nyregion/page-morton-black-who-sang-heavenly-jingle-dies-at-97.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Black was a cabaret singer known for her sprightly rendition of the Chock Full o’Nuts song in radio and television ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Gothamites of a certain vintage, it was as much a part of life as BUtterfield, ALgonquin and Horn & Hardart — a jaunty little waltz, its lyrics connoting warmth, fiscal security and celestial reward:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/nyregion/BLACK-obit/BLACK-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Page Morton Black, Who Sang Heavenly Jingle, Dies at 97', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Page Morton Black, 97; Sang Heavenly Jingle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Page Morton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Margalit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Chock Full o'Nuts", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T04:28:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4de63935-49fc-5e68-84ea-0aa0a503c700', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4de63935-49fc-5e68-84ea-0aa0a503c700'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (ESPN) NO LIMITS On Oct. 12, 2002, Audrey Mestre, a French free-diver, made a 561-foot plunge off the coast of the Dominican Republic under the watch of her husband, the diver Pipin Ferreras, in an attempt to break the world record of 525 feet set by Tanya Street that August. Although Ms. Mestre, above, had made even deeper dives in preparation, she never resurfaced. She was pronounced dead after Mr. Ferreras retrieved her unconscious body from the water more than eight and a half minutes later. In 2004 he recounted the events in the book “The Dive: A Story of Love and Obsession.” Two years later Carlos Serra, an organizer of Ms. Mestre’s record attempt, published “The Last Attempt,” a rebuttal that blamed Mr. Ferraras for his wife’s death. Alison Ellwood parses the tale in this installment of the “Nine for IX” documentary series.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/42cdd1bc-6ce1-5851-86a6-50ecf8f2b6de', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42cdd1bc-6ce1-5851-86a6-50ecf8f2b6de'}, {'abstract': 'The margins of the Atlantic Ocean west of the Shetland Islands off Scotland are becoming one of Europe’s key fossil-fuel frontier areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/business/energy-environment/chevron-to-spend-770-million-on-remote-projects.html', 'snippet': 'The margins of the Atlantic Ocean west of the Shetland Islands off Scotland are becoming one of Europe’s key fossil-fuel frontier areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABERDEEN, Scotland — Chevron said on Tuesday that it had awarded contracts worth more than £550 million, or more than $844 million, on its planned Rosebank and Alder oil and gas development projects in British waters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chevron to Spend $844 Million on Remote Projects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chevron to Spend $844 Million on Remote Projects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Sea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Statoil ASA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T07:24:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07be2af3-35fe-510e-bfa8-878bd39032f6', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07be2af3-35fe-510e-bfa8-878bd39032f6'}, {'abstract': 'Iron camels, hurtling across the Stans.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/the-new-railway-age/', 'snippet': 'Iron camels, hurtling across the Stans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m surprised that the econoblogosphere hasn’t taken much notice yet of Keith Bradsher’s interesting piece on the revival of the Silk Road — now not consisting of camels carrying Chinese silk, but of huge freight trains carrying Chinese electronics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Railway Age', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T07:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/043102df-643e-5707-b8f6-61e9cd057890', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/043102df-643e-5707-b8f6-61e9cd057890'}, {'abstract': 'No inflation was not a surprise.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/this-time-was-predictable/', 'snippet': 'No inflation was not a surprise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett continues his interesting series on inflation panic, this time focusing on the economists and politicians who keep predicting runaway inflation year after year after year, and never seem to acknowledge having been wrong. I thought his analogy between Shadowstats and the “unskewed” polls predicting a Romney victory was especially apt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Time Was Predictable', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T08:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizatio