anization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8724ef04-8196-500c-b85d-d0f9b537740f', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8724ef04-8196-500c-b85d-d0f9b537740f'}, {'abstract': 'The cash and stock deal, worth an implied $10.7 billion, comes amid signs of accelerating consolidation in Europe’s telecommunications sector.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/telefonica-to-buy-germanys-e-plus-from-kpn/', 'snippet': 'The cash and stock deal, worth an implied $10.7 billion, comes amid signs of accelerating consolidation in Europe’s telecommunications sector.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:10 a.m. | Updated BERLIN – The Spanish telecommunications giant Telefónica agreed on Tuesday to buy Germany’s smallest mobile operator, E-Plus, from its Dutch rival KPN in a cash and stock deal worth an implied 8.1 billion euros, amid signs of accelerating consolidation in Europe’s phone sector.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telefónica to Buy E-Plus of Germany From KPN', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telecom Merger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almunia, Joaquin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koninklijke KPN NV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telefonica SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T08:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': "By Kevin J. O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b005d9ad-f26f-5409-a1cd-c77421a6fe1c', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b005d9ad-f26f-5409-a1cd-c77421a6fe1c'}, {'abstract': 'What would happen if Manhattan had a free market for rental apartments?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/magazine/the-perverse-effects-of-rent-regulation.html', 'snippet': 'What would happen if Manhattan had a free market for rental apartments?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Alejandro Suarez, the change in the East Village is easily visible on the shelves of the bodega where he has worked for seven years. On the corner of East 12th Street and Avenue A, the store used to be at the borderline between the richer people to the West and the poorer people to the East. When Suarez started, he sold lots of beans and rice to the Hispanic people who lived on the block. But Goya products are now crammed on a tiny shelf way in the back, while up front, there’s a huge and growing selection of organic produce, vegetarian sandwiches and high-end energy bars.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28economy/mag-28Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 156, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28economy/mag-28Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 156}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28economy/mag-28Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type