 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e6d555e-4021-5581-8286-cf49b734b9bb', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e6d555e-4021-5581-8286-cf49b734b9bb'}, {'abstract': 'In Kandahar Province, one of the most volatile regions in Afghanistan, locals talk about a different breed of American Special Operations forces who settled in around 2005. They are said to drive civilian vehicles, wear local clothes, speak good Pashto – and yes, sport thick beards.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/tales-of-white-taliban-sketch-a-new-legend/', 'snippet': 'In Kandahar Province, one of the most volatile regions in Afghanistan, locals talk about a different breed of American Special Operations forces who settled in around 2005. They are said to drive civilian vehicles, wear local clothes, speak good P...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Afghanistan is a country built on legends – we trade on the tales we’ve told and retold each other over many generations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tales of ‘White Taliban’ Sketch a New Legend', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T16:38:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Habib Zahori', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Habib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zahori', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46226a9e-413e-5ddc-b467-089203ca1397', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46226a9e-413e-5ddc-b467-089203ca1397'}, {'abstract': 'A fatal stabbing and a robbery spree have rattled the image of Hollywood Boulevard as a tourist haven, presenting an early challenge to Los Angeles’ new mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/us/back-to-back-crimes-threaten-hollywoods-destination-appeal.html', 'snippet': 'A fatal stabbing and a robbery spree have rattled the image of Hollywood Boulevard as a tourist haven, presenting an early challenge to Los Angeles’ new mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Hollywood Boulevard is the West Coast equivalent of Times Square, an urban reclamation project that transformed a strip once notorious for crime, drug-dealing and prostitution into a tourist destination, a thriving night-life district and the home of movie premieres and the Academy Awards.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/us/24HOLLYWOOD-1/24HOLLYWOOD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/us/24HOLLYWOOD-1/24HOLLYWOOD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/us/24HOLLYWOOD-1/24HOLLYWOOD-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/us/24HOLLYWOOD-1/24HOLLYWOOD-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/us/24HOLLYWOOD-1/24HOLLYWOOD-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 