onment, people and history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Last month, at the peak of the standoff between demonstrators and the police over the fate of Gezi Park, the mayor of Istanbul, Kadir Topbas, assured a TV interviewer that the municipal authorities had already learned their lesson. Future urban development would only take place after wide consultation. “We won’t even change a bus stop without asking local people first,” he declared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hanging-by-a-Thread Gardens', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T16:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fc3d91d-9aa7-5210-985b-cd56bd3c7a67', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fc3d91d-9aa7-5210-985b-cd56bd3c7a67'}, {'abstract': 'In the latest incarnation of the hedge fund billionaires’ public spat over the nutritional supplements company Herbalife, one hedge fund manager (briefly) taunts another in a message on the Bloomberg terminal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/hedge-fund-drama-appearing-on-your-screen/', 'snippet': 'In the latest incarnation of the hedge fund billionaires’ public spat over the nutritional supplements company Herbalife, one hedge fund manager (briefly) taunts another in a message on the Bloomberg terminal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a locker room diss between billionaires. But it took place on the computer screens of traders across Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Drama, Appearing on Your Screen', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackman, William A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herbalife Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pershing Square Capital Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Third Point LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T16:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2280a95-8d2b-55b2-ae93-ac7db32e316f', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2280a95-8d2b-55b2-ae93-ac7db32e316f'}, {'abstract': 'Satellite images show that work has stopped on a new launching pad and missile assembly building, a research institute reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/world/asia/north-korea-is-said-to-halt-upgrades-at-rocket-launching-site.html', 'snippet': 'Satellite images show that work has stopped on a new launching pad and missile assembly building, a research institute reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Satellite images show that North Korea has halted work at a complex believed to have been intended to allow it to launch bigger and longer-range rockets, a Washington-based research organization reported on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Said to Stop Construction at Rocket Site', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Said to Stop Construction At Rocket Site', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US-Korea Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T16:55:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9f3f50c-d673-51a8-bfed-4bf3faf0a1fd', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9f3f50c-d673-51a8-bfed-4bf3faf0a1fd'}, {'abstract': 'The biggest issue in interpreting the new health care law appears to involve how a company determines whether employees whose hours fluctuate must be offered insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/the-i-r-s-interprets-the-employer-mandate-and-businesses-have-questions/', 'snippet': 'The biggest issue in interpreting the new health care law appears to involve how a company determines whether employees whose hours fluctuate must be offered insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As written, the employer mandate in the Affordable Care Act — what the law calls “shared responsibility” — is complicated enough. Just to understand how the penalty applies practically requires a flow chart. But as the Internal Revenue Service has tried to interpret the mandate, the agency and the businesses and employees affected by the mandate are discovering that it is even more challenging than it reads. In some cases, the agency has resolved some of the confusion. But in others, the answers it has come up with have raised still more questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The I.R.S. Interprets the Employer Mandate, and Businesses Have Questions', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Families USA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T17:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff9de219-e094-5c84-a5ef-6bfd79be5681', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff9de219-e094-5c84-a5ef-6bfd79be5681'}, {'abstract': 'QE2 Holdings announced plans to convert the Queen Elizabeth 2, one of the world’s most storied ocean liners, into a floating hotel, most likely in Hong Kong or Singapore.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/a-qe2-hotel-may-ply-the-waters/', 'snippet': 'QE2 Holdings announced plans to convert the Queen Elizabeth 2, one of the world’s most storied ocean liners, into a floating hotel, most likely in Hong Kong or Singapore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a nerve-racking few years for admirers of the Queen Elizabeth 2, one of the world’s most storied ocean liners. In 2007, the QE2 was purchased for $100 million by one of Dubai’s state-owned investment companies, which moved it to the Persian Gulf with plans to transform the ship into a floating Jumeirah hotel. Then the financial crisis hit, stalling the project.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A QE2 Hotel May Ply the Waters', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trending: A QE2 Hotel May Ply the Waters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunard Line Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dubai World', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T17:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb8c1ce-a543-55ae-b715-9f070f03532c', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb8c1ce-a543-55ae-b715-9f070f03532c'}, {'abstract': 'The audacity of the assaults on Sunday, in which hundreds of inmates escaped, underscored the deterioration of Iraq’s stability in recent months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/world/middleeast/al-qaeda-asserts-responsibility-for-iraqi-prison-breaks.html', 'snippet': 'The audacity of the assaults on Sunday, in which hundreds of inmates escaped, underscored the deterioration of Iraq’s stability in recent months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The brazen assaults on two prisons in Iraq this week were significant not only for the hundreds of prisoners who were freed but also for what they indicate about the growing capabilities of Al Qaeda’s Iraq affiliate, American officials and experts outside government said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/24iraq_span/24iraq_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/world/24iraq_span/24iraq_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/24iraq_span/24iraq_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/24iraq_span/24iraq_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/24iraq_span/24iraq_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/24/world/24iraq_span/24iraq