nnounced two more cancellations. The conductor and pianist Christoph Eschenbach has bowed out of his Friday evening and Sunday afternoon performances because of an ear infection that has made it impossible for him to travel. And the bass Ferruccio Furlanetto, who was to have sung in the Verdi concert that Mr. Nelsons was to have led, has dropped out of the roster because of a bad cold.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tanglewood Shows to Proceed Without Two Performers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tanglewood Loses Two Performers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tanglewood Music Festival (Lenox, Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eschenbach, Christoph', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Furlanetto, Ferruccio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T17:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/344a6398-55a0-51fd-aefe-004532ab7a26', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/344a6398-55a0-51fd-aefe-004532ab7a26'}, {'abstract': 'Is right-of-center economic populism ultimately a political impossibility?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/republicans-and-the-rich/', 'snippet': 'Is right-of-center economic populism ultimately a political impossibility?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a post questioning the plausibility\xa0of the much-discussed concept of “libertarian populism,” Will Wilkinson raises an eyebrow at the idea that the Republican Pa