ue': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, George T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBANESE, SAL F', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrion, Adolfo Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salgado, Erick J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T18:05:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/05f70e43-5609-5470-ba8f-81b6355c68cc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/05f70e43-5609-5470-ba8f-81b6355c68cc'}, {'abstract': 'More than 250,000 color transparencies and black-and-white negatives of New York artists and galleries taken by D. James Dee will go to the ARTstor archive.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/a-trove-of-new-york-art-images-finds-a-home/', 'snippet': 'More than 250,000 color transparencies and black-and-white negatives of New York artists and galleries taken by D. James Dee will go to the ARTstor archive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'D. James Dee retired this spring after 39 years in business as the SoHo Photographer, with a high reputation for documenting artwork and gallery installations, great stories about the New York art scene in the late 20th century and more than 250,000 color transparencies and black-and-white negatives for which he no longer had any use.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/23/arts/23artsbeat-dee/23artsbeat-dee-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trove of New York Art Images Finds a Home', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dee, D James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T18:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b3fc3a-5378-5b21-8ad2-0a2669a50aaa', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b3fc3a-5378-5b21-8ad2-0a2669a50aaa'}, {'abstract': 'The agency on Monday granted the maker of Plan B One-Step exclusive marketing rights for three years to sell the morning-after pill without a prescription for all ages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/health/fda-grants-exclusivity-to-plan-b-one-step.html', 'snippet': 'The agency on Monday granted the maker of Plan B One-Step exclusive marketing rights for three years to sell the morning-after pill without a prescription for all ages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The manufacturer of the best-known morning-after pill, Plan B One-Step, has been granted exclusive marketing rights for three years by the Food and Drug Administration. The decision means that the drug maker, Teva Pharmaceuticals, is — for now — the only company able to sell the drug over-the-counter and without a prescription for all ages. Manufacturers of generic versions of the pill can apply to the F.D.A. for permission to sell their versions in drugstore aisles, instead of behind a pharmacy counter. Even if the approval is granted they would not be able to sell their products to those under 17 until the three-year exclusivity period for Plan B One-Step ends. Plan B One-Step retails for about $50; generics sell for at least $10 or $15 less. The F.D.A. decision Monday night follows the government’s decision last month to comply with a federal court order to lift age and sale restrictions on Plan B One-Step, which had been available without a prescription only for ages 17 and older. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Grants Exclusivity to Plan B One-Step', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maker of Plan B Pill Wins Exclusivity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plan B (Contraceptive)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belluck, Pam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T18:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e11ed5ad-5a51-5c00-84dd-88569aaa7f65', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e11ed5ad-5a51-5c00-84dd-88569aaa7f65'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrations for the new prince featured elements both traditional and modern, but all with a distinctly British touch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000002352141/a-very-british-proclamation.html', 'snippet': 'Celebrations for the new prince featured elements both traditional and modern, but all with a distinctly British touch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Celebrations for the new prince featured elements both traditional and modern, but all with a distinctly British touch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':