tract': 'No, I won’t read the attached letter.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/how-not-to-be-seen-trivial-and-cranky/', 'snippet': 'No, I won’t read the attached letter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: I should have said that I’m not talking about spammers and scammers; I’m talking about things that sound like legitimate organizations — say, the Central Pacific Small Animal Commission, or the Institut fur Weltschmerz, or whatever — who probably are inviting me to give a lecture or attend a conference or something. But as I said, if they can’t be bothered to give me a hint as opposed to just attaching a pdf, I’m not going to follow up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Not To Be Seen (Trivial and Cranky)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T22:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17629be3-0a5c-5898-8bf5-3743bb7f5de9', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17629be3-0a5c-5898-8bf5-3743bb7f5de9'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Loeb’s exit from Yahoo raises the question of whether he was out to create true value or merely stir the pot.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/yahoos-share-buyback-is-legal-but-timing-is-suspect/', 'snippet': 'Daniel Loeb’s exit from Yahoo raises the question of whether he was out to create true value or merely stir the pot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is Yahoo damaged goods now that it has been abandoned by one of its biggest investors, Daniel Loeb and his hedge fund, Third Point?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'Th