 'Senator John McCain said Tuesday that he was lifting his hold on Gen. Martin E. Dempsey’s nomination for a second term as chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/us/politics/mccain-wont-delay-renomination-for-chairman-of-joint-chiefs.html', 'snippet': 'Senator John McCain said Tuesday that he was lifting his hold on Gen. Martin E. Dempsey’s nomination for a second term as chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator John McCain, who is calling for greater American involvement in the Syrian civil war, said Tuesday that he was lifting his hold on Gen. Martin E. Dempsey’s nomination for a second term as Joint Chiefs of Staff chairman. Mr. McCain, Republican of Arizona, said last week that he would block the nomination after he and the general had a testy exchange over whether the administration was doing enough to assist Syrian rebels. But on Tuesday, according to his spokesman, the senator said the president “has the right to choose the team around him, particularly as far as military advisers are concerned.” The senator criticized a letter from General Dempsey to the Armed Services Committee that listed the pros and cons of intervention in Syria. The general’s assessments “are beyond anything that any rational military thinker that I know would ever contemplate,” Mr. McCain said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McCain Won’t Delay Renomination for Chairman of Joint Chiefs', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mccain Won’t Delay Renomination For Chairman of Joint Chiefs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanker, Thom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-23T23:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc8befc0-b857-5d53-ac07-349c781b457c', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc8befc0-b857-5d53-ac07-349c781b457c'}, {'abstract': 'Home prices in this picturesque area near Long Island Sound are high, but entry-level co-ops are lower than they were five years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/realestate/a-zip-code-by-any-other-name.html', 'snippet': 'Home prices in this picturesque area near Long Island Sound are high, but entry-level co-ops are lower than they were five years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rebecca Salko moved to Larchmont in 1988. Her family’s first house, in the square mile that constitutes the village proper, was a three-bedroom colonial costing $480,000. Several years later, with two children in tow, she and her husband traded up, paying $1 million for a five-bedroom colonial in a part of the village called the Manor, which is known for its elaborate Victorians and other 19th-century homes, and which offers expansive views of the crenulated Long Island Sound. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/28LIVING