Editors Promoted at New York Times', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Editors Promoted At New York Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lacey, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Purdy, Matthew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMSON, JILL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T00:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c7380df-bf09-5d30-8fb8-61cd2941b04b', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c7380df-bf09-5d30-8fb8-61cd2941b04b'}, {'abstract': 'The House passed a bill aimed at amending No Child Left Behind. But no Democrat voted for the bill, and the Obama administration has threatened to veto it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/us/politics/education-overhaul-faces-a-test-of-partisanship.html', 'snippet': 'The House passed a bill aimed at amending No Child Left Behind. But no Democrat voted for the bill, and the Obama administration has threatened to veto it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the day that President George W. Bush signed No Child Left Behind into law in early 2002, he flew to a high school in Hamilton, Ohio, the home district of Representative John A. Boehner, a leading Republican supporter of the bill. Later that afternoon, the president appeared in Boston and praised the bill’s Democratic sponsor in the Senate, Edward M. Kennedy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/0