ecting citizens, but some in an area hit by flooding say getting government help has been slowed by onerous requirements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FISCHBECK, Germany — It has been three weeks since the waters of the Elbe receded from floods that experts are calling the worst natural disaster to hit postwar Germany, and Siegfried Leschien is already laying new floors in the house here where he was born.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flooded German Area Rebuilds, as Government Aid Lags', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flooded German Area Rebuilds, as Government Aid Lags', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T00:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9793a6f7-400f-50f7-8544-383fc9b0390f', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9793a6f7-400f-50f7-8544-383fc9b0390f'}, {'abstract': 'The French Canadian immigration experience shows that our obsession with border security is inconsistent with our history, undermines our economic vitality and is likely to fail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/opinion/bonjour-america.html', 'snippet': 'The French Canadian immigration experience shows that our obsession with border security is inconsistent with our history, undermines our economic vitality and is likely to fail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.C. — WATCHING the free-for-all in Washington over immigration reform, it’s easy to conclude that an airtight border has always been our national goal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/opinion/0724OPEDrollitt/0724OPEDrollitt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonjour, America!', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bonjour, America!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Stephen R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New England States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen R. Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/76e29c80-cebe-59a8-94d6-909054004f5e', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76e29c80-cebe-59a8-94d6-909054004f5e'}, {'abstract': 'Many experts, from architects to automobile executives, predict the ascendancy of the autonomous vehicle within three generations. Is that a good thing?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/23/driving-sideways/', 'snippet': 'Many experts, from architects to automobile executives, predict the ascendancy of the autonomous vehicle within three generations. Is that a good thing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The driverless car, like other utopian pursuits, seems always to be just out of reach. It’s captured the imagination of many for at least a century: in 1918, the Oakland Tribune reported (in a section I wish all newspapers would bring back called “New and Interesting Facts from Science and Life”) that “the new car will be all glass-enclosed and controlled entirely by a set of push buttons. It will have no clutch, gears or transmission, will sit low, have small clearance and punctureless tires.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Driving Sideways', 'kicker': 'Allison Arieff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Arieff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arieff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6931d1d-7cac-54ab-aa88-9ed42b626bdc', 'word_count': 1848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6931d1d-7cac-54ab-aa88-9ed42b626bdc'}, {'abstract': 'A cautionary tale for an activist prime minister still basking in victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/opinion/the-limits-on-nationalism-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'A cautionary tale for an activist prime minister still basking in victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANOVER, N.H. — THE landslide victory of Prime Minister Shinzo Abe’s Liberal Democratic Party in elections Sunday for the upper house of Japan’s Parliament immediately raised a question: Will it embolden Mr. Abe toward increasing nationalism that might further alienate Japan from some of its neighbors? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Limits on Nationalism in Japan', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Limits on Nationalism in Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lind, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:03:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Lind', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lind', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f38dc3f0-53a4-53e2-95b1-7c6c216d2778', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f38dc3f0-53a4-53e2-95b1-7c6c216d2778'}, {'abstract': 'The appeals for urgency appear to reflect the extent to which Prime Minister Shinzo Abe and his party now see themselves as under pressure to deliver on campaign promises.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/world/asia/japanese-premier-urges-speedy-action-to-further-aid-economy.html', 'snippet': 'The appeals for urgency appear to reflect the extent to which Prime Minister Shinzo Abe and his party now see themselves as under pressure to deliver on campaign promises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — In his first cabinet meeting since his party’s sweeping election victory over the weekend, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe on Tuesday warned his ministers against triumphalism, instructing them instead to take speedy action to strengthen the recovering economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Leader Urges Swift Action to Strengthen Economic Recovery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan’s Leader Urges Swift Action to Strengthen Economic Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberal Democratic Party (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8bd20d8-5861-5359-8b5c-fe030e514224', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8bd20d8-5861-5359-8b5c-fe030e514224'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government should not be making money off the backs of student borrowers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/opinion/the-student-loan-debacle.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government should not be making money off the backs of student borrowers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Elizabeth Warren, a Democrat of Massachusetts, spoke up for poor and middle-class Americans last week when she excoriated the federal government for making money on the student loan program. She also criticized Republicans for killing bills earlier this month that would have prevented interest rates on subsidized student loans from doubling. Rates on those loans have jumped from 3.4 percent to 6.8 percent, further burdening one-third of all college students who use them to pay for an education. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Student Loan Debacle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Student Loan Debacle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a686c87b-893e-51ef-b128-97be1f9fc309', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a686c87b-893e-51ef-b128-97be1f9fc309'}, {'abstract': 'With Michael Weiner, the union president, battling brain cancer, Tony Clark, who played in the majors for 15 seasons, was appointed deputy executive director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/sports/baseball/union-names-former-player-as-top-assistant.html', 'snippet': 'With Michael Weiner, the union president, battling brain cancer, Tony Clark, who played in the majors for 15 seasons, was appointed deputy executive director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major League Baseball’s players union Tuesday named Tony Clark, who played in the major leagues for 15 seasons, as its new second-in-command.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Union Names Former Player as Deputy to Ailing Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Union Names Former Player\r\nAs Deputy to Ailing Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball Players Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Michael S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:05:40+0000', 'doc