{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACA  Financial Guaranty Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paulson & Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a62f9f68-8576-5b8a-9c6b-7a43eaf614f0', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a62f9f68-8576-5b8a-9c6b-7a43eaf614f0'}, {'abstract': 'The cuts that are part of the mandatory sequestration are bringing misery to the reservations, but Congress offers no response.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/opinion/abandoned-in-indian-country.html', 'snippet': 'The cuts that are part of the mandatory sequestration are bringing misery to the reservations, but Congress offers no response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s an old American story: malign policies hatched in Washington leading to pain and death in Indian country. It was true in the 19th century. It is true now, at a time when Congress, heedless of its solemn treaty obligations to Indian tribes, is allowing the across-the-board budget cuts known as the sequester to threaten the health, safety and education of Indians across the nation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abandoned in Indian Country', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abandoned in Indian Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pine Ridge Indian Reservation (SD)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:08:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2ecb808-3cfa-5411-ba59-2660fa11d233', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2ecb808-3cfa-5411-ba59-2660fa11d233'}, {'abstract': 'Four years ago, a junior employee in Assemblyman Micah Z. Kellner’s office complained to her supervisor that she was being harassed, but her complaint never made it past Bill Collins, who ran the Assembly’s legal staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/nyregion/assembly-speaker-removing-lawyer-citing-ignored-claims-of-sexual-harassment.html', 'snippet': 'Four years ago, a junior employee in Assemblyman Micah Z. Kellner’s office complained to her supervisor that she was being harassed, but her complaint never made it past Bill Collins, who ran the Assembly’s legal staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Assembly Speaker Sheldon Silver’s office said Tuesday that a top Assembly lawyer would step down amid revelations that the Assembly staff failed to investigate sexual harassment claims involving another Assembly Democrat. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '