: {'original': 'By James Risen and Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Risen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7420b32-84c1-5524-a85e-bfb890e45b32', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7420b32-84c1-5524-a85e-bfb890e45b32'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony Weiner’s sexting scandal hasn’t gone away. He should take himself out of the mayoral race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/opinion/mr-weiner-and-the-elusive-truth.html', 'snippet': 'Anthony Weiner’s sexting scandal hasn’t gone away. He should take himself out of the mayoral race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At some point, the full story of Anthony Weiner and his sexual relationships and texting habits will finally be told. In the meantime, the serially evasive Mr. Weiner should take his marital troubles and personal compulsions out of the public eye, away from cameras, off the Web and out of the race for mayor of New York City.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Weiner and the Elusive Truth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Weiner and the Elusive Truth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f474b736-1f5b-5cda-9246-ff146da840fb', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f474b736-1f5b-5cda-9246-ff146da840fb'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, setting up possible override votes, rejected bills that he called “dangerous and irresponsible.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/nyregion/bloomberg-vetoes-measures-for-police-monitor-and-lawsuits.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, setting up possible override votes, rejected bills that he called “dangerous and irresponsible.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Setting up a final act in his prolonged confrontation with the New York City Council over stop-and-frisk practices, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Tuesday vetoed two contentious bills to increase oversight of the Police Department and expand the ability of New Yorkers to sue over police profiling of suspects.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Vetoes Measures for Police Monitor and Lawsuits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg Vetoes Measures for Police Monitor and Lawsuits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T01:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3e0b55f-947b-5c04-bd75-57382a620ae4', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3e0b55f-947b-5c04-bd75-57382a620ae4'}, {'abstract': 'Croatian officials long lobbied to get into the European Union, but some Croatians worry that the country is not ready.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/world/europe/as-croatia-struggles-some-wonder-if-it-won-entry-to-european-union-too-soon.html', 'snippet': 'Croatian officials long lobbied to get into the European Union, but some Croatians worry that the country is not ready.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZAGREB, Croatia — With a consignment of goods stuck at customs, Jadranka Boban Pejic, who runs an organic food company, soon found out that she needed to grease the wheels of Croatia’s creaky bureaucracy. So, she said, she reluctantly agreed to a little side deal to speed things up: about 130 euros worth of groceries for the customs officer’s wife.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/CROATIA/CROATIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/world/CROATIA/CROATIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/CROATIA/CROATIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/CROATIA/CROATIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop