', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e04f45ad-6a9a-5c2a-a800-1eb897ac1577', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e04f45ad-6a9a-5c2a-a800-1eb897ac1577'}, {'abstract': 'Former Maoists rebels join electoral politics in West Bengal’s Panchayat elections.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/amid-violence-hamlet-joins-electoral-politics-in-bengal/', 'snippet': 'Former Maoists rebels join electoral politics in West Bengal’s Panchayat elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hamlet Mandi, 27, a farmer from Kanko village in the abysmally poor West Midnapore district in the eastern state of West Bengal, was consumed by the neglect and the poverty engulfing the people of his region. A Maoist insurgency was gaining strength in the area and attracting many of India’s disenfranchised rural poor. Mr. Mandi was torn between suffering the slings and arrows of outrageous fortune and taking up arms against a sea of troubles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/world/asia/24-maoist-WB-IndiaInk/24-maoist-WB-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/world/asia/24-maoist-WB-IndiaInk/24-maoist-WB-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'x