-3332129ae531'}, {'abstract': 'Erin Luhmann, who has returned from her win-a-trip journey with Nick Kristof, writes up a list of international reporting hacks that she learned in the field.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/a-reporting-toolkit-from-win-a-trip/', 'snippet': 'Erin Luhmann, who has returned from her win-a-trip journey with Nick Kristof, writes up a list of international reporting hacks that she learned in the field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Erin Luhmann, who has returned from her win-a-trip journey with Nick Kristof, writes up a list of international reporting hacks she learned in the field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reporting Toolkit from Win-A-Trip', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T14:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erin Luhmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luhmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd48e600-619f-5026-8160-8ac24d26288f', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd48e600-619f-5026-8160-8ac24d26288f'}, {'abstract': 'I’m returning to the prison in Myanmar where I was detained as a political prisoner 15 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/back-to-a-burma-jail/', 'snippet': 'I’m returning to the prison in Myanmar where I was detained as a political prisoner 15 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANGON, Myanmar — Today I go back to Insein Prison, where I was detained in the late 1990s and where throughout the decades of military rule in Myanmar, most political opponents were interrogated, tried and held.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back to Jail in Burma', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solitary Confinement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T14:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Swe Win', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Swe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Win', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fb9ce4f-89c9-555f-ac5f-2546c41add49', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fb9ce4f-89c9-555f-ac5f-2546c41add49'}, {'abstract': 'Children engage with animals and the outdoors in two very different new picture books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/books/wait-wait-and-a-year-around-the-great-oak.html', 'snippet': 'Children engage with animals and the outdoors in two very different new picture books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of summer’s great gifts is the chance to adapt ourselves to nature; to slow down in the heat, to swim when the tide comes in, and to find our place, at least briefly, in the wild. In “Wait! Wait!” and “A Year Around the Great Oak,” two beautifully illustrated but very different books, children engage with animals and the outdoors in ways that are unpredictable, stimulating and ultimately confidence-inducing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/books/24childrens-span/24childrens-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'w