e', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8a1b13d-770b-5950-b857-bc9607dcef4a', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8a1b13d-770b-5950-b857-bc9607dcef4a'}, {'abstract': 'Owners take plenty of risk with their businesses. Should they be more conservative with their investments?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/do-business-owners-make-poor-investors/', 'snippet': 'Owners take plenty of risk with their businesses. Should they be more conservative with their investments?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a small-business guide to saving for retirement that we have just published, R.J. Lewis talks about leaving a corporate job to start his own business in 1999. The founder of eHealthcare Solutions, an online advertising network that is based in Ewing, N.J., and represents health care Web sites, Mr. Lewis depleted his 401(k) to start the business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Business Owners Make Poor Investors?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T16:13:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e626ca7f-19f7-555e-be15-3e2107e7535b', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e626ca7f-19f7-555e-be15-3e2107e7535b'}, {'abstract': 'A planned $175 million public offering of SFX Entertainment seeks to take advantage of the popularity of electronic dance music, but the numbers behind the scenes should give investors pause.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/a-dance-music-i-p-o-thats-a-little-off-key/', 'snippet': 'A planned $175 million public offering of SFX Entertainment seeks to take advantage of the popularity of electronic dance music, but the numbers behind the scenes should give investors pause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert F.X. Sillerman wants to throw Wall Street’s biggest dance party. The entrepreneur who rolled up the rock concert business is trying to do the same for electronic dance music with a planned $175 million public offering of SFX Entertainment. Though Mr. Sillerman’s track record is good and he is focusing on a hot slice of the music industry, this bash promises to be more fun for partygoers than investors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dance Music I.P.O. That’s a Little Off Key', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T16:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db7dcbc3-89bc-52b5-b979-ac3fc2eecad5', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db7dcbc3-89bc-52b5-b979-ac3fc2eecad5'}, {'abstract': 'The new musical is about five passengers stranded in an existential limbo.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/new-york-musical-theater-festival-report-standby/', '