s.com/2013/07/24/been-there-done-that-monetary-and-fiscal-policy-edition/', 'snippet': 'What we should have known since 1998.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noah Smith has a nice takedown of Martin Feldstein’s latest, which is the claim that the reason a vast expansion of the Fed’s balance sheet has produced no inflationary effect at all is the 0.25 percent — that’s right, 0.25 percent — rate of interest the Fed is paying on excess reserves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Been There, Done That: Monetary and Fiscal Policy Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T17:21:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e708e7d-c780-5add-91bc-1eff0df04284', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e708e7d-c780-5add-91bc-1eff0df04284'}, {'abstract': 'The collision, which is still under investigation, led to a multivehicle pileup and snarled traffic for hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/nyregion/wrong-way-crash-on-tappan-zee-leaves-1-dead-and-4-injured.html', 'snippet': 'The collision, which is still under investigation, led to a multivehicle pileup and snarled traffic for hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One person was killed and four others were seriously injured when an S.U.V. being driven the wrong way on the Tappan Zee Bridge crashed head-on into another vehicle, setting off a pileup and snarling traffic for hours, the police said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong-Way Crash on Tappan Zee Bridge Kills One', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Killed in Wrong-Way Crash on Tappan Zee Bridge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tappan Zee Bridge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockland County (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T17:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae05ed68-ac3c-5b02-b4d4-603fd6246bde', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae05ed68-ac3c-5b02-b4d4-603fd6246bde'}, {'abstract': 'On his birth Monday, the infant George Alexander Louis became third in line to the British throne, after his grandfather Prince Charles and his father, William.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/world/europe/and-the-name-isgeorge-alexander-louis.html', 'snippet': 'On his birth Monday, the infant George Alexander Louis became third in line to the British throne, after his grandfather Prince Charles and his father, William.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — With a haste unusual in the royal family’s handling of such matters, Prince William and his wife, the former Kate Middleton, announced Wednesday that they had named their 2-day-old son George Alexander Louis — thus setting him on a course, assuming he ascends the throne, to one day become King George VII.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images