hip.html', 'snippet': 'Carolyn Lynch, Mike Passell, Roger Bates, Garey Hayden, Marc Jacobus and Eddie Wold won the concluding 90-board match of the nine-day senior trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carolyn Lynch, Mike Passell, Roger Bates, Garey Hayden, Marc Jacobus and Eddie Wold won the concluding 90-board match of the nine-day senior trial last Friday and Saturday in Orlando, Fla. They thus became the USA-2 team in the d’Orsi Senior Trophy world championship in Bali, Indonesia, in September.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Team at Senior Trial Advances to World Championship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning Team at Senior Trial Advances to World Championship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T21:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/951faadb-fa35-571c-9201-424522151e61', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/951faadb-fa35-571c-9201-424522151e61'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for important and peculiar items. Wednesday’s selections include Google’s new streaming device, Chromecast, and a 97-year-old man who uses an 18-year-old version of Windows to create art.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/todays-scuttlebot-chromecast-and-painting-with-windows-95/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for important and peculiar items. Wednesday’s selections include Google’s new streaming device, Chromecast, and a 97-year-old man who uses an 18-year-old version of Windows to create art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Chromecast and Painting With Windows ’95', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T21:23:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0296f60-8a4b-5a6c-ba9c-201d36c85070', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0296f60-8a4b-5a6c-ba9c-201d36c85070'}, {'abstract': 'The musical “Storyville” is set in a saloon near the French Quarter in New Orleans in 1917.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/theater/reviews/storyville-is-revived-at-the-york-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The musical “Storyville” is set in a saloon near the French Quarter in New Orleans in 1917.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ed Bullins and Mildred Kayden musical “Storyville” may begin with a funeral procession, but in this revival at the York Theater, the mood is not mournful. Though Countess Willy Danger (the Broadway veteran Ernestine Jackson), a hostess and spirit guide of sorts for the audience in top hat and tails, looks back wistfully to events in New Orleans in 1917, this production, directed by Bill Castellino, is tirelessly exuberant.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/storyville/storyville-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/storyville/storyville-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/storyville/storyville-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/arts/storyville/storyville-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1180, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':