/rodriguez-angers-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'A challenge by Alex Rodriguez to the team physician over his diagnosis of an injury has infuriated the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — No one is exactly sure what will become of Alex Rodriguez in the next few days, months and years, but in the interim he continues to anger and mystify the Yankees for what they see as his ham-handed challenges to the team’s medical evaluations.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1506, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/sports/baseball/25yankees/25yankees-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodriguez and Yankees Clash Again Over His Status', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rodriguez and Yankees Clash Again Over His Status', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T21:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2607ea94-bfff-5762-858d-0561d134944b', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2607ea94-bfff-5762-858d-0561d134944b'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama tries to get the country to focus on the economic issues that really matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/opinion/the-middle-class-at-center-stage.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama tries to get the country to focus on the economic issues that really matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington is a city of sideshows, full of people who consider it their job to create distractions from the nation’s most serious problems. Politicians would rather argue about nonexistent scandals or plot to undermine each other’s programs than come up with ways to create jobs or elevate the hopes of the next generation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Middle Class at Center Stage', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Middle Class at Center Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T21:26:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/66daeca3-a977-577b-a59e-0ecf30f70445', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66daeca3-a977-577b-a59e-0ecf30f70445'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibition surveys a century of unrealized building projects and urban planning schemes for the city. Here are five of the most amazing.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/24/on-view-los-angeles-architecture-as-it-might-have-been/', 'snippet': 'A new exhibition surveys a century of unrealized building projects and urban planning schemes for the city. Here are five of the most amazing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Los Angeles is known as a place where anything is possible. But “Never Built: Los Angeles,” an exhibition that opens Sunday at the A+D Museum, reveals that for all the architectural gems built in the city, there were plenty of innovative projects — buildings, master plans, transportation schemes and more — that didn’t make it past the drawing board. Using renderings, blueprints, models and drawings (many of which will also appear in a companion book from Metropolis, out July 31) the show’s curators, Sam Lubell and Greg Goldin, paint a vivid picture of what might have been. Here, the five projects I most wish had been built.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Los Angeles Architecture, As It Might Have Been', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View: If Only...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koolhaas, Rem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nouvel, Jean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zumthor, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-24T21:27:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15037341-e6f7-539b-95f6-1266fc7e13eb', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15037341-e6f7-539b-95f6-1266fc7e13eb'}, {'abstract': 'The president spoke about the country’s economic progress and his vision for the rest of his presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000002354557/obama-speaks-in-illinois.html', 'snippet': 'The president spoke about the country’s economic progress and his vision for the rest of his presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president spoke about the country’s economic progress and his vision for the rest of his presidency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/us/politics/video-obama-illinois/video-obama-illinois-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/us/