rge-for-citys-aging-immigrant-population-study-says.html', 'snippet': 'Besides being one of the fastest-growing demographic groups, older immigrants are also one of the most vulnerable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After retiring from his job as a security guard in 2011, Wahid Ali spent his days struggling against tedium. Speaking only limited English and with few friends, he had little to do and mainly stayed at home, a small rented room in an illegal basement apartment in Coney Island.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/Elder-1/Elder-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigrant Struggles Compounded by Old Age', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Immigrant Struggles Compounded By Old Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Semple, Kirk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for an Urban Future', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T04:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dea2982-dbfe-5110-a2d7-d11212e7fa1d', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dea2982-dbfe-5110-a2d7-d11212e7fa1d'}, {'abstract': 'The network and cable company announced late Wednesday that they had agreed to an extension of their current contract, as they continue to wrangle over fees for CBS programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/business/media/cbs-and-time-warner-cable-call-a-timeout-in-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'The network and cable company announced late Wednesday that they had agreed to an extension of their current contract, as they continue to wrangle over fees for CBS programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two sides in the confrontation between CBS and Time Warner Cable called for a timeout Wednesday night, hours before a deadline that might have removed CBS programs from the cable lineup in cities including New York and Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS and Time Warner Cable Call a Timeout in Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T04:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e58b3133-ec0c-5a0b-bc30-e8a5216f6d9c', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e58b3133-ec0c-5a0b-bc30-e8a5216f6d9c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (WE) SANYA’S GLAM & GOLD Sanya Richards-Ross, a four-time Olympic track-and-field gold medalist, opens the door on her marriage to Aaron Ross (above with Ms. Richards-Ross), a New York Giants cornerback, and on the salon she and her sister, Shari, founded in Austin, Tex., in this new reality show. Ms. Richards-Ross credits her success in part to “Team S.R.R.,” which includes Archie, her father and manager; Sharon, her mother and agent; and Yolande, her cousin, publicist and stylist. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed4d055f-2af8-5b7e-9f2b-cea4f8ee7783', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed4d055f-2af8-5b7e-9f2b-cea4f8ee7783'}, {'abstract': 'The driver of a high-speed passenger train involved in one of Europe’s worst rail accidents in recent years had openly relished the idea of racing past the authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/world/europe/train-derails-in-spain.html', 'snippet': 'The driver of a high-speed passenger train involved in one of Europe’s worst rail accidents in recent years had openly relished the idea of racing past the authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTIAGO DE COMPOSTELA, Spain — The train driver did little to hide his taste for speed. He posted a photograph of a locomotive speedometer needle stuck at 200 kilometers, or about 125 miles, per hour on Facebook last year, boasting that the reading “has not been tampered with” and openly relishing the idea of racing past the authorities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spanish Train Inquiry Focuses on Driver With a Taste for Speed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spanish Train Inquiry Focuses on Driver With a Taste for Speed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garzon Amo, Francisco Jose', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Renfe Operadora', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T05:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Silvia Taulés and Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Silvia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taulés', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2ca32e7-e0a0-5e6e-9b0c-4d7a60f4d529', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2ca32e7-e0a0-5e6e-9b0c-4d7a60f4d529'}, {'abstract': 'Questions remain about whether Julian Assange can take office if he wins the election, given that he is holed up in Ecuador’s embassy in London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/world/asia/wikileaks-founder-assange-to-run-for-australian-senate.html', 'snippet': 'Questions remain about whether Julian Assange can take office if he wins the election, given that he is holed up in Ecuador’s embassy in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — Julian Assange, the founder of WikiLeaks, formally inaugurated a new political party bearing the name of his antisecrecy organization on Thursday and declared his own unorthodox candidacy for a seat in the Australian Senate in national elections to be held later this year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/world/26australia_inline/26australia_inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge'