k death penalty sentence, and several free concerts tonight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you remember a week ago? When it was 99 degrees in Central Park?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/nyregion/25nytoday-2/25nytoday-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: What Heat Wave?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T10:02:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40625d0e-3952-5cad-b207-2553838c4337', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40625d0e-3952-5cad-b207-2553838c4337'}, {'abstract': 'An indictment against SAC Capital Advisors is expected as soon as Thursday. | The government appears to be trying to put SAC out of business. | The founder of Dell is seeking a surer path to victory for his takeover effort. | The S.E.C. finally got its chance to attack the credibility of Fabrice P. Tourre, a former Goldman Sachs trader.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/morning-agenda-show-of-force-against-sac/', 'snippet': 'An indictment against SAC Capital Advisors is expected as soon as Thursday. | The government appears to be trying to put SAC out of business. | The founder of Dell is seeking a surer path to victory for his takeover effort. | The S.E.C. finally go...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A grand jury voted this week to approve an indictment against SAC Capital Advisors, the hedge fund owned by Steven A. Cohen, and authorities were expected to announce the case as soon as Thursday, DealBook’s Ben Protess and Peter Lattman report. The action caps a lengthy insider-trading investigation of SAC that intensified in recent months. Criminal charges might devastate SAC if the banks that trade with it and finance its operations abandon the hedge fund.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tough Stance on SAC', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T11:39:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c10ae861-c7d8-5d15-a8cf-c318cdc78fae', 'word_count': 1758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c10ae861-c7d8-5d15-a8cf-c318cdc78fae'}, {'abstract': 'A summer program at the University of Chicago is intended to let aspiring young data scientists apply their skills to urban and social problems. The program is led by Rayid Ghani, who was chief scientist in the Obama re-election campaign. He hopes the program will show young data experts the challenge and opportunity to do “things that really matter” for nonprofits, civic groups and local governments.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/a-summer-of-data-hacking-social-problems/', 'snippet': 'A summer program at the University of Chicago is intended to let aspiring young data scientists apply their skills to urban and social problems. The program is led by Rayid Ghani, who was chief scientist in the Obama re-election campaign. He hopes...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The idea, Rayid Ghani recalled, grew out of his experience speaking to computer science students at elite schools like Carnegie Mellon, Stanford and the University of Chicago. President Obama had just won his re-election bid last fall. And Mr. Ghani, chief scientist for the campaign, was on a kind of explanatory victory tour, describing how cutting-edge data analysis and computing tools gave its side an edge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/technology/24bits-ghani/24bits-ghani-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/technology/24bits-ghani/24bits-ghani-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight':