rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bef96850-b9f2-53ba-91ab-1cd60a0a6f31', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bef96850-b9f2-53ba-91ab-1cd60a0a6f31'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s youth may have been raised to respect their elders, but they have wearied of bowing to officials who ignore or exploit their needs.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/egyptians-quarter-life-crisis/', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s youth may have been raised to respect their elders, but they have wearied of bowing to officials who ignore or exploit their needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — There’s an army of young men beneath my balcony, flanking the street in tight formation. Their battle stations are rows of clothes racks. Their war cries are about prices: “Fifteen pounds for T-shirts!” “Best cotton underwear!” “Three for 18 pounds!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptians’ Quarter-life Crisis', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T11:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Golia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Golia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a25dddfe-60ad-5f41-8af0-88b1ef2b551c', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a25dddfe-60ad-5f41-8af0-88b1ef2b551c'}, {'abstract': 'Trent Reznor’s band will tour for the first time since 2009, in support of its new album “Hesitation Marks,” with a radically different sound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/arts/music/nine-inch-nails-is-back-onstage-with-a-vengeance.html', 'snippet': 'Trent Reznor’s band will tour for the first time since 2009, in support of its new album “Hesitation Marks,” with a radically different sound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Trent Reznor was not happy. Sitting ramrod straight, dressed in a black T-shirt and black shorts, he was staring with grim concentration as his band, Nine Inch Nails, worked through their set in a full-scale production rehearsal at the Los Angeles Sports Arena. Smoke, strobe lights and video screens on wheels restlessly reconfigured themselves as the band performed, without Mr. Reznor’s lead vocals and instruments. Through song after song, his glare and scowl barely wavered; he’d look away only to tap notes into his laptop. After the band ran through the full set, he convened the musicians and technicians in a back room, well away from a visiting journalist.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/arts/28NINE1_SPAN/28NINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/28/arts/28NINE1_SPAN/28NINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/arts/28NINE1_SPAN/28NINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/arts/28NINE1_SPAN/28NINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}