ars in economic costs would attend a burst of methane emissions from the warming Arctic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arctic Methane Credibility Bomb', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T16:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7f0c346-318f-5cc1-b5c7-cf064c18d35e', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7f0c346-318f-5cc1-b5c7-cf064c18d35e'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Rachel Mason taps into the creative potential of the controversial legislative tactic.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/after-hours-the-filibuster-as-performed-by-a-scary-clown/', 'snippet': 'The artist Rachel Mason taps into the creative potential of the controversial legislative tactic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a performance-art aspect to the strange parliamentary procedure known as the filibuster. As anyone who watched the recent, much publicized filibusters of Senator Rand Paul and the Texas State Senator Wendy Davis knows, viewers eventually lose track of the speaker’s topic, drawn in instead by his cadences, mannerisms and tics. (For the record, Paul’s filibuster was against the theoretical use of drones on American citizens inside the United States; Davis’s against her state’s attempt to ban all abortions after 20 weeks from conception.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | The Filibuster, As Performed by a Scary Clown', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T16:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c8ffa63-6d4f-5cff-919c-bc1f842645a7', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c8ffa63-6d4f-5cff-919c-bc1f842645a7'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan areas with large African-American populations tend to have lower rates of upward mobility. But lower-income whites in those regions also face longer odds of moving up economically.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/the-complex-story-of-race-and-upward-mobility/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan areas with large African-American populations tend to have lower rates of upward mobility. But lower-income whites in those regions also face longer odds of moving up economically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 7:35 p.m. | ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Complex Story of Race and Upward Mobility', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T16:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2929692-112e-5c15-a8fd-3755a4932f1e', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2929692-112e-5c15-a8fd-3755a4932f1e'}, {'abstract': 'The Revolution growth fund, started by Stephen M. Case and two former AOL colleagues, has invested in Bigcommerce, a start-up whose software helps companies create and manage online stores.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/revolution-fund-invests-40-million-in-e-commerce-start-up/', 'snippet': 'The Revolution growth fund, started by Stephen M. Case and two former AOL colleagues, has invested in Bigcommerce, a start-up whose software helps companies create and manage online stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen M. Case, the co-founder of AOL, sees a future in helping companies sell goods online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revolution Fund Invests $40 Million in E-Commerce Start-Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Case, Stephen M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolution LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T16:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52dfa27a-a6d1-5696-927b-0ae3dc318f6c', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52dfa27a-a6d1-5696-927b-0ae3dc318f6c'}, {'abstract': 'Cate Blanchett plays a wealthy woman who has lost her money and her bearings in “Blue Jasmine,” directed by Woody Allen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/movies/cate-blanchett-stars-in-woody-allens-blue-jasmine.html', 'snippet': 'Cate Blanchett plays a wealthy woman who has lost her money and her bearings in “Blue Jasmine,” directed by Woody Allen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Cate Blanchett first cruises into Woody Allen’s “Blue Jasmine,” playing a Park Avenue matron fallen on hard times, she looks like a million bucks. She’s wearing pearls and a white Chanel jacket, with an Hermès bag as big as a Shetland pony hanging off one arm. It’s the sort of important accessory worn by women accustomed to being chauffeured around town. Soon after, though, as she stands with her monogrammed luggage on a nondescript San Francisco sidewalk, she looks frightened, alone — like someone who could benefit from some kindness. Instead, she waves off a stranger and, posing a question that’s as existential as it is practical, demands, “Where am I, exactly?” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/arts/26BLUE_SPAN/26BLUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/26/arts/26BLUE_SPAN/26BLUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/arts/26BLUE_SPAN/26BLUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, '