 None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd56ac7-7995-5caf-8b3c-9007df947922', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd56ac7-7995-5caf-8b3c-9007df947922'}, {'abstract': 'The strange life of Jeremiah G. Hamilton, one of New York City’s first black tycoons.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/gothams-only-black-millionaire/', 'snippet': 'The strange life of Jeremiah G. Hamilton, one of New York City’s first black tycoons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing to Frederick Douglass in 1852, the black intellectual James McCune Smith noted Jeremiah G. Hamilton as “the only black millionaire in New York,” disparaging him for the crassness of his pursuit of wealth. But despite Hamilton’s prominence in his own lifetime, modern American historians have ignored him. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gotham’s Only Black Millionaire', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T17:15:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shane White', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'White', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/389dfd80-1a18-5fc4-8a04-658900f84a96', 'word_count': 2045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/389dfd80-1a18-5fc4-8a04-658900f84a96'}, {'abstract': 'The satellite-radio company reported $940 million in revenue for the quarter, and an increase of 716,000 in subscribers to 25.1 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/business/media/sirius-xm-reports-record-revenue-aided-by-auto-recovery.html', 'snippet': 'The satellite-radio company reported $940 million in revenue for the quarter, and an increase of 716,000 in subscribers to 25.1 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, Wall Street was closely focused on Netflix’s second-quarter results of 28.6 million subscribers and revenue of roughly $1 billion. On Thursday, another fast-growing subscription media company was in the spotlight: Sirius XM Radio reported $940 million in revenue for the quarter, a record for the company and more than most analysts had expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sirius XM Reports Record Revenue, Aided by Auto Recovery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sirius XM Radio Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberty Media Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, James E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T17:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d57804b9-45e2-5173-8f15-a06dee5aa946', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d57804b9-45e2-5173-8f15-a06dee5aa946'}, {'abstract': 'Taking inspiration from a number of cancer poets, Susan Gubar pieced together a quilt of poetry to convey the feeling of chaos so common among people with cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/living-with-cancer-a-quilt-of-poetry/', 'snippet': 'Taking inspiration from a number of cancer poets, Susan Gubar pieced together a quilt of poetry to convey the feeling of chaos so common among people with cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her book “My Poets,” Maureen McLane reminded me of a poetic form called the cento. It consists of snippets of verse composed by other writers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/health/25well_quilt/25well_quilt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/25/health/25well_quilt/25well_quilt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/health/25well_quilt/25well_quilt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/health/25well_quilt/25well_quilt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/health/25well_quilt/25well_quilt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/25/health/25well_quilt/25well_quilt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credi