M.&A. Tables Don’t Give Full Score', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lazard LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T19:52:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3ae0d85-40de-5c30-b788-e366f6483928', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3ae0d85-40de-5c30-b788-e366f6483928'}, {'abstract': 'SAC has almost no defense against the government’s charges, so the issue of punishment may be the real fight in the case.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/whats-next-in-the-case-against-sac/', 'snippet': 'SAC has almost no defense against the government’s charges, so the issue of punishment may be the real fight in the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The indictment of SAC Capital Advisors and three of its internal hedge fund companies on Thursday signals an important shift by the government away from its longstanding fear of charging an organization with a crime. The charges accuse the firms and, at least indirectly, their owner, Steven A. Cohen, of fostering a corporate culture that encouraged analysts and traders to use illegitimate means that resulted in “systematic insider trading.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Next in the Case Against SAC', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T19:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e718d66b-f721-5596-a2dd-2164fae90ab2', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e718d66b-f721-5596-a2dd-2164fae90ab2'}, {'abstract': 'Since Hippocrates, physicians have embraced the ideal of caring for all patients, regardless of who they might be. But what does the doctor do when the patient discriminates?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/when-the-patient-is-racist/', 'snippet': 'Since Hippocrates, physicians have embraced the ideal of caring for all patients, regardless of who they might be. But what does the doctor do when the patient discriminates?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After too many drinks, the motorcycle enthusiast in his 30s had driven off the side of the road. As one of the doctors-in-training covering trauma that night, I was responsible for his initial physical exam; but it wasn’t going to be easy. He was enormous, his feet hung over the flimsy emergency room gurney and his neck bulged out of the stiff cervical collar. Moreover, he was what the older nurses called a “mean drunk,” so it was with more than a little apprehension that I began palpating and poking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/health/26well_chen/26well_chen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Patient Is Racist', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T19:56:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eac7f2e-a462-5e9e-be20-2dad3e495fba', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eac7f2e-a462-5e9e-be20-2dad3e495fba'}, {'abstract': 'The legislation, which aims to resolve Bedouin landownership claims, could lead to the demolition of villages in the Negev desert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/world/middleeast/un-official-asks-israel-to-reconsider-bill-on-bedouins.html', 'snippet': 'The legislation, which aims to resolve Bedouin landownership claims, could lead to the demolition of villages in the Negev desert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United Nations human rights chief, Navi Pillay, urged Israel to reconsider legislation that could lead to the demolition of Bedouin villages in the Negev desert, asserting that Israel was actively pursuing discriminatory policies by forcibly displacing its Arab citizens.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Land Measure Called Discriminatory', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israeli Land Measure Called Discriminatory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nomadic People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pillay, Navi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T19:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo