t': 'In an effort to strengthen its global ties, the Metropolitan Museum of Art has organized what it is calling the “Global Museum Leaders Colloquium,” a two-week pilot program scheduled for April.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/met-to-host-conference-of-museum-directors/', 'snippet': 'In an effort to strengthen its global ties, the Metropolitan Museum of Art has organized what it is calling the “Global Museum Leaders Colloquium,” a two-week pilot program scheduled for April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike the Louvre or the Guggenheim, the Metropolitan Museum of Art has no plans to build an outpost in the Middle East. Yet its global reach can be glimpsed not only through its vast collections and traveling exhibitions but also in the many projects it finances around the world, including excavations in the Middle East and conservation initiatives with countries like India. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Met to Host Conference of Museum Directors', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T20:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a611ce85-3178-5ce8-aca1-acc77ae0f2b3', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a611ce85-3178-5ce8-aca1-acc77ae0f2b3'}, {'abstract': 'One of the summer’s better gallery group shows is this presentation of some two dozen works in various mediums by 17 artists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/arts/design/mind-is-outer-space.html', 'snippet': 'One of the summer’s better gallery group shows is this presentation of some two dozen works in various mediums by 17 artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey Kaplan', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mind Is Outer Space’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Mind Is Outer Space’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-25T20:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c44e23dd-4686-55ae-9705-4aea06a254a2', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c44e23dd-4686-55ae-9705-4aea06a254a2'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Irwin’s eye-filling yet barely-there mirage at the Whitney Museum makes the other art spectacles of summer seem overwrought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/arts/design/robert-irwins-light-and-space-work-returns-to-the-whitney.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Irwin’s eye-filling yet barely-there mirage at the Whitney Museum makes the other art spectacles of summer seem overwrought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York has seen its share of art spectacles this summer. The Museum of Modern Art has its Rain Room, where the computerized stop-and-go downpours have attracted mobs. The Park Avenue Armory is filled with Paul McCarthy’s sensurround onslaught of sexual and psychological chaos. At the Guggenheim, lines of people wait to see the immense digital light show that James Turrell has inserted into the soaring rotunda. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print