EPSIE, N.Y. — On a still summer day, a day so warm that even the song sparrows and dragonflies seemed listless, Guillermo Valdez and Will Blum, who are juniors at Vassar College, tugged at the roots of porcelain berry and honeysuckle plants. Sweat trickling down their necks, they were on a mission to expel the invasive vines from a patch of campus that is better known to birders in the area than students, and replace them with native species like marsh marigolds, swamp azaleas and cinnamon ferns.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/nyregion/garden/garden-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 