es.com/2013/07/26/opinion/inching-forward-in-the-mideast.html', 'snippet': 'Despite doubters, Secretary of State John Kerry presses forward with a strategy for peace negotiations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The week that Secretary of State John Kerry said could start the revival of Israeli-Palestinian peace talks is passing without visible progress. The naysayers are chortling, but Mr. Kerry, to his credit, is undeterred. His aides insist that plans to resume the dialogue on a two-state solution that collapsed in 2010 are on track; on Thursday, an Israeli minister said that talks could begin next week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inching Forward in the Mideast', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inching Forward in the Mideast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T01:17:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c2eb769-2472-50ed-a241-76520e609c0c', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c2eb769-2472-50ed-a241-76520e609c0c'}, {'abstract': 'Will voters show up at a recall election to defend two state lawmakers in Colorado who dared to defy the National Rifle Association?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/opinion/the-gun-lobby-takes-vengeful-aim.html', 'snippet': 'Will voters show up at a recall election to defend two state lawmakers in Colorado who dared to defy the National Rifle Association?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One welcome surprise in gun safety occurred this year in Colorado, where the Democratic-led Legislature dared to defy the gun lobby and mandated universal background checks on firearm sales and 15-round limits on ammunition magazines. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Lobby Takes Vengeful Aim', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Gun Lobby Takes Vengeful Aim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morse, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giron, Angela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T01:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/db4a8d08-40fa-51be-abce-bc90945026e4', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db4a8d08-40fa-51be-abce-bc90945026e4'}, {'abstract': 'The latest bad bill put forth by the Republicans in the majority is just another example of why nothing gets done by this Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/opinion/bait-and-switch-in-the-house.html', 'snippet': 'The latest bad bill put forth by the Republicans in the majority is just another example of why nothing gets done by this Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a bill in the House being pushed by the majority leader, Eric Cantor, and many of his Republican colleagues that sounds as innocent and upright as motherhood and apple pie: the Kids First Research Act of 2013. It pro