26T02:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e3a510f-0998-5c5a-ae73-773a7c3db334', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e3a510f-0998-5c5a-ae73-773a7c3db334'}, {'abstract': 'Friday fabulousness with Brendan Emmett Quigley.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/25/dropped-a-line/', 'snippet': 'Friday fabulousness with Brendan Emmett Quigley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial ‘Win Valuable Prizes’ Alert!: LOLLAPUZZOOLA is the best summertime crossword tournament held annually on a Saturday in August. Enjoy a full day of tournament puzzling — six original crosswords never published anywhere else, constructed by some of the best puzzlemakers in the solar system. There are separate skill divisions for superpro solvers and normal Earthlings, a unique Pairs Division if you’d like to solve with a friend, and our famous At-Home Division for those who can’t make it to NYC. They also have a one-of-a-kind “Google Ticket” system for players who need a little help along the way, an assortment of snacks and beverages, and for just an extra five bucks, you can stay for the fourth annual Ryan Hecht Pizza Social. $25 to pre-register for the whole day, $10 for the At-Home Division. Join co-hosts Brian Cimmet and Patrick Blindauer for a casual yet competitive tournament experience you won’t find anywhere else. Visit bemoresmarter.com for more information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dropped a Line', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'v