im Jong-un, the leader of North Korea, met with a top-ranking Chinese official at a time when relations between the two allies are being tested by the North’s nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, used his meeting with the visiting vice president of China this week to stress a “blood” alliance with Beijing, and expressed his support for reconvening six-nation talks on ending the North’s nuclear weapons program, the official news media of the two allies reported on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korean Leader Supports Resumption of Nuclear Talks, State Media Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korean Leader Backs Nuclear Talks, State Media Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Tests', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Yuanchao', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T06:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun and Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bf3404f-5a1a-535d-8d8e-24b132be68bf', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bf3404f-5a1a-535d-8d8e-24b132be68bf'}, {'abstract': 'India’s right-wing opposition parties stay together despite differences over leadership.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/indias-opposition-parties-stay-together-despite-differences-over-modi/', 'snippet': 'India’s right-wing opposition parties stay together despite differences over leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uddhav Thackeray, the Shiv Sena executive president, announced last Friday that his party would support the Bharatiya Janata Party in the national elections scheduled for next year. But his support was tempered by his next remark. “The country needs a strong government and a credible leader, but I can’t see anyone who fits that description,” Mr. Thackeray told reporters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/26/world/asia/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk/26-Uddhav-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Opposition Parties Stay Together Despite Differences Over Modi', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shiv Sena', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T06:49:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sumana Ramanan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sumana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramanan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4025accc-28d9-5bbe-8415-d6d3a30b31bb', 'word_count': 1169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4025accc-28d9-5bbe-8415-d6d3a30b31bb'}, {'abstract': 'Mikolaj Nowacki grew up along the river Odra in Poland, taking in its sounds and its smells. Years later, he returned with his camera to what he calls the “river of history.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/a-visual-ode-to-a-changing-river-in-poland/', 'snippet': 'Mikolaj Nowacki grew up along the river Odra in Poland, taking in its sounds and its smells. Years later, he returned with his camera to what he calls the “river of history.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mikolaj Nowacki calls Poland’s Odra the “river of history,” he might as well be talking about his own life. Having grown up along the river, which is also known as the Oder, even its damp smells linger in his memory. After originally pursuing a doctorate in space law, he turned his back on that profession to become a newspaper photographer. Two years ago, he was accepted into the mentor program at VII Photo, where he has been working with Antonin Kratochvil. Mr. Kratochvil taught him his most important lesson yet: “There’s only one way, and it’s your way.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ode to a Polish River', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wroclaw (Poland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt McCann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa319352-fae9-5739-8183-cdfae85ccd62', 'word_count': 1511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa319352-fae9-5739-8183-cdfae85ccd62'}, {'abstract': 'After announcing that Mohamed Morsi could face serious criminal charges, the Egyptian military orchestrated a display of military power in an effort to crack down on demonstrators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/world/middleeast/egypt.html', 'snippet': 'After announcing that Mohamed Morsi could face serious criminal charges, the Egyptian military orchestrated a display of military power in an effort to crack down on demonstrators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The Egyptian military stepped up its campaign against the Muslim Brotherhood on Friday, as officials announced the possibility of serious criminal charges carrying the death penalty against the ousted president, Mohamed Morsi, and hopes faded for any sort of political accommodation with the Islamist group. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/world/27egypt_337/27egypt_337-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/world/27egypt_337/27egypt_337-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/world/27egypt_337/27egypt_337-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/world/27egypt_337/27egypt_337-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/world/27egypt_337/27egypt_337-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub