91b4543910c'}, {'abstract': 'And the Hollywood-ingénue problem, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/magazine/mireille-enos-the-killing-star-avoids-the-police-procedural-trap.html', 'snippet': 'And the Hollywood-ingénue problem, too.', 'lead_paragraph': ' You tend toward serious roles, like the detective Sarah Linden in “The Killing,” which is about to conclude its third season on AMC. Do you have any desire to do something lighter?  For three years, everything I’ve done has been heartbreaking. I’m ready to do something that my daughter can see before she’s 18.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 1768, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1768}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 348, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/magazine/28talk/28talk-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mireille Enos: ‘The Killing’  Star Avoids the Police-Procedural Trap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘More Machines and Less Heart’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Julie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Killing (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Enos, Mireille', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Julie', 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/859c4dd2-a6c2-5fb0-9fda-c7a93f3c3e61', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/859c4dd2-a6c2-5fb0-9fda-c7a93f3c3e61'}, {'abstract': 'Could I now learn who they really were?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/magazine/my-fictional-grandparents.html', 'snippet': 'Could I now learn who they really were?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My mother was abandoned in a French orphanage in Fez in 1941. That year in Morocco, hundreds of people died in an outbreak of the plague; her parents were among the victims. Actually, no, they died in a horrific car crash on the newly built road from Marrakesh to Fez. No, no, no, my grandmother died in childbirth, and my grandfather, mad with grief, gave the baby away. The truth is: I don’t know how my mother ended up in a French orphanage in 1941. The nuns in black habits never told.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': '