gs to treat Type 2 diabetes could cause pancreatic inflammation or pancreatic cancer, a finding that might reassure patients while also removing a potential sales threat for Merck and some other drug companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Regulator Finds Little Risk in Diabetes Drugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Regulator Finds Little Risk in Diabetes Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pancreatic Cancer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Medicines Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T12:50:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46e05be3-fc83-5ed7-bc2f-ab7757dd3312', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46e05be3-fc83-5ed7-bc2f-ab7757dd3312'}, {'abstract': 'With Alex Rodriguez, the Yankees and now Mike Francesa all playing roles, it’s a script that defies belief. And never seems to end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/sports/a-farce-in-many-many-acts.html', 'snippet': 'With Alex Rodriguez, the Yankees and now Mike Francesa all playing roles, it’s a script that defies belief. And never seems to end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s good to know that heading into a nice summer weekend, we can take comfort in the Yankees-Alex Rodriguez melodrama settling back into its usual level of farcical entertainment, the kind we’re used to in summer reruns. That’s after the two combatants took a deep breath and realized they are stuck with each other, so let’s have a nice, smooth-everything-over teleconference, which included Rodriguez’s lawyer, because don’t all discussions of thigh injuries involve a lawyer?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 770}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1597, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Farce in Many, Many Acts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francesa, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T13:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ff2acd4-faee-5681-84af-e1443c681853', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ff2acd4-faee-5681-84af-e1443c681853'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not 1986 anymore.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/things-fell-apart/', 'snippet': 'It’s not 1986 anymore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ezra Klein has a good piece urging journalists to stop talking about the “center” — unless they first explain what they mean, which in practice would mean acknowledging that what they call the “center” isn’t at the center of anything, except maybe the prejudices of a self-referential elite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things Fell Apart', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T13:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae5abbc6-c9f7-5de7-a172-41d83d9680c5', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae5abbc6-c9f7-5de7-a172-41d83d9680c5'}, {'abstract': 'Because I was unable to tolerate my children’s disappointment, I never gained fluency with a very important two-letter word.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/confessions-of-a-mother-who-couldnt-say-no/', 'snippet': 'Because I was unable to tolerate my children’s disappointment, I never gained fluency with a very important two-letter word.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my first child was an infant, the doula handed me an article that championed benign neglect. Children, the article proposed, need to be left to their own devices to work things out. Parental intervention at every little grunt discourages resilience. This made sense, so I tried. Really hard. At least until I thought the baby needed me. And then I picked that baby up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions of a Mother Who Couldn’t Say ‘No’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T13:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Buttenwieser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buttenwieser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0608509-04c2-544d-a65c-9cf5924b9e7c', 'wo