ty for ignoring the lesson of 9/11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey has tried on a lot of costumes in the endless prequel to a presumed run for president in 2016. He’s styled himself as another Ronald Reagan, folksy (in a cruder, New Jersey way); a John McCain, blunt and plain spoken; a technocrat like Mitt Romney; even a “uniter” like George W. Bush.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Christie’s Giuliani Impression', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T16:15:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d54ee0f8-3092-522d-97d7-d3f31e3d3aa2', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d54ee0f8-3092-522d-97d7-d3f31e3d3aa2'}, {'abstract': 'Already criticized for failing to find those responsible for the February killing of another opposition figure, the government was under pressure to produce some answers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/world/middleeast/tunisia-assassination.html', 'snippet': 'Already criticized for failing to find those responsible for the February killing of another opposition figure, the government was under pressure to produce some answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — The government on Friday blamed an Islamist extremist cell linked to Al Qaeda for the killing of a leader of the political opposition and identifi