. Cohen to give up billions of dollars of assets will depend on showing that insider trading so infected SAC Capital Advisors that much of its money should be forfeited as the tainted proceeds of ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department did not file criminal charges accusing Steven A. Cohen of insider trading, but it did the next best thing by indicting his firm, SAC Capital Advisors. While the criminal case is likely to result in a conviction of SAC on at least some charges, a companion civil asset forfeiture action filed the same day gives the government a means to try to take a sizeable chunk of his fortune if the criminal case does not do so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going After Steven Cohen’s Wallet', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T19:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a55025ef-9086-5823-888a-8f8253fa1547', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a55025ef-9086-5823-888a-8f8253fa1547'}, {'abstract': 'The dance troupe known as L-E-V presented “House,” a work by Sharon Eyal, on Thursday night at the Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/arts/dance/l-e-v-performs-at-jacobs-pillow.html', 'snippet': 'The dance troupe known as L-E-V presented “House,” a work by Sharon Eyal, on Thursday night at the Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BECKET, Mass. — First, many voices in the darkness, incomprehensible and arriving in choppy waves as might inundate a deranged mind. Then, through the haze, a figure with metallic-colored skin emerges. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/LEV/LEV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Extraterrestrial Rave, Intense but Eerily Frosty', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Extraterrestrial Rave, Intense but Eerily Frosty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'L-E-V (Dance Co)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Jacob's Pillow Dance Festival", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eyal, Sharon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Behar, Gai', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T19:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/521dcce0-8bb5-5c52-9399-41dee9e62883', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/521dcce0-8bb5-5c52-9399-41dee9e62883'}, {'abstract': 'A treat of Mexican coastal towns, the cóctel de mariscos replaces the rubbery, ketchup-flavored appetizer, adding a rush of flavor and variety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/dining/a-flavorful-alternative-to-shrimp-cocktail-coctel-de-mariscos.html', 'snippet': 'A treat of Mexican coastal towns, the cóctel de mariscos replaces the rubbery, ketchup-flavored appetizer, adding a rush of flavor and variety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It feels almost un-American to admit that there’s no bottle of ketchup in my refrigerator. Certainly I was raised to believe there ought to be, along with a bottle of slightly thicker so-called “chili sauce.” Cocktail sauce, made the Midwestern way, combined the two in equal parts, along with a dab of horseradish. And cocktail sauce was the only thing to serve with cold, boiled shrimp, even in fancy restaurants. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/dining/31KITCH_SPAN/31KITCH2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/dining/31KITCH_SPAN/31KITCH2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheigh