es.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/theater/reviews/murmurs-brings-slapstick-to-the-lincoln-center-festival.html', 'snippet': '“Murmurs,” a mime/circus show by Victoria Thierrée Chaplin, explores illusions with a strange set and surreal scenes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The subject of “Murmurs,” an 80-minute mime/circus production conceived and directed by Victoria Thierrée Chaplin, is illusion. People sit on chairs — or lie on mattresses — that aren’t there. A man looks down to find that he has three arms. Individuals have movement dialogues with empty costumes that become animated or with walking people who suddenly crumble into mere bundles of clothes. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/27MURMUR/27MURMUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/27MURMUR/27MURMUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 566}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/27MURMUR/27MURMUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 965, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/27MURMUR/27MURMUR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1877, 'width': 1991, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/27MURMUR/27MURMUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/27/arts/27MURMUR/27MURMUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum