st with both the military and the Islamists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As hundreds of thousands of Egyptians crammed into dueling rallies in different parts of Cairo on Friday, responding to calls for support from rival political factions around the army and the Muslim Brotherhood, activists who mistrust both the military and the Islamists were left wondering how best to register their disgust.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tahrir Taken, Some Egyptians Look for ‘Third Square’ to Resist Islamists and Army', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Council of the Armed Forces (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-26T22:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/941ff5bf-b809-5917-a687-9c931204f562', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/941ff5bf-b809-5917-a687-9c931204f562'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for important and peculiar items. Friday’s selections feature a pair of Google product reviews and a theory about why Zynga folded on the gambling business.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/todays-scuttlebot-sizing-up-google/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for important and peculiar items. Friday’s selections feature a pair o