k': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Lutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b70218-289c-5e3d-866d-474215159a9a', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b70218-289c-5e3d-866d-474215159a9a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mitchell, who on a hunch began drilling shale rock formations, is credited with creating an unexpected natural gas boom in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/business/george-mitchell-a-pioneer-in-hydraulic-fracturing-dies-at-94.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mitchell, who on a hunch began drilling shale rock formations, is credited with creating an unexpected natural gas boom in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George P. Mitchell, the son of a Greek goatherd who capped a career as one of the most prominent independent oilmen in the United States by unlocking immense natural gas and petroleum resources trapped in shale rock formations, died on Friday in Galveston, Tex. He was 94.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 1994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/business/mitchell-obit/mitchell-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Mitchell, a Pioneer in Hydraulic Fracturing, Dies at 94', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'George Mitchell, 94, a Pioneer in Hydraulic Fracturing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Douglas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, George P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Woodlands, The (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T00:54:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b645b60-f61a-59ee-985a-a7db6cb3d368', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b645b60-f61a-59ee-985a-a7db6cb3d368'}, {'abstract': 'How can two versions of the same song — one by me, the other by Eleanor Friedberger of the Fiery Furnaces — be so different?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/26/staring-at-two-suns/', 'snippet': 'How can two versions of the same song — one by me, the other by Eleanor Friedberger of the Fiery Furnaces — be so different?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of years ago, I started to write songs with Eleanor Friedberger, the singer of the Fiery Furnaces, just before the release of her debut solo album, “Last Summer.” The first songs were ostensibly for the fictional band in my next novel, but things went well and we kept going. These co-written songs – a mixture of her words, my words, mutual melodies and disparate memories – have recently been released as her second album, “Personal Record.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staring at Two Suns', 'kicker': 'Measure for Measure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T01:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley Stace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d006b32c-bb50-5bec-a394-8d2b7d2495bb', 'word_count': 1591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d006b32c-bb50-5bec-a394-8d2b7d2495bb'}, {'abstract': 'The death of a sailor, the bickering over rule changes, the threat of boycotts and the name-calling of a team have hurt the lead-up to the America’s Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/sports/turbulent-journey-for-americas-cup.html', 'snippet': 'The death of a sailor, the bickering over rule changes, the threat of boycotts and the name-calling of a team have hurt the lead-up to the America’s Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — The race was scheduled to begin at 12:15 p.m., and fans were expected to pour into the well-manicured America’s Cup Park and line themselves all around the waterfront of San Francisco Bay to watch. Years of planning, promise and promotion were built toward what organizers called “America’s Cup Summer of Racing.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/sports/Y-JUMP-JAILING/Y-JUMP-JAILING-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turbulent Journey for America’s Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Turbulent Journey For Sailing’s Elite Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sailboats and Sailing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wollan, Malia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "AMERICA'S CUP", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Luna Rossa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Artemis Racing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oracle Racing Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emirates Team New Zealand', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellison, Lawrence J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T01:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch and Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3956a481-f109-53d1-9976-650f6ac9b1e0', 'word_count': 1703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3956a481-f109-53d1-9976-650f6ac9b1e0'}, {'abstract': 'As more lives are destroyed by the system that creates vast amounts of wealth for the few, the more heroic it sounds to “give back.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/opinion/the-charitable-industrial-complex.html', 'snippet': 'As more lives are destroyed by the system that creates vast amounts of wealth for the few, the more heroic it sounds to “give back.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I HAD spent much of my life writing music for commercials, film and television and knew little about the world of philanthropy as practiced by the very wealthy until what I call the big bang happened in 2006. That year, my father, Warren Buffett, made good on his commitment to give nearly all of his accumulated wealth back to society. In addition to making several large donations, he added generously to the three foundations that my parents had created years earlier, one for each of their children to run. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/opinion/0727OPEDopen/0727OPEDopen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/27/opinion/0727OPEDopen/0727OPEDopen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 923}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/opinion/0727OPEDopen/0727OPEDopen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/opinion/0727OPEDopen/0727OPEDopen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/27/opinion/0727OPEDopen/0727OPEDopen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':