ious-looking Vincent van Gogh. There are treasures by Matisse, Rivera, Picasso and Calder, to name only a few in Detroit’s vast collection. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Civic Treasure in Detroit', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Civic Treasure in Detroit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Institute of Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T01:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/44ae8575-d585-525e-b4f3-34cf60104df5', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44ae8575-d585-525e-b4f3-34cf60104df5'}, {'abstract': 'Policy makers should examine the bank’s involvement in commodity markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/opinion/goldman-sachss-aluminum-pile.html', 'snippet': 'Policy makers should examine the bank’s involvement in commodity markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'History is filled with examples of financial speculators who tried to make big profits by hoarding commodities like gold, silver and copper. Now, some big users of aluminum, including Coca-Cola and MillerCoors, say that the practices of large financial institutions like Goldman Sachs have driven up the price of that important metal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Sachs’s Aluminum Pile', 'kicker': 'Editorial', '