ecutives at the nation’s top corporations jumped 16 percent last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OFTEN relegated to the background, America’s low-wage workers have been making considerable noise lately by deploying an unusual weapon — one-day strikes — to make their message heard: they’re sick and tired of earning just $8, $9, $10 an hour. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Back Against Wretched Wages', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting Back Against Wretched Wages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T18:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ad7ea4b-84e1-52ce-88f7-5d46f739a7e1', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ad7ea4b-84e1-52ce-88f7-5d46f739a7e1'}, {'abstract': 'If the Celtic Tiger had simply wandered in, that meant it could wander out again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/opinion/sunday/the-psychology-of-an-irish-meltdown.html', 'snippet': 'If the Celtic Tiger had simply wandered in, that meant it could wander out again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — FOR the past month, Ireland has been outraged by tapes of Anglo Irish Bank officials, back in 2008, discussing lying to the government about how big a loan they needed, and how they knew there was no chance that the loan would ever be repaid. That loan was the first domino in a sequence that ended with the whole Irish economy flat on its face.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sunday-review/28IRELAND/28IRELAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Psychology of an Irish Meltdown', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Psychology of an Irish Meltdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anglo Irish Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T18:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tana French', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'French', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c603b1-34f9-5dc5-aa65-5d336cfc7853', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c603b1-34f9-5dc5-aa65-5d336cfc7853'}, {'abstract': 'The poor and powerless are at greater risk of early death.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/status-and-stress/', 'snippet': 'The poor and powerless are at greater risk of early death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although professionals may bemoan their long work hours and high-pressure careers, really, there’s stress, and then there’s Stress with a capital “S.” The former can be considered a manageable if unpleasant part of life; in the right amount, it may even strengthen one’s mettle. The latter kills.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Status and Stress', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Status and Stress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 