Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T19:24:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/33603f92-f38b-583b-8939-028f5cf3bd77', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33603f92-f38b-583b-8939-028f5cf3bd77'}, {'abstract': 'It is time to stop pretending that the notoriously burdensome airport screening procedures are all that stand between us and devastation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/opinion/sunday/airport-security-without-the-hassle.html', 'snippet': 'It is time to stop pretending that the notoriously burdensome airport screening procedures are all that stand between us and devastation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chance of dying in an airplane is vanishingly small. The chance of being killed by a terrorist in an airplane is smaller still. Mark Stewart, a civil engineer who studies probabilistic risk, has put the odds at one in 90 million a year. Looking at these figures dispassionately, one might wonder if the Transportation Security Administration has found the right balance between safety and convenience with its notoriously burdensome airport screening procedures. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Airport Security Without the Hassle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airport Security Without the Hassle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyw