tion game. Without him, the Yankees’ offense, facing Chris Archer, remained in a state of disrepair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/sports/baseball/with-jeter-still-sidelined-rays-archer-shuts-out-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter was eligible to be activated from the D.L. but instead played a simulation game. Without him, the Yankees’ offense, facing Chris Archer, remained in a state of disrepair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, the day Derek Jeter was eligible to be activated from the disabled list, he instead played a simulated game. The time was unannounced. The place was initially left to one’s imagination.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shutout by Rays Rookie Caps Week of Drama for Yankees', 'kicker': 'Rays 1, Yankees 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shutout by Rays Rookie Caps Week of Drama for Yankees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T20:47:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be67a6d8-05e1-51b6-8e8f-81f86024f30a', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be67a6d8-05e1-51b6-8e8f-81f86024f30a'}, {'abstract': 'The movie “2 Guns,” adapted from the comic books from Boom Studios, opens this week. Thanks to Boom’s “creator share” model, both the publisher and comic’s writer reap benefits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/business/sharing-the-wealth-as-a-comic-book-goes-to-hollywood.html', 'snippet': 'The movie “2 Guns,” adapted from the comic books from Boom Studios, opens this week. Thanks to Boom’s “creator share” model, both the publisher and comic’s writer reap benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EIGHT years ago, when the founder and chief executive of Boom Studios offered to publish a comic book called “2 Guns” about two undercover drug agents, he frankly told its writer: “The paycheck isn’t borderline insulting; it is insulting.”', 'print