an Lovett and Rob Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ab97a68-289c-592c-a6ce-bbe65b1466fc', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ab97a68-289c-592c-a6ce-bbe65b1466fc'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about the growing animal rights movement.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/treating-farm-animals-with-respect/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about the growing animal rights movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is a side trip from the issues I mostly write about, and has nothing to do with international relations or politics. Rather, it’s about our ethical obligations to animals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treating Farm Animals With Respect', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T21:17:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/617e76ea-71d1-5014-b91a-4377cb17d8bb', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/617e76ea-71d1-5014-b91a-4377cb17d8bb'}, {'abstract': 'As the Obama administration makes a push to revive the economy, Treasury Secretary Jacob J. Lew joins several programs this Sunday to talk about its approach.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/sunday-breakfast-menu-july-28/', 'snippet': 'As the Obama administration makes a push to revive the economy, Treasury Secretary Jacob J. Lew joins several programs this Sunday to talk about its approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After President Obama\xa0sharpened his focus on the economy last week, the treasury secretary, Jacob J. Lew, will appear on the Sunday shows on ABC, CNN, Fox and NBC to discuss the administration’s latest approach with Congressional fights looming over government spending and the debt ceiling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, July 28', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T21:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85f23060-63a6-5d39-acb1-55f33360e10c', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85f23060-63a6-5d39-acb1-55f33360e10c'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Reynolds builds more than just a puzzle for us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/27/fast-work/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Reynolds builds more than just a puzzle for us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — You know you’ve blogged a lot of crossword puzzles when you solve a grid about the MODEL T car and think to yourself, “Huh. Must be an anniversary.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast Work', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T22:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17cdc86a-afba-5bba-bb54-0969d4da4bb7', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17cdc86a-afba-5bba-bb54-0969d4da4bb7'}, {'abstract': 'The junior senator from Texas has joined a select group touring early primary states and denying they are interested in running for America’s top job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/us/how-ted-cruz-is-not-running-for-president.html', 'snippet': 'The junior senator from Texas has joined a select group touring early primary states and denying they are interested in running for America’s top job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a year since that impossible thing happened. Ted Cruz, in his first run for public office, beat the fabulously wealthy David Dewhurst — himself the winner of four previous statewide elections — in a Republican primary runoff for the United States Senate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Ted Cruz Is Not Running for President', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Ted Cruz Is Not Running For President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewhurst, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-27T22:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1fa2273-4cf4-58de-8dd8-8cb5b7b0546d', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1fa2273-4cf4-58de-8dd8-8cb5b7b0546d'}, {'abstract': 'Westerners go to Syria motivated by a desire to ease suffering by defeating the government, but there is concern that they will return home with jihadist zeal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/world/middleeast/worries-mount-as-syria-lures-wests-muslims.html', 'snippet': 'Westerners go to Syria motivated by a desire to ease suffering by defeating the government, but there is concern that they will return home with jihadist zeal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A rising number of radicalized young Muslims with Western passports are traveling to Syria to fight with the rebels against the government of Bashar al-Assad, raising fears among American and European intelligence officials of a new terrorist threat when the fighters return home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/world/sub-fighters/sub-fighters-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 273, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/28/world/sub-fighters/sub-fighter