 of the first laser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Distinguished Columbia University physicists, some of them Nobel Prize winners, called it a “harebrained scheme.” But James P. Gordon, principal builder of a refrigerator-size device that would help revolutionize modern life, believed in it enough to bet a bottle of bourbon that it would work.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1581, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Gordon, Who Paved Way for Lasers, Dies at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James Gordon, Who Paved Way for Lasers, Dies at 85', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, James P (1928-2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microwaves (Electromagnetic Waves)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laser (Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-28T01:51:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/58e9a409-1c96-5691-8e95-9c48f5e5bcdd', 'word_count': 1209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58e9a409-1c96-5691-8e95-9c48f5e5bcdd'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Ray, an instrumentalist and vocalist who began performing in the 1940s, worked steadily for seven decades and released her first recording as a lead singer this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/arts/music/carline-ray-an-enduring-pioneer-woman-of-jazz-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Ray, an instrumentalist and vocalist who began performing in the 1940s, worked steadily for seven decades and released her first recording as a lead singer this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carline Ray, a pioneering jazz instrumentalist and vocalist who joined the all-female International Sweethearts of Rhythm in the 1940s, later performed with Erskine Hawkins and Mary Lou Williams and this year released her first recording as a lead vocalist, died on July 18 in Manhattan. She was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 762}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 807, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1613, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/rayobit2/rayobit2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carline Ray, an Enduring Pioneer Woman of Jazz, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carline Ray, 88, an Enduring Pioneer Woman of Jazz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywo