': 'nyt://article/f74d9af2-e6c1-555f-8ce9-761788c279dd'}, {'abstract': 'The new exhibition will showcase the work of 26 artists from the 1950s to the 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/asia-society-to-present-modern-iranian-art/', 'snippet': 'The new exhibition will showcase the work of 26 artists from the 1950s to the 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new exhibition of modern Iranian art will showcase the work of 26 artists from the 1950s to the 1970s, when global art movements particularly influenced Iranian artists, the Asia Society Museum in New York is announcing on Monday. The show — coming amid stirrings of hope that Iran’s international relations will relax under its new president, Hassan Rouhani — will include more than 100 works that focus on what the museum calls the little-known pre-Islamic Revolution era.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asia Society to Present Modern Iranian Art', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia Society to Present Modern Iranian Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-28T20:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0824623-9557-5b70-9d5c-79e0cd87a5af', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0824623-9557-5b70-9d5c-79e0cd87a5af'}, {'abstract': 'For students of my generation in Iran, translated works opened a wider philosophical imagination, where borders between East and West dissolved.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/found-in-translation/', 'snippet': 'For students of my generation in Iran, translated works opened a wider philosophical imagination, where borders between East and West dissolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though it is common to lament the shortcomings of reading an important work in any language other than the original and of the “impossibility” of translation, I am convinced that works of philosophy (or literature for that matter — are they different?) in fact gain far more than they lose in translation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Found in Translation', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARABIC LANGUAGE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation and Interpreters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-28T21:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hamid Dabashi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hamid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dabashi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef5952a5-6dca-5499-b84b-c2fe5f2b4d1e', 'word_count': 1740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef5952a5-6dca-5499-b84b-c2fe5f2b4d1e'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Löscher, head of the electronics and engineering conglomerate since 2007, is taking the blame for a series of missteps that have plagued Siemens last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/business/siemens-ousts-chief-over-string-of-setbacks.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Löscher, head of the electronics and engineering conglomerate since 2007, is taking the blame for a series of missteps that have plagued Siemens last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The supervisory board of Siemens, one of Germany’s largest companies, said that it would fire its chief executive at a meeting on Wednesday and replace him with an insider following a string of problems that led to a profit warning last week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/business/siemens/siemens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name':