8d34-aec2-59d5-99b1-af36fe76f1bc'}, {'abstract': 'Sinead O’Connor made a foray into traditional religious music with “Gospel Sessions” at Alice Tully Hall as part of the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/arts/music/sinead-oconnor-in-gospel-sessions-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'Sinead O’Connor made a foray into traditional religious music with “Gospel Sessions” at Alice Tully Hall as part of the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not unusual for a mid- or late-career white pop singer to declare an interest in African-American gospel music, especially from the 1950s, considered its late golden age. Gospel contains forces such singers might desire access to: virtuosity, resistance, belief, magic. But the picture feels different when the pop singer is, say, a 46-year-old Irish female priest — ordained in 1999 by an independent Catholic group not recognized by the church — with serious interests in Rastafari and Hinduism and serious problems with organized religion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/sinead/sinead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 541, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/sinead/sinead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 541}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/sinead/sinead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/sinead/sinead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1847, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': Non