 first estimate of second-quarter gross domestic product, ADP employment for July, and the Chicago Purchasing Manager Index report for July (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims, Institute for Supply Management data for July and auto sales for July (Thursday); and the United States unemployment report for July, factory orders for June and consumer spending for June (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week of July 29', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Reports for the Week of July 29', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-28T23:44:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8a09729-720f-509b-ab21-7ba53909c564', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8a09729-720f-509b-ab21-7ba53909c564'}, {'abstract': 'Cases against two services that change how viewers watch TV are far from settled, but the stakes, which would affect broadcasters’ profits, could not be bigger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/business/media/vcrs-past-is-guiding-televisions-future.html', 'snippet': 'Cases against two services that change how viewers watch TV are far from settled, but the stakes, which would affect broadcasters’ profits, could not be bigger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last few weeks have been a rugged legal stretch for incumbent television companies. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'so