r his return to the national team and the national stage. Nor was he credited with the assist. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1455, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Goal, but Plenty for U.S. to Celebrate in Gold Cup Final', 'kicker': 'United States 1, Panama 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Goal, but Plenty for U.S. to Celebrate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T01:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb8f73de-376e-5f7a-bac4-2a0834238ddf', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb8f73de-376e-5f7a-bac4-2a0834238ddf'}, {'abstract': 'New rules would help guard big banks from failure and the public from bailouts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/opinion/not-too-big-to-fail.html', 'snippet': 'New rules would help guard big banks from failure and the public from bailouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New rules on bank capital, recently proposed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation and other bank regulators, are a welcome step toward a safer and sounder financial system. And they come at a politically timely moment. Big banks invariably argue that new rules will impede their ability to thrive and, in the process, harm the economy. But their profits are soaring, even as the economy slows, a situation that makes their shopworn anti-regulatory argument all the more threadbare.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Too Big to Fail', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Too Big to Fail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T01:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d855b7f-40a4-5e40-afa6-29557b0acf7a', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d855b7f-40a4-5e40-afa6-29557b0acf7a'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City mayoral candidates need to build on Mayor Michael Bloomberg’s transit improvements, in every borough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/opinion/a-straphangers-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City mayoral candidates need to build on Mayor Michael Bloomberg’s transit improvements, in every borough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say this for Rudolph Giuliani: In 1997 he made it free to ride the Staten Island Ferry, a small daily improvement in commuters’ lives that, multiplied by millions of rides and many years, surely adds up to something monumental. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Straphangers’ Campaign', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Straphangers’ Campaign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transportation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '