', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/150b33d0-9b49-5023-b944-6d215023030f', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/150b33d0-9b49-5023-b944-6d215023030f'}, {'abstract': 'While more votes have been cast in favor of Michael S. Dell and Silver Lake’s takeover proposal, the tally is not enough to win without a change in rules.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/voting-rule-change-is-viewed-as-crucial-to-dell-founders-takeover-bid/', 'snippet': 'While more votes have been cast in favor of Michael S. Dell and Silver Lake’s takeover proposal, the tally is not enough to win without a change in rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A seemingly small concession during the original negotiations over the proposed takeover of Dell by the company’s founder has come into focus in the increasingly protracted deal saga.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting Rule Change Is Seen as Crucial to Dell Founder’s Takeover Bid', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voting Rule Change Is Viewed as Crucial to Dell Founder’s Takeover Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T01:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/807b70c5-4247-5a06-9ce8-a91aa1effb6a', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/807b70c5-4247-5a06-9ce8-a91aa1effb6a'}, {'abstract': 'Protests for the the government and the National Constituent Assembly to resign continued around the country Sunday on the fourth day after the assassination of an opposition legislator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/world/africa/protesters-press-tunisian-government-to-resign-as-ruling-party-supporters-rally.html', 'snippet': 'Protests for the the government and the National Constituent Assembly to resign continued around the country Sunday on the fourth day after the assassination of an opposition legislator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — Protests continued around the country Sunday on the fourth day after the assassination of an opposition legislator. Demonstrators were back out in front of the National Assembly building after police officers broke up their camp overnight and opposition parties continued to press for the government and the National Constituent Assembly to resign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters Press Tunisian Government to Resign, as Ruling Party Supporters Rally', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters Press Tunisian Government to Resign, as Ruling Party Supporters Rally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gall, Carlotta', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'v