2'}, {'abstract': 'The lunch, in the president’s private dining room, will be one of several times that Mrs. Clinton and Mr. Obama have seen each other since she stepped down as secretary of state in February.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/28/obama-invites-hillary-clinton-to-lunch/', 'snippet': 'The lunch, in the president’s private dining room, will be one of several times that Mrs. Clinton and Mr. Obama have seen each other since she stepped down as secretary of state in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and Hillary Rodham Clinton will have a private lunch at the White House on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Invites Hillary Clinton to Lunch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T02:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6685d78a-1d58-56a9-b56a-fff36f861c90', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6685d78a-1d58-56a9-b56a-fff36f861c90'}, {'abstract': 'Robin Nagle is a chronicler of, and a zealous advocate for, the workers who perform some of the most essential but least heralded jobs in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/nyregion/nagle-a-fascination-with-sanitation-work-and-the-resume-to-prove-it.html', 'snippet': 'Robin Nagle is a chronicler of, and a zealous advocate for, the workers who perform some of the most essential but least heralded jobs in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robin Nagle, a self-described “P.K. — preacher’s kid,” offers a benediction for the city’s sanitation worker