d relationship with Marina Reverte (Ximena Navarrete, a former Miss Universe, above with Mr. Levy), a beautiful refugee from the city who has abandoned her career in hotel management to lead the local fishery, in this new Spanish-language telenovela, which translates as “The Storm.” But galelike forces are intent on keeping them apart — among them, the mayor (César Évora) and his daughter (Laura Carmine); Marina’s biological mother (Daniela Romo) and twin sister (Ms. Navarrete again); her former schoolmate (Iván Sánchez), with links to the mafia; and the mobster (Manuel Ojeda), who separated Marina from her family in the first place. Christina Aguilera performs with Alejandro Fernández on the opening soundtrack. Closed captioning in English is available.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/59047659-4a80-5f38-b0c6-eb804db754f6', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59047659-4a80-5f38-b0c6-eb804db754f6'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Blattman knows what it’s like to be unemployed for months, but always believing in happy endings, he now has one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/booming/reinvented-in-his-60s-after-26-jobless-months.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Blattman knows what it’s like to be unemployed for months, but always believing in happy endings, he now has one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I