adline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T11:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab20cef-1f94-52ee-926f-c8276b64c1bf', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab20cef-1f94-52ee-926f-c8276b64c1bf'}, {'abstract': 'Saks Inc. has agreed to sell itself to the Hudson’s Bay Company for about $2.4 billion in cash, uniting the storied luxury retailer with Lord & Taylor and the Canadian chain Hudson’s Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/saks-to-sell-itself-to-owner-of-lord-taylor/', 'snippet': 'Saks Inc. has agreed to sell itself to the Hudson’s Bay Company for about $2.4 billion in cash, uniting the storied luxury retailer with Lord & Taylor and the Canadian chain Hudson’s Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 8:49 p.m. |  When the real estate scion Richard A. Baker\xa0acquired the department store chain Lord & Taylor\xa0at the market peak in 2006, retail industry players laughed. Mr. Baker, they snickered, was just the latest money guy who would get clobbered trying to break into the fashion business.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunting for Luxury, Retail Giant Buys Saks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hunting For Luxury, Retail Giant Buys Saks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Richard A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Hudson's Bay Co", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saks Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T11:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman and Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ffd914-11cc-5655-a7ed-e79b046b5b1d', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ffd914-11cc-5655-a7ed-e79b046b5b1d'}, {'abstract': 'The merger of Omnicom and Publicis signals that advertising is in the business of personal information. | A seemingly small change to the voting rules for the proposed buyout of Dell could have a big effect. | What were SAC Capital’s compliance officers doing? | A son of Warren E. Buffett discusses the pitfalls of philanthropy.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/morning-agenda-advertising-in-the-business-of-big-data/', 'snippet': 'The merger of Omnicom and Publicis signals that advertising is in the business of personal information. | A seemingly small change to the voting rules for the proposed buyout of Dell could have a big effect. | What were SAC Capital’s compliance of...', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN MERGER, AD GIANTS CHASE GOOGLE \xa0|\xa0 The announcement on Sunday that Omnicom and Publicis would merge to create the largest advertising company in the world signals that advertising is now in the business of Big Data: collecting and selling the personal information of millions of consumers, Tanzina Vega writes in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Advertising in the Business of Big Data', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T12:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abe4c8dc-f9f0-5cb5-bcab-02858f210f4f', 'word_count': 1883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abe4c8dc-f9f0-5cb5-bcab-02858f210f4f'}, {'abstract': 'Seven months after the Delhi rape, India’s popular culture continues to fail the gender test.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/after-the-delhi-rape-small-victories-for-women-in-indias-popular-culture/', 'snippet': 'Seven months after the Delhi rape, India’s popular culture continues to fail the gender test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few better places to advertise products of mass appeal than the back of an auto-rickshaw. In the recent past, we have seen the gainful surface being used to sell, among other things, CDs of the self-help superstar Shiv Khera and books of the popular fiction phenomenon Chetan Bhagat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/world/asia/29-demonstration-IndiaInk/29-demonstration-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Delhi Rape, Small Victories for Women in India’s Popular Culture', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akhtar, Farhan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rukh Khan, Shah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T12:23:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Snigdha Poonam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Snigdha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poonam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7930b21a-76a5-596a-802b-eb62c1011ff2', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7930b21a-76a5-596a-802b-eb62c1011ff2'}, {'abstract': '“If someone is gay and he searches for the Lord and has good will, who am I to judge?” Francis was quoted as saying on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/world/europe/pope-francis-gay-priests.html', 'snippet': '“If someone is gay and he searches for the Lord and has good will, who am I to judge?” Francis was quoted as saying on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — For generations, homosexuality has largely been a taboo topic for the Vatican, ignored altogether or treated as “an intrinsic moral evil,” in the words of the previous pope.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/europe/30pope_cnd/30pope_cnd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/world/europe/30pope_cnd/30pope_cnd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/europe/30pope_cnd/30pope_cnd-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '