gotry', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fierstein, Harvey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louganis, Greg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T14:34:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d70aa0f-3be0-5ce2-baa9-fe76dc35c113', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d70aa0f-3be0-5ce2-baa9-fe76dc35c113'}, {'abstract': 'At what is usually crunch time in Congress, lawmakers are facing a sleepy final week before their long summer recess.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/us/politics/at-the-11th-hour-a-languid-congress.html', 'snippet': 'At what is usually crunch time in Congress, lawmakers are facing a sleepy final week before their long summer recess.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Congressional lawmakers will straggle into the Capitol this week for the last legislative days before their long summer recess, crunch time in past Congresses but a sleepy time for the underachieving 113th.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the 11th Hour, a Languid Congress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T14:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c0c7b61-e351-5fe1-a7b3-006ba6313794', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c0c7b61-e351-5fe1-a7b3-006ba6313794'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Scranton, heir to a fortune in railroads and utilities, was a congressman and governor before running unsuccessfully for the Republican Party’s presidential nomination in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/us/politics/william-scranton-former-pennsylvania-governor-dies-at-96.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Scranton, heir to a fortune in railroads and utilities, was a congressman and governor before running unsuccessfully for the Republican Party’s presidential nomination in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William W. Scranton, the moderate Republican governor of Pennsylvania from 1963 to 1967, who lost a run for his party’s presidential nomination in 1964 and later served as the United States representative to the United Nations, died on Sunday in Montecito, Calif. He was 96. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/SCRANTON-1-obit/SCRANTON-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy