'', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fdc7d5b-565f-55cc-bb41-ddd42d53672e', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fdc7d5b-565f-55cc-bb41-ddd42d53672e'}, {'abstract': 'A look at top travel stories from the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/walkabout-jewel-thief-strikes-france-american-business-travelers-return-to-europe/', 'snippet': 'A look at top travel stories from the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hitchcockian A jewel thief left the Carlton Intercontinental Hotel in Cannes, France, above, on Sunday morning with a glittering haul worth perhaps $50 million. And, no, it’s not a plot from “To Catch a Thief.” (New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout: Jewel Thief Strikes France; American Business Travelers Return to Europe', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T18:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2967d72-1ef9-5ba8-ba6c-7c8da90e946c', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2967d72-1ef9-5ba8-ba6c-7c8da90e946c'}, {'abstract': 'When William Close invents an instrument, experimentation is key. But to create the Earth Harp, an instrument that can span 1,000 feet and attach to mountains, took a feat of physics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/science/harnessing-physics-in-grand-spaces-to-make-music.html', 'snippet': 'When William Close invents an instrument, experimentation is key. But to create the Earth Harp, an instrument that can span 1,000 feet and attach to mountains, took a feat of physics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the stage of the Shanghai Grand Theater in China more than a dozen strings stretch from a wooden wing out across the audience and disappear into the darkness of the upper balconies. It’s an instrument unlike anything Bach or Beethoven could have ever imagined. The entire concert hall has been recruited as an echo chamber to create a unique, ethereal sound. But this instrument has turned even grander spaces into music makers. When anchored to the Colosseum in Rome or Seattle’s Space Needle, the world’s largest string instrument is both a powerful sonic experience and an arresting visual image.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harnessing Physics in Grand Spaces to Make Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Close, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T18:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Hiler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hiler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0cd17a5-14b9-5481-8c23-149c69e2d8be', 'word_count': 1625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0cd17a5-14b9-5481-8c23-149c69e2d8be'}, {'abstract': 'The filling for these tacos can be served alone or inside a warm tortilla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/health/potato-salad-and-tomatillo-tacos.html', 'snippet': 'The filling for these tacos can be served alone or inside a warm tortilla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filling for these tacos can also stand alone as a potato salad, but it’s very nice and comforting inside a warm tortilla.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Potato ‘Salad’ and Tomatillo Tacos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatillos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam