ations', 'value': 'Forbes Magazine', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T18:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ee82f0d-7178-5788-bee1-dbf108f9b460', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ee82f0d-7178-5788-bee1-dbf108f9b460'}, {'abstract': 'Did he really want to run? Does he get why the 47 percent comment was a big deal?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/romneys-reflections/', 'snippet': 'Did he really want to run? Does he get why the 47 percent comment was a big deal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two of the big questions about Mitt Romney when he was running for president in 2012 were: How much did he want the job? And, just how out of touch with reality was he? The answers, judging from an excerpt in the Washington Post of Dan Balz’s new book “Collision 2012,” are: Not much, and more than we ever imagined.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Reflections', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T18:12:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffd8037-48ee-5fa6-bac7-b98a1245c333', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffd8037-48ee-5fa6-bac7-b98a1245c333'}, {'abstract': 'Heat syncope, or fainting, is a risk on hot summer days, and responding properly is necessary to avoid complications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/health/fainting-in-heat.html', 'snippet': 'Heat syncope, or fainting, is a risk on hot summer days, and responding properly is necessary to avoid complications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With temperatures in the Northeast often in the 90s this summer — and the heat index sometimes surpassing 100 degrees — just standing on the street or on a steamy subway platform can place the body under excessive stress. In New York City during the week of July 14, 911 calls were up by 9 percent over the previous year, with many related to the heat, the fire department said. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/health/30after/30after-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fainting in Heat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fainting In Heat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vasovagal Syncope (Fainting)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T18:14:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Jacobson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab33257f-7d9a-5059-a1ae-2fcab59d667f', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab33257f-7d9a-5059-a1ae-2fcab59d667f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Pinkham joins the cast of “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love and Murder” while LaChanze will appear in “If/Then,” a new musical.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/bryce-pinkham-and-lachanze-are-broadway-bound/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Pinkham joins the cast of “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love and Murder” while LaChanze will appear in “If/Then,” a new musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casting additions to two shows scheduled for the coming Broadway season were announced on Monday. Bryce Pinkham, who is playing Longaville in the Public Theater’s Shakespeare in the Park production of “Love’s Labour’s Lost,” will join the cast of “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love and Murder,” the musical by Robert L. Freedman and Steven Lutvak that had a successful run in Hartford last fall and opens on Broadway at the Walter Kerr Theater on Oct. 22. Mr. Pinkham is to play Monty Navarro, who stands to become the Earl of Highhurst once he dispatches the eight better claimants. Those eight heirs are all portrayed by Jefferson Mays, who played the octuple role in Hartford. The show is directed by Darko Tresnjak. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/arts/29artsbeat-lachanze/29artsbeat-lachanze-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bryce Pinkham and LaChanze Are Broadway Bound', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway-Bound Shows Announce More Actors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Acorn Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T18:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4af1dd83-f995-5f30-9128-2e803dfba363', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4af1dd83-f995-5f30-9128-2e803dfba363'}, {'abstract': 'The prevailing narrative among experts is that neither the Israelis nor the Palestinians appear remotely prepared to make the hard calls needed to cement a lasting peace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/kerry-appoints-veteran-diplomat-to-manage-mideast-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The prevailing narrative among experts is that neither the Israelis nor the Palestinians appear remotely prepared to make the hard calls needed to cement a lasting peace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For all of the intricacies of issues like the shape of future borders, security arrangements and the status of Jerusalem, the Middle East peace talks that resumed Monday night are dominated by two simple questions: If it took Secretary of State John Kerry countless phone calls and six trips to the Middle East just to get Israeli and Palestinian officials to the negotiating table, how will it be possible to achieve a comprehensive peace agreement? And what will happen if his herculean negotiating efforts fall short?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/30diplo/30diplo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Talks Begin on Mideast, to Doubts on All Sides', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talks Begin On Mideast, To Doubts On All Sides', '