 11:47 a.m. One minute later, it rested.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Updated, 7:50 p.m. | Lawyers for Fabrice Tourre, the former Goldman Sachs trader accused of defrauding investors in a mortgage deal six years ago, rested their defense on Monday without calling any witnesses, a surprise move that now sets the stage for the closing of one of the most prominent cases from the financial crisis to go to trial.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tourre’s Defense Rests Without Calling a Witness', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trader’s Defense Rests Without Calling a Witness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACA Management LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IKB Deutsche Industriebank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paulson & Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T19:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb56