', '_id': 'nyt://video/e00ef90d-097c-5a61-b49a-cf96f06d51c9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e00ef90d-097c-5a61-b49a-cf96f06d51c9'}, {'abstract': 'In case you missed it, Emily Bazelon wrote an illuminating column on Slate about the so-called evidence behind Todd Akin’s “legitimate rape” comment.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/uncovering-the-truth-behind-a-twisted-anti-abortion-tale/', 'snippet': 'In case you missed it, Emily Bazelon wrote an illuminating column on Slate about the so-called evidence behind Todd Akin’s “legitimate rape” comment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November, the magazine published\xa0Emily Bazelon’s profile of Charmaine Yoest, the head of the Americans United for Life, an anti-abortion group, which has been working with Republican state legislators to write laws making access to abortion more difficult. In her article, Bazelon wrote about the controversy that was sparked when Todd Akin, a Republican congressman from Missouri who was running for the Senate, claimed that victims of “legitimate rape” cannot become pregnant. Akin’s comments had apparently been based on, as Bazelon wrote, a“1972 essay by an obstetrician named Fred Mecklenburg, who cited a Nazi experiment in which women were told they were on their way to die in the gas chambers — and then were allowed to live, so that doctors could check whether they would still ovulate. Since few did, Mecklenburg claimed that women exposed to the emotional trauma of rape wouldn’t be able to become pregnant, either.” Mecklenburg’s essay was published in a book financed by the anti-abortion group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncovering the Truth Behind a Twisted Anti-Abortion Tale', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoest, Charmaine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Americans United for Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T21:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ilena Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ilena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/210ae54c-6c3d-50e3-821c-6756aa079f59', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://ar