nsylvania graduate students to help clean and restore some of its 1,316 mausoleums and 150,000 monuments and gravestones.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/bronx-cemetery-offers-a-different-sort-of-internship/', 'snippet': 'Woodlawn has enlisted four University of Pennsylvania graduate students to help clean and restore some of its 1,316 mausoleums and 150,000 monuments and gravestones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even the best internships can require some degree of menial labor: answering phones, working copy machines, making Starbucks runs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/nyregion/29cityroom-woodlawn/29cityroom-woodlawn-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Summer Internship at a Place Where Most People Stay for Good', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cemeteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Woodlawn Cemetery (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T21:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1644fc9-2c4e-5ee0-8660-78082c0adeca', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1644fc9-2c4e-5ee0-8660-78082c0adeca'}, {'abstract': 'Why the billable hour no longer makes economic sense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/magazine/whats-an-idea-worth.html', 'snippet': 'Why the billable hour no longer makes economic sense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a lot of accountants, Jason Blumer never really wanted to be an accountant; he wanted to play guitar in a hair-metal band. But like most guys who want to play guitar in a hair-metal band, Blumer eventually realized that there wasn’t much money in touring bars and being paid in beer-smeared $20 bills. So he changed gears and decided to follow his dad into what seemed like one of the more steady businesses around. After college, he bought some suits, joined a midsize firm in South Carolina and processed his clients’ payroll and tax returns. He billed them by the hour. He hated every second of it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 734}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1738, 'width': 1421, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04economy/mag-04Economy-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s an Idea Worth?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "What's an Hour of  Your Time Worth?", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blumer, Jason', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-29T22:06:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/769d5d00-1dad-5bb1-a919-fe60018ae1a1', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/769d5d00-1dad-5bb1-a919-fe60018ae1a1'}, {'abstract': 'A channel for young people called Pivot, which will become available in 40 million homes on Thursday, aims for “entertainment that inspires and compels social change.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/business/media/pivot-tv-pitches-to-young-viewers.html', 'snippet': 'A channel for young people called Pivot, which will become available in 40 million homes on Thursday, aims for “entertainment that inspires and compels social change.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toward the end of Evan Shapiro’s semester-long course on television management at New York University, he spends an hour on the topic “Building a Post-Network Channel from the Ground Up.” For the 19- and 20-year-old students — the fickle viewers that advertisers and programmers so desperately w