', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/tunnel-vision/', 'snippet': 'A short impressionistic film shot from New York City subway trains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This movie runs thousands of times every day. It’s in 3D and Sensurround and it’s an entertainment bargain thrown in free with the price of every subway swipe. The best seating is actually standing, at the head or rear of the train, eyes glued to the window. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tunnel Vision’', 'kicker': 'Jeff Scher', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Scher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac28e61c-7368-55fa-93ee-994b60de6a18', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac28e61c-7368-55fa-93ee-994b60de6a18'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki is in danger of losing control of his country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/opinion/al-qaeda-in-iraq-scores-big.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki is in danger of losing control of his country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jailbreaks are common in Iraq, but the brazen assaults on the prisons at Abu Ghraib and Taji last week are in a class by themselves. The attacks freed perhaps as many as 800 militants, who are now sought by Interpol as a “major threat” to global security. The attacks showed the fearsome and growing strength of Al Qaeda in Iraq, seemingly on the decline only a few years ago. They also raised new questions about the effectiveness of Iraq’s authoritarian prime minister, Nuri Kamal al-Maliki, as well as the stability of Iraq itself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Qaeda in Iraq Scores Big', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Al Qaeda in Iraq Scores Big', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ABU GHRAIB (IRAQ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taji (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/25513cd3-95c8-5e76-8858-8743530445d2', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25513cd3-95c8-5e76-8858-8743530445d2'}, {'abstract': 'Janet Yellen is clearly the best choice. Will President Obama see that?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/opinion/choosing-the-next-fed-leader.html', 'snippet': 'Janet Yellen is clearly the best choice. Will President Obama see that?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite a campaign from allies both inside and outside the White House, the recent drive to install Lawrence Summers as the next chairman of the Federal Reserve seems to be faltering — and with good reason: He is not the best person for the job, as a group of Democratic senators made clear in a letter to President Obama last week calling for the nomination of Janet Yellen, the vice chairwoman of the Fed’s board of governors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Choosing the Next Fed Leader', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Choosing the Next Fed Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Lawrence H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0bc7dae-b4cd-5347-85ed-26688f9505b8', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0bc7dae-b4cd-5347-85ed-26688f9505b8'}, {'abstract': 'Support is growing for an important proposal that would give independent military prosecutors the power to decide which sexual assault crimes to try.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/opinion/an-escalating-fight-over-military-justice.html', 'snippet': 'Support is growing for an important proposal that would give independent military prosecutors the power to decide which sexual assault crimes to try.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite powerful evidence that the military’s approach to sexual assault needs an overhaul, the resistance to change among military brass and their enablers on Capitol Hill remains fierce.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Escalating Fight Over Military Justice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Escalating Fight Over Military Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Carl M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/69c5c2a8-f25c-5c2e-a731-56463d75fbc2', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69c5c2a8-f25c-5c2e-a731-56463d75fbc2'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration has prodded Egypt’s generals to restore a democratic government while trying not to jeopardize any future influence on the military or undermine security arrangements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/for-us-balancing-act-with-egypt-grows-more-complicated.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration has prodded Egypt’s generals to restore a democratic government while trying not to jeopardize any future influence on the military or undermine security arrangements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In four weeks of quiet but intense diplomacy, the Obama administration has engaged in a balancing act, prodding Egypt’s generals to avoid violence and restore a democratic government while trying not to jeopardize any future influence on the military or undermine security arrangements that have been at the heart of a three-decade relationship.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Balancing Act With Egypt Grows Trickier', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Balancing Act With Egypt Grows Trickier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdul-Fattah el-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf17b02-a453-548c-aef5-b6b8fbb88ffa', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf17b02-a453-548c-aef5-b6b8fbb88ffa'}, {'abstract': 'A new group dedicated to paving the way for a Hillary Clinton campaign in 2016 has recruited dozens of the Democratic Party’s most elite donors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/us/politics/a-bet-on-clinton-if-they-network-she-will-run.html', 'snippet': 'A new group dedicated to paving the way for a Hillary Clinton campaign in 2016 has recruited dozens of the Democratic Party’s most elite donors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new group dedicated to paving the way for a Hillary Clinton campaign in 2016 has already recruited dozens of the Democratic Party’s elite donors and bundlers, effectively kicking off the presidential money hunt more than three years before Election Day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/0730CLINTON01/0730CLINTON01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/us/0730CLINTON01/0730CLINTON01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/0730CLINTON01/0730CLINTON01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/0730CLINTON01/0730CLINTON01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/us/0730CLINTON01/0730CLINTON01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/us/0730CLINTON01/0730CLINTON01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'