'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:49:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae723ba7-37f9-5138-a4a1-78ca9b5931ae', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae723ba7-37f9-5138-a4a1-78ca9b5931ae'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Ali Laarayedh announced Monday that elections would be held Dec. 17 and said the government would stay in office to see through the transition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/world/africa/tunisia-prime-minister-calls-for-december-elections.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Ali Laarayedh announced Monday that elections would be held Dec. 17 and said the government would stay in office to see through the transition.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In a concession to opposition groups that have been calling for his Islamist-led coalition to resign, Prime Minister Ali Laarayedh announced Monday that elections would be held Dec. 17. Mr. Laarayedh said the government would stay in office to see through the transition. “We are not clinging to power, but we have a duty and a responsibility that we will exercise to the end,” he said in comments on state television. One of the smaller parties in the ruling coalition, Ettakatol, has joined opposition calls for a government of national unity to replace the current government after the assassination of the legislator Mohamed Brahmi last week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisia: Prime Minister Calls for December Elections', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunisia: Prime Minister Calls for December Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gall, Carlotta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laarayedh, Ali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:50:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5041e5c8-9933-58f3-98a7-b38cc87ebcb4', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5041e5c8-9933-58f3-98a7-b38cc87ebcb4'}, {'abstract': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad of Iran, whose tumultuous two-term tenure is in its final few days, will be moving to academia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/world/middleeast/iran-ahmadinejad-granted-license-to-start-university.html', 'snippet': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad of Iran, whose tumultuous two-term tenure is in its final few days, will be moving to academia.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad of Iran, whose tumultuous two-term tenure is in its final few days, will be moving to academia. The government’s Islamic Republic News Agency announced Monday that Mr. Ahmadinejad had been granted a license to start an international university in Tehran. It was the first official confirmation of Mr. Ahmadinejad’s postpresidential plans, which had been the subject of speculation for some time. The news agency said the charter of Mr. Ahmadinejad’s university, which apparently has not been named yet, must still be approved by two government ministries. Mr. Ahmadinejad, who could not run for a third term, is to relinquish the presidency on Sunday to the cleric Hassan Rouhani. Mr. Rouhani has promised a less confrontational style than Mr. Ahmadinejad, a conservative whose eight years in office were marked by fewer personal freedoms, more economic problems, fraud accusations and violent protests over his re-election in 2009, and Iran’s increased isolation over its disputed nuclear energy program. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Ahmadinejad Granted License to Start University', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Ahmadinejad Granted License to Start University', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T01:54:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6141da7-ada1-5d14-bd58-802b6494cc26', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6141da7-ada1-5d14-bd58-802b6494cc26'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 30, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/pageoneplus/corrections-july-30-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on July 30, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 30, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T02:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/422c3394-259e-55de-acc1-fd32faab110b', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/422c3394-259e-55de-acc1-fd32faab110b'}, {'abstract': 'Peter A. Collins is making a list for us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/29/on-the-list/', 'snippet': 'Peter A. Collins is making a list for us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — If music was a formative part of your journey to adulthood, this is a puzzle for you. It took me a while to settle in to the execution of the grid (I was a bit thrown by the way “LIKE A ROLLING STONE” was broken up), but once I did, I found myself humming along with Peter A. Collins’s tribute to the ROLLING STONE list of the “500 Greatest Songs of All Time.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the List', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T02:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_