on of the Voting Rights Act of 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Days after his administration filed suit against Texas to protect minority voters, President Obama told civil rights leaders and local officials on Monday that the federal government would vigorously enforce voting rights in the country despite a Supreme Court ruling against a core section of a landmark 1965 law, several participants said after a White House meeting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Reassures Leaders on Enforcing Voting Rights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Reassures Leaders on Enforcing Voting Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T02:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f51b98d2-a56f-5119-b79b-54e72ab8e0eb', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f51b98d2-a56f-5119-b79b-54e72ab8e0eb'}, {'abstract': 'Despite his slight build, the Yankees’ Alfonso Soriano has consistently used one of the heaviest bats in baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/sports/baseball/for-soriano-a-heavy-bat-has-always-felt-just-right.html', 'snippet': 'Despite his slight build, the Yankees’ Alfonso Soriano has consistently used one of the heaviest bats in baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About a decade ago, during Alfonso Soriano’s first stint with the Ya