any said it would not back down in a fight against settlement claims it viewed as false.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/business/global/bp-reports-drop-in-second-quarter-income.html', 'snippet': 'The British oil company said it would not back down in a fight against settlement claims it viewed as false.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British oil giant BP plans to step up its defense against litigation stemming from the 2010 Gulf of Mexico oil spill as it continues to endure the financial fallout from the disaster, reporting weaker-than-expected earnings on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spill Claims Rising, BP Announces Weak Results', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spill Claims Rising, BP Announces Weak Results', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T08:40:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/741ed004-c281-57c6-a480-69085107bc01', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/741ed004-c281-57c6-a480-69085107bc01'}, {'abstract': 'A new documentary airing on PBS explores the shortcomings of the assisted living industry.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/a-dark-view-of-assisted-living/', 'snippet': 'A new documentary airing on PBS explores the shortcomings of the assisted living industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Assisted living underwent a big growth spurt in the 1990s as major corporations built and bought facilities, and almost ever since advocacy groups and researchers have been warning that however attractive these places look — chandeliered lobbies, pleasant individual apartments, the inevitable gazebo outside — the care they provide tends to be mediocre at best.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dark View of Assisted Living', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T09:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/868c3f0f-b568-5f5b-b963-c17fa312fdbe', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/868c3f0f-b568-5f5b-b963-c17fa312fdbe'}, {'abstract': 'The Toronto-based photographer Ian Willms went to Alberta, Canada, to document the profitable yet hazardous oil sands, which have disfigured the landscape and its indigenous people.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/a-shining-sun-blotted-by-oil-sands/', 'snippet': 'The Toronto-based photographer Ian Willms went to Alberta, Canada, to document the profitable yet hazardous oil sands, which have disfigured the landscape and its indigenous people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ian Willms has photographed the effects of oil extraction on First Nations land in Fort McKay and Fort Chipewyan, in northern Alberta, Canada. Mr. Willms, 28, based in Toronto, is a founding member of the Boreal Collective and spent several months over the last three years photographing his project “As Long as the Sun Shines.” His interview with James Estrin has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Indigenous Way of Life Threatened by Oil Sands in Canada', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T09:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54bdeb2a-4053-5928-b701-1303823a7210', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54bdeb2a-4053-5928-b701-1303823a7210'}, {'abstract': 'What is the predicted loss of sales for Southern crops like peaches and tomatoes this year?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/6-qs-about-the-news-a-small-rainy-harvest-for-southern-farms/', 'snippet': 'What is the predicted loss of sales for Southern crops like peaches and tomatoes this year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Too Much Rain in the South, Too Little Produce on the Shelves,” Kim Severson writes about the effects on many summer favorites like watermelons and peaches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed