, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17fabe4-3d8d-5683-bd57-869ff121fb92'}, {'abstract': 'Yahoo does have some influence, the author notes. It has a representative on Alibaba’s board and the right to appoint an investment bank to help run any offering process.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/why-an-alibaba-i-p-o-is-both-promise-and-problem-for-yahoo/', 'snippet': 'Yahoo does have some influence, the author notes. It has a representative on Alibaba’s board and the right to appoint an investment bank to help run any offering process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alibaba is Yahoo’s best investment, and its most frustrating problem. Its 24 percent stake in Alibaba, China’s biggest online retailer, is probably worth more than Yahoo’s entire booked assets of $16 billion. But a future initial public offering, in which Yahoo has promised to sell half its shares, may deliver much less. That is because Alibaba holds most of the cards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why an Alibaba I.P.O. Is Both Promise and Problem for Yahoo', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALIBABA.COM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T15:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Foley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24fa6bb7-24ed-50e4-b505