ions-in-us-subsidies-go-to-dead-farmers.html', 'snippet': 'A report by the Government Accountability Office found that the Agriculture Department lacked the proper controls to make sure the money it sent was going to the right people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The federal government pays millions of dollars in farm subsidies each year to farmers who have died, because the Agriculture Department lacks the proper controls to make sure the money it sends is going to the right people, a government audit has found.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions in U.S. Subsidies Go to Dead Farmers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crop Controls and Subsidies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T16:59:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f484dfff-534c-5a85-9d01-999a29b87164', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f484dfff-534c-5a85-9d01-999a29b87164'}, {'abstract': 'Being a concours judge must be difficult; they have to choose winners out of so many gorgeous cars.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/fantasy-at-the-2013-concours-delegance-of-america/', 'snippet': 'Being a concours judge must be difficult; they have to choose winners out of so many gorgeous cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PLYMOUTH, Mich. — As I admired the 374 cars on display at Sunday’s Concours d’Elegance of America here, it occurred to me that I’d make a bad concours judge. I can recognize a fine automobile, but my objectivity is clouded by passion. Although that may disqualify me as an arbiter of automotive worth, it’s conducive to enjoying a day at a car show. All that follows is based on owner interviews and documentation provided by the concours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/29/automobiles/wheels/35-alfa-1/35-alfa-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'he