icine-bottles-even-more-child-resistant/', 'snippet': 'If you don’t get the cap all the way back on, most 3- and 4-year olds can drain a bottle of sweetened medicine in minutes. New flow restrictors could help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study, published in the Journal of Pediatrics, found that most 3- and 4-year-olds were able to open, and within two minutes swallow, what was left in uncapped or incompletely closed child-resistant liquid medication bottles (96 percent for uncapped and 82 percent for incompletely closed).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Medicine Bottles Even More Child-Resistant', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T17:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b118116-8be0-5e19-bc3f-6174f1879b2c', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b118116-8be0-5e19-bc3f-6174f1879b2c'}, {'abstract': 'Floyd Cardoz, executive chef at North End Grill, searches for inspiration by returning to his Indian roots, finding spicy, sweet and sour flavors in two New Jersey towns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/dining/100000002364292/finding-ones-own-masala.html', 'snippet': 'Floyd Cardoz, executive chef at North End Grill, searches for inspiration by returning to his Indian roots, findi