Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b656032-f879-5cfe-b103-0ae6bd15cdc1', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b656032-f879-5cfe-b103-0ae6bd15cdc1'}, {'abstract': 'This elegant beauty from Atelier Cologne raises the bar for stylish travel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/30/feeling-for-a-travel-size-fragrance-pouch-in-monogrammed-leather/', 'snippet': 'This elegant beauty from Atelier Cologne raises the bar for stylish travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many fragrance brands offer complimentary travel-size bottles of perfume along with a larger purchase. But Atelier Cologne ups the ante in the most elegant way imaginable. Perhaps this is no surprise, considering that the three-year-old fragrance house’s founders live in Paris and New York, and surely appreciate the value of traveling in style. When you purchase any 200-milliliter bottle of one of their clean, unisex scents — Orange Sanguine, Grand Néroli, Vétiver Fatal — you get a 30-milliliter travel spray of your choice along with a French leather case that comes with custom hand-engraving. There are seven possible shades of leather — aubergine, turquoise, lilac, red, burgundy, black and gray — and your choice of silver or gold lettering. Simple initials are probably classiest, but the brand offers you up to 20 characters to say what you want. You can also purchase the pouches à la carte.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | A Travel-Size Fragrance Pouch in Monogrammed Leather', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-30T22:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/201f8740-3372-5f4d-ac30-573dcaf3bb47', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/201f8740-3372-5f4d-ac30-573dcaf3bb47'}, {'abstract': 'The contract for the fifth and sixth batch of fighter jets calls for lower prices than the Defense Department paid in the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/business/pentagon-buys-71-more-f-35s-from-lockheed-martin.html', 'snippet': 'The contract for the fifth and sixth batch of fighter jets calls for lower prices than the Defense Department paid in the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Defense Department on Tuesday announced an agreement in principle to buy 71 more F-35 fighter jets from Lockheed Martin at somewhat lower prices than last year. Pentagon officials said they would pay 4 percent less for 36 of the radar-evading jets under the new orders and 8 percent less than last year’s price for the other 35.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/business/JET/JET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/business/JET/JET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 488}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/business/JET/JET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty