/sports/ncaafootball/three-penn-state-officials-are-ordered-to-stand-trial.html', 'snippet': 'The three former university officials, including the former president Graham B. Spanier, are charged with perjury, conspiracy and other crimes in the Jerry Sandusky case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three former high-ranking Penn State officials, including the university’s former president, Graham B. Spanier, were ordered Tuesday to stand trial on charges that they were part of a cover-up related to the child sexual abuse scandal involving the former football coach Jerry Sandusky. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Penn State Officials Are Ordered to Stand Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Former Penn State Officials Will Be Tried', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perjury', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spanier, Graham B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schultz, Gary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curley, Tim', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueary, Mike', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T00:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2af10e34-dc58-5537-aa33-8910dde6fc11', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2af10e34-dc58-5537-aa33-8910dde6fc11'}, {'abstract': 'The San Diego City Council voted to file a lawsuit against Mayor Bob Filner to recover any damages the city may have to pay as a result of a sexual harassment lawsuit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/us/politics/california-san-diego-city-council-to-sue-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'The San Diego City Council voted to file a lawsuit against Mayor Bob Filner to recover any damages the city may have to pay as a result of a sexual harassment lawsuit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The San Diego City Council on Tuesday unanimously voted to file a lawsuit against Mayor Bob Filner to recover any damages the city may have to pay as a result of a sexual harassment lawsuit that has been filed against him and the city. The mayor’s former communications deputy, Irene McCormack Jackson, sued last week, alleging that he harassed her on the job. Six more women have since accused him of harassment, though no more lawsuits have been filed. The Council’s lawsuit does not admit any liability, but moves to hold Mr. Filner responsible for any damages and legal fees. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: San Diego City Council to Sue Mayor', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: San Diego City Council To Sue Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filner, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 5, 'majo