tle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c4a4de-bb3c-5467-93c4-7d9ebaba71fc', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c4a4de-bb3c-5467-93c4-7d9ebaba71fc'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Smash and Grab” has inside tales of the Pink Panthers, an international high-stakes crime ring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/movies/smash-and-grab-goes-inside-the-pink-panthers.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Smash and Grab” has inside tales of the Pink Panthers, an international high-stakes crime ring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The insider’s level of detail that gives so many good crime movies their bite is also what makes the documentary “Smash and Grab: The Story of the Pink Panthers” guiltily absorbing. In sketching out the story of the Serbian thievery ring of the title, named after the Inspector Clouseau movies, this unpretty but titillatingly informative film from Havana Marking essentially lets two criminals give a master class in high-stakes robbery. Their accounts cover preparation (cast a distracting woman to case the joint), execution (no job should last more than a half-minute) and aftermath (fencing goods is no picnic, and expect a permanent hangover of paranoia).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/smash1/smash1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/smash1/smash1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/smash1/smash1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 869, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJum