ent most of his adult years, requires long drives down country roads, time that King, whose mind is restless, likes to fill by listening to books on tape. In the ’80s, however, he sometimes could not find the books he wanted on tape — or maybe he just did not bother. He had three children: Naomi, Joe and Owen. They could read, couldn’t they? All King had to do was press record. Which is how his school-age children came to furnish their father, over the years, with a small library’s worth of books on tape.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/mag-04King-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/mag-04King-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/mag-04King-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/mag-04King-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1534, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/04king1-thumb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/04king1-thumb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04king1-thumb/04king1-thumb-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephen King’s Family Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Children of the Pen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Naomi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Tabitha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Joe (1972- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Owen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braffet, Kelly', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0250a72d-a190-5161-90ae-a474a46b448f', 'word_count': 6294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0250a72d-a190-5161-90ae-a474a46b448f'}, {'abstract': 'In a “Turning Point” interview, a young photographer discusses how the work of his inspiration, Gordon Parks, showed him the importance of patience, and gaining trust.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/be-a-human-first-then-take-the-photo/', 'snippet': 'In a “Turning Point” interview, a young photographer discusses how the work of his inspiration, Gordon Parks, showed him the importance of patience, and gaining trust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Demetrius Freeman is one of two photo interns at The New York Times from Western Kentucky University. Before joining The Times, Mr. Freeman, 27, spent two years after high school traveling in Denmark, Spain, Germany and Atlanta, Ga., while picking up freelance photo assignments for clients including Home Depot, Norfolk Southern and the Georgia Innocence Project. Originally from Atlanta, he recently completed a semester abroad at the Danish School of Media and Journalism and will be returning to Western Kentucky in the fall to complete his degree in photojournalism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Be a Human First, Then Take the Photo', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parks, Gordon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T09:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Whitney Richardson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Whitney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richardson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7112e239-31eb-57ea-be91-b8a6d5d6dc92', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7112e239-31eb-57ea-be91-b8a6d5d6dc92'}, {'abstract': 'What verdict did a military judge hand down in the trial of Pfc. Bradley Manning?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/6-qs-about-the-news-bradley-manning-found-not-guilty-of-aiding-the-enemy/', 'snippet': 'What verdict did a military judge hand down in the trial of Pfc. Bradley Manning?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the video “Inside the Bradley Manning Trial,” the case’s verdict is outlined.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | Bradley Manning Found Not Guilty of Aiding the Enemy', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T09:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a19f613b-ca6e-5608-b1e7-5812a00180c9', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a19f613b-ca6e-5608-b1e7-5812a00180c9'}, {'abstract': 'More than one million people lost electricity for more than 24 hours after a power cooperative was cut off for $92 million in unpaid bills.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/world/asia/power-is-cut-to-philippine-province-over-unpaid-bills.html', 'snippet': 'More than one million people lost electricity for more than 24 hours after a power cooperative was cut off for $92 million in unpaid bills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — A Philippine province of 1.2 million people was without electricity for more than a day after the corporation that runs the national grid cut it off over $92 million in unpaid bills, officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bills Unpaid, Power Is Cut to Province in Philippines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bills Unpaid, Power Is Cut To Province In Philippines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T09:33:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By