, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e51c95f-cd57-5eb9-a0b2-cef800e7db18', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e51c95f-cd57-5eb9-a0b2-cef800e7db18'}, {'abstract': 'Capt. André Cailloux, the first black hero of the Union Army.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/the-rock-of-new-orleans/', 'snippet': 'Capt. André Cailloux, the first black hero of the Union Army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, July 29, 1863, an unprecedented crowd of slaves, runaways and free people of color gathered along the downtown streets of federally occupied New Orleans. They did so not only to honor and bid farewell to one of their own, Capt. André Cailloux of the 1st Regiment of the Louisiana Native Guards, who had fallen at the siege of Port Hudson, La., but also to send a message of defiance to white New Orleanians, most of whom favored the Confederate cause. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rock of New Orleans', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T15:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Ochs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Ochs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c4c3ff-d7f7-560b-a639-2500e6387862', 'word_count': 2225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c4c3ff-d7f7-560b-a639-2500e6387862'}, {'abstract': 'The Great Recession was not as bad as we thought, and the recovery since then has been a little better than we thought, according to the latest government revisions.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/a-not-so-great-great-recession/', 'snippet': 'The Great Recession was not as bad as we thought, and the recovery since then has been a little better than we thought, according to the latest government revisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 2:03 p.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Not-So-Great Great Recession', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T15:47:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9006b94-eaf8-53b8-9e09-b69f99667a1b', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9006b94-eaf8-53b8-9e09-b69f99667a1b'}, {'abstract': 'Times readers share the inspiration that made them devote their lives or careers to popular music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/arts/music/first-crush-pop-music.html', 'snippet': 'Times readers share the inspiration that made them devote their lives or careers to popular music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer, a number of New York Times critics are writing about their cultural first crushes — the moments or works that prompted them to write about the arts. A new essay will arrive each week, paired with stories from readers who work within the given discipline about their own cultural epiphanies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/music/31-firstcrush-pop/31-firstcrush-pop-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your First Crush', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T15:50:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3476e037-23f1-564d-9147-1de89623bff2', 'word_count': 1306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3476e037-23f1-564d-9147-1de89623bff2'}, {'abstract': 'The public editor takes on readers’ questions, offering some answers.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/perfectly-reasonable-question-no-1-on-direct-quotations-in-articles/', 'snippet': 'The public editor takes on readers’ questions, offering some answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A reader, Edward Hershey of Portland, Ore., wrote to me some time ago about an article in Sports by the basketball writer Howard Beck. Mr. Hershey, who described himself as “a former sportswriter in the Red Smith-Jimmy Cannon era,” wondered about Mr. Beck’s use of a quotation from the Miami Heat forward LeBron James. It came deep within what he accurately called “a compelling deadline story following the first game of the N.B.A. championship series.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perfectly Reasonable Question No. 1: On Direct Quotations in Articles', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T15:50:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfa21e1f-51b6-5438-b9de-5f16c818228b', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfa21e1f-51b6-5438-b9de-5f16c818228b'}, {'abstract': 'Debate over the controversial 2008 gun battle in Batla House area of Delhi continues.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/debate-over-controversial-delhi-encounter-continues/', 'snippet': 'Debate over the controversial 2008 gun battle in Batla House area of Delhi continues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI – The questions surrounding the controversial Batla House encounter in New Delhi continue to be unresolved. On Tuesday, a local court sentenced Shahzad Ahmad, 24, the only person arrested after the September 19, 2008 gunfight between Delhi police officials and suspected terrorists in Batla House area of south Delhi, to life imprisonment for killing a police officer. But human rights activists contesting the police version say that the legal battles around the half a decade old episode are far from over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/30-batla-house-encounter-IndiaInk/30-batla-house-encounter-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/30/world/30-batla-house-encounter-IndiaInk/30-batla-house-encounter-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/world/30-batla-house-encounter-IndiaInk/30-batla-house-encounter-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c