'', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Eisinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc208de5-3c56-5879-a748-b3e55f30df8b', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc208de5-3c56-5879-a748-b3e55f30df8b'}, {'abstract': 'Swiss researchers have found evidence that the lunar cycle may affect sleep patterns, with total sleep time lowest at full moon.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/moon-phases-tied-to-sleep-cycles/', 'snippet': 'Swiss researchers have found evidence that the lunar cycle may affect sleep patterns, with total sleep time lowest at full moon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lunar cycle has been tied to a range of mysterious powers, from increases in violent crimes and hospital admissions to fertility and blood loss, and scientists consider most such beliefs nonsensical.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/science/31wellmoon/31wellmoon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/science/31wellmoon/31wellmoon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/science/31wellmoon/31wellmoon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/science/31wellmoon/31wellmoon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': 