ible for revealing that J.K. Rowling wrote a mystery novel under a pen name, also apologized to her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The London law firm responsible for revealing that J.\u2009K. Rowling is the author of the detective novel “The Cuckoo’s Calling” has agreed to make a “substantial” donation to charity as part of an apology.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Make It Up to Rowling, Law Firm Makes a Donation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Law Firm in Rowling Flap to Make Amends With a Charitable Donation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russells', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T18:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/682eb743-96de-5a44-b0f0-e61aea787f64', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/682eb743-96de-5a44-b0f0-e61aea787f64'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh fruit should not become a casualty in the sugar wars, many nutrition experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/making-the-case-for-eating-fruit/', 'snippet': 'Fresh fruit should not become a casualty in the sugar wars, many nutrition experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Experts agree that we are eating too much sugar, which is contributing to obesity and other health problems. But in the rush to avoid sugar, many low-carb dieters and others are avoiding fruits. But fresh fruit should not become a casualty in the sugar wars, many nutrition experts say. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/25/science/25wellfruit/25wellfruit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Case for Eating Fruit', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T18:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophie Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/011cf953-2f18-513c-ae8b-742b56db4bd9', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/011cf953-2f18-513c-ae8b-742b56db4bd9'}, {'abstract': '“Stars Dance,” her fourth album, sold 97,000 copies in its first week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/selena-gomez-hits-no-1/', 'snippet': '“Stars Dance,” her fourth album, sold 97,000 copies in its first week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After five weeks of rap albums topping the Billboard charts, it’s back to pop. Selena Gomez, who made her name as part of Disney’s fold of singing, smiling teens, has scored her first No. 1 album with “Stars Dance” (Hollywood). The album, her fourth, sold 97,000 copies last week, according to Nielsen SoundScan, and Billboard notes that Ms. Gomez, now 21, enjoys a distinction that is getting rarer: each of her last three albums has opened with more sales than the one before it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-music/31artsbeat-music-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-music/31artsbeat-music-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 848}}, {'rank': 0,