 in February.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/business/media/essence-magazine-names-new-top-editor.html', 'snippet': 'This is its fifth editor in 13 years. The last one had been dismissed in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After being without an editor in chief since February, Essence magazine has announced a new leader, its fifth in 13 years. Vanessa K. Bush will assume the top job immediately.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Essence Magazine Names New Top Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Essence Magazine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T18:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7988dde-2db7-5270-a4db-67c9cc2c16d2', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7988dde-2db7-5270-a4db-67c9cc2c16d2'}, {'abstract': 'George Saunders shared with us his notes for a speech he gave at Syracuse University, in which he shares how one of his biggest regrets sprang from something very small.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/george-saunderss-advice-to-graduates/', 'snippet': 'George Saunders shared with us his notes for a speech he gave at Syracuse University, in which he shares how one of his biggest regrets sprang from something very small.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s long past graduation season, but we recently learned that George Saunders delivered the convocation speech at Syracuse University for the class of 2013, and George was kind enough to send it our way and allow us to reprint it here. The speech touches on some of the moments in his life and larger themes (in his life and work) that George spoke about in the profile we ran back in January — the need for kindness and all the things working against our actually achieving it, the risk in focusing too much on “success,” the trouble with swimming in a river full of monkey feces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Saunders’s Advice to Graduates', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saunders, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T18:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/433f48b9-42a0-53ed-bead-0376df22de2c', 'word_count': 1833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/433f48b9-42a0-53ed-bead-0376df22de2c'}, {'abstract': 'But the shares of the social network giant still have a way to go. In comparison, the Nasdaq market is up more than 20 percent, and Google more than 40 percent since the May 17, 2012, market debut of Facebook.,', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/facebooks-i-p-o-breakthrough/', 'snippet': 'But the shares of the social network giant still have a way to go. In comparison, the Nasdaq market is up more than 20 percent, and Google more than 40 percent since the May 17, 2012, market debut of Facebook.,', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook has at last mobilized back to square one. Its shares finally broke above the $38 price set in the company’s messy initial public offering 14 months ago. That’s largely thanks to Mark Zuckerberg, the chief executive, making the social network’s platform work on smartphones and tablets even as his tech rivals mostly flounder at the task.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook’s I.P.O. Breakthrough', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Reid Garrett', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LinkedIn Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T18:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32841a4f-1887-53d9-b5f8-d5ea9233710d', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32841a4f-1887-53d9-b5f8-d5ea9233710d'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/the-gun-report-july-31-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 18, four young girls were caught in the crossfire of a shooting in a residential neighborhood in East Lansdowne, Pa., and yesterday they told the local ABC News affiliate what it was like.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: July 31, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T19:01:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f430a88c-4f3e-557e-af5f-0a2fc6340dbc', 'word_count': 1424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f430a88c-4f3e-557e-af5f-0a2fc6340dbc'}, {'abstract': 'What a more “liberal” papacy might offer to conservative believers.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/conservative-catholics-and-the-new-pope/', 'snippet': 'What a more “liberal” papacy might offer to conservative believers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A number of Catholics of my acquaintance are resistant to the idea, raised in my last post on Pope Francis, that there might be real daylight between the new pontiff’s emerging program and the approach of his two predecessors. In their view, the possibility that Francis intends to be a social-justice pope who deliberately soft-pedals debates over doctrine and morals is just a media creation, reflecting press caricatures of the church’s divisions rather than Francis’s actual statements and intent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservative Catholics and the New Pope', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T19:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cd29eac-4fc7-52a5-9b71-0e550405660a', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cd29eac-4fc7-52a5-9b71-0e550405660a'}, {'abstract': 'Finn Wittrock has dropped out of the Classic Stage Company’s “Romeo and Juliet,” and William Hurt has signed on as Friar Laurence.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/in-search-of-her-romeo-this-juliet-gains-a-friar-laurence/', 'snippet': 'Finn Wittrock has dropped out of the Classic Stage Company’s “Romeo and Juliet,” and William Hurt has signed on as Friar Laurence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classic Stage Company’s new production of “Romeo and Juliet” has lost its leading man to a film, but gained a film star and onetime New York theater luminary – William Hurt – in the role of Friar Laurence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 790}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1411, 'width': 1071, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-hurt/31artsbeat-hurt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': '