if the slighter third and fourth movements disappoint at all, it can only be in relation to that impossibly beautiful first half, with its heavenly lengths.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1125, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/arts/31artsbeat-piano/31artsbeat-piano-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Consolations of a Schubert Sonata Surplus', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schubert, Franz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T19:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5ff6ede-d31e-53c1-921d-c7f0b6016c4a', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5ff6ede-d31e-53c1-921d-c7f0b6016c4a'}, {'abstract': 'After years as a renter, David Karpa was hoping to buy a one-bedroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/realestate/the-wind-shifts-to-buy-and-east-harlem-beckons.html', 'snippet': 'After years as a renter, David Karpa was hoping to buy a one-bedroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Karpa used to be dead set against buying. It seemed financially imprudent. “I don’t want to stretch just to get into an apartment,” Mr. Karpa would say. His Midtown rent was $2,400 and, for the same price, he didn’t think he could find a nicer place to buy.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt-main-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt-main-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt-main-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im