ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/13221517-4399-5fe1-ad6f-922baa6adc1c', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13221517-4399-5fe1-ad6f-922baa6adc1c'}, {'abstract': 'As mobility and collaboration become standards of work, the design and function of things like document creation and sharing are changing, too.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/a-shifting-workplace-experience/', 'snippet': 'As mobility and collaboration become standards of work, the design and function of things like document creation and sharing are changing, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Compared with offices of the past, the modern workplace is paradoxically both more informal and more relentless. Doors have been replaced by cubicles, formal desks with tables, and long-planned meetings with ad hoc collaboration. Work and home have blended, to the general benefit of work: more and more of us are available at all times, on smartphones and tablets, for e-mail and instant messaging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/technology/bits-at-symbol/bits-at-symbol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 235, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/technology/bits-at-symbol/bits-at-symbol-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 235, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/30/technology/bits-at-symbol/bits-at-symbol-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/30/technology/bits-at-symbol/bits-at-symbol-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shifting Workplace Experience', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Word Processing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Box Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evernote Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T20:08:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfb00a7f-ff8d-5a6c-867b-a28cec7ffdfa', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfb00a7f-ff8d-5a6c-867b-a28cec7ffdfa'}, {'abstract': 'On the recommendation of Narciso Rodriguez, Barneys New York picked up exclusive handbags from the French leather-goods house Moreau-Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/in-store-french-satchels-make-their-debut-stateside/', 'snippet': 'On the recommendation of Narciso Rodriguez, Barneys New York picked up exclusive handbags from the French leather-goods house Moreau-Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French leather-goods house Moreau-Paris dates back to the mid-19th century and finally made its stateside debut last week at Barneys New York. “It happened through a rather unorthodox referral,” said Daniella Vitale, C.O.O. and executive vice president of Barneys. “Narciso Rodriguez was in Paris on holiday and walked past a tiny shop on Rue de Miromesnil, and sent me an e-mail telling me that I should take a look at it next time we were in Paris.” The brand is most famous for its embossed leather travel trunks and accessories, but in recent years, under the design leadership of Fedor Georges Savchenko, formerly of Goyard, it has gained interest for its hand-sewn carryalls. In this five-piece collection designed exclusively for Barneys, fine and exotic leathers are complemented with clean lines, minimal hardware and sophisticated shapes ranging from messenger bags to the open and zip totes sure to be spotted during fashion week. While the just-released basic leather versions are worth a trip to Madison Avenue or barneys.com, the crocodile versions that come out in September may be worth the wait.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | French Satchels Make Their Debut Stateside', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crocodiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Narciso', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barneys New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T20:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f796ca16-b76d-5148-b7a7-819d9fb17f52', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f796ca16-b76d-5148-b7a7-819d9fb17f52'}, {'abstract': 'Crowdsourced mobile apps can provide new perspectives, but how much may depend on the size of the crowd weighing in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/technology/personaltech/using-the-masses-to-improve-apps.html', 'snippet': 'Crowdsourced mobile apps can provide new perspectives, but how much may depend on the size of the crowd weighing in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crowds are a hit. Millions of people, connected by the Internet, are now contributing ideas and information to projects big and small. Crowdsourcing, as it is called, is helping to solve tricky problems and providing localized information. And with the right mobile apps, contributing to the crowd — and using its wisdom — is easier than ever.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 921, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 921}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1335, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/business/SMART2/SMART2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Using the Masses to Improve Apps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using the Masses to Improve Apps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton, Kit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-07-31T20:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09c40a9d-8833-502e-af88-a46af81642de', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09c40a9d-8833-502e-af88-a46af81642de'}, {'abstract': 'The company will mount Eric Simonson’s play that features Derek Jeter, Yogi Berra and other Yankees stars as characters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/bronx-bombers-a-yankees-play-comes-to-primary-stages/', 'snippet': 'The company will mount Eric Simonson’s play that features Derek Jeter, Yogi Berra and other Yankees stars as characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The playwright Eric Simonson has explored the worlds of professional basketball (“Magic/Bird”) and football (“Lombardi”) in recent New York theater seasons. Now it’s baseball’s turn. On Monday the Off Broadway company Primary Stages announced that Mr. Simonson would direct his latest play, “Bronx Bombers,” a drama about the New York Yankees, this fall at the Duke on 42nd Street. The show is to run Sept. 17 through Oct. 19, with opening night to be announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank